ID   1.1.1.14
DE   L-iditol 2-dehydrogenase.
AN   glucitol dehydrogenase.
AN   polyol dehydrogenase.
AN   sorbitol dehydrogenase.
CA   L-iditol + NAD(+) = keto-L-sorbose + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme is widely distributed and has been described in archaea,
CC       bacteria, yeast, plants and animals.
CC   -!- It acts on a number of sugar alcohols, including (but not limited to)
CC       L-iditol, D-glucitol, D-xylitol, and D-galactitol.
CC   -!- Enzymes from different organisms or tissues display different
CC       substrate specificity.
CC   -!- The enzyme is specific to NAD(+) and can not use NADP(+).
DR   Q06004, DHSO_BACSU ;  Q02912, DHSO_BOMMO ;  Q58D31, DHSO_BOVIN ;
DR   Q9Z9U1, DHSO_HALH5 ;  Q00796, DHSO_HUMAN ;  Q4R639, DHSO_MACFA ;
DR   Q64442, DHSO_MOUSE ;  Q29318, DHSO_PIG   ;  Q5R5F3, DHSO_PONAB ;
DR   P27867, DHSO_RAT   ;  P07846, DHSO_SHEEP ;  Q59787, SDH_CERSP  ;
//
ID   1.1.1.15
DE   D-iditol 2-dehydrogenase.
CA   D-iditol + NAD(+) = keto-D-sorbose + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- Also converts xylitol into L-xylulose and L-glucitol into L-fructose.
DR   Q70FD1, ALX1_AMBMO ;
//
ID   1.1.1.16
DE   galactitol 2-dehydrogenase.
CA   galactitol + NAD(+) = keto-D-tagatose + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- Also converts other alditols containing an L-threo-configuration
CC       adjacent to a primary alcohol group into the corresponding sugars.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Agrobacterium rubrum C58 is part of D-altritol and
CC       galactitol degradation pathways.
DR   A9CES4, GDH_AGRFC  ;  Q1MLL4, GDH_RHIJ3  ;  Q59787, SDH_CERSP  ;
//
