//
ID   1.1.1.24
DE   quinate/shikimate dehydrogenase (NAD(+)).
AN   quinate 5-dehydrogenase.
AN   quinate dehydrogenase.
AN   quinic dehydrogenase.
CA   L-quinate + NAD(+) = 3-dehydroquinate + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found mostly in bacteria (mostly, but not exclusively in
CC       Gram-positive bacteria), fungi, and plants, participates in the
CC       degradation of quinate and shikimate with a strong preference for
CC       NAD(+) as a cofactor.
CC   -!- While the enzyme can act on both quinate and shikimate, activity is
CC       higher with the former. cf. EC 1.1.1.25, EC 1.1.1.282,
CC       and EC 1.1.5.8.
DR   Q8FSF0, AROE_COREF ;  A4QB65, AROE_CORGB ;  Q9X5C9, AROE_CORGL ;
DR   P25415, DHQA_EMENI ;  P11635, DHQA_NEUCR ;
//
ID   1.1.1.25
DE   shikimate dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
AN   5-dehydroshikimate reductase.
AN   5-dehydroshikimic reductase.
AN   dehydroshikimic reductase.
AN   DHS reductase.
AN   shikimate 5-dehydrogenase.
AN   shikimate dehydrogenase.
AN   shikimate oxidoreductase.
CA   shikimate + NADP(+) = 3-dehydroshikimate + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- NAD(+) cannot replace NADP(+).
CC   -!- In higher organisms, this enzyme forms part of a multienzyme complex
CC       with EC 4.2.1.10. cf. EC 1.1.1.24, EC 1.1.1.282, and EC 1.1.5.8.
