CC       hydroxy groups of glycerol 1-phosphate to give unsaturated
CC       archaetidic acid, which is acted upon by EC 2.7.7.67 to form CDP-
CC       unsaturated archaeol.
CC   -!- The final step in the pathway involves the addition of L-serine, with
CC       concomitant removal of CMP, leading to the production of unsaturated
CC       archaetidylserine.
CC   -!- Activity of the enzyme is stimulated by K(+).
