//
ID   1.1.1.268
DE   2-(R)-hydroxypropyl-CoM dehydrogenase.
AN   2-(2-(R)-hydroxypropylthio)ethanesulfonate dehydrogenase.
CA   (R)-2-hydroxypropyl-coenzyme M + NAD(+) = 2-oxopropyl-coenzyme M + NADH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Highly specific for (R)-2-hydroxyalkyl thioethers of CoM, in contrast
CC       to EC 1.1.1.269, which is highly specific for the (S)-enantiomer.
CC   -!- Forms component III of a four-component enzyme system (comprising
CC       EC 4.4.1.23 (component I), EC 1.8.1.5 (component II), EC 1.1.1.268
CC       (component III) and EC 1.1.1.269 (component IV)) that is involved in
CC       epoxyalkane carboxylation in Xanthobacter sp. strain Py2.
DR   Q56840, HCDR1_XANP2;
//
ID   1.1.1.269
DE   2-(S)-hydroxypropyl-CoM dehydrogenase.
AN   2-(2-(S)-hydroxypropylthio)ethanesulfonate dehydrogenase.
CA   (S)-2-hydroxypropyl-coenzyme M + NAD(+) = 2-oxopropyl-coenzyme M + NADH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Highly specific for (S)-2-hydroxyalkyl thioethers of CoM, in contrast
CC       to EC 1.1.1.268, which is highly specific for the (R)-enantiomer.
CC   -!- Forms component IV of a four-component enzyme system (comprising
CC       EC 4.4.1.23 (component I), EC 1.8.1.5 (component II), EC 1.1.1.268
CC       (component III) and EC 1.1.1.269 (component IV)) that is involved in
CC       epoxyalkane carboxylation in Xanthobacter sp. strain Py2.
DR   Q56841, HCDS1_XANP2;  A7IQH5, HCDS3_XANP2;
//
ID   1.1.1.270
DE   3beta-hydroxysteroid 3-dehydrogenase.
AN   3-keto-steroid reductase.
AN   3-KSR.
CA   a 3beta-hydroxysteroid + NADP(+) = a 3-oxosteroid + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on multiple 3beta-hydroxysteroids.
CC   -!- Participates in the biosynthesis of zemosterol and cholesterol, where
CC       it catalyzes the reaction in the opposite direction to that shown.
CC   -!- The mammalian enzyme is bifunctional and also catalyzes EC 1.1.1.62.
