ID   1.1.1.272
DE   D-2-hydroxyacid dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
CA   a (2R)-2-hydroxycarboxylate + NADP(+) = a 2-oxocarboxylate + NADPH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, characterized from the halophilic archaeon Haloferax
CC       mediterranei and the mold Aspergillus oryzae, catalyzes a reversible
CC       stereospecific reduction of 2-oxocarboxylic acids into the
CC       corresponding D-2-hydroxycarboxylic acids.
CC   -!- The enzyme prefers substrates with a main chain of 5 carbons (such as
CC       4-methyl-2-oxopentanoate) to those with a shorter chain, and can use
CC       NADH with much lower efficiency. cf. EC 1.1.1.345.
DR   Q2UH56, HADHA_ASPOR;  Q2U0N3, MORA_ASPOR ;  Q05709, VANH_ENTFC ;
//
ID   1.1.1.273
DE   vellosimine dehydrogenase.
CA   10-deoxysarpagine + NADP(+) = vellosimine + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on related alkaloids with an endo-aldehyde group such as
CC       vellosimine (same stereochemistry at C-16) but only slight activity
CC       with exo-aldehydes (epimeric at C-16).
CC   -!- Detected in many cell suspension cultures of plants from the family
CC       Apocynaceae.
//
ID   1.1.1.274
DE   2,5-didehydrogluconate reductase (2-dehydro-D-gluconate-forming).
AN   2,5-diketo-D-gluconate reductase.
CA   2-dehydro-D-gluconate + NADP(+) = 2,5-didehydro-D-gluconate + NADPH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the catabolism of 2,5-didehydrogluconate.
CC       cf. EC 1.1.1.346.
DR   P15339, DKGB_CORSS ;
//
ID   1.1.1.275
DE   (+)-trans-carveol dehydrogenase.
AN   carveol dehydrogenase.
CA   (1R,5S)-carveol + NAD(+) = (S)-carvone + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- NADP(+) cannot replace NAD(+).
CC   -!- Forms part of the monoterpenoid biosynthesis pathway in Carum carvi
CC       (caraway) seeds.
//
ID   1.1.1.276
DE   serine 3-dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
AN   serine 3-dehydrogenase.
CA   L-serine + NADP(+) = aminoacetaldehyde + CO2 + NADPH.
CC   -!- NAD(+) cannot replace NADP(+) (cf. EC 1.1.1.387).
DR   Q8U8I2, SDH_AGRFC  ;  Q9KWN1, SDH_AGRTU  ;
//
ID   1.1.1.277
DE   3beta-hydroxy-5beta-steroid dehydrogenase.
AN   3beta-hydroxysteroid 5beta-oxidoreductase.
AN   3beta-hydroxysteroid 5beta-progesterone oxidoreductase.
CA   3beta-hydroxy-5beta-pregnane-20-one + NADP(+) = 5beta-pregnan-3,20-dione
CA   + NADPH + H(+).
//
ID   1.1.1.278
DE   3beta-hydroxy-5alpha-steroid dehydrogenase.
CA   3beta-hydroxy-5alpha-pregnane-20-one + NADP(+) = 5alpha-pregnane-3,20-
CA   dione + NADPH + H(+).
//
ID   1.1.1.279
DE   (R)-3-hydroxyacid-ester dehydrogenase.
AN   3-oxo ester (R)-reductase.
CA   ethyl (R)-3-hydroxyhexanoate + NADP(+) = ethyl 3-oxohexanoate + NADPH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on ethyl (R)-3-oxobutanoate and some other (R)-3-hydroxy
CC       acid esters.
CC   -!- The (R)- symbol is allotted on the assumption that no substituents
CC       change the order of priority from O-3>C-2>C-4.
CC   -!- A subunit of Saccharomyces cerevisiae EC 2.3.1.86. cf. EC 1.1.1.280.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.1.55.
//
ID   1.1.1.280
DE   (S)-3-hydroxyacid-ester dehydrogenase.
AN   3-oxo ester (S)-reductase.
CA   ethyl (S)-3-hydroxyhexanoate + NADP(+) = ethyl 3-oxohexanoate + NADPH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on 4-oxo- and 5-oxo-fatty acids and their esters. cf.
CC       EC 1.1.1.279.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.1.56.
//
ID   1.1.1.281
DE   GDP-4-dehydro-6-deoxy-D-mannose reductase.
AN   GDP-4-keto-6-deoxy-D-mannose reductase.
AN   GDP-6-deoxy-D-lyxo-4-hexulose reductase.
CA   (1) GDP-alpha-D-rhamnose + NAD(+) = GDP-4-dehydro-alpha-D-rhamnose + NADH
CA   + H(+).
CA   (2) GDP-alpha-D-rhamnose + NADP(+) = GDP-4-dehydro-alpha-D-rhamnose +
CA   NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Differs from EC 1.1.1.187 in that the only product formed is GDP-
CC       alpha-D-rhamnose (GDP-6-deoxy-alpha-D-mannose).
CC   -!- D-rhamnose is a constituent of lipopolysaccharides of Gram-negative
CC       plant and human pathogenic bacteria.
DR   Q6T1X6, RMD_ANETH  ;  Q9HTB6, RMD_PSEAE  ;
//
ID   1.1.1.282
DE   quinate/shikimate dehydrogenase [NAD(P)(+)].
AN   quinate/shikimate dehydrogenase.
CA   (1) L-quinate + NADP(+) = 3-dehydroquinate + NADPH + H(+).
CA   (2) L-quinate + NAD(+) = 3-dehydroquinate + NADH + H(+).
CA   (3) shikimate + NADP(+) = 3-dehydroshikimate + NADPH + H(+).
CA   (4) shikimate + NAD(+) = 3-dehydroshikimate + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- This is the second shikimate dehydrogenase enzyme found in
CC       Escherichia coli.
CC   -!- It can use both quinate and shikimate as substrates and either NAD(+)
CC       or NADP(+) as acceptor.
CC   -!- The low catalytic efficiency with both quinate and shikimate suggests
CC       that neither may be the physiological substrate. cf. EC 1.1.1.24,
CC       EC 1.1.1.25, and EC 1.1.5.8.
