ID   1.1.1.284
DE   S-(hydroxymethyl)glutathione dehydrogenase.
AN   ADH3.
AN   chi-ADH.
AN   class III alcohol dehydrogenase.
AN   FDH.
AN   formaldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   formaldehyde dehydrogenase (glutathione).
AN   formic dehydrogenase.
AN   GD-FALDH.
AN   glutathione-dependent formaldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   GS-FDH.
AN   NAD- and glutathione-dependent formaldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD-dependent formaldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD-linked formaldehyde dehydrogenase.
CA   (1) S-(hydroxymethyl)glutathione + NADP(+) = S-formylglutathione + NADPH
CA   + H(+).
CA   (2) S-(hydroxymethyl)glutathione + NAD(+) = S-formylglutathione + NADH +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The substrate, S-(hydroxymethyl)glutathione, forms spontaneously from
CC       glutathione and formaldehyde; its rate of formation is increased in
CC       some bacteria by the presence of EC 4.4.1.22.
CC   -!- Forms part of the pathway that detoxifies formaldehyde, since the
CC       product is hydrolyzed by EC 3.1.2.12.
CC   -!- Also specifically reduces S-nitrosylglutathione.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.1.1.
