CC   -!- Involved in taurine degradation.
CC   -!- The bacterium Chromohalobacter salexigens strain DSM 3043 possesses
CC       two enzymes that catalyze this reaction, a constitutive enzyme
CC       (encoded by isfD2) and an inducible enzyme (encoded by isfD).
CC   -!- The latter is induced by taurine, and is responsible for most of the
CC       activity observed in taurine-grown cells. cf. EC 1.1.1.433.
DR   Q1QU27, ISFD2_CHRI1;  Q1R183, ISFD_CHRI1 ;  D3U1D9, ISFD_KLEOX ;
//
ID   1.1.1.314
DE   Transferred entry: 1.14.14.95.
