ID   1.1.1.315
DE   11-cis-retinol dehydrogenase.
CA   11-cis-retinol--[retinol-binding protein] + NAD(+) = 11-cis-retinal-
CA   -[retinol-binding protein] + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, abundant in the retinal pigment epithelium, catalyzes
CC       the reduction of 11-cis-retinol to 11-cis-retinal while the substrate
CC       is bound to the retinal-binding protein.
CC   -!- This is a crucial step in the regeneration of 11-cis-retinal,
CC       the chromophore of rhodopsin.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also accept other cis forms of retinol.
DR   O75452, RDH16_HUMAN;  O54909, RDH16_MOUSE;  P50170, RDH16_RAT  ;
DR   Q27979, RDH5_BOVIN ;  Q92781, RDH5_HUMAN ;  O55240, RDH5_MOUSE ;
//
ID   1.1.1.316
DE   L-galactose 1-dehydrogenase.
AN   L-galactose dehydrogenase.
AN   L-GalDH.
CA   L-galactose + NAD(+) = L-galactono-1,4-lactone + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes a step in the ascorbate biosynthesis in higher
CC       plants (Smirnoff-Wheeler pathway).
CC   -!- The activity with NADP(+) is less than 10% of the activity with
CC       NAD(+).
DR   O81884, GALDH_ARATH;
//
ID   1.1.1.317
DE   perakine reductase.
CA   raucaffrinoline + NADP(+) = perakine + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- The biosynthesis of raucaffrinoline from perakine is a side route of
