ID   1.1.1.422
DE   pseudoephedrine dehydrogenase.
CA   (1S,2S)-pseudoephedrine + NAD(+) = (S)-2-methylamino-1-phenylpropan-1-one
CA   + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Arthrobacter sp. TS-15,
CC       acts on a broad range of different aryl-alkyl ketones, such as
CC       haloketones, ketoamines, diketones, and ketoesters.
CC   -!- It accepts various types of aryl groups including phenyl-, pyridyl-,
CC       thienyl-, and furyl-rings, but the presence of an aromatic ring is
CC       essential for the activity.
CC   -!- In addition, the presence of a functional group on the alkyl chain,
CC       such as an amine, a halogen, or a ketone, is also crucial.
CC   -!- The enzyme exhibits a strict anti-Prelog enantioselectivity.
CC   -!- When acting on diketones, it catalyzes the reduction of only the keto
CC       group closest to the ring, with no further reduction to the diol. cf.
CC       EC 1.1.1.423.
