ID   1.1.98.3
DE   decaprenylphospho-beta-D-ribofuranose 2-dehydrogenase.
AN   decaprenylphosphoryl-beta-D-ribofuranose 2'-epimerase.
CA   trans,octa-cis-decaprenylphospho-beta-D-ribofuranose + FAD + H(+) =
CA   trans,octa-cis-decaprenylphospho-beta-D-erythro-pentofuranosid-2-ulose +
CA   FADH2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Mycobacterium smegmatis,
CC       is involved, along with EC 1.1.1.333 in the epimerization of
CC       trans,octacis-decaprenylphospho-beta-D-ribofuranose to trans,octacis-
CC       decaprenylphospho-beta-D-arabinofuranose, the arabinosyl donor for
CC       the biosynthesis of mycobacterial cell wall arabinan polymers.
DR   A0R607, DPRE1_MYCS2;  P9WJF0, DPRE1_MYCTO;  P9WJF1, DPRE1_MYCTU;
//
ID   1.1.98.4
DE   F420H2:quinone oxidoreductase.
CA   oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + a quinol + H(+) = reduced
CA   coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + a quinone.
//
ID   1.1.98.5
DE   secondary-alcohol dehydrogenase (coenzyme-F420).
AN   F420-dependent alcohol dehydrogenase.
AN   F420-dependent secondary alcohol dehydrogenase.
CA   a secondary alcohol + oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + H(+) =
CA   a ketone + reduced coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n).
CC   -!- The enzyme isolated from the methanogenic archaea Methanogenium
CC       liminatans catalyzes the reversible oxidation of various secondary
CC       and cyclic alcohols to the corresponding ketones.
//
ID   1.1.98.6
DE   ribonucleoside-triphosphate reductase (formate).
AN   anaerobic ribonucleoside-triphosphate reductase.
CA   a ribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate + formate + H(+) =
CA   a 2'-deoxyribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate + CO2 + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is expressed in the bacterium Escherichia coli
CC       during anaerobic growth, contains an iron sulfur center.
CC   -!- The active form of the enzyme contains an oxygen-sensitive glycyl
CC       (1-amino-2-oxoethan-1-yl) radical that is generated by the activating
CC       enzyme NrdG via chemistry involving S-adenosylmethionine (SAM) and a
CC       [4Fe-4S] cluster.
CC   -!- The glycyl radical is involved in generation of a transient thiyl
CC       (sulfanyl) radical on a cysteine residue, which attacks the
CC       substrate, forming a ribonucleotide 3'-radical, followed by water
CC       loss to form a ketyl (alpha-oxoalkyl) radical.
CC   -!- The ketyl radical gains an electron from a cysteine residue and a
CC       proton from formic acid, forming 3'-keto-deoxyribonucleotide and
CC       generating a thiosulfuranyl (1lambda(4)-disulfan-1-yl) radical bridge
CC       between methionine and cysteine residues.
CC   -!- Oxidation of formate by the thiosulfuranyl radical results in the
CC       release of CO2 and regeneration of the thiyl radical. cf. EC 1.17.4.1
CC       and EC 1.17.4.2.
DR   P07071, NRDD_BPT4  ;  P28903, NRDD_ECOLI ;  P43752, NRDD_HAEIN ;
DR   Q9L646, NRDD_SALTY ;
//
ID   1.1.98.7
DE   serine-type anaerobic sulfatase-maturating enzyme.
CA   L-seryl-[sulfatase] + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3-oxo-L-alanyl-
CA   [sulfatase] + 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + H(+).
CC   -!- A bacterial radical S-adenosyl-L-methionine (AdoMet) enzyme that
CC       contains three [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in some bacteria, activates a type I sulfatase
CC       enzyme (EC 3.1.6.1) by converting a conserved L-serine residue in the
CC       active site to a unique 3-oxo-L-alanine residue that is essential for
CC       the sulfatase activity.
CC   -!- While the enzyme from Klebsiella pneumoniae is specific for L-serine,
CC       the enzyme from Clostridium perfringens can also act on L-cysteine,
CC       see EC 1.8.98.7.
DR   Q02550, ANSME_BACTN;  P20714, ANSME_KLEAE;  Q9X758, ANSME_KLEPN;
