ID   1.1.99.29
DE   pyranose dehydrogenase (acceptor).
AN   PDH.
AN   pyranose dehydrogenase.
AN   pyranose-quinone oxidoreductase.
AN   quinone-dependent pyranose dehydrogenase.
CA   (1) pyranose + acceptor = pyranos-2-ulose + reduced acceptor.
CA   (2) pyranose + acceptor = pyranos-3-ulose + reduced acceptor.
CA   (3) pyranose + acceptor = pyranos-2,3-diulose + reduced acceptor.
CA   (4) a pyranoside + acceptor = a pyranosid-3-ulose + reduced acceptor.
CA   (5) a pyranoside + acceptor = a pyranosid-3,4-diulose + reduced acceptor.
CC   -!- A number of aldoses and ketoses in pyranose form, as well as
CC       glycosides, gluco-oligosaccharides, sucrose and lactose can act as a
CC       donor.
CC   -!- 1,4-Benzoquinone or ferricenium ion (ferrocene oxidized by removal of
CC       one electron) can serve as acceptor.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.1.3.10, this fungal enzyme does not interact with O2 and
CC       exhibits extremely broad substrate tolerance with variable
CC       regioselectivity (C-3, C-2 or C-3 + C-2 or C-3 + C-4) for
CC       (di)oxidation of different sugars.
CC   -!- D-glucose is exclusively or preferentially oxidized at C-3 (depending
CC       on the enzyme source), but can also be oxidized at C-2 + C-3.
CC   -!- The enzyme also acts on 1->4-alpha- and 1->4-beta-gluco-
CC       oligosaccharides, non-reducing gluco-oligosaccharides and
CC       L-arabinose, which are not substrates of EC 1.1.3.10.
CC   -!- Sugars are oxidized in their pyranose but not in their furanose form.
DR   Q3L1D1, PDH1_AGABI ;  V5NDL4, PDH1_AGACM ;  V5NC32, PDH1_AGAXA ;
