DE   soluble quinoprotein glucose dehydrogenase.
AN   glucose dehydrogenase (PQQ-dependent).
AN   soluble glucose dehydrogenase.
CA   D-glucose + A = D-glucono-1,5-lactone + AH2.
CC   -!- Soluble periplasmic enzyme containing PQQ as cofator, bound to a
CC       calcium ion.
CC   -!- Electron acceptor is not known.
CC   -!- It is assayed with Wurster's Blue or phenazine methosulfate.
CC   -!- It has negligible sequence or structure similarity to other
CC       quinoproteins.
CC   -!- It catalyzes an exceptionally high rate of oxidation of a wide range
CC       of aldose sugars, including D-glucose, galactose, arabinose and
