ID   1.1.99.42
DE   4-pyridoxate dehydrogenase.
CA   4-pyridoxate + A = 5-formyl-3-hydroxy-2-methylpyridine-4-carboxylate +
CA   AH2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Pseudomonas sp. MA-1 and
CC       Mesorhizobium loti, participates in the degradation of pyridoxine
CC       (vitamin B6).
CC   -!- It is membrane bound and contains FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been assayed in vitro in the presence of the
CC       artificial electron acceptor dichloroindophenol (DCPIP).
DR   Q988C9, 4PADH_RHILO;
