ID   1.2.1.8
DE   betaine-aldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   BADH.
AN   betaine aldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   betaine aldehyde oxidase.
CA   betaine aldehyde + NAD(+) + H2O = glycine betaine + NADH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- In many bacteria, plants and animals, the osmoprotectant betaine is
CC       synthesized in two steps: (1) choline to betaine aldehyde and (2)
CC       betaine aldehyde to betaine.
CC   -!- This enzyme is involved in the second step and appears to be the same
CC       in plants, animals and bacteria.
CC   -!- In contrast, different enzymes are involved in the first reaction.
CC   -!- In plants, this reaction is catalyzed by EC 1.14.15.7, whereas in
CC       animals and many bacteria, it is catalyzed by either membrane-bound
CC       EC 1.1.99.1 or soluble EC 1.1.3.17.
CC   -!- In some bacteria, betaine is synthesized from glycine through the
CC       actions of EC 2.1.1.156 and EC 2.1.1.157.
