ID   1.2.1.10
DE   acetaldehyde dehydrogenase (acetylating).
AN   acylating acetaldehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   aldehyde dehydrogenase (acylating).
CA   acetaldehyde + NAD(+) + CoA = acetyl-CoA + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts, more slowly, on glycolaldehyde, propanal and butanal.
CC   -!- In several bacterial species this enzyme forms a bifunctional complex
CC       with EC 4.1.3.39.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the bacteria Burkholderia xenovorans and Thermus
CC       thermophilus also perform the reaction of EC 1.2.1.87.
CC   -!- Involved in the meta-cleavage pathway for the degradation of phenols,
CC       methylphenols and catechols.
CC   -!- NADP(+) can replace NAD(+) but the rate of reaction is much slower.
