ID   1.2.1.25
DE   branched-chain alpha-keto acid dehydrogenase system.
AN   2-oxoisovalerate dehydrogenase (acylating).
AN   branched-chain alpha-keto acid dehydrogenase complex.
CA   3-methyl-2-oxobutanoate + NAD(+) + CoA = 2-methylpropanoyl-CoA + CO2 +
CA   NADH.
CC   -!- This enzyme system catalyzes the oxidative decarboxylation of
CC       branched-chain alpha-keto acids derived from L-leucine, L-isoleucine,
CC       and L-valine to branched-chain acyl-CoAs.
CC   -!- It belongs to the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase system family, which also
CC       includes EC 1.2.1.104, EC 1.2.1.105, EC 1.4.1.27 and EC 2.3.1.190.
CC   -!- With the exception of the glycine cleavage system, which contains 4
CC       components, the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase systems share a common
CC       structure, consisting of three main components, namely a 2-oxoacid
CC       dehydrogenase (E1), a dihydrolipoamide acyltransferase (E2),
CC       and dihydrolipoamide dehydrogenase (E3).
CC   -!- The reaction catalyzed by this system is the sum of three activities:
CC       EC 1.2.4.4, EC 2.3.1.168 and EC 1.8.1.4.
CC   -!- The system also acts on (S)-3-methyl-2-oxopentanoate and 4-methyl-2-
CC       oxopentanoate.
//
