DE   carboxylate reductase (NADP(+)).
AN   aryl-aldehyde dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
CA   an aromatic aldehyde + AMP + diphosphate + NADP(+) =
CA   an aromatic carboxylate + ATP + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme contains an adenylation domain, a phosphopantetheinyl
CC       binding domain, and a reductase domain, and requires activation by
CC       attachment of a phosphopantetheinyl group.
CC   -!- The enzyme activates its substrate to an adenylate form, followed by
CC       a transfer to the phosphopantetheinyl binding domain.
CC   -!- The resulting thioester is subsequently transferred to the reductase
CC       domain, where it is reduced to an aldehyde and released.
