ID   1.2.1.50
DE   long-chain-fatty-acyl-CoA reductase.
AN   acyl-CoA reductase.
CA   a long-chain fatty aldehyde + NADP(+) + CoA = a long-chain fatty acyl-CoA
CA   + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Together with EC 6.2.1.19 forms a fatty acid reductase system which
CC       produces the substrate of EC 1.14.14.3, thus being part of the
CC       bacterial luciferase system.
DR   Q03324, LUXC1_PHOLE;  P29236, LUXC2_PHOLE;  P12748, LUXC_ALIFS ;
DR   Q7N577, LUXC_PHOLL ;  P23113, LUXC_PHOLU ;  P19841, LUXC_PHOPO ;
DR   P08639, LUXC_VIBHA ;
//
ID   1.2.1.51
DE   pyruvate dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
AN   pyruvate:NADP(+) oxidoreductase.
CA   pyruvate + NADP(+) + CoA = acetyl-CoA + CO2 + NADPH.
CC   -!- The Euglena enzyme can also use FAD or methylviologen as acceptor,
CC       more slowly.
CC   -!- Inhibited by oxygen.
DR   Q968X7, PNO_CRYPV  ;  Q94IN5, PNO_EUGGR  ;
//
ID   1.2.1.52
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   1.2.1.53
DE   4-hydroxyphenylacetaldehyde dehydrogenase.
CA   (4-hydroxyphenyl)acetaldehyde + NAD(+) + H2O = 4-hydroxyphenylacetate +
CA   NADH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- With EC 4.2.1.87, brings about the metabolism of octopamine in
CC       Pseudomonas.
//
ID   1.2.1.54
DE   gamma-guanidinobutyraldehyde dehydrogenase.
CA   4-guanidinobutanal + NAD(+) + H2O = 4-guanidinobutanoate + NADH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Involved in the degradation of arginine in Pseudomonas putida (cf.
CC       EC 1.2.1.19).
