ID   1.2.1.57
DE   butanal dehydrogenase.
CA   (1) butanal + NAD(+) + CoA = butanoyl-CoA + NADH + H(+).
CA   (2) butanal + NADP(+) + CoA = butanoyl-CoA + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on acetaldehyde, but more slowly.
//
ID   1.2.1.58
DE   phenylglyoxylate dehydrogenase (acylating).
CA   phenylglyoxylate + NAD(+) + CoA = benzoyl-CoA + CO2 + NADH.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Azoarcus evansii is specific for phenylglyoxylate.
CC   -!- 2-oxoisovalerate is oxidized at 15% of the rate for phenylglyoxylate.
CC   -!- Also reduces viologen dyes.
DR   Q8L3B3, PADE_AROEV ;  Q8L3B2, PADF_AROEV ;  Q8L3B1, PADG_AROEV ;
DR   Q8L3B0, PADH_AROEV ;  Q8L3A9, PADI_AROEV ;
