ID   1.2.1.73
DE   sulfoacetaldehyde dehydrogenase.
CA   sulfoacetaldehyde + NAD(+) + H2O = sulfoacetate + NADH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Part of a bacterial pathway that can utilize the amino group of
CC       taurine as a sole source of nitrogen for growth.
CC   -!- At physiological concentrations, NAD(+) cannot be replaced by
CC       NADP(+).
CC   -!- Specific for sulfoacetaldehyde, as formaldehyde, acetaldehyde,
CC       betaine aldehyde, propanal, glyceraldehyde, phosphonoaldehyde,
CC       glyoxylate, glycolaldehyde and 2-oxobutyrate are not substrates.
DR   Q2BN77, SAFD_NEPCE ;
//
ID   1.2.1.74
DE   abieta-7,13-dien-18-al dehydrogenase.
AN   abietadienal dehydrogenase.
CA   abieta-7,13-dien-18-al + NAD(+) + H2O = abieta-7,13-dien-18-oate + NADH +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- Abietic acid is the principle component of conifer resin.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the last step of the pathway of abietic acid
CC       biosynthesis in Abies grandis (grand fir).
CC   -!- The activity has been demonstrated in cell-free stem extracts of A.
CC       grandis, was present in the cytoplasm, and required NAD(+) as
CC       cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme is expressed constitutively at a high level, and is not
CC       inducible by wounding of the plant tissue.
//
ID   1.2.1.75
DE   malonyl CoA reductase (malonate semialdehyde-forming).
AN   malonyl CoA reductase (NADP).
AN   NADP-dependent malonyl CoA reductase.
CA   3-oxopropanoate + NADP(+) + CoA = malonyl-CoA + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Catalyzes the reduction of malonyl-CoA to malonate semialdehyde,
CC       a key step in the 3-hydroxypropanoate and the
CC       3-hydroxypropanoate/4-hydroxybutyrate cycles, autotrophic CO2
CC       fixation pathways found in some green non-sulfur phototrophic
CC       bacteria and some thermoacidophilic archaea, respectively.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Sulfolobus tokodaii has been purified, and found to
CC       contain one RNA molecule per two subunits.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Chloroflexus aurantiacus is bifunctional, and also
CC       catalyzes the next reaction in the pathway, EC 1.1.1.298.
DR   A4YEN2, MCR_METS5  ;  Q96YK1, MCR_SULTO  ;
//
ID   1.2.1.76
DE   succinate-semialdehyde dehydrogenase (acetylating).
AN   coenzyme-A-dependent succinate-semialdehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   succinyl-CoA reductase.
CA   succinate semialdehyde + NADP(+) + CoA = succinyl-CoA + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Catalyzes the NADPH-dependent reduction of succinyl-CoA to succinate
CC       semialdehyde.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been described in Clostridium kluyveri, where it
CC       participates in succinate fermentation, and in Metallosphaera sedula,
CC       where it participates in the 3-hydroxypropanoate/4-hydroxybutyrate
CC       cycle, an autotrophic CO2 fixation pathway found in some
CC       thermoacidophilic archaea.
DR   P38947, SUCD_CLOK5 ;  A4YGN0, SUCD_METS5 ;
//
ID   1.2.1.77
DE   3,4-dehydroadipyl-CoA semialdehyde dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
AN   3,4-dehydroadipyl-CoA semialdehyde dehydrogenase.
CA   (3Z)-6-oxohex-3-enoyl-CoA + NADP(+) + H2O = cis-3,4-dehydroadipyl-CoA +
CA   NADPH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a step in the aerobic benzoyl-coenzyme A
CC       catabolic pathway in Azoarcus evansii and Burkholderia xenovorans.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.1.n1.
DR   Q84HH8, BOXD_AROEV ;
//
ID   1.2.1.78
DE   2-formylbenzoate dehydrogenase.
AN   2-carboxybenzaldehyde dehydrogenase.
CA   2-formylbenzoate + NAD(+) + H2O = phthalate + NADH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in phenanthrene degradation.
DR   Q79EM7, PHDK_NOCSK ;
//
ID   1.2.1.79
DE   succinate-semialdehyde dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
CA   succinate semialdehyde + NADP(+) + H2O = succinate + NADPH + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme participates in the degradation of glutamate and
CC       4-aminobutyrate.
CC   -!- It is similar to EC 1.2.1.24 and EC 1.2.1.16 but is specific for
CC       NADP(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli is 20-fold more active with NADP(+)
CC       than NAD(+).
