ID   1.2.3.1
DE   aldehyde oxidase.
AN   quinoline oxidase.
AN   retinal oxidase.
CA   an aldehyde + O2 + H2O = a carboxylate + H2O2 + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from liver exhibits a broad substrate specificity, and is
CC       involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics, including the oxidation of
CC       N-heterocycles and aldehydes and the reduction of N-oxides,
CC       nitrosamines, hydroxamic acids, azo dyes, nitropolycyclic aromatic
CC       hydrocarbons, and sulfoxides.
CC   -!- The enzyme is also responsible for the oxidation of retinal,
CC       an activity that was initially attributed to a distinct enzyme
CC       (EC 1.2.3.11).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.3.11.
