ID   1.2.3.7
DE   indole-3-acetaldehyde oxidase.
AN   IAAld oxidase.
AN   IAA oxidase.
AN   indoleacetaldehyde oxidase.
CA   indole-3-acetaldehyde + O2 + H2O = (indol-3-yl)acetate + H2O2 + H(+).
CC   -!- Isoform of EC 1.2.3.1.
CC   -!- Has a preference for aldehydes having an indole-ring structure as
CC       substrate.
CC   -!- May play a role in plant hormone biosynthesis as its activity is
CC       higher in the auxin-overproducing mutant, super-root1, than in wild-
CC       type Arabidopsis thaliana.
CC   -!- While (indol-3-yl)acetaldehyde is the preferred substrate, it also
CC       oxidizes indole-3-carbaldehyde and acetaldehyde, but more slowly.
DR   Q7G193, ALDO1_ARATH;  O23887, ALDO1_MAIZE;  Q7G192, ALDO2_ARATH;
DR   O23888, ALDO2_MAIZE;  Q7G9P4, ALDO3_ARATH;  Q7G191, ALDO4_ARATH;
