ID   1.2.3.14
DE   abscisic-aldehyde oxidase.
AN   AOdelta.
CA   2-cis-(+)-abscisic aldehyde + O2 + H2O = 2-cis-(+)-abscisate + H2O2 +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Acts on both (+)- and (-)-abscisic aldehyde.
CC   -!- Involved in the abscisic-acid biosynthesis pathway in plants, along
CC       with EC 1.1.1.288, EC 1.13.11.51 and EC 1.14.13.93.
CC   -!- While abscisic aldehyde is the best substrate, the enzyme also acts
CC       with indole-3-aldehyde, 1-naphthaldehyde and benzaldehyde as
CC       substrates, but more slowly.
DR   Q7G9P4, ALDO3_ARATH;
