ID   1.2.5.3
DE   aerobic carbon monoxide dehydrogenase.
AN   molybdoenzyme carbon monoxide dehydrogenase.
CA   CO + a quinone + H2O = a quinol + CO2.
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in carboxydotrophic bacteria, catalyzes the
CC       oxidation of CO to CO2 under aerobic conditions.
CC   -!- The enzyme belongs to the xanthine oxidoreductase family.
CC   -!- The CO2 that is produced is assimilated by the Calvin-Benson-Basham
CC       cycle, while the electrons are transferred to a quinone via the FAD
CC       site, and continue through the electron transfer chain to a dioxygen
CC       terminal acceptor. cf. EC 1.2.7.4.
DR   P19919, DCML_AFIC5 ;  P19916, DCML_AFICR ;  P19913, DCML_HYDPS ;
DR   P19920, DCMM_AFIC5 ;  P19917, DCMM_AFICR ;  P19914, DCMM_HYDPS ;
DR   P19921, DCMS_AFIC5 ;  P19918, DCMS_AFICR ;  P19915, DCMS_HYDPS ;
