ID   1.2.7.1
DE   pyruvate synthase.
AN   2-oxobutyrate-ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
AN   2-oxobutyrate synthase.
AN   alpha-ketobutyrate-ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
AN   alpha-ketobutyrate synthase.
AN   pyruvate oxidoreductase.
AN   pyruvate synthetase.
AN   pyruvic-ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
CA   2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + pyruvate + CoA = 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-
CA   [ferredoxin] + acetyl-CoA + CO2 + H(+).
CC   -!- Contains thiamine diphosphate and [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- The enzyme, common in bacteria, archaea, and some algae, catalyzes
CC       the reversible decarboxylation of pyruvate with the formation of
CC       acetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- Enzymes from different organisms catalyze the reaction in different
CC       directions depending on their metabolic needs.
CC   -!- The enzyme also decarboxylates 2-oxobutanoate with lower efficiency,
CC       but shows no activity with 2-oxoglutarate.
CC   -!- In some organisms ferredoxin may be replaced by the flavin
CC       mononucleotide (FMN)-containing flavodoxin under conditions of low
CC       iron and high oxygen (cf. EC 1.2.8.1).
CC   -!- This enzyme is a member of the 2-oxoacid oxidoreductases, a family of
CC       enzymes that oxidatively decarboxylate different 2-oxoacids to form
CC       their CoA derivatives, and are differentiated based on their
CC       substrate specificity.
CC   -!- For examples of other members of this family, see EC 1.2.7.3 and
CC       EC 1.2.7.7.
