ID   1.2.7.5
DE   aldehyde ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
AN   AOR.
AN   tungsten-containing aldehyde ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
CA   an aldehyde + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + H2O = a carboxylate +
CA   2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 3 H(+).
CC   -!- This is an oxygen-sensitive enzyme.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the oxidation of aldehydes (including crotonaldehyde,
CC       acetaldehyde, formaldehyde and glyceraldehyde) to their corresponding
CC       acids.
CC   -!- However, it does not oxidize glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate (see
CC       EC 1.2.7.6).
CC   -!- Can use ferredoxin or methylviologen but not NAD(P)(+) as electron
CC       acceptor.
