ID   1.3.1.108
DE   caffeoyl-CoA reductase.
AN   caffeoyl-CoA reductase-Etf complex.
AN   electron-bifurcating caffeoyl-CoA reductase.
CA   hydrocaffeoyl-CoA + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 NAD(+) = (E)-
CA   caffeoyl-CoA + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 NADH.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Acetobacterium woodii,
CC       couples the endergonic ferredoxin reduction with NADH as reductant to
CC       the exergonic reduction of caffeoyl-CoA with the same reductant.
CC   -!- It uses the mechanism of electron bifurcation to overcome the steep
CC       energy barrier in ferredoxin reduction.
CC   -!- It also reduces 4-coumaroyl-CoA and feruloyl-CoA.
DR   H6LGM6, CARC_ACEWD ;  H6LGM7, CARD_ACEWD ;  H6LGM8, CARE_ACEWD ;
