DE   tryptophan alpha,beta-oxidase.
AN   L-tryptophan 2',3'-oxidase.
AN   L-tryptophan alpha,beta-dehydrogenase.
CA   L-tryptophan + O2 = alpha,beta-didehydrotryptophan + H2O2.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Chromobacterium violaceum is specific for tryptophan
CC       derivatives possessing its carboxyl group free or as an amide or
CC       ester, and an unsubstituted indole ring.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes the alpha,beta dehydrogenation of L-tryptophan side
CC       chains in peptides.
CC   -!- The product of the reaction can hydrolyze spontaneously to form
CC       indolepyruvate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.3.17.
