ID   1.3.3.13
DE   albonoursin synthase.
AN   cyclic dipeptide oxidase.
CA   cyclo(L-phenylalanyl-L-leucyl) + 2 O2 = albonoursin + 2 H2O2.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also oxidize several other cyclo dipeptides, the best
CC       being cyclo(L-tryptophyl-L-tryptophyl) and cyclo(L-phenylalanyl-L-
CC       phenylalanyl).
DR   Q8GED9, ALBA_STRNR ;
//
ID   1.3.3.14
DE   aclacinomycin-A oxidase.
AN   aclacinomycin oxidoreductase.
AN   AknOx.
CA   aclacinomycin A + O2 = aclacinomycin Y + H2O2.
CC   -!- This bifunctional enzyme is a secreted flavin-dependent enzyme that
CC       is involved in the modification of the terminal sugar residues in the
CC       biosynthesis of aclacinomycins.
CC   -!- The enzyme utilizes the same active site to catalyze the oxidation of
CC       the rhodinose moiety of aclacinomycin N to the cinerulose A moiety of
CC       aclacinomycin A (cf. EC 1.1.3.45) and the oxidation of the latter to
CC       the L-aculose moiety of aclacinomycin Y.
DR   Q0PCD7, AKNOX_STRGJ;
