ID   1.3.8.1
DE   short-chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenase.
AN   butanoyl-CoA dehydrogenase.
AN   butyryl dehydrogenase.
AN   short-chain acyl CoA dehydrogenase.
AN   unsaturated acyl-CoA reductase.
CA   a short-chain 2,3-saturated fatty acyl-CoA + oxidized [electron-transfer
CA   flavoprotein] + H(+) = a short-chain (2E)-enoyl-CoA + reduced [electron-
CA   transfer flavoprotein].
CC   -!- One of several enzymes that catalyze the first step in fatty acids
CC       beta-oxidation.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of saturated short-chain acyl-CoA
CC       thioesters to give a trans 2,3-unsaturated product by removal of the
CC       two pro-R hydrogen atoms.
CC   -!- The enzyme from beef liver accepts substrates with acyl chain lengths
CC       of 3 to 8 carbon atoms.
CC   -!- The highest activity was reported with either butanoyl-CoA or
CC       pentanoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme from rat has only 10% activity with hexanoyl-CoA (compared
CC       to butanoyl-CoA) and no activity with octanoyl-CoA. cf. EC 1.3.8.7,
CC       EC 1.3.8.8 and EC 1.3.8.9.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.2.1 and EC 1.3.99.2.
