ID   1.3.8.6
DE   glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (ETF).
AN   glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase.
CA   glutaryl-CoA + oxidized [electron-transfer flavoprotein] + 2 H(+) = (2E)-
CA   butenoyl-CoA + reduced [electron-transfer flavoprotein] + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of glutaryl-CoA to glutaconyl-CoA
CC       (which remains bound to the enzyme), and the decarboxylation of the
CC       latter to crotonyl-CoA (cf. EC 7.2.4.5).
CC   -!- FAD is the electron acceptor in the oxidation of the substrate,
CC       and its reoxidation by electron-transfer flavoprotein completes the
CC       catalytic cycle.
CC   -!- The anaerobic, sulfate-reducing bacterium Desulfococcus multivorans
CC       contains two glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenases: a decarboxylating enzyme
CC       (this entry), and a non-decarboxylating enzyme that only catalyzes
CC       the oxidation to glutaconyl-CoA (EC 1.3.99.32).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.7.
