//
ID   1.4.3.12
DE   cyclohexylamine oxidase.
CA   cyclohexylamine + O2 + H2O = cyclohexanone + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Some other cyclic amines can act instead of cyclohexylamine, but not
CC       simple aliphatic and aromatic amides.
//
ID   1.4.3.13
DE   protein-lysine 6-oxidase.
AN   lysyl oxidase.
CA   L-lysyl-[protein] + O2 + H2O = (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoyl-[protein] + H2O2
CA   + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on protein 5-hydroxylysine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the final known enzymic step required for collagen and
CC       elastin cross-linking in the biosynthesis of normal mature
CC       extracellular matrices.
CC   -!- These reactions play an important role for the development,
CC       elasticity and extensibility of connective tissue.
CC   -!- Also active on free amines, such as cadaverine or benzylamine.
DR   F1QQC3, LOL2A_DANRE;  A1L1V4, LOL2B_DANRE;  F1RD85, LOX3A_DANRE;
DR   B8A4W9, LOX3B_DANRE;  Q95L39, LOXL1_BOVIN;  Q08397, LOXL1_HUMAN;
DR   P97873, LOXL1_MOUSE;  A6H737, LOXL2_BOVIN;  E1C3U7, LOXL2_CHICK;
DR   Q9Y4K0, LOXL2_HUMAN;  P58022, LOXL2_MOUSE;  Q5RFQ6, LOXL2_PONAB;
DR   B5DF27, LOXL2_RAT  ;  Q08B63, LOXL2_XENLA;  B4F6N6, LOXL2_XENTR;
DR   P58215, LOXL3_HUMAN;  Q9Z175, LOXL3_MOUSE;  Q8MJ24, LOXL4_BOVIN;
DR   Q96JB6, LOXL4_HUMAN;  Q924C6, LOXL4_MOUSE;  P33072, LYOX_BOVIN ;
DR   Q05063, LYOX_CHICK ;  P28300, LYOX_HUMAN ;  P28301, LYOX_MOUSE ;
DR   P45845, LYOX_PIG   ;  P16636, LYOX_RAT   ;
//
ID   1.4.3.14
DE   L-lysine oxidase.
CA   L-lysine + O2 + H2O = 6-amino-2-oxohexanoate + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Also acts, more slowly, on L-ornithine, L-phenylalanine, L-arginine
CC       and L-histidine.
DR   S4S6Z0, LAAO4_HEBCY;
//
ID   1.4.3.15
DE   D-glutamate(D-aspartate) oxidase.
CA   (1) D-glutamate + O2 + H2O = 2-oxoglutarate + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CA   (2) D-aspartate + O2 + H2O = oxaloacetate + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- D-glutamate and D-aspartate are oxidized at the same rate.
CC   -!- Other D-monoaminodicarboxylates, and other D- and L-amino acids,
CC       are not oxidized. cf. EC 1.4.3.7 and EC 1.4.3.1.
//
ID   1.4.3.16
DE   L-aspartate oxidase.
AN   LASPO.
CA   L-aspartate + O2 = iminosuccinate + H2O2.
CC   -!- L-Aspartate oxidase catalyzes the first step in the de novo
CC       biosynthesis of NAD(+) in some bacteria.
CC   -!- O2 can be replaced by fumarate as electron acceptor, yielding
CC       succinate.
CC   -!- The ability of the enzyme to use both O2 and fumarate in cofactor
CC       reoxidation enables it to function under both aerobic and anaerobic
CC       conditions.
CC   -!- Iminosuccinate can either be hydrolyzed to form oxaloacetate and NH3
CC       or can be used by EC 2.5.1.72 in the production of quinolinate.
DR   A0A1S3YEG8, AO2A_TOBAC ;  A0A1S4BJT3, AO2B_TOBAC ;  Q8XWM7, NADB1_RALN1;
DR   Q8XQG4, NADB2_RALN1;  Q6F9B6, NADB_ACIAD ;  Q8U8J4, NADB_AGRFC ;
DR   O66973, NADB_AQUAE ;  Q94AY1, NADB_ARATH ;  P38032, NADB_BACSU ;
DR   Q9A4C3, NADB_CAUVC ;  Q97K95, NADB_CLOAB ;  Q8XNE2, NADB_CLOPE ;
DR   Q8XA23, NADB_ECO57 ;  P10902, NADB_ECOLI ;  Q9KDJ5, NADB_HALH5 ;
