ID   1.4.3.19
DE   glycine oxidase.
CA   glycine + O2 + H2O = glyoxylate + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Bacillus subtilis is active with glycine, sarcosine,
CC       N-ethylglycine, D-alanine, D-alpha-aminobutyrate, D-proline,
CC       D-pipecolate and N-methyl-D-alanine.
CC   -!- It differs from EC 1.4.3.3 due to its activity on sarcosine and
CC       D-pipecolate.
CC   -!- The intermediate 2-iminoacetate is used directly by EC 2.8.1.10.
DR   S5FMM4, GLYOX_BACLI;  O31616, GLYOX_BACSU;  Q5L2C2, GLYOX_GEOKA;
DR   P33642, GLYOX_PSEAE;  Q88Q83, GLYOX_PSEPK;  Q8YRC9, THIOG_NOSS1;
DR   Q55710, THIOG_SYNY3;  Q3M859, THIOG_TRIV2;
//
ID   1.4.3.20
DE   L-lysine 6-oxidase.
AN   L-lysine-epsilon-oxidase.
AN   Lod.
AN   marinocine.
CA   L-lysine + O2 + H2O = (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Differs from EC 1.4.3.13 by using free L-lysine rather than the
CC       protein-bound form.
CC   -!- N(2)-acetyl-L-lysine is also a substrate, but N(6)-acetyl-L-lysine,
CC       which has an acetyl group at position 6, is not.
CC   -!- Also acts on L-ornithine, D-lysine and 4-hydroxy-L-lysine, but more
CC       slowly.
CC   -!- The amines cadaverine and putrescine are not substrates.
DR   F2JXJ3, LODA_MARM1 ;
//
ID   1.4.3.21
DE   primary-amine oxidase.
AN   amine oxidase.
AN   amine oxidase (copper-containing).
AN   benzylamine oxidase.
AN   CAO.
AN   copper amine oxidase.
CA   a primary methyl amine + O2 + H2O = an aldehyde + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- A group of enzymes that oxidize primary monoamines but have little or
CC       no activity toward diamines, such as histamine, or toward secondary
CC       and tertiary amines.
CC   -!- They are copper quinoproteins (2,4,5-trihydroxyphenylalanine quinone)
CC       and, unlike EC 1.4.3.4, are sensitive to inhibition by carbonyl-group
CC       reagents, such as semicarbazide.
CC   -!- In some mammalian tissues the enzyme also functions as a vascular-
CC       adhesion protein (VAP-1).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.3.6.
DR   Q07121, AMO1_ARTS1 ;  P0DO00, AMO2_ARATH ;  Q07123, AMO2_ARTS1 ;
DR   P46883, AMO_ECOLI  ;  P49250, AMO_KLEAE  ;  P80695, AMO_KLEM8  ;
DR   P49252, AMO_LENCU  ;  Q43077, AMO_PEA    ;  P12807, AMO_PICAN  ;
