ID   1.4.3.22
DE   diamine oxidase.
AN   amine oxidase.
AN   amine oxidase (copper-containing).
AN   CAO.
AN   copper amine oxidase.
AN   Cu-containing amine oxidase.
AN   diamino oxhydrase.
AN   histaminase.
AN   histamine deaminase.
AN   semicarbazide-sensitive amine oxidase.
AN   SSAO.
CA   histamine + O2 + H2O = imidazole-4-acetaldehyde + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- A group of enzymes that oxidize diamines, such as histamine, and also
CC       some primary monoamines but have little or no activity toward
CC       secondary and tertiary amines.
CC   -!- They are copper quinoproteins (2,4,5-trihydroxyphenylalanine quinone)
CC       and, like EC 1.4.3.21 but unlike EC 1.4.3.4, they are sensitive to
CC       inhibition by carbonyl-group reagents, such as semicarbazide.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.3.6.
DR   Q12556, AMO1_ASPNG ;  Q59118, AMOH_ARTGO ;  P19801, AOC1_HUMAN ;
DR   Q8JZQ5, AOC1_MOUSE ;  Q9TRC7, AOC1_PIG   ;  P36633, AOC1_RAT   ;
//
ID   1.4.3.23
DE   7-chloro-L-tryptophan oxidase.
CA   7-chloro-L-tryptophan + O2 = 3-(7-chloroindol-3-yl)-2-iminopropanoate +
CA   H2O2.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a step in the biosynthesis of rebeccamycin,
CC       an indolocarbazole alkaloid produced by the bacterium Lechevalieria
CC       aerocolonigenes.
CC   -!- During catalysis, the bound FAD is reoxidized at the expense of
CC       molecular oxygen, producing one molecule of hydrogen peroxide.
CC   -!- The enzyme shows significant preference for 7-chloro-L-tryptophan
CC       over L-tryptophan.
DR   Q8KHS0, REBO_LENAE ;  Q9S3V1, VIOA_CHRVO ;
//
ID   1.4.3.24
DE   Transferred entry: 1.4.2.3.
//
ID   1.4.3.25
DE   L-arginine oxidase.
CA   L-arginine + O2 + H2O = 5-guanidino-2-oxopentanoate + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from cyanobacteria can also act on other basic amino acids
CC       with lower activity.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp. TPU 7192 is highly
CC       specific.
DR   S4S6Z0, LAAO4_HEBCY;  Q96RQ9, OXLA_HUMAN ;  O09046, OXLA_MOUSE ;
DR   O08615, OXLA_MUSSP ;
//
ID   1.4.3.26
DE   pre-mycofactocin synthase.
CA   3-amino-5-[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-4,4-dimethyl-2-pyrrolidin-2-one +
CA   O2 + H2O = pre-mycofactocin + H2O2 + NH4(+).
CC   -!- A flavoprotein (FMN).
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of the enzyme cofactor
CC       mycofactocin.
CC   -!- The enzyme uses oxygen as an electron source to oxidize a C-N bond,
CC       followed by spontaneous exchange with water to form an alpha-keto
CC       moiety on the resulting molecule.
DR   A0QSB9, MFTD_MYCS2 ;  P9WND6, MFTD_MYCTO ;  P9WND7, MFTD_MYCTU ;
DR   A0PM50, MFTD_MYCUA ;
//
ID   1.4.3.27
DE   homospermidine oxidase.
CA   sym-homospermidine + 2 O2 + H2O = 1-formylpyrrolizidine + 2 H2O2 +
CA   2 NH4(+).
CC   -!- The copper-containing enzyme has been isolated from the plant
CC       Heliotropium indicum.
CC   -!- It is involved in the biosynthesis of the pyrrolizidine alkaloid (-)-
CC       trachelanthamidine which acts as a secondary metabolite for the
CC       defense against herbivores.
CC   -!- The oxidation of sym-homospermidine proceeds in three steps and
CC       results in a cyclization.
//
ID   1.4.4.1
DE   Transferred entry: 1.21.4.1.
//
ID   1.4.4.2
DE   glycine dehydrogenase (aminomethyl-transferring).
AN   glycine-cleavage complex P-protein.
AN   glycine cleavage system P-protein.
AN   glycine decarboxylase.
AN   glycine dehydrogenase (decarboxylating).
CA   N(6)-[(R)-lipoyl]-L-lysyl-[glycine-cleavage complex H protein] + glycine
CA   + H(+) = N(6)-[(R)-S(8)-aminomethyldihydrolipoyl]-L-lysyl-[glycine-
CA   cleavage complex H protein] + CO2.
CC   -!- A component of the glycine cleavage system, which is composed of four
CC       components that only loosely associate: the P protein (EC 1.4.4.2),
CC       the T protein (EC 2.1.2.10), the L protein (EC 1.8.1.4) and the
CC       lipoyl-bearing H protein.
CC   -!- Previously known as glycine synthase.
