ID   1.4.5.1
DE   D-amino acid dehydrogenase (quinone).
AN   DadA.
CA   a D-alpha-amino acid + a quinone + H2O = a 2-oxocarboxylate + a quinol +
CA   NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Helicobacter pylori is highly specific
CC       for D-proline, while the enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli B
CC       is most active with D-alanine, D-phenylalanine and D-methionine.
CC   -!- This enzyme may be the same as EC 1.4.99.6.
DR   Q9ZKQ7, DADA_HELPJ ;  A3KEZ1, DADA_HELPX ;  O25597, DADA_HELPY ;
//
ID   1.4.7.1
DE   glutamate synthase (ferredoxin).
AN   ferredoxin-dependent glutamate synthase.
CA   2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 L-glutamate = L-glutamine +
CA   2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2-oxoglutarate + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The protein is composed of two domains, one hydrolyzing L-glutamine
CC       to NH3 and L-glutamate (cf. EC 3.5.1.2), the other combining the
CC       produced NH3 with 2-oxoglutarate to produce a second molecule of
CC       L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The NH3 is channeled through a 24 A channel in the active protein.
CC   -!- No hydrolysis of glutamine takes place without ferredoxin and
CC       2-oxoglutarate being bound to the protein.
DR   Q9ZNZ7, GLTB1_ARATH;  Q9T0P4, GLTB2_ARATH;  Q06434, GLTB_ANTSP ;
DR   O19906, GLTB_CYACA ;  Q08258, GLTB_HORVU ;  P23225, GLTB_MAIZE ;
DR   Q69RJ0, GLTB_ORYSJ ;  P51375, GLTB_PORPU ;  Q1XDB2, GLTB_PYRYE ;
DR   Q43155, GLTB_SPIOL ;  P55037, GLTB_SYNY3 ;  P55038, GLTS_SYNY3 ;
//
ID   1.4.9.1
DE   methylamine dehydrogenase (amicyanin).
AN   amine dehydrogenase.
AN   MADH.
AN   methylamine dehydrogenase.
AN   primary-amine dehydrogenase.
CA   2 oxidized [amicyanin] + methylamine + H2O = 2 reduced [amicyanin] +
CA   formaldehyde + NH4(+) + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme oxidizes aliphatic monoamines and diamines, histamine and
CC       ethanolamine, but not secondary and tertiary amines, quaternary
CC       ammonium salts or aromatic amines.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.98.1 and EC 1.4.99.3.
DR   Q49124, DHMH_METEA ;  Q50420, DHMH_METFK ;  Q59542, DHMH_METME ;
DR   P29894, DHMH_PARDE ;  P23006, DHMH_PARVE ;  P00372, DHML_METEA ;
DR   Q50425, DHML_METFK ;  Q59543, DHML_METME ;  P22619, DHML_PARDE ;
DR   P22641, DHML_PARVE ;
//
ID   1.4.9.2
DE   aralkylamine dehydrogenase (azurin).
AN   aromatic amine dehydrogenase.
AN   arylamine dehydrogenase.
CA   an aralkylamine + 2 oxidized [azurin] + H2O = an aromatic aldehyde +
CA   2 reduced [azurin] + NH4(+) + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Phenazine methosulfate can act as acceptor.
CC   -!- Acts on aromatic amines and, more slowly, on some long-chain
CC       aliphatic amines, but not on methylamine or ethylamine.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.99.4.
DR   P84887, AAUA_ALCFA ;  P84888, AAUB_ALCFA ;
