ID   1.5.1.28
DE   opine dehydrogenase.
CA   (2S)-2-[(R)-1-carboxyethylamino]pentanoate + NAD(+) + H2O = L-2-
CA   aminopentanoate + pyruvate + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- in the forward direction, the enzyme from Arthrobacter sp. acts also
CC       on secondary amine dicarboxylates such as
CC       N-(1-carboxyethyl)methionine and N-(1-carboxyethyl)phenylalanine.
CC   -!- Dehydrogenation forms an imine, which dissociates to the amino acid
CC       and pyruvate.
CC   -!- In the reverse direction, the enzyme acts also on neutral amino acids
CC       as an amino donor.
CC   -!- They include L-amino acids such as 2-aminopentanoic acid,
CC       2-aminobutyric acid, 2-aminohexanoic acid, 3-chloroalanine,
CC       O-acetylserine, methionine, isoleucine, valine, phenylalanine,
CC       leucine and alanine.
CC   -!- The amino acceptors include 2-oxoacids such as pyruvate,
CC       oxaloacetate, glyoxylate and 2-oxobutyrate.
DR   Q44297, ODH_ARTSC  ;
