ID   1.5.3.12
DE   dihydrobenzophenanthridine oxidase.
CA   (1) dihydrosanguinarine + O2 + H(+) = sanguinarine + H2O2.
CA   (2) dihydrochelirubine + O2 + H(+) = chelirubine + H2O2.
CA   (3) dihydromacarpine + O2 + H(+) = macarpine + H2O2.
CC   -!- Found in higher plants.
CC   -!- Produces oxidized forms of the benzophenanthridine alkaloids.
//
ID   1.5.3.13
DE   N(1)-acetylpolyamine oxidase.
AN   PAO.
AN   polyamine oxidase.
CA   (1) N(1)-acetylspermidine + O2 + H2O = 3-acetamidopropanal + putrescine +
CA   H2O2.
CA   (2) N(1)-acetylspermine + O2 + H2O = 3-acetamidopropanal + spermidine +
CA   H2O2.
CC   -!- The enzyme also catalyzes the reaction: N(1),N(12)-diacetylspermine +
CC       O2 + H2O = N(1)-acetylspermidine + 3-acetamamidopropanal + H2O2.
CC   -!- No or very weak activity with spermine, or spermidine in absence of
CC       aldehydes.
CC   -!- In presence of aldehydes the enzyme catalyzes the reactions: 1.
CC   -!- spermine + O2 + H2O = spermidine + 3-aminopropanal + H2O2, and with
CC       weak efficiency 2.
CC   -!- spermidine + O2 + H2O = putrescine + 3-aminopropanal + H2O2.
CC   -!- Found in mammalian peroxisomes and oxidizes N(1)-acetylated
CC       polyamines at the exo (three-carbon) side of the secondary amine,
CC       forming 3-acetamamidopropanal.
CC   -!- Since the products of the reactions are deacetylated polyamines, this
CC       process is known as polyamine back-conversion.
CC   -!- Differs in specificity from EC 1.5.3.14, EC 1.5.3.15, EC 1.5.3.16 and
CC       EC 1.5.3.17.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.5.3.11, EC 1.5.3.n3, EC 1.5.3.n4 and EC 1.5.3.n10.
DR   Q865R1, PAOX_BOVIN ;  Q6QHF9, PAOX_HUMAN ;  Q8C0L6, PAOX_MOUSE ;
//
ID   1.5.3.14
DE   polyamine oxidase (propane-1,3-diamine-forming).
AN   maize PAO.
AN   MPAO.
CA   spermidine + O2 + H2O = 4-aminobutanal + propane-1,3-diamine + H2O2.
CC   -!- As the products of the reaction cannot be converted directly to other
CC       polyamines, this class of polyamine oxidases is considered to be
CC       involved in the terminal catabolism of polyamines.
CC   -!- Catalyzes less efficiently the oxidation of N(1)-acetylspermine and
CC       spermine.
CC   -!- Differs in specificity from EC 1.5.3.13, EC 1.5.3.15, EC 1.5.3.16 and
CC       EC 1.5.3.17.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.5.3.11, EC 1.5.3.n6, EC 1.5.3.n7, EC 1.5.3.n8 and
CC       EC 1.5.3.n9.
DR   O64411, PAO1_MAIZE ;
