DE   coenzyme F420:methanophenazine dehydrogenase.
AN   F420H2 dehydrogenase.
CA   methanophenazine + reduced coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) =
CA   dihydromethanophenazine + oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in some methanogenic archaea, is responsible for
CC       the reoxidation of coenzyme F420, which is reduced during
CC       methanogenesis, and for the reduction of methanophenazine to
CC       dihydromethanophenazine, which is required by EC 1.8.98.1.
CC   -!- The enzyme is membrane-bound, and is coupled to proton translocation
CC       across the cytoplasmic membrane, generating a proton motive force
CC       that is used for ATP generation.
