ID   1.5.99.12
DE   cytokinin dehydrogenase.
AN   cytokinin oxidase.
CA   N(6)-dimethylallyladenine + A + H2O = 3-methyl-2-butenal + adenine + AH2.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the oxidation of cytokinins, a family of N(6)-substituted
CC       adenine derivatives that are plant hormones, where the substituent is
CC       a prenyl group.
CC   -!- Although this activity was previously thought to be catalyzed by a
CC       hydrogen-peroxide-forming oxidase, this enzyme does not require
CC       oxygen for activity and does not form hydrogen peroxide.
CC   -!- 2,6-dichloroindophenol, methylene blue, nitroblue tetrazolium,
CC       phenazine methosulfate and copper(II) in the presence of imidazole
CC       can act as acceptors.
CC   -!- This enzyme plays a part in regulating rice-grain production, with
CC       lower levels of the enzyme resulting in enhanced grain production.
