//
ID   1.6.3.1
DE   NAD(P)H oxidase (H2O2-forming).
AN   dual oxidase.
AN   NAD(P)H oxidase.
AN   ThOX.
AN   THOX2.
AN   thyroid NADPH oxidase.
AN   thyroid oxidase.
AN   thyroid oxidase 2.
CA   (1) NADPH + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NADP(+).
CA   (2) NADH + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NAD(+).
CC   -!- When calcium is present, this transmembrane glycoprotein generates
CC       H2O2 by transfering electrons from intracellular NAD(P)H to
CC       extracellular molecular oxygen.
CC   -!- The electron bridge within the enzyme contains one molecule of FAD
CC       and probably two heme groups.
CC   -!- This flavoprotein is expressed at the apical membrane of thyrocytes,
CC       and provides H2O2 for the thyroid peroxidase-catalyzed biosynthesis
CC       of thyroid hormones.
