//
ID   1.6.3.2
DE   NAD(P)H oxidase (H2O-forming).
CA   (1) 2 NADPH + O2 + 2 H(+) = 2 NADP(+) + 2 H2O.
CA   (2) 2 NADH + O2 + 2 H(+) = 2 NAD(+) + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- NADPH is a better substrate than NADH.
CC   -!- By removal of oxygen the enzyme is involved in aerobic tolerance in
CC       the thermophilic anaerobic archaeon Thermococcus profundus and in
CC       Giardia intestinalis, a microaerophilic single-celled parasite of the
CC       order Diplomonadida.
DR   Q5JGP4, NSR_THEKO  ;
//
ID   1.6.3.3
DE   NADH oxidase (H2O2-forming).
AN   H2O2-forming NADH oxidase.
CA   NADH + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NAD(+).
CC   -!- The bacterium Streptococcus mutans contains two distinct NADH
CC       oxidases, a H2O2-forming enzyme and a H2O-forming enzyme (cf.
CC       EC 1.6.3.4).
CC   -!- The enzymes from the anaerobic archaea Methanocaldococcus jannaschii
CC       and Pyrococcus furiosus also produce low amounts of H2O.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.6.3.1 it has no activity toward NADPH.
//
ID   1.6.3.4
DE   NADH oxidase (H2O-forming).
AN   H2O-forming NADH oxidase.
CA   2 NADH + O2 + 2 H(+) = 2 NAD(+) + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The bacterium Streptococcus mutans contains two distinct NADH
CC       oxidases, a H2O-forming enzyme and a H2O2-forming enzyme (cf.
CC       EC 1.6.3.3).
DR   Q97K92, FPRA1_CLOAB;  Q97GC0, FPRA2_CLOAB;  P37061, NAOX_ENTFA ;
