ID   1.6.3.5
DE   renalase.
AN   alpha-NAD(P)H oxidase/anomerase.
CA   (1) 1,2-dihydro-beta-NAD + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NAD(+).
CA   (2) 1,2-dihydro-beta-NADP + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NADP(+).
CA   (3) 1,6-dihydro-beta-NAD + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NAD(+).
CA   (4) 1,6-dihydro-beta-NADP + O2 + H(+) = H2O2 + NADP(+).
CC   -!- Renalase, previously thought to be a hormone, is a flavoprotein
CC       secreted into the blood by the kidney that oxidizes the 1,2-dihydro-
CC       and 1,6-dihydro- isomeric forms of beta-NAD(P)H back to beta-
CC       NAD(P)(+).
CC   -!- These isomeric forms, generated by non-specific reduction of beta-
CC       NAD(P)(+) or by tautomerization of beta-NAD(P)H, are potent
CC       inhibitors of primary metabolism dehydrogenases and pose a threat to
CC       normal respiration.
DR   Q5VYX0, RNLS_HUMAN ;  A7RDN6, RNLS_MOUSE ;  Q48MT7, RNLS_PSE14 ;
