ID   1.7.2.4
DE   nitrous-oxide reductase.
CA   N2 + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] + H2O = nitrous oxide + 2 Fe(II)-
CA   [cytochrome c] + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The reaction is observed only in the direction of nitrous oxide
CC       reduction.
CC   -!- Contains the mixed-valent dinuclear CuA species at the electron entry
CC       site of the enzyme, and the tetranuclear Cu-Z center in the active
CC       site.
CC   -!- In Paracoccus pantotrophus, the electron donor is cytochrome c552.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.7.99.6.
DR   P94127, NOSZ_ACHCY ;  Q89XJ6, NOSZ_BRADU ;  Q8YBC6, NOSZ_BRUME ;
DR   Q8FX16, NOSZ_BRUSU ;  Q59105, NOSZ_CUPNH ;  P0DXY7, NOSZ_DESNS ;
DR   Q51705, NOSZ_PARDE ;  Q9HYL2, NOSZ_PSEAE ;  Q01710, NOSZ_PSEAI ;
DR   Q9F0W4, NOSZ_PSEFL ;  Q8XQB8, NOSZ_RALN1 ;  Q59746, NOSZ_RHIME ;
DR   P0DXY8, NOSZ_SPOA4 ;  P19573, NOSZ_STUST ;
