ID   1.7.3.4
DE   Transferred entry: 1.7.2.6 and 1.7.3.6.
//
ID   1.7.3.5
DE   3-aci-nitropropanoate oxidase.
CA   propionate 3-nitronate + O2 + H2O = 3-oxopropanoate + nitrite + H2O2 +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The primary products of the enzymatic reaction are probably the
CC       nitropropanoate free radical and superoxide.
CC   -!- Also acts, more slowly, on 4-aci-nitrobutanoate.
//
ID   1.7.3.6
DE   hydroxylamine oxidase (cytochrome).
AN   HAO.
AN   hydroxylamine oxidase.
AN   hydroxylamine oxidoreductase.
CA   hydroxylamine + O2 = nitrite + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the heterotrophic nitrifying bacterium Paracoccus
CC       denitrificans contains three to five non-heme, non-iron-sulfur iron
CC       atoms and interacts with cytochrome c556 and pseudoazurin.
CC   -!- Under anaerobic conditions in vitro only nitrous oxide is formed.
CC   -!- Presumably nitroxyl is released and combines with a second nitroxyl
CC       to give nitrous oxide and water.
CC   -!- When oxygen is present, nitrite is formed.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.7.3.4.
//
ID   1.7.5.1
DE   nitrate reductase (quinone).
AN   dissimilatory nitrate reductase.
AN   nitrate reductase A.
AN   nitrate reductase Z.
AN   quinol/nitrate oxidoreductase.
AN   quinol-nitrate oxidoreductase.
CA   nitrate + a quinol = a quinone + nitrite + H2O.
CC   -!- A membrane-bound enzyme which supports anaerobic respiration on
CC       nitrate under anaerobic conditions and in the presence of nitrate
CC       Escherichia coli expresses two forms NarA and NarZ, both being
CC       comprised of three subunits.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.7.99.4.
