DE   2-oxopropyl-CoM reductase (carboxylating).
AN   2-KPCC.
AN   NADPH:2-(2-ketopropylthio)ethanesulfonate oxidoreductase/carboxylase.
AN   NADPH:2-ketopropyl-coenzyme M oxidoreductase/carboxylase.
CA   coenzyme M + acetoacetate + NADP(+) = 2-oxopropyl-coenzyme M + CO2 +
CA   NADPH.
CC   -!- Also acts on thioethers longer in chain length on the oxo side, e.g.
CC       2-oxobutyl-CoM, but this portion must be attached to CoM
CC       (2-sulfanylethane-1-sulfonate); no CoM analogs will substitute.
CC   -!- Forms component II of a four-component enzyme system (comprising
CC       EC 4.4.1.23 (component I), EC 1.8.1.5 (component II), EC 1.1.1.268
CC       (component III) and EC 1.1.1.269 (component IV)) that is involved in
CC       epoxyalkane carboxylation in Xanthobacter sp. strain Py2.
