ID   1.8.1.12
DE   trypanothione-disulfide reductase.
AN   N(1),N(8)-bis(glutathionyl)spermidine reductase.
AN   NADPH:trypanothione oxidoreductase.
AN   trypanothione reductase.
CA   trypanothione + NADP(+) = trypanothione disulfide + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- Trypanothione disulfide is the oxidized form of N(1),N(8)-
CC       bis(glutathionyl)-spermidine from the insect-parasitic trypanosomatid
CC       Crithidia fasciculata.
CC   -!- The activity is dependent on a redox-active cystine at the active
