ID   1.8.4.15
DE   protein dithiol oxidoreductase (disulfide-forming).
CA   [DsbA protein]-disulfide + [protein]-dithiol = [DsbA protein]-dithiol +
CA   [protein]-disulfide.
CC   -!- DsbA is a periplasmic thiol:disulfide oxidoreductase found in Gram-
CC       negative bacteria that promotes protein disulfide bond formation.
CC   -!- DsbA contains a redox active disulfide bond that is catalytically
CC       transferred via disulfide exchange to a diverse range of newly
CC       translocated protein substrates.
CC   -!- The protein is restored to the oxidized state by EC 1.8.5.9.
//
ID   1.8.4.16
DE   thioredoxin:protein disulfide reductase.
CA   [protein]-dithiol + [thioredoxin]-disulfide = [protein]-disulfide +
CA   [thioredoxin]-dithiol.
CC   -!- The DsbD protein is found in Gram-negative bacteria and transfers
CC       electrons from cytoplasmic thioredoxin to the periplasmic substrate
CC       proteins DsbC, DsbG and CcmG, reducing disulfide bonds in the target
CC       proteins to dithiols.
CC   -!- NrdH redoxins, which are found in Gram-positive bacteria, catalyze a
CC       similar reaction.
//
