ID   1.8.7.3
DE   ferredoxin:CoB-CoM heterodisulfide reductase.
CA   coenzyme B + coenzyme M + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] = coenzyme
CA   M-coenzyme B heterodisulfide + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- HdrABC is an enzyme complex that is found in most methanogens and
CC       catalyzes the reduction of the CoB-CoM heterodisulfide back to CoB
CC       and CoM.
CC   -!- HdrA contains a FAD cofactor that acts as the entry point for
CC       electrons, which are transferred via HdrC to the HdrB catalytic
CC       subunit.
CC   -!- One form of the enzyme from Methanosarcina acetivorans (HdrA2B2C2)
CC       can also catalyze EC 1.8.98.4. cf. EC 1.8.98.5, EC 1.8.98.6,
CC       and EC 1.8.98.1.
DR   Q8TLB0, HDRA1_METAC;  Q8TM02, HDRA2_METAC;  Q8Q0T0, HDRA_METMA ;
DR   Q8TLB2, HDRB1_METAC;  Q8TIB8, HDRB2_METAC;  Q8PY83, HDRB_METMA ;
DR   Q8TLB1, HDRC1_METAC;  Q8TIB9, HDRC2_METAC;  Q8PY84, HDRC_METMA ;
//
ID   1.8.98.1
DE   dihydromethanophenazine:CoB--CoM heterodisulfide reductase.
AN   CoB--CoM heterodisulfide reductase.
AN   heterodisulfide reductase.
CA   methanophenazine + coenzyme B + coenzyme M = dihydromethanophenazine +
CA   coenzyme M-coenzyme B heterodisulfide.
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in methanogenic archaea that belong to the
CC       Methanosarcinales order, regenerates CoM and CoB after the action of
CC       EC 2.8.4.1.
CC   -!- It is a membrane-bound enzyme that contains (per heterodimeric unit)
CC       two distinct b-type hemes and two [4Fe-4S] clusters. cf. EC 1.8.7.3,
CC       EC 1.8.98.5, EC 1.8.98.6 and EC 1.8.98.4.
DR   Q8TSV7, HDRD_METAC ;  P96797, HDRD_METBF ;  Q8PVW3, HDRD_METMA ;
DR   A0A0E3NEE1, HDRD_METTT ;  Q8TSV8, HDRE_METAC ;  P96796, HDRE_METBF ;
DR   Q8PVW4, HDRE_METMA ;  A0A0E3NFS5, HDRE_METTT ;
//
ID   1.8.98.2
DE   sulfiredoxin.
AN   peroxiredoxin-(S-hydroxy-S-oxocysteine) reductase.
CA   S-hydroxy-S-oxy-L-cysteinyl-[peroxiredoxin] + [protein]-dithiol + ATP =
CA   S-hydroxy-L-cysteinyl-[peroxiredoxin] + [protein]-disulfide + ADP +
CA   phosphate.
CC   -!- In the course of the reaction of EC 1.11.1.15, its cysteine residue
CC       is alternately oxidized to the sulfenic acid, S-hydroxycysteine,
CC       and reduced back to cysteine.
CC   -!- Occasionally the S-hydroxycysteine residue is further oxidized to the
CC       sulfinic acid S-hydroxy-S-oxocysteine, thereby inactivating the
CC       enzyme.
CC   -!- The reductase provides a mechanism for regenerating the active form
CC       of peroxiredoxin, i.e. the peroxiredoxin-(S-hydroxycysteine) form.
CC   -!- Apparently the reductase first catalyzes the phosphorylation of the
CC       -S(O)-OH group by ATP to give -S(O)-O-P, which is attached to the
CC       peroxiredoxin by a cysteine residue, forming an -S(O)-S- link between
CC       the two enzymes.
CC   -!- Attack by a thiol splits this bond, leaving the peroxiredoxin as the
CC       sulfenic acid and the reductase as the thiol.
DR   Q9URV9, SRX1_SCHPO ;  P36077, SRX1_YEAST ;  Q9BYN0, SRXN1_HUMAN;
DR   Q9D975, SRXN1_MOUSE;  Q8GY89, SRX_ARATH  ;  Q9VX10, SRX_DROME  ;
//
ID   1.8.98.3
DE   sulfite reductase (coenzyme F420).
AN   coenzyme F420-dependent sulfite reductase.
CA   3 oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + hydrogen sulfide + 3 H2O +
CA   2 H(+) = 3 reduced coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + sulfite.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the archaeon Methanocaldococcus jannaschii,
CC       is involved in sulfite detoxification and assimilation.
DR   Q58280, FSR_METJA  ;
//
ID   1.8.98.4
DE   coenzyme F420:CoB-CoM heterodisulfide,ferredoxin reductase.
CA   coenzyme B + 2 oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + coenzyme M +
CA   2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 4 H(+) = coenzyme M-coenzyme B
CA   heterodisulfide + 2 reduced coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + 2 oxidized
CA   [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin].
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Methanosarcina
CC       acetivorans, catalyzes the reduction of CoB-CoM heterodisulfide back
CC       to CoB and CoM.
CC   -!- The enzyme consists of three components, HdrA, HdrB and HdrC, all of
CC       which contain [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- Electrons enter at HdrA, which also contains FAD, and are transferred
CC       via HdrC to the catalytic component, HdrB.
CC   -!- During methanogenesis from acetate the enzyme catalyzes the activity
CC       of EC 1.8.7.3.
CC   -!- However, it can also use electron bifurcation to direct electron
CC       pairs from reduced coenzyme F420 toward the reduction of both
CC       ferredoxin and CoB-CoM heterodisulfide.
CC   -!- This activity is proposed to take place during Fe(III)-dependent
CC       anaerobic methane oxidation. cf. EC 1.8.98.5, EC 1.8.98.6,
CC       and EC 1.8.98.1.
DR   Q8TM02, HDRA2_METAC;  Q8TIB8, HDRB2_METAC;  Q8TIB9, HDRC2_METAC;
//
ID   1.8.98.5
DE   H2:CoB-CoM heterodisulfide,ferredoxin reductase.
CA   coenzyme B + coenzyme M + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 H(+) =
CA   coenzyme M-coenzyme B heterodisulfide + 2 H2 + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-
CA   [ferredoxin].
CC   -!- This enzyme complex is found in H2-oxidizing CO2-reducing
CC       methanogenic archaea such as Methanothermobacter thermautotrophicus.
CC   -!- It consists of a cytoplasmic complex of HdrABC reductase and MvhAGD
CC       hydrogenase.
CC   -!- Electron pairs donated by the hydrogenase are transferred via its
CC       Delta subunit to the HdrA subunit of the reductase, where they are
CC       bifurcated, reducing both ferredoxin and CoB-CoM heterodisulfide.
CC   -!- The reductase can also form a similar complex with formate
CC       dehydrogenase, see EC 1.8.98.6, formate:CoB-CoM
CC       heterodisulfide,ferredoxin reductase. cf. EC 1.8.7.3, EC 1.8.98.4,
CC       and EC 1.8.98.1.
DR   Q6LWL2, HDRA_METMP ;  O27434, HDRA_METTH ;  Q50756, HDRA_METTM ;
DR   Q6LY38, HDRB1_METMP;  Q6LYD8, HDRB2_METMP;  O27907, HDRB_METTH ;
DR   Q50755, HDRB_METTM ;  Q6LY39, HDRC1_METMP;  Q6LYD7, HDRC2_METMP;
DR   O27906, HDRC_METTH ;  Q50754, HDRC_METTM ;
//
ID   1.8.98.6
DE   formate:CoB-CoM heterodisulfide,ferredoxin reductase.
CA   coenzyme B + coenzyme M + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 CO2 =
CA   coenzyme M-coenzyme B heterodisulfide + 2 formate + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-
CA   [ferredoxin].
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in formate-oxidizing CO2-reducing methanogenic
CC       archaea such as Methanococcus maripaludis.
CC   -!- It consists of a cytoplasmic complex of HdrABC reductase and formate
CC       dehydrogenase.
CC   -!- Electron pairs donated by formate dehydrogenase are transferred to
CC       the HdrA subunit of the reductase, where they are bifurcated,
CC       reducing both ferredoxin and CoB-CoM heterodisulfide. cf. EC 1.8.7.3,
CC       EC 1.8.98.4, EC 1.8.98.5, and EC 1.8.98.1.
DR   Q6LWL2, HDRA_METMP ;  Q6LY38, HDRB1_METMP;  Q6LYD8, HDRB2_METMP;
DR   Q6LY39, HDRC1_METMP;  Q6LYD7, HDRC2_METMP;
//
ID   1.8.98.7
DE   cysteine-type anaerobic sulfatase-maturating enzyme.
AN   anaerobic sulfatase maturase.
AN   Cys-type anaerobic sulfatase-maturating enzyme.
CA   L-cysteinyl-[sulfatase] + S-adenosyl-L-methionine + H2O = 3-oxo-L-alanyl-
CA   [sulfatase] + hydrogen sulfide + 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- A radical S-adenosylmethionine (AdoMet) enzyme that contains three
CC       [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in some bacteria, activates a type I sulfatase
CC       enzyme (EC 3.1.6.1) by converting a conserved L-cysteine residue in
CC       the active site to a unique 3-oxo-L-alanine residue that is essential
CC       for the sulfatase activity.
CC   -!- Some enzymes can also act on L-serine, see EC 1.1.98.7 and
CC       EC 1.8.3.7.
DR   A0Q2E1, ANSME_CLONN;  Q0TTH1, ANSME_CLOP1;  Q8XMQ3, ANSME_CLOPE;
//
ID   1.8.98.8
DE   thioredoxin-disulfide reductase (factor 420-dependent).
AN   (coenzyme F420)-dependent thioredoxin-disulfide reductase.
AN   deazaflavin-dependent flavin-containing thioredoxin reductase.
AN   F420-dependent thioredoxin-disulfide reductase.
CA   oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + [thioredoxin]-dithiol + H(+) =
CA   reduced coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + [thioredoxin]-disulfide.
CC   -!- A flavoprotein (FAD).
CC   -!- The enzyme is found only in methanogenic archaea living in deep-sea
CC       volcanoes, and requires high partial pressure of hydrogen, which
CC       effects the reducing potential of the F420/F420H2 pair. cf.
CC       EC 1.8.1.9.
//
ID   1.8.99.1
DE   Deleted entry.
//
