ID   1.10.3.11
DE   ubiquinol oxidase (non-electrogenic).
AN   cyanide-insensitive oxidase.
AN   plant alternative oxidase.
AN   ubiquinol oxidase.
CA   2 a ubiquinol + O2 = 2 a ubiquinone + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, described from the mitochondria of plants and some fungi
CC       and protists, is an alternative terminal oxidase that is not
CC       sensitive to cyanide inhibition and does not generate a proton motive
CC       force.
CC   -!- The function of this oxidase is believed to be dissipating excess
CC       reducing power, minimizing oxidative stress, and optimizing
CC       photosynthesis in response to changing conditions.
DR   Q39219, AOX1A_ARATH;  O82807, AOX1A_ORYSJ;  O23913, AOX1B_ARATH;
DR   O82766, AOX1B_ORYSJ;  O22048, AOX1C_ARATH;  Q8W855, AOX1C_ORYSJ;
DR   Q40294, AOX1_MANIN ;  P22185, AOX1_SAUVE ;  Q07185, AOX1_SOYBN ;
DR   Q41224, AOX1_TOBAC ;  O22049, AOX2_ARATH ;  Q41266, AOX2_SOYBN ;
DR   Q40578, AOX2_TOBAC ;  Q8LEE7, AOX3_ARATH ;  O03376, AOX3_SOYBN ;
