DE   catalase.
CA   2 H2O2 = O2 + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- A manganese protein containing Mn(III) in the resting state, which
CC       also belongs here, is often called pseudocatalase.
CC   -!- The enzymes from some organisms, such as Penicillium simplicissimum,
CC       can also act as a peroxidase (EC 1.11.1.7) for which several organic
CC       substances, especially ethanol, can act as a hydrogen donor.
CC   -!- Enzymes that exhibit both catalase and peroxidase activity belong
CC       under EC 1.11.1.21.
