ID   1.11.2.6
DE   L-tyrosine peroxygenase.
CA   L-tyrosine + H2O2 = L-dopa + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Streptomyces lincolnensis participates
CC       in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic lincomycin A, while that from
CC       Streptomyces refuineus is involved in anthramycin biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which contains a heme b cofactor, is rapidly inactivated
CC       in the presence of hydrogen peroxide, but the presence of L-tyrosine
CC       protects it. cf. EC 1.11.2.5.
//
ID   1.11.2.7
DE   torosachrysone-coupling peroxygenase.
CA   2 (R)-torosachrysone + H2O2 = phlegmacin + 2 H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the mushroom Calonarius odorifer,
CC       catalyzes the regioselective coupling of two molecules of the
CC       phenolic compound (R)-torosachrysone at the corresponding C7 and C10'
CC       positions, forming the 7,10'-coupled dimeric product (phlegmacin).
CC   -!- The enzyme produces both atropisomers of the product.
