DE   indole 2,3-dioxygenase.
AN   indole oxidase.
CA   indole + O2 = 2-formamidobenzaldehyde.
CC   -!- Enzymes from the plants Tecoma stans, Jasminum grandiflorum and Zea
CC       mays are flavoproteins containing copper.
CC   -!- They are part of enzyme systems that form either anthranil (3,4-
CC       benzoisoxazole) (Tecoma stans), anthranilate (Jasminum grandiflorum)
CC       or both (Zea mays) as the final product.
CC   -!- A second enzyme from Tecoma stans is not a flavoprotein, does not
CC       require copper, and is part of a system that forms anthranilate as
CC       the final product.
//
ID   1.13.11.18
DE   persulfide dioxygenase.
AN   sulfur dioxygenase.
AN   sulfur oxygenase.
CA   S-sulfanylglutathione + O2 + H2O = sulfite + glutathione + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Perthiols, formed spontaneously by interactions between thiols and
CC       elemental sulfur or sulfide, are the only acceptable substrate to the
CC       enzyme.
CC   -!- The sulfite that is formed by the enzyme can be further converted
CC       into sulfate, thiosulfate or S-sulfoglutathione (GSSO3(-)) non-
CC       enzymically.
