ID   1.13.11.63
DE   beta-carotene 15,15'-dioxygenase.
AN   beta-carotene 15,15'-monooxygenase.
AN   carotene 15,15'-dioxygenase.
AN   carotene dioxygenase.
CA   all-trans-beta-carotene + O2 = 2 all-trans-retinal.
CC   -!- Requires Fe(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme cleaves beta-carotene symmetrically, producing two
CC       molecules of all-trans-retinal.
CC   -!- Both atoms of the oxygen molecule are incorporated into the products.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also process beta-cryptoxanthin, 8'-apo-beta-
CC       carotenal, 4'-apo-beta-carotenal, alpha-carotene and gamma-carotene
CC       in decreasing order.
CC   -!- The presence of at least one unsubstituted beta-ionone ring in a
CC       substrate greater than C30 is mandatory.
CC   -!- A prokaryotic enzyme has been reported from the uncultured marine
CC       bacterium 66A03, where it is involved in the proteorhodopsin system,
CC       which uses retinal as its chromophore.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.13.11.21, EC 1.13.11.n2 and EC 1.14.99.36.
DR   Q9I993, BCDO1_CHICK;  Q9HAY6, BCDO1_HUMAN;  Q9JJS6, BCDO1_MOUSE;
DR   Q91XT5, BCDO1_RAT  ;  Q9HNE6, BLH_HALSA  ;  Q4PNI0, BLH_UNCMB  ;
DR   B0R5N7, BRP_HALS3  ;  Q9HPU7, BRP_HALSA  ;  S0ENQ2, CARX_GIBF5 ;
//
ID   1.13.11.64
DE   5-nitrosalicylate dioxygenase.
CA   5-nitrosalicylate + O2 = 2-oxo-3-(5-oxofuran-2-ylidene)propanoate +
CA   nitrite + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the soil bacterium Bradyrhizobium sp.
CC       JS329, is involved in the pathway of 5-nitroanthranilate degradation.
CC   -!- It is unusual in being able to catalyze the ring fission without the
CC       requirement for prior removal of the nitro group.
CC   -!- The product undergoes spontaneous lactonization, with concurrent
CC       elimination of the nitro group.
DR   D3WZ86, NAAB_BRASZ ;
//
ID   1.13.11.65
DE   carotenoid isomerooxygenase.
CA   all-trans-zeaxanthin + O2 = (3R)-11-cis-3-hydroxyretinal + (3R)-all-
CA   trans-3-hydroxyretinal.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the moth Galleria mellonella and the
CC       fruit fly Drosophila melanogaster, is involved in the synthesis of
CC       retinal from dietary caroteoids in insects.
CC   -!- The enzyme accepts different all-trans carotenoids, including beta-
CC       carotene, alpha-carotene and lutein, and catalyzes the symmetrical
CC       cleavage of the carotenoid and the simultaneous isomerization of only
CC       one of the products to a cis configuration.
CC   -!- When the substrate is hydroxylated only in one side (as in
CC       cryptoxanthin), the enzyme preferentially isomerizes the hydroxylated
CC       part of the molecule.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.164.
DR   Q9VFS2, NINAB_DROME;  A8Y9I2, NINAB_GALME;
//
ID   1.13.11.66
DE   hydroquinone 1,2-dioxygenase.
AN   hydroquinone dioxygenase.
CA   hydroquinone + O2 = (2E,4Z)-4-hydroxy-6-oxohexa-2,4-dienoate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is an extradiol-type dioxygenase, and is a member of the
CC       nonheme-iron(II)-dependent dioxygenase family.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the ring cleavage of a wide range of hydroquinone
CC       substrates to produce the corresponding 4-hydroxymuconic
CC       semialdehydes.
DR   Q9WXE6, LINE_SPHIU ;
//
ID   1.13.11.67
DE   8'-apo-beta-carotenoid 14',13'-cleaving dioxygenase.
CA   8'-apo-beta-carotenol + O2 = 14'-apo-beta-carotenal + (3E,5E)-7-hydroxy-
CA   6-methylhepta-3,5-dienal.
CC   -!- A thiol-dependent enzyme.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.13.11.63, it is not active toward beta-carotene.
CC   -!- The secondary product has not been characterized, but may be (3E,5E)-
CC       7-hydroxy-6-methylhepta-3,5-dien-2-one.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.13.12.12.
//
ID   1.13.11.68
DE   9-cis-beta-carotene 9',10'-cleaving dioxygenase.
CA   9-cis-beta-carotene + O2 = 9-cis-10'-apo-beta-carotenal + beta-ionone.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in a pathway leading to biosynthesis of
CC       strigolactones, plant hormones involved in promotion of symbiotic
CC       associations known as arbuscular mycorrhiza.
DR   Q7XJM2, CCD7_ARATH ;  Q7XU29, CCD7_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   1.13.11.69
DE   carlactone synthase.
CA   9-cis-10'-apo-beta-carotenal + 2 O2 = (2E,4E,6E)-7-hydroxy-4-methylhepta-
CA   2,4,6-trienal + (11R)-carlactone.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in a pathway leading to biosynthesis of
CC       strigolactones, plant hormones involved in promotion of symbiotic
CC       associations known as arbuscular mycorrhiza.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes EC 1.13.11.70, but 10-fold slower.
DR   Q8LIY8, CCD8B_ORYSJ;  Q8VY26, CCD8_ARATH ;
//
ID   1.13.11.70
DE   all-trans-10'-apo-beta-carotenal 13,14-cleaving dioxygenase.
AN   carotenoid cleavage dioxygenase 8.
CA   all-trans-10'-apo-beta-carotenal + O2 = (2E,4E,6E)-4-methylocta-2,4,6-
CA   trienedial + 13-apo-beta-carotenone.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana also catalyzes
CC       EC 1.13.11.69, 10-fold faster.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.99.n5.
DR   Q8LIY8, CCD8B_ORYSJ;  Q8VY26, CCD8_ARATH ;
//
ID   1.13.11.71
DE   carotenoid-9',10'-cleaving dioxygenase.
AN   beta-carotene 9',10'-monooxygenase.
CA   all-trans-beta-carotene + O2 = beta-ionone + all-trans-10'-apo-beta-
CA   carotenal.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the asymmetric oxidative cleavage of
CC       carotenoids.
CC   -!- The mammalian enzyme can also cleave all-trans-lycopene.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.99.n2.
DR   Q9BYV7, BCDO2_HUMAN;  Q8HXG8, BCDO2_MACFA;  Q99NF1, BCDO2_MOUSE;
DR   Q6QT07, BCDO2_MUSPF;  Q5RF16, BCDO2_PONAB;
//
ID   1.13.11.72
DE   2-hydroxyethylphosphonate dioxygenase.
AN   HEPD.
CA   2-hydroxyethylphosphonate + O2 = hydroxymethylphosphonate + formate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from some bacteria including Streptomyces hygroscopicus and
CC       Streptomyces viridochromogenes.
CC   -!- The pro-R hydrogen at C-2 of the ethyl group is retained by the
CC       formate ion.
CC   -!- Any stereochemistry at C-1 of the ethyl group is lost.
