CC       the carboxylic group of D-firefly luciferin and AMP, with the release
CC       of diphosphate.
CC   -!- An oxygenation follows, with release of the AMP group and formation
CC       of a very short-lived peroxide that cyclizes into a dioxetanone
CC       structure, which collapses, releasing a CO2 molecule.
CC   -!- The spontaneous breakdown of the dioxetanone (rather than the
CC       hydrolysis of the adenylate) releases the energy (about 50 kcal/mole)
CC       that is necessary to generate the excited state of oxyluciferin.
CC   -!- The excited luciferin then emits a photon, returning to its ground
CC       state.
CC   -!- The enzyme has a secondary acyl-CoA ligase activity when acting on
CC       L-firefly luciferin.
