CC       Lingulodinium polyedrum, Noctiluca scintillans, and Pyrocystis
CC       lunula.
CC   -!- It is a single protein with three luciferase domains.
CC   -!- The luciferin is strongly bound by a luciferin binding protein above
CC       a pH of 7.
DR   O77206, LUCIF_LINPO;
//
ID   1.13.12.19
DE   2-oxoglutarate dioxygenase (ethylene-forming).
AN   ethylene-forming enzyme.
CA   2-oxoglutarate + O2 + 2 H(+) = ethene + 3 CO2 + H2O.
CC   -!- This is one of two simultaneous reactions catalyzed by the enzyme,
CC       which is responsible for ethylene production in bacteria of the
CC       Pseudomonas syringae group.
CC   -!- In the other reaction (EC 1.14.11.34) the enzyme catalyzes the mono-
CC       oxygenation of both 2-oxoglutarate and L-arginine, forming succinate,
CC       carbon dioxide and L-hydroxyarginine, which is subsequently cleaved
CC       into guanidine and (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate.
CC   -!- The enzymes catalyze two cycles of the ethylene-forming reaction for
CC       each cycle of the succinate-forming reaction, so that the
CC       stoichiometry of the products ethylene and succinate is 2:1.
DR   Q9Z377, EFE_PSEAQ  ;  Q7BS31, EFE_PSECA  ;  Q7BS32, EFE_PSESG  ;
DR   P32021, EFE_PSESH  ;  Q9Z3T0, EFE_PSESJ  ;  Q8XPV7, EFE_RALN1  ;
//
ID   1.13.12.20
DE   noranthrone monooxygenase.
AN   norsolorinate anthrone oxidase.
CA   noranthrone + O2 = norsolorinic acid + H2O.
CC   -!- Involved in the synthesis of aflatoxins in the fungus Aspergillus
CC       parasiticus.
DR   B8NI03, HYPC_ASPFN ;
//
ID   1.13.12.21
DE   tetracenomycin-F1 monooxygenase.
CA   tetracenomycin F1 + O2 = tetracenomycin D3 + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of the anthracycline
CC       antibiotic tetracenomycin C by the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       glaucescens.
DR   P39889, TCMH_STRGA ;
//
ID   1.13.12.22
DE   deoxynogalonate monooxygenase.
AN   12-deoxynogalonic acid monooxygenase.
AN   12-deoxynogalonic acid oxidoreductase.
AN   deoxynogalonate oxidase.
CA   deoxynogalonate + O2 = nogalonate + H2O + H(+).
