ID   1.14.11.69
DE   [histone H3]-trimethyl-L-lysine(36) demethylase.
CA   N(6),N(6),N(6)-trimethyl-L-lysyl(36)-[histone H3] + 2 2-oxoglutarate +
CA   2 O2 = N(6)-methyl-L-lysyl(36)-[histone H3] + 2 formaldehyde +
CA   2 succinate + 2 CO2.
CC   -!- Requires iron(II).
CC   -!- This entry describes a group of enzymes that demethylate N-methylated
CC       Lys(36) residues in the tail of the histone protein H3 (H3K36).
CC   -!- This lysine residue can exist in three methylation states (mono-,
CC       di- and trimethylated), but this group of enzymes only act on the the
CC       tri- and di-methylated forms.
CC   -!- The enzymes are dioxygenases and act by hydroxylating the methyl
CC       group, forming an unstable hemiaminal that leaves as formaldehyde.
CC   -!- Since trimethylation of H3K36 enhances transcription, this enzyme
CC       acts as a transcription repressor.
CC   -!- The enzymes that possess this activity often also catalyze the
CC       activity of EC 1.14.11.66, cf. EC 1.14.11.27.
DR   Q8RWR1, JMJ30_ARATH;  Q9V333, KDM4A_DROME;  O75164, KDM4A_HUMAN;
