ID   1.14.13.82
DE   vanillate monooxygenase.
AN   4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzoate demethylase.
AN   vanillate demethylase.
CA   vanillate + NADH + O2 + H(+) = 3,4-dihydroxybenzoate + formaldehyde +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- Forms part of the vanillin degradation pathway in Arthrobacter sp.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.3.12.
DR   P12609, VANA_PSES9 ;  O05616, VANA_PSEUH ;
//
ID   1.14.13.83
DE   precorrin-3B synthase.
AN   precorrin-3X synthase.
CA   precorrin-3A + NADH + O2 + 2 H(+) = precorrin-3B + NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- An oxygen atom from dioxygen is incorporated into the macrocycle at
CC       C-20.
CC   -!- In the aerobic cobalamin biosynthesis pathway, four enzymes are
CC       involved in the conversion of precorrin-3A to precorrin-6A.
CC   -!- This enzyme carries out the first of the four steps, yielding
CC       precorrin-3B as the product.
CC   -!- This is followed by three methylation reactions, which introduce a
CC       methyl group at C-17 (CobJ; EC 2.1.1.131), C-11 (CobM; 2.1.1.133) and
CC       C-1 (CobF; EC 2.1.1.152) of the macrocycle, giving rise to precorrin-
CC       4, precorrin-5 and precorrin-6A, respectively.
DR   P21637, COBG_SINSX ;
//
ID   1.14.13.84
DE   4-hydroxyacetophenone monooxygenase.
AN   HAPMO.
CA   4'-hydroxyacetophenone + NADPH + O2 + H(+) = 4-acetoxyphenol + NADP(+) +
CA   H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Pseudomonas fluorescens ACB catalyzes the conversion
CC       of a wide range of acetophenone derivatives.
CC   -!- Highest activity occurs with compounds bearing an electron-donating
CC       substituent at the para position of the aromatic ring.
CC   -!- In the absence of substrate, the enzyme can act as an NADPH oxidase
CC       (EC 1.6.3.1).
DR   Q93TJ5, HAPMO_PSEFL;
