ID   1.14.13.131
DE   dissimilatory dimethyl-sulfide monooxygenase.
AN   dimethyl sulfide C-monooxygenase.
AN   dimethylsulfide monooxygenase.
AN   dimethyl sulfide monooxygenase.
CA   dimethyl sulfide + NADH + O2 + H(+) = methanethiol + formaldehyde +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates exclusively in sulfur dissimilation.
CC   -!- It has lower activity with diethyl sulfide and other short-chain
CC       alkyl methyl sulfides.
CC   -!- Its activity is stimulated by combined addition of FMN, and, after
CC       depletion of cations, of Mg(2+) and Fe(2+).
CC   -!- The enzymes from bacteria of the Hyphomicrobium genus are a two
CC       component system that includes an FMN-dependent reductase subunit and
CC       a monooxygenase subunit.
DR   E9JFX9, DMOA_HYPSL ;
