ID   1.14.13.166
DE   4-nitrocatechol 4-monooxygenase.
CA   (1) 4-nitrocatechol + NADPH + O2 = 2-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone + nitrite +
CA   NADP(+) + H2O.
CA   (2) 4-nitrocatechol + NADH + O2 = 2-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone + nitrite +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of 4-nitrocatechol with the
CC       concomitant removal of the nitro group as nitrite.
CC   -!- Forms a two-component system with a flavoprotein reductase.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the bacteria Lysinibacillus sphaericus JS905 and
CC       Rhodococcus sp. strain PN1 were shown to also catalyze EC 1.14.13.29,
CC       while the enzyme from Pseudomonas sp. WBC-3 was shown to also
CC       catalyze EC 1.14.13.167.
DR   Q6F4M8, NPCA_RHOOP ;  Q6F4M9, NPCB_RHOOP ;
//
ID   1.14.13.167
DE   4-nitrophenol 4-monooxygenase.
CA   4-nitrophenol + NADPH + O2 + H(+) = 1,4-benzoquinone + nitrite +
CA   NADP(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the first step in a degradation pathway for
CC       4-nitrophenol, the oxidation of 4-nitrophenol at position 4 with the
CC       concomitant removal of the nitro group as nitrite.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp. WBC-3 also catalyzes
CC       EC 1.14.13.166.
DR   C1I201, PNPA_PSEWB ;
//
ID   1.14.13.168
DE   indole-3-pyruvate monooxygenase.
CA   indole-3-pyruvate + NADPH + O2 + H(+) = (indol-3-yl)acetate + CO2 +
