DE   2-heptyl-3-hydroxy-4(1H)-quinolone synthase.
AN   2-heptyl-3,4-dihydroxyquinoline synthase.
CA   2-heptyl-4(1H)-quinolone + NADH + O2 + H(+) = 2-heptyl-3-hydroxy-4(1H)-
CA   quinolone + NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa catalyzes the
CC       terminal step in biosynthesis of the signal molecule 2-heptyl-3,4-
CC       dihydroxyquinoline that plays a role in regulation of virulence
CC       genes.
DR   A0A0E4AFG7, AQDB1_RHOER;  A0A0E4AFH6, AQDB2_RHOER;  B1MFK1, AQDB_MYCA9 ;
