DE   benzoyl-CoA 2,3-epoxidase.
AN   benzoyl-CoA 2,3-dioxygenase.
AN   benzoyl-CoA dioxygenase/reductase.
CA   benzoyl-CoA + NADPH + O2 + H(+) = 2,3-epoxy-2,3-dihydrobenzoyl-CoA +
CA   NADP(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in aerobic benzoate metabolism in Azoarcus
CC       evansii.
CC   -!- BoxB functions as the oxygenase part of benzoyl-CoA oxygenase in
CC       conjunction with BoxA, the reductase component, which upon binding of
CC       benzoyl-CoA, transfers two electrons to the ring in the course of
CC       dioxygenation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.12.21 and EC 1.14.12.n1.
DR   Q9AIX6, BOXA_AROEV ;  Q9AIX7, BOXB_AROEV ;
//
ID   1.14.13.209
DE   salicyloyl-CoA 5-hydroxylase.
CA   2-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA + NADH + O2 + H(+) = 2,5-dihydroxybenzoyl-CoA +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces sp. WA46,
CC       participates in a pathway for salicylate degradation. cf.
CC       EC 1.14.13.172.
DR   Q7X281, SDGC_STRSQ ;
//
ID   1.14.13.210
DE   4-methyl-5-nitrocatechol 5-monooxygenase.
AN   4-methyl-5-nitrocatechol oxygenase.
AN   MNC monooxygenase.
CA   (1) 4-methyl-5-nitrocatechol + NADPH + O2 = 2-hydroxy-5-methylquinone +
CA   nitrite + NADP(+) + H2O + H(+).
CA   (2) 4-methyl-5-nitrocatechol + NADH + O2 = 2-hydroxy-5-methylquinone +
CA   nitrite + NAD(+) + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Burkholderia sp. DNT, can use
CC       both NADH and NADPH, but prefers NADPH.
CC   -!- It has a narrow substrate range, but can also act on 4-nitrocatechol.
DR   Q2PWU9, DNTB_BURSP ;
//
ID   1.14.13.211
DE   rifampicin monooxygenase.
AN   RIF-O.
CA   (1) rifampicin + NADPH + O2 = rifampicin para-naphthoquinone carboxamide
CA   + NADP(+) + H2O + H(+).
CA   (2) rifampicin + NADH + O2 = rifampicin para-naphthoquinone carboxamide +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme has been found in a variety of environmental bacteria,
CC       notably Rhodococcus, Nocardia, and Streptomyces.
CC   -!- It hydroxylates C-2 of rifampicin leading to the linearization of the
CC       molecule.
DR   Q5YTV5, ROX_NOCFA  ;  P95598, ROX_RHOHA  ;  F2R776, ROX_STRVP  ;
//
ID   1.14.13.212
DE   1,3,7-trimethyluric acid 5-monooxygenase.
CA   1,3,7-trimethylurate + NADH + O2 + H(+) = 1,3,7-trimethyl-5-
CA   hydroxyisourate + NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp. CBB1,
CC       is part of the bacterial C-8 oxidation-based caffeine degradation
CC       pathway.
CC   -!- The product decomposes spontaneously to a racemic mixture of 3,6,8-
CC       trimethylallantoin.
CC   -!- The enzyme shows no acitivity with urate. cf. EC 1.14.13.113.
//
ID   1.14.13.213
DE   Transferred entry: 1.14.14.131.
