ID   1.14.13.215
DE   protoasukamycin 4-monooxygenase.
CA   protoasukamycin + NADH + O2 + H(+) = 4-hydroxyprotoasukamycin + NAD(+) +
CA   H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces nodosus
CC       subsp. asukaensis, is involved in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic
CC       asukamycin.
DR   D7P5V0, ASUE1_STRNS;
//
ID   1.14.13.216
DE   asperlicin C monooxygenase.
CA   (1) asperlicin C + NADH + O2 + H(+) = asperlicin E + NAD(+) + H2O.
CA   (2) asperlicin C + NADPH + O2 + H(+) = asperlicin E + NADP(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the fungus Aspergillus alliaceus,
CC       contains an FAD cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme inserts a hydroxyl group, leading to formation of a
CC       N-C bond that creates an additional cycle between the bicyclic indole
CC       and the tetracyclic core moieties, resulting in the heptacyclic
CC       asperlicin E.
DR   P0DOW1, ASCM_PETAA ;
//
ID   1.14.13.217
DE   protodeoxyviolaceinate monooxygenase.
AN   protoviolaceinate synthase.
CA   (1) protodeoxyviolaceinate + NADPH + O2 + H(+) = protoviolaceinate +
CA   NADP(+) + H2O.
CA   (2) protodeoxyviolaceinate + NADH + O2 + H(+) = protoviolaceinate +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Chromobacterium
CC       violaceum, participates in the biosynthesis of the violet pigment
CC       violacein.
CC   -!- The immediate product, protoviolaceinate, can be acted upon by
CC       EC 1.14.13.224, leading to violacein production.
CC   -!- However, it is very labile, and in the presence of oxygen can be
CC       converted to the shunt product proviolacein.
DR   Q9S3U8, VIOD_CHRVO ;
//
ID   1.14.13.218
DE   5-methylphenazine-1-carboxylate 1-monooxygenase.
CA   5-methyl-phenazine-1-carboxylate + NADH + O2 + 2 H(+) = pyocyanin + CO2 +
CA   NAD(+) + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of pyocyanine, a toxin produced and
CC       secreted by the organism.
CC   -!- It can also act on phenazine-1-carboxylate, converting it into
CC       1-hydroxyphenazine.
DR   A0A172J1S0, PHZS_LYSAN ;  Q9HWG9, PHZS_PSEAE ;
