ID   1.14.14.5
DE   alkanesulfonate monooxygenase.
AN   FMNH2-dependent aliphatic sulfonate monooxygenase.
AN   sulfate starvation-induced protein 6.
CA   an alkanesulfonate + FMNH2 + O2 = an aldehyde + FMN + sulfite + H2O +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli catalyzes the desulfonation of a
CC       wide range of aliphatic sulfonates (unsubstituted C1- to C14-
CC       sulfonates as well as substituted C2-sulfonates).
CC   -!- Does not desulfonate taurine (2-aminoethanesulfonate) or aromatic
CC       sulfonates.
CC   -!- Does not use FMN as a bound cofactor.
CC   -!- Instead, it uses reduced FMN (i.e., FMNH2) as a substrate.
CC   -!- FMNH2 is provided by SsuE, the associated FMN reductase
CC       (EC 1.5.1.38).
