ID   1.14.14.8
DE   anthranilate 3-monooxygenase (FAD).
AN   anthranilate 3-hydroxylase.
AN   anthranilate hydroxylase.
CA   anthranilate + FADH2 + O2 = 3-hydroxyanthranilate + FAD + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Geobacillus
CC       thermodenitrificans, participates in the pathway of tryptophan
CC       degradation.
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of a system that also includes a bifunctional
CC       riboflavin kinase/FMN adenylyltransferase and an FAD reductase, which
CC       ensures ample supply of FAD to the monooxygenase.
DR   A4IT51, HPAH_GEOTN ;
//
ID   1.14.14.9
DE   4-hydroxyphenylacetate 3-monooxygenase.
AN   4 HPA 3-hydroxylase.
AN   4-hydroxyphenylacetic acid-3-hydroxylase.
AN   p-hydroxyphenylacetate 3-hydroxylase.
CA   4-hydroxyphenylacetate + FADH2 + O2 = 3,4-dihydroxyphenylacetate + FAD +
CA   H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli attacks a broad spectrum of phenolic
CC       compounds.
CC   -!- The enzyme uses FADH2 as a substrate rather than a cofactor.
CC   -!- FADH2 is provided by EC 1.5.1.36.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.3.
DR   Q57160, HPAB_ECOLX ;  Q48440, HPAB_KLEOX ;  Q9HWT7, HPAB_PSEAE ;
DR   Q5SJP8, HPAB_THET8 ;  Q6Q272, HPAH_ACIBA ;  Q4L1M7, HPAH_GEOP9 ;
DR   A4IT51, HPAH_GEOTN ;  C0SPC0, YOAI_BACSU ;
//
ID   1.14.14.10
DE   nitrilotriacetate monooxygenase.
CA   nitrilotriacetate + FMNH2 + O2 = aminodiacetate + FMN + glyoxylate + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Aminobacter aminovorans (previously Chelatobacter
CC       heintzii) is part of a two component system that also includes
CC       EC 1.5.1.42 (FMN reductase), which provides reduced flavin
CC       mononucleotide for this enzyme.
DR   P54989, NTAA_AMIAI ;
//
ID   1.14.14.11
DE   styrene monooxygenase.
CA   styrene + FADH2 + O2 = (S)-styrene oxide + FAD + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the first step in the aerobic styrene
CC       degradation pathway.
CC   -!- It forms a two-component system with a reductase (StyB) that utilizes
CC       NADH to reduce FAD, which is then transferred to the oxygenase.
DR   O06834, STYA_PSEFL ;  O50214, STYA_PSESP ;
//
ID   1.14.14.12
DE   3-hydroxy-9,10-secoandrosta-1,3,5(10)-triene-9,17-dione monooxygenase.
CA   3-hydroxy-9,10-secoandrosta-1,3,5(10)-triene-9,17-dione + FMNH2 + O2 =
CA   3,4-dihydroxy-9,10-secoandrosta-1,3,5(10)-triene-9,17-dione + FMN + H2O +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme participates in the degradation of several
CC       steroids, including cholesterol and testosterone.
CC   -!- It can use either FADH or FMNH2 as flavin cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a two-component system with a reductase (HsaB) that
CC       utilizes NADH to reduce the flavin, which is then transferred to the
CC       oxygenase subunit.
