CA   hydroxy-C21-steroid + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H2O +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Requires NADPH and EC 1.6.2.4.
CC   -!- Catalyzes two independent reactions at the same active site - the
CC       17alpha-hydroxylation of pregnenolone and progesterone, which is part
CC       of glucocorticoid hormones biosynthesis, and the conversion of the
CC       17alpha-hydroxylated products via a 17,20-lyase reaction to form
CC       androstenedione and dehydroepiandrosterone, leading to sex hormone
CC       biosynthesis (EC 1.14.14.32).
CC   -!- The ratio of the 17alpha-hydroxylase and 17,20-lyase activities is an
CC       important factor in determining the directions of steroid hormone
CC       biosynthesis toward biosynthesis of glucocorticoid or sex hormones.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.1.7, EC 1.14.99.9 and EC 1.99.1.9.
