CA   EDTA + 2 FMNH2 + 2 O2 = ethylenediaminediacetate + 2 FMN + 2 glyoxylate +
CA   2 H2O + 3 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of a two component system that also includes
CC       EC 1.5.1.42 which provides reduced flavin mononucleotide for this
CC       enzyme.
CC   -!- While the enzyme has a substrate overlap with EC 1.14.14.10, it has a
CC       much wider substrate range, which includes nitrilotriacetate (NTA)
CC       and diethylenetriaminepentaacetate (DTPA) in addition to EDTA.
//
ID   1.14.14.34
DE   methanesulfonate monooxygenase (FMNH2).
CA   methanesulfonate + FMNH2 + O2 = FMN + sulfite + formaldehyde + H2O +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Pseudomonas strains, allows the
CC       organisms to utilize methanesulfonate as their sulfur source.
CC   -!- It acts in combination with a dedicated NADH-dependent FMN reductase
CC       (EC 1.5.1.42), which provides it with reduced FMN. cf.
CC       EC 1.14.13.111.
//
ID   1.14.14.35
DE   dimethylsulfone monooxygenase.
CA   dimethyl sulfone + FMNH2 + O2 = methanesulfinate + FMN + formaldehyde +
CA   H2O + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Pseudomonas spp., is involved in a
CC       dimethyl sulfide degradation pathway.
CC   -!- It is dependent on NAD(P)H-dependent FMN reductase (EC 1.5.1.38,
CC       1.5.1.39, or 1.5.1.42), which provides it with reduced FMN.
CC   -!- The product, methanesulfinate, is oxidized spontaneously to
CC       methanesulfonate in the presence of dioxygen and FMNH2.
DR   Q3KC85, SFNG_PSEPF ;  Q65YW9, SFNG_PSEPU ;
//
ID   1.14.14.36
DE   tyrosine N-monooxygenase.
AN   CYP79A1.
AN   tyrosine N-hydroxylase.
CA   L-tyrosine + 2 reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + 2 O2 = (E)-4-
CA   hydroxyphenylacetaldehyde oxime + 2 oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase] + CO2 + 3 H2O + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Sorghum is involved in the biosynthesis of the
CC       cyanogenic glucoside dhurrin.
CC   -!- In Sinapis alba (white mustard) the enzyme is involved in the
CC       biosynthesis of the glucosinolate sinalbin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.41.
DR   Q43135, C79A1_SORBI;
//
