ID   1.14.14.45
DE   aromatic aldoxime N-monooxygenase.
AN   CYP83B1.
CA   (1) (E)-(indol-3-yl)acetaldehyde oxime + glutathione + reduced [NADPH-
CA   -hemoprotein reductase] + O2 = (E)-1-(glutathione-S-yl)-2-(1H-indol-3-
CA   yl)acetohydroximate + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + 2 H2O +
CA   H(+).
CA   (2) (E)-phenylacetaldehyde oxime + glutathione + reduced [NADPH-
CA   -hemoprotein reductase] + O2 = (Z)-1-(glutathione-S-yl)-2-
CA   phenylacetohydroximate + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + 2 H2O
CA   + H(+).
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of glucosinolates in plants.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the N-hydroxylation of aromatic aldoximes
CC       derived from L-tryptophan and L-phenylalanine, forming an aci-nitro
CC       intermediate that reacts non-enzymically with glutathione to produce
CC       an N-alkyl-thiohydroximate adduct, the committed precursor of
CC       glucosinolates.
CC   -!- In the absence of glutathione, the enzyme is suicidal, probably due
CC       to interaction of the reactive aci-nitro compound with catalytic
CC       residues in the active site.
DR   O65782, C83B1_ARATH;
//
ID   1.14.14.46
DE   pimeloyl-[acyl-carrier protein] synthase.
AN   CYP107H1.
CA   a C2-C8-saturated long-chain fatty acyl-[ACP] + 2 reduced [flavodoxin] +
CA   3 O2 = 6-carboxyhexanoyl-[ACP] + a fatty aldehyde + 2 oxidized
CA   [flavodoxin] + 3 H2O + 3 H(+).
CC   -!- Catalyzes an oxidative C-C bond cleavage of long-chain acyl-[acyl-
CC       carrier protein]s of various lengths to generate pimeloyl-[acyl-
CC       carrier protein], an intermediate in the biosynthesis of biotin.
CC   -!- The preferred substrate of the enzyme from the bacterium Bacillus
CC       subtilis is palmitoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] which then gives
CC       heptanal as the alkanal.
CC   -!- The mechanism is similar to EC 1.14.15.6, followed by a hydroxylation
CC       step, which may occur spontaneously.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.15.12.
DR   P53554, BIOI_BACSU ;
//
ID   1.14.14.47
DE   nitric-oxide synthase (flavodoxin).
AN   nitric oxide synthetase.
AN   NO synthase.
CA   3 reduced [flavodoxin] + 2 L-arginine + 4 O2 = 3 oxidized [flavodoxin] +
CA   2 L-citrulline + 2 nitric oxide + 4 H2O + 5 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in bacteria and archaea, consist of only an
CC       oxygenase domain and functions together with bacterial ferredoxins or
CC       flavodoxins.
CC   -!- The orthologous enzymes from plants and animals also contain a
CC       reductase domain and use only NADPH as the electron donor (cf.
CC       EC 1.14.13.39).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.165.
DR   O34453, NOSO_BACSU ;  Q9RR97, NOSO_DEIRA ;  Q5HEK7, NOSO_STAAC ;
