CA   reductase] + 2 O2 = a 3',5'-dihydroxyflavanone + 2 oxidized [NADPH-
CA   -hemoprotein reductase] + 2 H2O + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) protein found in plants.
CC   -!- The 3',5'-dihydroxyflavanone is formed via the 3'-hydroxyflavanone.
CC   -!- In Petunia hybrida the enzyme acts on naringenin, eriodictyol,
CC       dihydroquercetin (taxifolin) and dihydrokaempferol (aromadendrin).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the hydroxylation of 5,7,4'-trihydroxyflavanone
CC       (naringenin) at either the 3' position to form eriodictyol or at both
CC       the 3' and 5' positions to form 5,7,3',4',5'-pentahydroxyflavanone
CC       (dihydrotricetin).
CC   -!- The enzyme also catalyzes the hydroxylation of
CC       3,5,7,3',4'-pentahydroxyflavanone (taxifolin) at the 5' position,
CC       forming ampelopsin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.88.
