ID   1.14.14.172
DE   3,5,6-trichloropyridin-2-ol monooxygenase.
CA   (1) 3,5,6-trichloropyridin-2-ol + FADH2 + O2 = 3,6-dichloropyridine-2,5-
CA   dione + FAD + chloride + H2O + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) 3,6-dichloropyridine-2,5-diol + FADH2 + O2 = 6-chloro-3-
CA   hydroxypyridine-2,5-dione + FAD + chloride + H2O + 2 H(+).
CA   (3) 6-chloropyridine-2,3,5-triol + FADH2 + O2 = 3,6-dihydroxypyridine-
CA   2,5-dione + FAD + chloride + H2O + 3 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from a number of bacterial species,
CC       participates in the degradation of 3,5,6-trichloropyridin-2-ol (TCP),
CC       a metabolite of the common organophosphorus insecticide chlorpyrifos.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a multifunctional flavin-dependent monooxygenase that
CC       displaces three chlorine atoms by attacking three different positions
CC       in the substrate.
CC   -!- Each reaction catalyzed by the enzyme displaces a single chlorine and
CC       results in formation of a dione, which must be reduced by FADH2
CC       before the monooxygenase could catalyze the next step.
CC   -!- The large amount of FADH2 that is required is generated by a
CC       dedicated flavin reductase (TcpX). cf. EC 1.14.14.173.
//
ID   1.14.14.173
DE   2,4,6-trichlorophenol monooxygenase.
CA   2,4,6-trichlorophenol + FADH2 + O2 = 2-chloro-6-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone
CA   + FAD + 2 chloride + 3 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Cupriavidus pinatubonensis,
CC       participates in the degradation of 2,4,6-trichlorophenol, a compound
CC       that has been used for decades as a wood preservative.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a multifunctional flavin-dependent monooxygenase that
CC       catalyzes two different reactions to displace two chlorine atoms,
CC       a monooxygenase reaction followed by a hydrolysis reaction that takes
CC       advantage of the reactivity of the product of the first reaction,
CC       2,6-dichloro-1,4-benzoquinone.
CC   -!- The large amount of FADH2 that is required is generated by a
CC       dedicated flavin reductase (TcpB). cf. EC 1.14.14.172.
DR   Q471I2, TCPA_CUPPJ ;
//
