CA   (1) narbomycin + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + O2 + 2 H(+) =
CA   pikromycin + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + H2O.
CA   (2) narbomycin + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + O2 + 2 H(+) =
CA   neopikromycin + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + H2O.
CA   (3) narbomycin + 4 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 O2 + 4 H(+) =
CA   novapikromycin + 4 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 H2O.
CA   (4) 10-deoxymethymycin + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + O2 + 2 H(+) =
CA   methymycin + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + H2O.
CA   (5) 10-deoxymethymycin + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + O2 + 2 H(+) =
CA   neomethymycin + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + H2O.
CA   (6) 10-deoxymethymycin + 4 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 O2 + 4 H(+)
CA   = novamethymycin + 4 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) protein.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of a number of bacterial macrolide
CC       antibiotics containing a desosamine glycoside unit.
CC   -!- With narbomycin it hydroxylates at either C-12 to give pikromycin or
CC       C-14 to give neopikromycin or both positions to give narvopikromycin.
CC   -!- With 10-deoxymethymycin it hydroxylates at either C-10 to give
CC       methymycin or C-12 to give neomethymycin or both positions to give
CC       novamethymycin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.185.
