ID   1.14.19.4
DE   acyl-lipid (11-3)-desaturase.
AN   acyl-lipid 8-desaturase.
AN   Delta(8)-desaturase.
AN   SLD.
CA   (1) an (11Z,14Z)-icosadienoyl-containing glycerolipid + 2 Fe(II)-
CA   [cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = an (8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosatrienoyl-containing
CA   glycerolipid + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.
CA   (2) an (11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosatrienoyl-containing glycerolipid + 2 Fe(II)-
CA   [cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = an (8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-
CA   containing glycerolipid + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the protist Euglena gracilis and the
CC       microalga Rebecca salina, introduces a cis double bond at the
CC       8-position in 20-carbon fatty acids that are incorporated into a
CC       glycerolipid and have an existing Delta(11) desaturation.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a front-end desaturase, introducing the new double bond
CC       between the pre-existing double bond and the carboxyl-end of the
CC       fatty acid.
CC   -!- It contains a cytochrome b5 domain that acts as the direct electron
CC       donor to the active site of the desaturase, and does not require an
CC       external cytochrome.
CC   -!- Involved in alternative pathways for the biosynthesis of the
CC       polyunsaturated fatty acids arachidonate and icosapentaenoate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.19.n1.
DR   Q9SWQ9, SLD1_EUGGR ;
//
ID   1.14.19.5
DE   acyl-CoA 11-(Z)-desaturase.
AN   Delta(11) desaturase.
AN   Delta(11)-fatty-acid desaturase.
AN   Delta(11)-palmitoyl-CoA desaturase.
AN   fatty acid Delta(11)-desaturase.
AN   Z/E11-desaturase.
CA   an 11,12-saturated fatty acyl-CoA + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + O2 +
CA   2 H(+) = an (11Z)-Delta(11)-fatty acyl-CoA + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] +
CA   2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme introduces a cis double bond at position C-11 of saturated
CC       fatty acyl-CoAs.
CC   -!- In moths the enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of their sex
CC       pheromones.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the marine microalga Thalassiosira pseudonana is
CC       specific for palmitoyl-CoA (16:0), that from the leafroller moth
CC       Choristoneura rosaceana desaturates myristoyl-CoA (14:0), while that
CC       from the moth Spodoptera littoralis accepts both substrates.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains three histidine boxes that are conserved in all
CC       desaturases.
CC   -!- It is membrane-bound, and contains a cytochrome b5-like domain at the
CC       N-terminus that serves as the electron donor for the active site of
CC       the desaturase.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.19.n2 and EC 1.14.99.32.
DR   Q8ISS3, ACO11_CHORO;  Q6US81, ACO11_SPOLI;  O44390, ACO11_TRINI;
DR   Q75PL7, DESAT_BOMMO;
//
