CC       reinhardtii, is a front-end desaturase that introduces a cis double
CC       bond in omega(9) unsaturated C18 or C20 fatty acids incorporated into
CC       lipids, at a position 4 carbon atoms from the existing omega(9) bond,
CC       toward the carboxy end of the fatty acid (at the omega(13) position).
CC   -!- When acting on 20:2Delta(11,14) and 20:3Delta(11,14,17) substrates it
CC       introduces the new double bond between carbons 7 and 8.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a cytochrome b5 domain that acts as the direct
CC       electron donor for the active site of the desaturase.
