DE   sphingolipid 8-(E)-desaturase.
AN   8 fatty acid desaturase.
AN   8-sphingolipid desaturase.
CA   an N-acylsphing-4-enine + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) =
CA   a (4E,8E)-4-sphinga-4,8-dienine ceramide + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] +
CA   2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the yeasts Kluyveromyces lactis and
CC       Candida albicans and from the diatom Thalassiosira pseudonana,
CC       introduces a trans double bond at the 8-position of sphingoid bases
CC       in sphingolipids.
CC   -!- The enzyme determines the position of the double bond by its distance
CC       from the alcohol end of the sphingoid base, and contains a cytochrome
CC       b5 domain that acts as the direct electron donor to the active site
CC       of the desaturase.
CC   -!- The homologous enzymes from higher plants, EC 1.14.19.29, act on
CC       phytosphinganine (4-hydroxysphinganine) and produces a mixture of
CC       trans and cis isomers.
