CA   (1) an (8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosatrienoyl-containing glycerolipid + 2 Fe(II)-
CA   [cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-
CA   containing glycerolipid + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O.
CA   (2) an (8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-containing glycerolipid +
CA   2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = a (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-
CA   eicosapentaenoyl-containing glycerolipid + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] +
CA   2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has been characterized from multiple organisms
CC       including the moss Physcomitrella patens, the marine microalga
CC       Rebecca salina, and the filamentous fungus Mortierella alpina,
CC       introduces a cis double bond at the 5-position in 20-carbon
CC       polyunsaturated fatty acids incorporated in a glycerolipid that
CC       contain a Delta(8) double bond.
