CC   -!- The enzyme introduces a cis double bond at carbon 5 of acyl-CoAs that
CC       contain a double bond at position 8.
CC   -!- The enzymes from algae, mosses, mammals and the protozoan Leishmania
CC       major catalyze the desaturation of dihomo-gamma-linoleate
CC       ((8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosa-8,11,14-trienoate) and (8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-
CC       8,11,14,17-tetraenoate to generate arachidonate and
CC       (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-5,8,11,14,17-pentaenoate, respectively.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a cytochrome b5 domain that acts as the direct
CC       electron donor to the desaturase active site and does not require an
CC       external cytochrome. cf. EC 1.14.19.37.
DR   B2KKL4, FAD1_SIGCA ;  D8X2C5, FAD2_SIGCA ;  O60427, FADS1_HUMAN;
DR   Q920L1, FADS1_MOUSE;  A4UVI1, FADS1_PAPAN;  Q920R3, FADS1_RAT  ;
DR   Q9DEX7, FADS2_DANRE;  G5EG11, FAT4_CAEEL ;
