ID   1.14.19.45
DE   sn-1 oleoyl-lipid 12-desaturase.
CA   a 1-[(9Z)-octadecenoyl]-2-acyl-glycerolipid + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-
CA   [ferredoxin] + O2 + 2 H(+) = a 1-[(9Z,12Z)-octadecdienoyl]-2-acyl-
CA   glycerolipid + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from cyanobacteria, introduces a cis double
CC       bond at carbon 12 of oleoyl groups (18:1) attached to the sn-1
CC       position of glycerolipids.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a methyl-end desaturase, introducing the new double
CC       bond between a pre-existing double bond and the methyl-end of the
CC       fatty acid.
CC   -!- It is non-specific with respect to the polar head group of the
CC       glycerolipid.
DR   Q79F72, DESA_ANAVA ;  Q54794, DESA_LIMPL ;  Q55231, DESA_PICP2 ;
DR   P20388, DESA_SYNY3 ;  Q55230, DESA_SYNY4 ;
