CC       C4a-hydroperoxyflavin, which then reacts with chloride to produce a
CC       hypochlorite ion.
CC   -!- The latter reacts with an active site lysine to generate a
CC       chloramine, which chlorinates the substrate. Cf. EC 1.14.19.9 and
