ID   1.14.19.78
DE   decanoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] acetylenase.
CA   decanoyl-[ACP] + 4 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 O2 + 4 H(+) = dec-9-
CA   ynoyl-[ACP] + 4 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 4 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Teredinibacter turnerae,
CC       is specific for decanoyl-[acyl-carrier protein].
CC   -!- Activity is maximal when decanoate is loaded onto a dedicated acyl-
CC       carrier protein (TtuC), which is encoded by a gene in the same
CC       operon.
DR   C5BK13, TTUB_TERTT ;
//
ID   1.14.19.79
DE   3beta,22alpha-dihydroxysteroid 3-dehydrogenase.
AN   CYP90A1.
CA   (1) (22S)-22-hydroxycampesterol + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase]
CA   + O2 = (22S)-22-hydroxycampest-4-en-3-one + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase] + 2 H2O + H(+).
CA   (2) 6-deoxoteasterone + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O2 =
CA   3-dehydro-6-deoxoteasterone + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   2 H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- This cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) enzyme, characterized from the
CC       plant Arabidopsis thaliana, catalyzes C-3 dehydrogenation of all
CC       3beta-hydroxy brassinosteroid synthesis intermediates with
CC       22-hydroxylated or 2(2),2(3)-dihydroxylated side chains.
DR   Q42569, C90A1_ARATH;  I1IUJ6, C90A1_BRADI;
//
ID   1.14.19.80
DE   (19E)-geissoschizine oxidase.
AN   CYP71D1V1.
CA   (19E)-geissoschizine + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O2 =
CA   akuammicine + formate + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H2O +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- A cytochrome P450 (heme-thiolate) enzyme characterized from the plant
CC       Catharanthus roseus (Madagascar periwinkle), that participates in the
CC       biosynthesis of a number of monoterpene alkaloids, as well as the
CC       bisindole alkaloids vinblastine and vincristine.
CC   -!- The enzyme generates a nine-carbon ring that contains a nitrogen
CC       atom.
CC   -!- The direct product of the enzyme, 3,17-didehydrostemmadenine,
CC       is unstable, and in the absence of other enzymes becomes akuammicine
CC       non-enzymically.
CC   -!- However, in the presence of two dehydrogenases it is converted to
CC       stemmadenine via 17-dehydrostemmadenine.
DR   A0A9E7S4M4, GO_ALSSC   ;  I1TEM0, GO_CATRO   ;  P0DO79, GO_STRNX   ;
DR   P0DO88, GO_STRYX   ;  A0A9E7S4M3, RHS_ALSSC  ;
//
