ID   1.14.99.48
DE   heme oxygenase (staphylobilin-producing).
AN   heme oxidase.
AN   heme oxygenase.
AN   heme oxygenase (decyclizing).
CA   (1) heme b + 5 AH2 + 4 O2 + 2 H(+) = delta-staphylobilin + Fe(2+) +
CA   formaldehyde + 5 A + 4 H2O.
CA   (2) heme b + 5 AH2 + 4 O2 + 2 H(+) = beta-staphylobilin + Fe(2+) +
CA   formaldehyde + 5 A + 4 H2O.
CC   -!- This enzyme, which is found in some pathogenic bacteria, is involved
CC       in an iron acquisition system that catabolizes the host's hemoglobin.
CC   -!- The two enzymes from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus, encoded by
CC       the isdG and isdI genes, produce 67.5 % and 56.2 % delta-
CC       staphylobilin, respectively.
