ID   1.16.1.8
DE   [methionine synthase] reductase.
AN   [methionine synthase]-cobalamin methyltransferase (cob(II)alamin
AN   reducing).
AN   methionine synthase cob(II)alamin reductase (methylating).
AN   methionine synthase reductase.
CA   2 methylcob(III)alamin-[methionine synthase] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + NADP(+) + H(+) = 2 cob(II)alamin-[methionine synthase] +
CA   2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine + NADPH.
CC   -!- The substrate of the enzyme is the inactivated cobalt(II) form of
CC       EC 2.1.1.13.
CC   -!- Electrons are transferred from NADPH to FAD to FMN.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.135.
DR   Q4JIJ2, MTRR_BOVIN ;  Q17574, MTRR_CAEEL ;  Q9UBK8, MTRR_HUMAN ;
DR   Q8C1A3, MTRR_MOUSE ;  Q498R1, MTRR_RAT   ;
//
ID   1.16.1.9
DE   ferric-chelate reductase (NADPH).
AN   ferric chelate reductase.
AN   iron chelate reductase.
AN   NADPH:Fe(3+)-EDTA reductase.
CA   2 a Fe(II)-siderophore + NADP(+) + H(+) = 2 a Fe(III)-siderophore +
CA   NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is widespread among bacteria, catalyzes the
CC       reduction of ferric iron bound to a variety of iron chelators
CC       (siderophores), including ferric triscatecholates and ferric
CC       dicitrate, resulting in the release of ferrous iron.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli has the highest
CC       efficiency with the hydrolyzed ferric enterobactin complex ferric
CC       N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine. cf. EC 1.16.1.7 and EC 1.16.1.10.
DR   Q5A446, FRE1_CANAL ;  P32791, FRE1_YEAST ;  P36033, FRE2_YEAST ;
DR   Q08905, FRE3_YEAST ;  P53746, FRE4_YEAST ;  Q08908, FRE5_YEAST ;
DR   Q12473, FRE6_YEAST ;  A6ZN61, FRE7_YEAS7 ;  Q12333, FRE7_YEAST ;
DR   Q04800, FRP1_SCHPO ;  O94727, FRP2_SCHPO ;  Q2U6T7, KAP2_ASPOR ;
DR   Q46871, YQJH_ECOLI ;
//
ID   1.16.1.10
DE   ferric-chelate reductase [NAD(P)H].
AN   ferric reductase.
CA   (1) 2 a Fe(II)-siderophore + NAD(+) + H(+) = 2 a Fe(III)-siderophore +
CA   NADH.
CA   (2) 2 a Fe(II)-siderophore + NADP(+) + H(+) = 2 a Fe(III)-siderophore +
CA   NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reduction of bound ferric iron in a variety
CC       of iron chelators (siderophores), resulting in the release of ferrous
CC       iron.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the hyperthermophilic archaeon Archaeoglobus fulgidus
CC       is not active with uncomplexed Fe(III). cf. EC 1.16.1.7 and
CC       EC 1.16.1.9.
DR   A0A1E3M8P2, BAUF_ACIBA ;  O29428, FERCR_ARCFU;  A0A1W7HCY1, IUTB_VIBVL ;
//
ID   1.16.2.1
DE   iron--cytochrome-c reductase.
AN   iron-cytochrome c reductase.
CA   Fe(3+) + Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] = Fe(2+) + Fe(III)-[cytochrome c].
CC   -!- The MtrC and OmcA proteins of the bacterium Shewanella oneidensis
CC       MR-1 are decaheme c-type cytochromes that reduce iron oxides
CC       extracellularly, passing the electrons to MtrA, another decaheme
CC       c-type cytochrome located in the periplasm.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.9.98.1.
//
