ID   1.17.1.5
DE   nicotinate dehydrogenase.
AN   nicotinate hydroxylase.
AN   nicotinic acid hydroxylase.
CA   nicotinate + NADP(+) + H2O = 6-hydroxynicotinate + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is capable of acting on a variety of nicotinate analogs to
CC       varying degrees, including pyrazine-2-carboxylate, pyrazine 2,3-
CC       dicarboxylate, trigonelline and 6-methylnicotinate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Clostridium barkeri also possesses a catalytically
CC       essential, labile selenium that can be removed by reaction with
CC       cyanide.
CC   -!- Forms part of the nicotinate-fermentation catabolism pathway in
CC       Eubacterium barkeri.
CC   -!- Other enzymes involved in this pathway are EC 1.3.7.1, EC 3.5.2.18,
CC       EC 1.1.1.291, EC 5.4.99.4, EC 5.3.3.6, EC 4.2.1.85 and EC 4.1.3.32.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.5.1.13.
DR   Q0QLF4, NDFS_EUBBA ;  Q0QLF2, NDLMS_EUBBA;  Q0QLF1, NDMMS_EUBBA;
DR   Q0QLF3, NDSFS_EUBBA;
