ID   1.17.1.8
DE   4-hydroxy-tetrahydrodipicolinate reductase.
AN   dihydrodipicolinate reductase.
CA   (1) (S)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate + NAD(+) + H2O = (2S,4S)-4-
CA   hydroxy-2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate + NADH + H(+).
CA   (2) (S)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate + NADP(+) + H2O = (2S,4S)-4-
CA   hydroxy-2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate + NADPH + H(+).
CC   -!- The substrate of the enzyme was initially thought to be (S)-2,3-
CC       dihydrodipicolinate, and the enzyme was classified accordingly as
CC       EC 1.3.1.26.
CC   -!- Later studies of the enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli have
CC       suggested that the actual substrate of the enzyme is (2S,4S)-4-
CC       hydroxy-2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate, and that its activity
CC       includes a dehydration step, and thus the enzyme has been
CC       reclassified as 4-hydroxy-tetrahydrodipicolinate reductase.
CC   -!- However, the identity of the substrate is still controversial,
CC       as more recently it has been suggested that it may be (S)-2,3-
CC       dihydrodipicolinate after all.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.1.26.
