ID   1.17.7.3
DE   (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-enyl-diphosphate synthase (flavodoxin).
AN   (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-enyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate synthase.
CA   (2E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-enyl diphosphate + oxidized [flavodoxin] +
CA   H2O + 2 H(+) = 2-C-methyl-D-erythritol 2,4-cyclic diphosphate + reduced
CA   [flavodoxin].
CC   -!- Forms part of an alternative non-mevalonate pathway for isoprenoid
CC       biosynthesis that is found in most bacteria.
CC   -!- Plants and cyanobacteria have a similar enzyme that utilizes
CC       ferredoxin rather than flavodoxin (cf. EC 1.17.7.1).
