ID   1.17.9.1
DE   4-methylphenol dehydrogenase (hydroxylating).
AN   4-cresol dehydrogenase (hydroxylating).
AN   p-cresol-(acceptor) oxidoreductase (hydroxylating).
AN   p-cresol methylhydroxylase.
CA   4-methylphenol + 4 oxidized [azurin] + H2O = 4 reduced [azurin] +
CA   4-hydroxybenzaldehyde + 4 H(+).
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme contains a flavin (FAD) subunit and a
CC       cytochrome c subunit.
CC   -!- The flavin subunit abstracts two hydrogen atoms from the substrate,
CC       forming a quinone methide intermediate, then hydrates the latter at
CC       the benzylic carbon with a hydroxyl group derived from water.
CC   -!- The protons are lost to the bulk solvent, while the electrons are
CC       passed to the heme on the cytochrome subunit, and from there to
CC       azurin, a small copper-binding protein that is co-localized with the
CC       enzyme in the periplasm.
CC   -!- The first hydroxylation forms 4-hydroxybenzyl alcohol; a second
CC       hydroxylation converts this into 4-hydroxybenzaldehyde.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.17.99.1.
DR   P09788, DH4C_PSEPU ;
//
ID   1.17.9.2
DE   (+)-pinoresinol hydroxylase.
AN   pinoresinol alpha-hydroxylase.
CA   (+)-pinoresinol + 2 oxidized [azurin] + H2O = (+)-6-hydroxypinoresinol +
CA   2 reduced [azurin] + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Contains FAD.
CC   -!- This enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp SG-MS2,
CC       catalyzes the incorporation of an oxygen atom originating from a
CC       water molecule into position C-6 of the lignan (+)-pinoresinol.
CC   -!- The enzyme consists of a flavoprotein subunit and a c-type cytochrome
CC       subunit.
CC   -!- Electrons that originate in the substrate are transferred via the FAD
CC       cofactor and the cytochrome subunit to the blue-copper protein
CC       azurin.
//
ID   1.17.98.1
DE   Transferred entry: 1.1.1.395.
//
ID   1.17.98.2
DE   bacteriochlorophyllide c C-7(1)-hydroxylase.
CA   a bacteriochlorophyllide c + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine + H2O =
CA   a bacteriochlorophyllide e + 2 5'-deoxyadenosine + 2 L-methionine +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae), is a
CC       radical S-adenosyl-L-methionine (AdoMet) enzyme.
CC   -!- It catalyzes two consecutive hydroxylation reactions of the C-7
CC       methyl group of bacteriochlorophyllide c to form a geminal diol
CC       intermediate that spontaneously dehydrates to produce the formyl
CC       group of bacteriochlorophyllide e.
DR   N0DKX5, BCID_CHLLM ;
//
ID   1.17.98.3
DE   formate dehydrogenase (coenzyme F420).
AN   coenzyme F420-dependent formate dehydrogenase.
AN   coenzyme F420 reducing formate dehydrogenase.
CA   oxidized coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + formate + 2 H(+) = reduced
CA   coenzyme F420-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme from methanogenic archaea is a involved in formate-
CC       dependent H2 production.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.99.9.
DR   Q6LXQ1, FDHA1_METMP;  F1SVN3, FDHA2_METMP;  P06131, FDHA_METFO ;
