ID   1.17.99.9
DE   heme a synthase.
CA   Fe(II)-heme o + 2 A + H2O = Fe(II)-heme a + 2 AH2.
CC   -!- Contains a heme b cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the conversion of heme o to heme a by two
CC       successive hydroxylations of the methyl group at C-8, using water as
CC       the oxygen source.
CC   -!- The first hydroxylation forms heme i, the second hydroxylation
CC       results in an unstable dihydroxymethyl group, which spontaneously
CC       dehydrates, resulting in the formyl group of heme a.
CC   -!- The electrons produced by the reaction are transferred to a heme b
CC       cofactor.
CC   -!- However, the electron acceptor that is used to restore the heme b
CC       cofactor to its oxidized state is still not known (both a
CC       thioredoxin-like protein and menaquinol have been proposed).
