//
ID   1.17.99.10
DE   steroid C-25 hydroxylase.
AN   cholesterol C-25 dehydrogenase.
AN   steroid C-25 dehydrogenase.
CA   cholest-4-en-3-one + A + H2O = 25-hydroxycholest-4-en-3-one + AH2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Sterolibacterium
CC       denitrificans, participates in the anaerobic degradation of
CC       cholesterol.
CC   -!- The enzyme can accept several substrates including vitamin D3.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a bis(guanylyl molybdopterin) cofactor, five
CC       [Fe-S] clusters, and one heme b. cf. EC 1.14.99.38.
//
ID   1.17.99.11
DE   3-oxo-Delta(1)-steroid hydratase/dehydrogenase.
CA   a 3-oxo-Delta(1)-steroid + A + H2O = a steroid 1,3-dione + AH2.
CC   -!- A molybdenum enzyme.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Steroidobacter
CC       denitrificans, is involved in the anaetrobic degradation of steroids.
CC   -!- It is specific to 3-oxo-Delta(1)-steroids such as androsta-1-ene-
CC       3,17-dione and Delta(1)-dihydrotestosterone and does not act on
CC       3-oxo-Delta(4)-steroids.
//
ID   1.18.1.1
DE   rubredoxin--NAD(+) reductase.
AN   dihydronicotinamide adenine dinucleotide-rubredoxin reductase.
AN   NADH-rubredoxin oxidoreductase.
AN   NADH-rubredoxin reductase.
AN   reduced nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide-rubredoxin reductase.
AN   rubredoxin-NAD reductase.
AN   rubredoxin-nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide reductase.
AN   rubredoxin reductase.
CA   2 reduced [rubredoxin] + NAD(+) + H(+) = 2 oxidized [rubredoxin] + NADH.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Clostridium acetobutylicum reduces rubredoxin,
CC       ferricyanide and dichlorophenolindophenol, but not ferredoxin or
CC       flavodoxin.
CC   -!- The reaction does not occur when NADPH is substituted for NADH.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.7.2.
DR   Q9AL95, NROR_CLOAB ;  P42454, RURE_ACIAD ;  Q0VTB0, RURE_ALCBS ;
DR   P17052, RURE_ECTOL ;  Q9HTK9, RURE_PSEAE ;  Q9L4M8, RURE_PSEPU ;
//
ID   1.18.1.2
DE   ferredoxin--NADP(+) reductase.
CA   2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + NADP(+) + H(+) = 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-
CA   [ferredoxin] + NADPH.
CC   -!- In chloroplasts and cyanobacteria the enzyme acts on plant-type [2Fe-
CC       2S] ferredoxins, but in other bacteria it can also reduce bacterial
CC       2[4Fe-4S] ferredoxins and flavodoxin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.7.1 and EC 1.6.99.4.
