ID   1.18.6.1
DE   nitrogenase.
CA   N2 + 8 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 16 ATP + 16 H2O = H2 + 8 oxidized
CA   [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 NH4(+) + 16 ADP + 16 phosphate + 6 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is a complex of two components (namely dinitrogen
CC       reducatse and dinitrogenase).
CC   -!- Dinitrogen reductase is a [4Fe-4S] protein, which, in the presence of
CC       two molecules of ATP, transfers an electron from ferredoxin to the
CC       dinitrogenase component.
CC   -!- Dinitrogenase is a molybdenum-iron protein that reduces dinitrogen to
CC       two molecules of ammonia in three successive two-electron reductions
CC       via diazene and hydrazine.
CC   -!- The reduction is initiated by formation of hydrogen in stoichiometric
CC       amounts.
CC   -!- Acetylene is reduced to ethylene (but only very slowly to ethane),
CC       azide to nitrogen and ammonia, and cyanide to methane and ammonia.
CC   -!- In the absence of a suitable substrate, hydrogen is slowly formed.
CC   -!- Ferredoxin may be replaced by flavodoxin (see EC 1.19.6.1).
CC   -!- The enzyme does not reduce CO (cf. EC 1.18.6.2).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.18.2.1.
