ID   1.20.4.4
DE   arsenate reductase (thioredoxin).
CA   arsenate + [thioredoxin]-dithiol + H(+) = arsenite + [thioredoxin]-
CA   disulfide + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized in bacteria of the Firmicutes phylum,
CC       is specific for thioredoxin.
CC   -!- It has no activity with glutaredoxin (cf. EC 1.20.4.1).
CC   -!- Although the arsenite formed is more toxic than arsenate, it can be
CC       extruded from some bacteria by EC 7.3.2.7; in other organisms,
CC       arsenite can be methylated by EC 2.1.1.137 in a pathway that produces
CC       non-toxic organoarsenical compounds.
CC   -!- The enzyme also has the activity of EC 3.1.3.48.
