ID   1.21.3.6
DE   aureusidin synthase.
CA   (1) 2',4,4',6'-tetrahydroxychalcone 4'-O-beta-D-glucoside + O2 =
CA   aureusidin 6-O-beta-glucoside + H2O.
CA   (2) 2 2',3,4,4',6'-pentahydroxychalcone 4'-O-beta-D-glucoside + O2 +
CA   2 H(+) = 2 aureusidin 6-O-beta-glucoside + 2 H2O.
CA   (3) 2',3,4,4',6'-pentahydroxychalcone 4'-O-beta-D-glucoside + O2 + H(+) =
CA   bracteatin 6-O-beta-glucoside + H2O.
CC   -!- Plays a key role in the yellow coloration of flowers such as
CC       Antirrhinum majus (snapdragon).
CC   -!- The enzyme is a homolog of plant polyphenol oxidase and catalyzes two
CC       separate chemical transformations, i.e. 3-hydroxylation and oxidative
CC       cyclization (2',-dehydrogenation).
CC   -!- H2O2 activates reaction (1) but inhibits reaction (2).
CC   -!- Originally considered to act on the phenol but now thought to mainly
CC       act on the 4'-O-beta-glucoside in vivo.
DR   Q9FRX6, AS1_ANTMA  ;
//
ID   1.21.3.7
DE   tetrahydrocannabinolic acid synthase.
AN   Delta(1)-tetrahydrocannabinolic acid synthase.
AN   THCA synthase.
CA   cannabigerolate + O2 = Delta(9)-tetrahydrocannabinolate + H2O2.
CC   -!- The cofactor is covalently bound.
CC   -!- Part of the cannabinoids biosynthetic pathway in the plant Cannabis
CC       sativa.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also convert cannabinerolate (the (Z)-isomer of
CC       cannabigerolate) to Delta(9)-THCA with lower efficiency.
CC   -!- The traditional numbering called Delta(9)-tetrahydrocannabinolate,
CC       Delta(1)-tetrahydrocannabinolate.
CC   -!- Systematic peripheral numbering is now recommended.
DR   Q8GTB6, THCAS_CANSA;
//
ID   1.21.3.8
DE   cannabidiolic acid synthase.
AN   CBDA synthase.
CA   cannabigerolate + O2 = cannabidiolate + H2O2.
CC   -!- Part of the cannabinoids biosynthetic pathway of the plant Cannabis
CC       sativa.
