ID   1.21.3.11
DE   precondylocarpine acetate synthase.
CA   O-acetyl-15alpha-stemmadenine + O2 = precondylocarpine acetate + H2O2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Catharanthus roseus
CC       (Madagascar periwinkle), participates in a pathway that leads to the
CC       production of a number of monoterpene alkaloids, as well as the
CC       bisindole alkaloids vinblastine and vincristine, which are used as
CC       anticancer drugs.
CC   -!- The enzyme is similar to berberine bridge enzymes such as EC 1.21.3.3
CC       and requires an FAD cofactor.
DR   A0A2S1XB67, ASO_CATRO  ;  A0A5B8X6A1, PAS1_TABIB ;  A0A5B8X7E6, PAS2_TABIB ;
