ID   1.21.4.5
DE   tetrachlorohydroquinone reductive dehalogenase.
CA   (1) 2,6-dichlorohydroquinone + glutathione disulfide + chloride + H(+) =
CA   2,3,6-trichlorohydroquinone + 2 glutathione.
CA   (2) 2,3,6-trichlorohydroquinone + glutathione disulfide + chloride =
CA   2,3,5,6-tetrachlorohydroquinone + 2 glutathione.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Sphingobium
CC       chlorophenolicum, converts tetrachlorohydroquinone to 2,6-
CC       dichlorohydroquinone in two steps, via 2,3,6-trichlorohydroquinone,
CC       using glutathione as the reducing agent.
CC   -!- The enzyme is sensitive to oxidation - when an internal L-cysteine
CC       residue is oxidized, the enzyme produces 2,3,5-trichloro-6-
CC       (glutathion-S-yl)-hydroquinone and 2,6-dichloro-3-(glutathion-S-yl)-
CC       hydroquinone instead of its normal products.
