ID   1.21.98.2
DE   dichlorochromopyrrolate synthase.
CA   2 3-(7-chloroindol-3-yl)-2-iminopropanoate + H2O2 =
CA   dichlorochromopyrrolate + NH4(+) + 2 H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a step in the biosynthesis of rebeccamycin,
CC       an indolocarbazole alkaloid produced by the bacterium Lechevalieria
CC       aerocolonigenes.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a dimeric heme-protein oxidase that catalyzes the
CC       oxidative dimerization of two L-tryptophan-derived molecules to form
CC       dichlorochromopyrrolic acid, the precursor for the fused six-ring
CC       indolocarbazole scaffold of rebeccamycin.
CC   -!- In vivo the enzyme uses hydrogen peroxide, formed by the enzyme
CC       upstream in the biosynthetic pathway (EC 1.4.3.23) as the electron
CC       acceptor.
CC   -!- However, the enzyme is also able to catalyze the reaction using
CC       molecular oxygen.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.21.3.9 and EC 4.3.1.26.
DR   Q8KHV6, REBD_LENAE ;
