ID   1.21.99.5
DE   tetrachloroethene reductive dehalogenase.
AN   tetrachloroethene reductase.
CA   trichloroethene + chloride + A + H(+) = tetrachloroethene + AH2.
CC   -!- This enzyme allows the common pollutant tetrachloroethene to support
CC       bacterial growth and is responsible for disposal of a number of
CC       chlorinated hydrocarbons by this organism.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in the reverse direction.
CC   -!- The enzyme also reduces trichloroethene to dichloroethene.
CC   -!- Although the physiological reductant is unknown, the supply of
CC       reductant in some organisms is via reduced menaquinone, itself formed
CC       from molecular hydrogen, via EC 1.12.5.1.
