ID   1.97.1.13
DE   aliphatic sulfonate oxidoreductase.
CA   an aliphatic sulfonate + 4 oxidized [4Fe-4S]-[ferredoxin] + 2 H2O =
CA   4 reduced [4Fe-4S]-[ferredoxin] + a carboxylate + sulfite + 6 H(+).
CC   -!- An oxygen-sensitive enzyme that contains tungsten-molybdopterin and
CC       iron-sulfur clusters, isolated the hyperthermophilic archaeon
CC       Pyrococcus furiosus.
CC   -!- In that organism the enzyme is heterodimeric, comprising a catalytic
CC       subunit that contains the active site tungsto-bispyranopterin
CC       cofactor and a [4Fe-4S] cluster and an electron-transfer subunit that
CC       contains four additional [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- The activity involves two steps: an oxidative desulfonation reaction,
CC       followed by the activation of a second water molecule and oxidation
CC       of the resulting aldehyde (cf. EC 1.2.7.5).
DR   E7FHH1, ASOR_PYRFU ;
//
ID   1.97.1.14
DE   selenate reductase (quinol).
CA   selenite + a quinone + H2O = selenate + a quinol.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mesobacillus
CC       selenatarsenatis, is a membrane anchored type I molybdoenzyme.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a complex comprising three heterologous subunits that
CC       contains a guanylyl molybdenum cofactor and multiple iron-sulfur
CC       clusters.
CC   -!- The enzyme receives electrons directly from the membrane quinol pool
CC       and reduces selenate to selenite.
DR   A0A0A8X0K1, SRDA_MESS1 ;  A0A0A8X5N4, SRDB_MESS1 ;  A0A0A8X338, SRDC_MESS1 ;
//
ID   1.97.1.15
DE   2-(all-trans-polyprenyl)phenol 6-hydroxylase (prephenate).
CA   (1) a 2-(all-trans-polyprenyl)phenol + prephenate + A + H(+) = a 3-(all-
CA   trans-polyprenyl)benzene-1,2-diol + 3-phenylpyruvate + AH2 + CO2.
CA   (2) a 2-methoxy-6-(all-trans-polyprenyl)phenol + prephenate + A + H(+) =
CA   a 2-methoxy-6-(all-trans-polyprenyl)benzene-1,4-diol + 3-phenylpyruvate +
CA   AH2 + CO2.
CA   (3) a 5-methoxy-2-methyl-3-(all-trans-polyprenyl)benzene-1,4-diol +
CA   prephenate + A + H(+) = a 3-demethylubiquinol + 3-phenylpyruvate + AH2 +
CA   CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli,
CC       catalyzes three hydroxylation reactions in the oxygen-independent
CC       pathway for ubiquinone (UQ) biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The reaction involves an electron acceptor whose identity remains
CC       unknown as of 2024.
CC   -!- The Escherichia coli enzyme is a heterodimer, with both subunits
CC       containing a [4Fe-4S] cluster that is essential for activity and may
CC       serve as part of an electron transfer chain from the substrate to the
CC       unidentified electron acceptor.
DR   P45527, UBIU_ECOLI ;  P45475, UBIV_ECOLI ;
