ID   2.1.1.15
DE   fatty-acid O-methyltransferase.
CA   a fatty acid + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a fatty acid methyl ester +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- Oleic acid is the most effective fatty acid acceptor.
DR   Q9RMN9, MTF2_MYCS2 ;
//
ID   2.1.1.16
DE   methylene-fatty-acyl-phospholipid synthase.
AN   cyclopropane synthetase.
AN   unsaturated-phospholipid methyltransferase.
CA   a 1-acyl-2-(9Z)-enoyl-sn-glycero-3-phospholipid + S-adenosyl-L-methionine
CA   = a 1-acyl-2-(10-methylene)-acyl-sn-glycero-3-phospholipid + S-adenosyl-
CA   L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme transfers a methyl group to the 10-position of a Delta(9)-
CC       olefinic acyl chain in phosphatidylglycerol, phosphatidylinositol,
CC       or, more slowly, phosphatidylethanolamine; subsequent proton transfer
CC       produces a 10-methylene group (cf. EC 2.1.1.79).
//
ID   2.1.1.17
DE   phosphatidylethanolamine N-methyltransferase.
CA   a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-N-methylethanolamine + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + H(+).
