ID   2.1.1.41
DE   sterol 24-C-methyltransferase.
AN   24-sterol C-methyltransferase.
AN   Delta(24)-methyltransferase.
AN   Delta(24)-sterol methyltransferase.
AN   phytosterol methyltransferase.
AN   S-adenosyl-4-methionine:sterol Delta(24)-methyltransferase.
AN   S-adenosyl-L-methionine:Delta(24(23))-sterol methyltransferase.
AN   SMT1.
AN   zymosterol-24-methyltransferase.
CA   zymosterol + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = fecosterol + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- Acts on a range of sterols with a 24(25)-double bond in the side
CC       chain.
CC   -!- While zymosterol is the preferred substrate it also acts on
CC       desmosterol, 5alpha-cholesta-7,24-dien-3beta-ol, 5alpha-cholesta-
CC       5,7,24-trien-3beta-ol, 4alpha-methylzymosterol and others.
CC   -!- S-Adenosyl-L-methionine attacks the Si face of the 24(25) double bond
CC       and the C-24 hydrogen is transferred to C-25 on the Re face of the
CC       double bond.
