//
ID   2.1.1.46
DE   isoflavone 4'-O-methyltransferase.
CA   a 4'-hydroxyisoflavone + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a 4'-methoxyisoflavone
CA   + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the methylation of daidzein and genistein.
CC   -!- It does not methylate naringenin, apigenin, luteolin or kaempferol.
DR   Q84KK6, I4OMT_GLYEC;  Q84KK4, I4OMT_LOTJA;  Q29U70, I4OMT_MEDTR;
DR   O24305, M3OM1_PEA  ;
//
ID   2.1.1.47
DE   indolepyruvate C-methyltransferase.
AN   indolepyruvate 3-methyltransferase.
AN   indolepyruvate methyltransferase.
AN   indolepyruvic acid methyltransferase.
CA   indole-3-pyruvate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (R)-3-(indol-3-yl)-2-
CA   oxobutanoate + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces griseus,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of the antibacterial drug indolmycin.
DR   A0A0D4BS77, IND1_STRGR ;
//
ID   2.1.1.48
DE   Transferred entry: 2.1.1.181, 2.1.1.182, 2.1.1.183 and 2.1.1.184.
//
ID   2.1.1.49
DE   amine N-methyltransferase.
AN   arylamine N-methyltransferase.
AN   nicotine N-methyltransferase.
AN   tryptamine N-methyltransferase.
CA   (1) a primary amine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a methylated primary
CA   amine + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (2) a secondary amine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a methylated secondary
CA   amine + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (3) a tertiary amine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a methylated tertiary
CA   amine + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- An enzyme of very broad specificity; many primary, secondary and
CC       tertiary amines can act as acceptors, including tryptamine, aniline,
CC       nicotine and a variety of drugs and other xenobiotics.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.81.
DR   O95050, INMT_HUMAN ;  P40936, INMT_MOUSE ;  Q5RFR7, INMT_PONAB ;
DR   O97972, INMT_RABIT ;
//
ID   2.1.1.50
DE   loganate O-methyltransferase.
CA   loganate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = loganin + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- Also acts on secologanate.
CC   -!- Methylates the 11-carboxy group of the monoterpenoid loganate.
DR   B2KPR3, LAMT_CATRO ;
