//
ID   2.1.1.54
DE   deoxycytidylate C-methyltransferase.
CA   dCMP + (6R)-5,10-methylene-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate =
CA   5-methyldeoxycytidine 5'-phosphate + 7,8-dihydrofolate.
CC   -!- dCMP is methylated by formaldehyde in the presence of
CC       tetrahydrofolate.
CC   -!- CMP, dCTP and CTP can act as acceptor, more slowly.
//
ID   2.1.1.55
DE   tRNA (adenine-N(6)-)-methyltransferase.
CA   an adenosine in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = an N(6)-methyladenosine
CA   in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
//
ID   2.1.1.56
DE   mRNA (guanine-N(7))-methyltransferase.
AN   guanine-7-methyltransferase.
AN   messenger ribonucleate guanine 7-methyltransferase.
AN   messenger RNA guanine 7-methyltransferase.
CA   a 5'-end (5'-triphosphoguanosine)-ribonucleoside in mRNA + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine = a 5'-end (N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-ribonucleoside
CA   in mRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- The terminal N(7)-methylguanosine facilitates gene expression in
CC       eukaryotic cells and is recognized by cap-binding proteins.
