ID   2.1.1.69
DE   5-hydroxyfuranocoumarin 5-O-methyltransferase.
AN   bergaptol 5-O-methyltransferase.
AN   bergaptol methyltransferase.
AN   bergaptol O-methyltransferase.
AN   BMT.
AN   furanocoumarin 5-methyltransferase.
AN   furanocoumarin 5-O-methyltransferase.
CA   (1) a 5-hydroxyfurocoumarin + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   a 5-methoxyfurocoumarin + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (2) bergaptol + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = bergapten + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine.
CC   -!- Converts bergaptol into bergapten, which has therapeutic potential in
CC       the treatment of psoriasis as it has photosensitizing and
CC       antiproliferative activities.
CC   -!- Methylates the 5-hydroxy group of some hydroxy- and methylcoumarins,
CC       such as 5-hydroxyxanthotoxin, but has little activity on non-coumarin
CC       phenols; caffeate, 5-hydroxyferulate and daphnetin are not
CC       substrates.
CC   -!- Cu(2+), Zn(2+) and Co(2+) cause enzyme inhibition.
CC   -!- See also EC 2.1.1.70.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.92.
DR   Q6T1F6, BMT_AMMMJ  ;  A8J6X1, BMT_GLELI  ;  A0A166U5H3, BMT_KITPR  ;
DR   A0A4P8DY91, COMTS_KITPR;
//
ID   2.1.1.70
DE   8-hydroxyfuranocoumarin 8-O-methyltransferase.
AN   furanocoumarin 8-methyltransferase.
AN   furanocoumarin 8-O-methyl-transferase.
AN   xanthotoxol 8-O-methyltransferase.
AN   XMT.
CA   (1) an 8-hydroxyfurocoumarin + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   an 8-methoxyfurocoumarin + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (2) xanthotoxol + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = xanthotoxin + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- Converts xanthotoxol into xanthotoxin, which has therapeutic
CC       potential in the treatment of psoriasis as it has photosensitizing
CC       and antiproliferative activities.
CC   -!- Methylates the 8-hydroxy group of some hydroxy- and methylcoumarins,
CC       but has little activity on non-coumarin phenols.
CC   -!- See also EC 2.1.1.69.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.93.
DR   A0A4P8DY91, COMTS_KITPR;
//
ID   2.1.1.71
DE   phosphatidyl-N-methylethanolamine N-methyltransferase.
CA   a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-N-methylethanolamine + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine = a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-N,N-dimethylethanolamine +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- Also catalyzes the transfer of a further methylgroup, producing
CC       phosphatidylcholine.
