ID   2.1.1.74
DE   methylenetetrahydrofolate--tRNA-(uracil(54)-C(5))-methyltransferase
DE   [NAD(P)H-oxidizing].
AN   folate/FAD-dependent tRNA T54 methyltransferase.
AN   folate-dependent ribothymidyl synthase.
CA   (1) uridine(54) in tRNA + (6R)-5,10-methylene-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate +
CA   NADH + H(+) = 5-methyluridine(54) in tRNA + (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate
CA   + NAD(+).
CA   (2) uridine(54) in tRNA + (6R)-5,10-methylene-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate +
CA   NADPH + H(+) = 5-methyluridine(54) in tRNA + (6S)-5,6,7,8-
CA   tetrahydrofolate + NADP(+).
CC   -!- A flavoprotein (FAD).
CC   -!- Up to 25% of the bases in mature tRNA are post-translationally
CC       modified or hypermodified.
CC   -!- One almost universal post-translational modification is the
CC       conversion of U(54) into ribothymidine in the TPsiC loop, and this
CC       modification is found in most species studied to date.
CC   -!- Unlike this enzyme, which uses 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate and
CC       NAD(P)H to supply the atoms for methylation of U(54), EC 2.1.1.35
CC       uses S-adenosyl-L-methionine.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.2.12.
