ID   2.1.1.90
DE   methanol--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase.
AN   methanol--5-hydroxybenzimidazolylcobamide Co-methyltransferase.
CA   Co(I)-[methanol-specific corrinoid protein] + methanol + H(+) = methyl-
CA   Co(III)-[methanol-specific corrinoid protein] + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of methyl groups from
CC       methanol to a methanol-specific corrinoid protein (MtaC), is involved
CC       in methanogenesis from methanol.
CC   -!- Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to
CC       be in the Co(I) state.
CC   -!- During methylation the cobalt is oxidized to the Co(III) state.
CC   -!- Free cob(I)alamin can substitute for the corrinoid protein in vitro.
CC   -!- Inactivated by oxygen and other oxidizing agents, and reactivated by
CC       catalytic amounts of ATP and hydrogen.
DR   Q46EH3, MTAB_METBF ;
