ID   2.1.1.107
DE   uroporphyrinogen-III C-methyltransferase.
AN   adenosylmethionine-uroporphyrinogen III methyltransferase.
AN   S-adenosyl-L-methionine-dependent uroporphyrinogen III methylase.
AN   SUMT.
AN   urogen III methylase.
AN   uroporphyrin-III C-methyltransferase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen III methylase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen-III methylase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen-III methyltransferase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen methyltransferase.
CA   uroporphyrinogen III + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = precorrin-2 +
CA   2 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes two sequential methylation reactions, the first
CC       forming precorrin-1 and the second leading to the formation of
CC       precorrin-2.
CC   -!- It is the first of three steps leading to the formation of siroheme
CC       from uroporphyrinogen III.
CC   -!- The second step involves an NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation to form
CC       sirohydrochlorin from precorrin-2 (EC 1.3.1.76) and the third step
CC       involves the chelation of Fe(2+) to sirohydrochlorin to form siroheme
CC       (EC 4.99.1.4).
CC   -!- In Saccharomyces cerevisiae, the last two steps are carried out by a
CC       single bifunctional enzyme, Met8p.
CC   -!- In some bacteria, steps 1-3 are catalyzed by a single multifunctional
CC       protein called CysG, whereas in Bacillus megaterium, three separate
CC       enzymes carry out each of the steps, with SirA being responsible for
CC       the above reaction.
CC   -!- Also involved in the biosynthesis of cobalamin.
