CC       precorrin-6A.
CC   -!- The first of the four steps is carried out by EC 1.14.13.83 (CobG),
CC       yielding precorrin-3B as the product.
CC   -!- This is followed by three methylation reactions, which introduce a
CC       methyl group at C-17 (CobJ; EC 2.1.1.131), C-11 (CobM; EC 2.1.1.133)
CC       and C-1 (CobF; EC 2.1.1.152) of the macrocycle, giving rise to
CC       precorrin-4, precorrin-5, and precorrin-6A, respectively.
CC   -!- See EC 2.1.1.271 for the C(11)-methyltransferase enzyme that
CC       participates in the anaerobic cobalamin biosynthesis pathway.
