ID   2.1.1.197
DE   malonyl-[acyl-carrier protein] O-methyltransferase.
CA   malonyl-[ACP] + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = malonyl-[ACP] methyl ester +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- Involved in an early step of biotin biosynthesis in Gram-negative
CC       bacteria.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group to the omega-
CC       carboxyl group of malonyl-[acyl-carrier protein] forming a methyl
CC       ester.
CC   -!- The methyl ester is recognized by the fatty acid synthetic enzymes,
CC       which process it via the fatty acid elongation cycle to give pimelyl-
CC       [acyl-carrier-protein] methyl ester.
CC   -!- While the enzyme can also accept malonyl-CoA, it has a much higher
CC       activity with malonyl-[acyl-carrier protein].
