ID   2.1.1.200
DE   tRNA (cytidine(32)/uridine(32)-2'-O)-methyltransferase.
AN   TrMet(Xm32).
CA   (1) cytidine(32) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-
CA   methylcytidine(32) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (2) uridine(32) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-
CA   methyluridine(32) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- In Escherichia coli TrmJ is the only methyltransferase responsible
CC       for the formation of 2'-O-methylcytidine(32) in tRNA.
CC   -!- No methylation of cytosine(34) in tRNA(Leu)(CAA).
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme 2'-O-methylates cytidine(34) of tRNA(Ser1) and
CC       uridine(32) of tRNA(Gln2).
