//
ID   2.1.1.201
DE   2-methoxy-6-polyprenyl-1,4-benzoquinol methylase.
AN   COQ5.
CA   a 2-methoxy-6-(all-trans-polyprenyl)benzene-1,4-diol + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine = a 5-methoxy-2-methyl-3-(all-trans-polyprenyl)benzene-1,4-
CA   diol + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme is involved in ubiquinone biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Ubiquinones from different organisms have a different number of
CC       prenyl units (for example, ubiquinone-6 in Saccharomyces, ubiquinone-
CC       9 in rat and ubiquinone-10 in human), and thus the natural substrate
CC       for the enzymes from different organisms has a different number of
CC       prenyl units.
CC   -!- However, the enzyme usually shows a low degree of specificity
CC       regarding the number of prenyl units.
CC   -!- For example, when the COQ5 gene from Saccharomyces cerevisiae is
CC       introduced into Escherichia coli, it complements the respiratory
CC       deficiency of an ubiE mutant.
CC   -!- The bifunctional enzyme from E.coli also catalyzes the methylation of
CC       demethylmenaquinol-8 (this activity is classified as EC 2.1.1.163).
