ID   2.1.1.202
DE   multisite-specific tRNA:(cytosine-C(5))-methyltransferase.
CA   (1) cytidine(34) in tRNA precursor + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   5-methylcytidine(34) in tRNA precursor + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   H(+).
CA   (2) cytidine(40) in tRNA precursor + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   5-methylcytidine(40) in tRNA precursor + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   H(+).
CA   (3) cytidine(48) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 5-methylcytidine(48)
CA   in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (4) cytidine(49) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 5-methylcytidine(49)
CA   in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Saccharomyces cerevisiae is responsible for complete
CC       5-methylcytosine methylations of yeast tRNA.
CC   -!- The incidence of modification depends on the cytosine position in
CC       tRNA.
CC   -!- At positions 34 and 40, 5-methylcytosine is found only in two yeast
CC       tRNAs (tRNA(Leu)(CUA) and tRNA(Phe)(GAA), respectively), whereas most
CC       other elongator yeast tRNAs bear either 5-methylcytosine(48) or
CC       5-methylcytosine(49), but never both in the same tRNA molecule.
CC   -!- The formation of 5-methylcytosine(34) and 5-methylcytosine(40) is a
CC       strictly intron-dependent process, whereas the formation of
CC       5-methylcytosine(48) and 5-methylcytosine(49) is an intron-
CC       independent process.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.29.
DR   P38205, NCL1_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.1.1.203
DE   tRNA (cytosine(34)-C(5))-methyltransferase.
CA   cytidine(34) in tRNA precursor + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   5-methylcytidine(34) in tRNA precursor + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The human enzyme is specific for C(5)-methylation of cytosine(34) in
CC       tRNA precursors.
CC   -!- The intron in the human pre-tRNA(Leu)(CAA) is indispensable for the
CC       C(5)-methylation of cytosine in the first position of the anticodon.
CC   -!- It is not able to form 5-methylcytosine at positions 48 and 49 of
CC       human and yeast tRNA precursors.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.29.
DR   Q5ZLV4, NSUN2_CHICK;  Q9W4M9, NSUN2_DROME;  Q08J23, NSUN2_HUMAN;
DR   Q1HFZ0, NSUN2_MOUSE;  Q4V7N2, NSUN2_XENLA;  Q28E61, NSUN2_XENTR;
DR   Q9HGQ2, TRM4A_SCHPO;
//
ID   2.1.1.204
DE   tRNA (cytosine(38)-C(5))-methyltransferase.
CA   cytidine(38) in tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 5-methylcytidine(38) in
CA   tRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The eukaryotic enzyme catalyzes methylation of cytosine(38) in the
CC       anti-codon loop of tRNA(Asp)(GTC), tRNA(Val)(AAC) and tRNA(Gly)(GCC).
CC   -!- Methylation by Dnmt2 protects tRNAs against stress-induced cleavage
CC       by ribonuclease.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.29.
DR   P40999, PMT1M_SCHPO;  F4JWT7, TRDMT_ARATH;  Q7YS61, TRDMT_BOVIN;
DR   O14717, TRDMT_HUMAN;  O55055, TRDMT_MOUSE;  Q4G073, TRDMT_RAT  ;
DR   A0A2H1VE33, TRDMT_SPOFR;
