ID   2.1.1.215
DE   tRNA (guanine(26)-N(2)/guanine(27)-N(2))-dimethyltransferase.
CA   guanosine(26)/guanosine(27) in tRNA + 4 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N(2)-
CA   dimethylguanosine(26)/N(2)-dimethylguanosine(27) in tRNA + 4 S-adenosyl-
CA   L-homocysteine + 4 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Aquifex aeolicus is similar to the TRM1
CC       methyltransferases of archaea and eukarya (see EC 2.1.1.216).
CC   -!- However, it catalyzes the double methylation of guanines at both
CC       positions 26 and 27 of tRNA.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.32.
DR   O67010, TRM1_AQUAE ;
//
ID   2.1.1.216
DE   tRNA (guanine(26)-N(2))-dimethyltransferase.
AN   tRNA (m(2)2G26)dimethyltransferase.
CA   guanosine(26) in tRNA + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N(2)-
CA   dimethylguanosine(26) in tRNA + 2 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme dissociates from its tRNA substrate between the two
CC       consecutive methylation reactions.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 2.1.1.215, this enzyme does not catalyze the
CC       methylation of guanine(27) in tRNA.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.32.
