//
ID   2.1.1.224
DE   23S rRNA (adenine(2503)-C(8))-methyltransferase.
CA   adenosine(2503) in 23S rRNA + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] +
CA   2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 8-methyladenosine(2503) in 23S rRNA +
CA   5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- This enzyme is a member of the 'AdoMet radical' (radical SAM) family.
CC   -!- S-adenosyl-L-methionine acts as both a radical generator and as the
CC       source of the appended methyl group.
CC   -!- Cfr is an plasmid-acquired methyltransferase that protects cells from
CC       the action of antibiotics.
CC   -!- The enzyme methylates adenosine at position 2503 of 23S rRNA by a
CC       radical mechanism, transferring a CH2 group from S-adenosyl-L-
CC       methionine while retaining the hydrogen at the C-8 position of the
CC       adenine.
CC   -!- Cfr first transfers an CH2 group to a conserved cysteine (Cys(338) in
CC       Staphylococcus aureus), the generated radical from a second
CC       S-adenosyl-L-methionine then attacks the methyl group, exctracting a
CC       hydrogen.
CC   -!- The formed radical forms a covalent intermediate with the adenine
CC       group of the tRNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme will also methylate 2-methyladenine produced by the action
CC       of EC 2.1.1.192.
DR   A7Z1T2, CFR_BACVZ  ;  A7FX96, CFR_CLOB1  ;  A5I5U3, CFR_CLOBH  ;
DR   B1IL14, CFR_CLOBK  ;  A7GH77, CFR_CLOBL  ;  B1KZ37, CFR_CLOBM  ;
DR   A9KK15, CFR_LACP7  ;  Q9FBG4, CFR_MAMSC  ;  Q5WJ42, CFR_SHOC1  ;
DR   A5HBL2, CFR_STAAU  ;  A2AXI2, CFR_STAWA  ;
//
ID   2.1.1.225
DE   tRNA:m(4)X modification enzyme.
CA   (1) cytidine(4) in tRNA(Pro) + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-
CA   methylcytidine(4) in tRNA(Pro) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (2) cytidine(4) in tRNA(Gly)(GCC) + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-
CA   methylcytidine(4) in tRNA(Gly)(GCC) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CA   (3) adenosine(4) in tRNA(His) + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-
CA   methyladenosine(4) in tRNA(His) + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Saccharomyces cerevisiae 2'-O-methylates cytidine(4)
CC       in tRNA(Pro) and tRNA(Gly)(GCC), and adenosine(4) in tRNA(His).
