ID   2.1.1.230
DE   23S rRNA (adenosine(1067)-2'-O)-methyltransferase.
AN   23S rRNA A(1067) 2'-methyltransferase.
AN   nosiheptide-resistance methyltransferase.
AN   thiostrepton-resistance methylase.
CA   adenosine(1067) in 23S rRNA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2'-O-
CA   methyladenosine(1067) in 23S rRNA + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The methylase that is responsible for autoimmunity in the
CC       thiostrepton producer Streptomyces azureus, renders ribosomes
CC       completely resistant to thiostrepton.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.66.
DR   P52391, NSHR_STRAS ;  P18644, TSNR_STRAJ ;  P52393, TSNR_STRLU ;
//
ID   2.1.1.231
DE   flavonoid 4'-O-methyltransferase.
AN   4'-hydroxyisoflavone methyltransferase.
AN   isoflavone O-methyltransferase.
CA   a 4'-hydroxyflavanone + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = a 4'-methoxyflavanone +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the 4'-methylation of naringenin.
CC   -!- In vitro it catalyzes the 4'-methylation of apigenin, quercetin,
CC       daidzein and genistein.
DR   C6TAY1, SOMT2_SOYBN;
//
ID   2.1.1.232
DE   naringenin 7-O-methyltransferase.
CA   (2S)-naringenin + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (2S)-sakuranetin +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the sakuranetin,
CC       an inducible defense mechanism of Oryza sativa against pathogen
CC       attack.
DR   K0I977, FOMT1_OCIBA;  K0II72, FOMT2_OCIBA;  Q0IP69, NOMT_ORYSJ ;
DR   Q6VMW2, OMT1A_MENPI;  Q6VMW1, OMT1B_MENPI;
//
ID   2.1.1.233
DE   [phosphatase 2A protein]-leucine-carboxy methyltransferase.
AN   leucine carboxy methyltransferase-1.
CA   [phosphatase 2A protein]-C-terminal L-leucine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   [phosphatase 2A protein]-C-terminal L-leucine methyl ester + S-adenosyl-
CA   L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- Methylates the C-terminal leucine of phosphatase 2A.
CC   -!- A key regulator of protein phosphatase 2A.
CC   -!- The methyl ester is hydrolyzed by EC 3.1.1.89.
CC   -!- Occurs mainly in the cytoplasm, Golgi region and late endosomes.
DR   Q8VY08, LCMT1_ARATH;  Q4WS57, LCMT1_ASPFU;  Q3T0H0, LCMT1_BOVIN;
DR   Q60YU0, LCMT1_CAEBR;  P46554, LCMT1_CAEEL;  Q5A387, LCMT1_CANAL;
