ID   2.1.1.243
DE   5-guanidino-2-oxopentanoate (3R)-methyltransferase.
AN   2-ketoarginine methyltransferase.
CA   5-guanidino-2-oxopentanoate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (3R)-5-guanidino-
CA   3-methyl-2-oxopentanoate + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in production of the rare amino acid (3R)-3-
CC       methyl-L-arginine.
CC   -!- The compound is used by the epiphytic bacterium Pseudomonas syringae
CC       pv. syringae as an antibiotic against the related pathogenic species
CC       Pseudomonas savastanoi pv. glycinea.
CC   -!- Other bacteria incorporate the compound into more complex compounds
CC       such as the peptidyl nucleoside antibiotic arginomycin.
DR   M1T9N7, ARGN_STREL ;  D5FKJ3, MRSA_PSESY ;
//
ID   2.1.1.244
DE   protein N-terminal methyltransferase.
CA   (1) N-terminal L-alanyl-L-prolyl-L-lysyl-[protein] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine = N-terminal N,N,N-trimethyl-L-alanyl-L-prolyl-L-lysyl-
CA   [protein] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 3 H(+).
CA   (2) N-terminal L-seryl-L-prolyl-L-lysyl-[protein] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine = N-terminal N,N,N-trimethyl-L-seryl-L-prolyl-L-lysyl-
CA   [protein] + 3 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 3 H(+).
CA   (3) N-terminal L-prolyl-L-prolyl-L-lysyl-[protein] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine = N-terminal N,N-dimethyl-L-prolyl-L-prolyl-L-lysyl-[protein]
CA   + 2 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme methylates the N-terminus of target proteins containing
CC       the N-terminal motif [Ala/Pro/Ser]-Pro-Lys after the initiator
CC       L-methionine is cleaved.
CC   -!- When the terminal amino acid is L-proline, the enzyme catalyzes two
CC       successive methylations of its alpha-amino group.
CC   -!- When the first amino acid is either L-alanine or L-serine, the enzyme
CC       catalyzes three successive methylations.
CC   -!- The Pro-Lys in positions 2-3 cannot be exchanged for other amino
CC       acids.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.n5.
DR   Q4KL94, NT1AA_XENLA;  Q4KLE6, NT1AB_XENLA;  D2H163, NTM1A_AILME;
DR   Q2T9N3, NTM1A_BOVIN;  Q6NWX7, NTM1A_DANRE;  Q9BV86, NTM1A_HUMAN;
DR   Q8R2U4, NTM1A_MOUSE;  Q5BJX0, NTM1A_RAT  ;  B1H2P7, NTM1A_XENTR;
