ID   2.1.1.245
DE   5-methyltetrahydrosarcinapterin:corrinoid/iron-sulfur protein
DE   Co-methyltransferase.
CA   5,6,7,8-tetrahydrosarcinapterin + methyl-Co(III)-[corrinoid Fe-S protein]
CA   = 5-methyltetrahydrosarcinapterin + Co(I)-[corrinoid Fe-S protein] +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from the cobamide cofactor
CC       of a corrinoid/Fe-S protein to the N5 group of
CC       tetrahydrosarcinapterin.
CC   -!- Forms, together with EC 1.2.7.4 and EC 2.3.1.169 the acetyl-CoA
CC       decarbonylase/synthase complex that catalyzes the demethylation of
CC       acetyl-CoA in a reaction that also forms CO2.
CC   -!- This reaction is a key step in methanogenesis from acetate.
DR   Q8PZ09, ACDG1_METMA;  Q50539, ACDG1_METTE;  Q8PV87, ACDG2_METMA;
DR   Q9C4Z0, ACDG2_METTE;  O29871, ACDG_ARCFU ;  Q8TH44, ACDG_METAC ;
DR   Q57576, ACDG_METJA ;  Q8TXF1, ACDG_METKA ;  O27748, ACDG_METTH ;
