ID   2.1.1.319
DE   type I protein arginine methyltransferase.
CA   L-arginyl-[protein] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N(omega),N(omega)-
CA   dimethyl-L-arginyl-[protein] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- This eukaryotic enzyme catalyzes the sequential dimethylation of one
CC       of the terminal guanidino nitrogen atoms in arginine residues,
CC       resulting in formation of asymmetric dimethylarginine residues.
CC   -!- Some forms (e.g. PRMT1) have a very wide substrate specificity, while
CC       others (e.g. PRMT4 and PRMT6) are rather specific.
CC   -!- The enzyme has a preference for methylating arginine residues that
CC       are flanked by one or more glycine residues.
CC   -!- PRMT1 is responsible for the bulk (about 85%) of total protein
CC       arginine methylation activity in mammalian cells. cf. EC 2.1.1.320,
CC       EC 2.1.1.321 and EC 2.1.1.322.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.23, EC 2.1.1.124, EC 2.1.1.125 and EC 2.1.1.126.
