ID   2.1.1.320
DE   type II protein arginine methyltransferase.
CA   L-arginyl-[protein] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   N(omega),N(omega)'-dimethyl-L-arginyl-[protein] + 2 S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the methylation of one of the terminal guanidino
CC       nitrogen atoms in arginine residues within proteins, forming
CC       monomethylarginine, followed by the methylation of the second
CC       terminal nitrogen atom to form a symmetrical dimethylarginine.
CC   -!- The mammalian enzyme is active in both the nucleus and the cytoplasm,
CC       and plays a role in the assembly of snRNP core particles by
CC       methylating certain small nuclear ribonucleoproteins. cf.
CC       EC 2.1.1.319, EC 2.1.1.321 and EC 2.1.1.322.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.23, EC 2.1.1.124, EC 2.1.1.125 and EC 2.1.1.126.
