ID   2.1.1.321
DE   type III protein arginine methyltransferase.
CA   L-arginyl-[protein] + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N(omega)-methyl-L-
CA   arginyl-[protein] + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- Type III protein arginine methyltransferases catalyze the single
CC       methylation of one of the terminal nitrogen atoms of the guanidino
CC       group in an L-arginine residue within a protein.
CC   -!- Unlike type I and type II protein arginine methyltransferases, which
CC       also catalyze this reaction, type III enzymes do not methylate the
CC       substrate any further. cf. EC 2.1.1.319, EC 2.1.1.320 and
CC       EC 2.1.1.322.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.23, EC 2.1.1.124, EC 2.1.1.125 and EC 2.1.1.126.
DR   A6QQV6, ANM7_BOVIN ;  Q5ZIB9, ANM7_CHICK ;  Q99MI9, ANM7_CRILO ;
DR   A2AV36, ANM7_DANRE ;  Q9NVM4, ANM7_HUMAN ;  Q922X9, ANM7_MOUSE ;
DR   Q5U4E8, ANM7_RAT   ;  Q6PCI6, ANM7_XENLA ;
