CC       of histone H4 (H4K20).
CC   -!- This event is usually followed by further methylation by
CC       EC 2.1.1.362, [histone H4]-N-methyl-L-lysine(20) N-methyltransferase.
CC   -!- This enzyme plays a pivotal role in DNA replication.
CC   -!- Activity is high during the G2 and M phases, but declines
CC       significantly during G1 and S phases.
CC   -!- Mutations in the enzyme have severe consequences, including DNA
CC       double-strand breaks, activation of DNA damage checkpoints, defective
CC       cell cycle progression, and reduced cell proliferation.
