CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in methanogenic archaea, catalyzes a modification
CC       of an L-arginine residue at the active site of EC 2.8.4.1, which
CC       catalyzes the last and methane-releasing step of methanogenesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a radical AdoMet (radical SAM) enzyme and contains an
CC       [4Fe-4S] cluster and a Coalpha-[alpha-(5-hydroxybenzimidazolyl)]-
CC       cobamide cofactor.
CC   -!- The methyl group, which is derived from S-adenosyl-L-methionine,
CC       is transferred to the cob(I)amide cofactor, forming
CC       methylcob(III)amide as an intermediate carrier, before being
CC       transferred to the arginine residue.
DR   Q8THG6, MCRAM_METAC;  Q58251, MCRAM_METJA;
//
ID   2.1.1.380
DE   3-amino-4-hydroxybenzoate 4-O-methyltransferase.
CA   3-amino-2,4-dihydroxybenzoate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3-amino-2-
CA   hydroxy-4-methoxybenzoate + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces cremeus,
CC       is involved in cremeomycin biosynthesis.
DR   A0A0K2JL91, CREN_STRCM ;
//
ID   2.1.1.381
DE   arginine N(omega)-methyltransferase.
CA   L-arginine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N(omega)-methyl-L-arginine +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       achromogenes subsp. streptozoticus, participates in the biosynthesis
CC       of the glucosamine-nitrosourea antibiotic streptozotocin.
DR   A0A411EW25, SZNE_STRC2 ;
//
ID   2.1.1.382
DE   methoxylated aromatic compound--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase.
CA   a methoxylated aromatic compound + Co(I)-[methoxylated-aromatic-compound-
CA   specific corrinoid protein] + H(+) = a phenol + methyl-Co(III)-
CA   [methoxylated-aromatic-compound-specific corrinoid protein].
CC   -!- This entry stands for a family of enzymes that have been
CC       characterized from acetogenic bacteria and archaeal species.
CC   -!- Different members of this family have different substrate
CC       specificity.
CC   -!- In the methanogenic archaeon Methermicoccus shengliensis the enzyme
CC       participates in methanogenesis from methoxylated aromatic compounds,
CC       while in acetogenic bacteria and in non-methanogenic archaea it
CC       participates in methoxydotrophic growth.
CC   -!- Most of the enzymes have a wide specificity and were shown to act on
CC       a large number of methoxylated aromatic compounds, carrying a methoxy
CC       group at positions 2, 3 or 4 of the aromatic ring.
CC   -!- Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to
CC       be in the Co(I) state; during methylation the cobalt is oxidized to
CC       the Co(III) state.
//
ID   2.1.1.383
DE   L-carnitine--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase.
CA   Co(I)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein] + (R)-carnitine +
CA   H(+) = (3R)-4-(dimethylamino)-3-hydroxybutanoate + methyl-Co(III)-
CA   [quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Eubacterium limosum,
CC       is a component of a system that transfers a methyl group from
CC       L-carnitine to tetrahydrofolate, as part of an L-carnitine
CC       degradation pathway.
CC   -!- The resulting 5-methyltetrahydrofolate is processed to acetyl-CoA via
CC       the Wood--Ljungdahl pathway.
DR   P0DX06, MTCB_EUBLI ;
//
ID   2.1.1.384
DE   [methyl-Co(III) methoxylated-aromatic-compound-specific corrinoid
DE   protein]--tetrahydromethanopterin methyltransferase.
CA   5,6,7,8-tetrahydromethanopterin + methyl-Co(III)-[methoxylated-aromatic-
CA   compound-specific corrinoid protein] = 5-methyl-5,6,7,8-
CA   tetrahydromethanopterin + Co(I)-[methoxylated-aromatic-compound-specific
CA   corrinoid protein] + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from several archaeal species.
CC   -!- In the methanogenic archaeon Methermicoccus shengliensis the enzyme
CC       participates in methanogenesis from methoxylated aromatic compounds,
CC       while in the non-methanogenic Archaeoglobus fulgidus it participates
CC       in methoxydotrophic growth.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group bound to the
CC       cobalt cofactor of a dedicated corrinoid protein (MtoC) to
CC       tetrahydromethanopterin or tetrahydrosarcinapterin. cf. EC 2.1.1.385.
//
ID   2.1.1.385
DE   [methyl-Co(III) methoxylated-aromatic-compound-specific corrinoid
DE   protein]--tetrahydrofolate methyltransferase.
CA   methyl-Co(III)-[methoxylated-aromatic-compound-specific corrinoid
CA   protein] + (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate = Co(I)-[methoxylated-aromatic-
CA   compound-specific corrinoid protein] + (6S)-5-methyl-5,6,7,8-
CA   tetrahydrofolate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in acetogenic bacteria, participates in a pathway
CC       for the degradation of methoxylated aromatic compounds
CC       (methoxydotrophic growth).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group bound to the
CC       cobalt cofactor of a dedicated corrinoid protein (MtvC) to
CC       tetrahydrofolate. cf. EC 2.1.1.384.
//
ID   2.1.1.386
DE   small RNA 2'-O-methyltransferase.
CA   small RNA 3'-end nucleotide + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = small RNA 3'-end
CA   2'-O-methylnucleotide + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme adds a 2'-O-methyl group to the ribose of the last
CC       nucleotide in several types of small RNAs (sRNAs), protecting the
CC       3'-end of sRNAs from uridylation activity and subsequent degradation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.n8.
DR   Q9C5Q8, HEN1_ARATH ;  H9JDT2, HENMT_BOMMO;  P34283, HENMT_CAEEL;
DR   E1BVR9, HENMT_CHICK;  Q568P9, HENMT_DANRE;  Q7K175, HENMT_DROME;
DR   Q5T8I9, HENMT_HUMAN;  Q4R3W5, HENMT_MACFA;  Q8CAE2, HENMT_MOUSE;
DR   Q32PY6, HENMT_RAT  ;  Q9UST9, HENMT_SCHPO;  Q230X8, HENMT_TETTS;
DR   C0IN03, HENMT_XENTR;
//
ID   2.1.1.387
DE   5-dehydro-6-demethoxy-6-hydroxyfumagillol O-methyltransferase.
CA   5-dehydro-6-demethoxy-6-hydroxyfumagillol + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   5-dehydrofumagillol + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the mold Aspergillus fumigatus,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the meroterpenoid fumagillin.
DR   A0A067Z9B6, FMAD_ASPFU ;
//
ID   2.1.1.388
DE   proline betaine--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase.
CA   Co(I)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein] + L-proline betaine +
CA   H(+) = methyl-Co(III)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein] +
CA   N-methyl-L-proline.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Eubacterium limosum,
CC       is a component of a system that transfers a methyl group from
CC       L-proline betaine to tetrahydrofolate, as part of an L-proline
CC       betaine degradation pathway.
CC   -!- The resulting 5-methyltetrahydrofolate is processed to acetyl-CoA via
CC       the Wood--Ljungdahl pathway.
//
ID   2.1.1.389
DE   [methyl-Co(III) quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein]-
DE   -tetrahydrofolate methyltransferase.
CA   methyl-Co(III)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid protein] + (6S)-
CA   5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate = Co(I)-[quaternary-amine-specific corrinoid
CA   protein] + (6S)-5-methyl-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the acetogenic gut bacterium
CC       Eubacterium limosum, participates in a pathway for the degradation of
CC       some quaternary amine compounds (L-proline betaine and L-carnitine).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group bound to the
CC       cobalt cofactor of a dedicated corrinoid protein (bacterial MtqC) to
CC       tetrahydrofolate.
CC   -!- The resulting 5-methyltetrahydrofolate is processed to acetyl-CoA via
CC       the Wood--Ljungdahl pathway.
//
ID   2.1.1.390
DE   gentamicin X2 methyltransferase.
AN   gentamicin C-methyltransferase.
CA   gentamicin X2 + AH2 + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = geneticin +
CA   5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + A + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Micromonospora echinospora,
CC       has a single [4Fe-4S] cluster per monomer.
CC   -!- It is a radical S-adenosyl-L-methionine (SAM) enzyme with a
CC       methylcob(III)alamin cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme uses two molecues of SAM for the reaction.
CC   -!- One molecule forms a 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical, while the other is
CC       used to methylate the cobalamin cofactor.
CC   -!- It catalyzes methylation of the 6'-carbon of gentamicin X2 (GenX2) to
CC       produce genetricin (G418) during the biosynthesis of gentamicins.
CC   -!- The 6'-pro-R-hydrogen atom of GenX2 is stereoselectively abstracted
CC       by the 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical and methylation occurs with retention
CC       of configuration at C(6)'.
CC   -!- The regeneration of cob(I)alamin from cob(III)alamin is carried out
CC       with an as yet unidentified electron donor.
//
ID   2.1.1.391
DE   demethylgadusol O-methyltransferase.
AN   desmethyl gadusol O-methyltransferase.
AN   gadusol synthase.
CA   demethylgadusol + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = gadusol + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in egg-laying vertebrates, is involved in
CC       biosynthesis of the UV absorbing compound gadusol.
CC   -!- It is a bifunctional enzyme that also catalyzes EC 1.3.1.126.
//
ID   2.1.1.392
DE   norajmaline N-methyltransferase.
CA   norajmaline + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = ajmaline + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Rauvolfia serpentina (Indian
CC       snakeroot), catalyzes the last step in the pathway for the
CC       biosynthesis of the monoterpenoid indole alkaloid ajmaline.
CC   -!- Also reacts with 4-methylnorajmaline.
DR   A0A075D6M1, NNMT_RAUSE ;
//
ID   2.1.1.393
DE   ajmaline N-methyltransferase.
CA   ajmaline + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 4-methylajmaline + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Rauvolfia serpentina (Indian snakeroot).
CC   -!- The enzyme can also methylate norajmaline, with lower activity.
DR   A0A075D654, ANMT_RAUSE ;
//
ID   2.1.1.394
DE   2-(S-pantetheinyl)-carbapenam-3-carboxylate methyltransferase.
CA   (1) (2R,3R,5R)-2-(S-pantetheinyl)-carbapenam-3-carboxylate + AH2 +
CA   2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (2R,3R,5S,6R)-6-(methyl)-2-(S-pantetheinyl)-
CA   carbapenam-3-carboxylate + 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + A +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) (2R,3R,5S,6R)-6-(methyl)-2-(S-pantetheinyl)-carbapenam-3-carboxylate
CA   + AH2 + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = (2R,3R,5S,6R)-6-(ethyl)-2-
CA   (S-pantetheinyl)-carbapenam-3-carboxylate + 5'-deoxyadenosine +
CA   L-methionine + A + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- A radical SAM (AdoMet) enzyme that catalyzes two consecutive
CC       methylations during the biosynthesis of complex carbapenem
CC       antibiotics.
CC   -!- The enzyme adds a methyl group at position 6, followed by a second
CC       methylation that converts the methyl group to an ethyl group.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster and requires a cobalamin cofactor
CC       and an electron donor.
CC   -!- Methyl viologen can be used in vitro.
DR   Q83XP3, THNK_STREN ;
//
ID   2.1.1.395
DE   7'-O-demethylcephaeline methyltransferase.
CA   7'-O-demethylcephaeline + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = cephaeline +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + H(+).
CC   -!- This activity is the penultimate step in the bionsynthesis of the
CC       alkaloid emetine.
CC   -!- It is catalyzed by two enzymes isolated from the roots of the
CC       tropical plant Carapichea ipecacuanha, IpeOMT2 and CiOMT1.
CC   -!- The latter also catalyzes the activity of EC 2.1.1.396, but with much
CC       lower activity.
DR   E7FL15, CIOMT_CARIP;  D3KY99, OMT2_CARIP ;
