DE   phosphoribosylglycinamide formyltransferase 1.
AN   2-amino-N-ribosylacetamide 5'-phosphate transformylase.
AN   5,10-methenyltetrahydrofolate:2-amino-N-ribosylacetamide ribonucleotide
AN   transformylase.
AN   5'-phosphoribosylglycinamide transformylase.
AN   GAR formyltransferase.
AN   GART.
AN   GAR TFase.
AN   GAR transformylase.
AN   glycinamide ribonucleotide transformylase.
CA   N(1)-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)glycinamide + (6R)-10-
CA   formyltetrahydrofolate = N(2)-formyl-N(1)-(5-phospho-beta-D-
CA   ribosyl)glycinamide + (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + H(+).
CC   -!- Two enzymes are known to catalyze the third step in de novo purine
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- This enzyme utilizes 10-formyltetrahydrofolate as the formyl donor,
CC       while the other enzyme, EC 6.3.1.21, utilizes formate.
CC   -!- In vertebrates this activity is catalyzed by a trifunctional enzyme
CC       that also catalyzes the activities of EC 6.3.4.13 and EC 6.3.3.1.
