//
ID   2.1.3.16
DE   ureidoglycine carbamoyltransferase.
AN   UGTCase.
CA   (S)-2-ureidoglycine + carbamoyl phosphate = allantoate + phosphate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Rubrobacter
CC       xylanophilus, is involved in a purine degradation pathway.
DR   Q1AS69, URGC_RUBXD ;
//
ID   2.1.4.1
DE   glycine amidinotransferase.
CA   L-arginine + glycine = guanidinoacetate + L-ornithine.
CC   -!- Canavanine can act instead of arginine.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.6.2.1.
DR   Q2HJ74, GATM_BOVIN ;  Q9I9K9, GATM_CHICK ;  Q6PH19, GATM_DANRE ;
DR   P50440, GATM_HUMAN ;  Q4R806, GATM_MACFA ;  Q9D964, GATM_MOUSE ;
DR   P50441, GATM_PIG   ;  Q5RFB9, GATM_PONAB ;  P50442, GATM_RAT   ;
DR   Q9IAJ6, GATM_XENLA ;  Q6P832, GATM_XENTR ;
//
ID   2.1.4.2
DE   scyllo-inosamine-4-phosphate amidinotransferase.
AN   Inosamine-P amidinotransferase.
AN   inosamine-phosphate amidinotransferase.
AN   L-arginine:inosamine-P-amidinotransferase.
AN   L-arginine:inosamine phosphate amidinotransferase.
CA   1-amino-1-deoxy-scyllo-inositol 4-phosphate + L-arginine = 1-guanidino-1-
CA   deoxy-scyllo-inositol 4-phosphate + L-ornithine.
CC   -!- 1D-1-Guanidino-3-amino-1,3-dideoxy-scyllo-inositol 6-phosphate,
CC       streptamine phosphate and 2-deoxystreptamine phosphate can also act
CC       as acceptors.
CC   -!- Canavanine can act as donor.
DR   Q54258, STRB1_STRGA;  P08078, STRB1_STRGR;  Q54264, STRB2_STRGA;
DR   P29780, STRB2_STRGR;
//
ID   2.1.4.3
DE   L-arginine:L-lysine amidinotransferase.
CA   L-lysine + L-arginine = L-homoarginine + L-ornithine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas savastanoi
CC       pv. phaseolicola, is involved in the biosynthesis of the toxin
CC       phaseolotoxin, a modified tripeptide that causes the 'halo blight'
CC       disease of beans.
DR   Q9RBU1, AMTA_PSESH ;
//
ID   2.1.4.4
DE   valine amidinotransferase.
CA   L-valine + L-arginine = N-amidino-L-valine + L-ornithine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Salinispora tropica,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of ketomemicins.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme could use multiple other amino acids, including
CC       L-cysteine, L-isoleucine, L-leucine, L-methionine, L-tyrosine,
CC       L-phenylalanine and L-tryptophan instead of L-valine.
DR   A4X5N0, AMDT_SALTO ;
//
ID   2.1.4.5
DE   arginine amidinotransferase.
CA   2 L-arginine = N-amidino-L-arginine + L-ornithine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Micromonospora sp.
CC       ATCC 39149 and Streptomyces mobaraensis, participates in the
CC       biosynthesis of ketomemicins.
DR   P0DY14, AMDT_MICS3 ;  M3B4Q3, AMDT_STRM1 ;
//
ID   2.1.5.1
DE   sesamin methylene transferase.
CA   (1) (+)-sesamin + (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolyl-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) = (+)-
CA   sesamin monocatechol + (6R)-5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolyl-(gamma-L-
CA   Glu)(n).
CA   (2) (+)-sesamin monocatechol + (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolyl-(gamma-L-
CA   Glu)(n) = (+)-sesamin dicatechol + (6R)-5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolyl-
CA   (gamma-L-Glu)(n).
DR   A0A1J1EM40, SESA_SINX2 ;
//
ID   2.2.1.1
DE   transketolase.
AN   glycoaldehyde transferase.
CA   D-sedoheptulose 7-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate = aldehydo-D-
CA   ribose 5-phosphate + D-xylulose 5-phosphate.
CC   -!- Wide specificity for both reactants, e.g. converts hydroxypyruvate
CC       and R-CHO into CO2 and R-CHOH-CO-CH2OH.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Alcaligenes faecalis shows high
CC       activity with D-erythrose 4-phosphate as acceptor.
