//
ID   2.2.1.11
DE   6-deoxy-5-ketofructose 1-phosphate synthase.
AN   DKFP synthase.
CA   (1) beta-D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate + methylglyoxal = 1-deoxy-D-threo-
CA   hexo-2,5-diulose 6-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate.
CA   (2) beta-D-fructose 1-phosphate + methylglyoxal = 1-deoxy-D-threo-hexo-
CA   2,5-diulose 6-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde.
CC   -!- The enzyme plays a key role in an alternative pathway of the
CC       biosynthesis of 3-dehydroquinate (DHQ), which is involved in the
CC       canonical pathway for the biosynthesis of aromatic amino acids.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the reaction of EC 4.1.2.13.
DR   Q58980, DKFP_METJA ;
//
ID   2.2.1.12
DE   3-acetyloctanal synthase.
CA   (2E)-octenal + pyruvate + H(+) = (S)-3-acetyloctanal + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Serratia marcescens,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic prodigiosin.
CC   -!- The enzyme decarboxylates pyruvate, followed by attack of the
CC       resulting two-carbon fragment on (E)-oct-2-enal, resulting in a
CC       Stetter reaction.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme can act on a number of alpha,beta-unsaturated
CC       carbonyl compounds, including aldehydes and ketones, and can catalyze
CC       both 1-2 and 1-4 carboligations depending on the substrate.
DR   Q5W251, PIGD_SERMA ;  Q5W268, PIGD_SERS3 ;
//
ID   2.2.1.13
DE   apulose-4-phosphate transketolase.
CA   apulose 4-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate = D-xylulose
CA   5-phosphate + dihydroxyacetone phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from several bacterial species, is involved
CC       in a catabolic pathway for D-apiose.
DR   A6VKQ4, APTA_ACTSZ ;  A6KXB4, APTA_PHOV8 ;  A6VKQ3, APTB_ACTSZ ;
DR   A6KXB3, APTB_PHOV8 ;
//
ID   2.2.1.14
DE   6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose transaldolase.
CA   6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate = D-fructose
CA   6-phosphate + (2S)-3-sulfolactaldehyde.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacillus aryabhattai
CC       SOS1, is involved in a degradation pathway for 6-sulfo-D-quinovose.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use D-erythrose 4-phosphate as the acceptor,
CC       forming D-sedoheptulose 7-phosphate.
DR   A0A7W3N5X5, SFTAL_PRIAR;  D5E1T2, SFTAL_PRIM1;
//
ID   2.2.1.15
DE   6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose transketolase.
AN   6-deoxy-6-sulfo-erythrulose transketolase.
CA   (1) 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate = 4-deoxy-
CA   4-sulfo-D-erythrose + D-xylulose 5-phosphate.
CA   (2) 4-deoxy-4-sulfo-D-erythrulose + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate =
CA   sulfoacetaldehyde + D-xylulose 5-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Clostridium sp. MSTE9,
CC       is involved in a D-sulfoquinovose degradation pathway.
DR   J0MXK0, SQWG_CLOS9 ;  J1H0Z7, SQWH_CLOS9 ;
