ID   2.3.1.9
DE   acetyl-CoA C-acetyltransferase.
AN   acetoacetyl-CoA thiolase.
CA   2 acetyl-CoA = acetoacetyl-CoA + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in both eukaryotes and prokaryotes, catalyzes the
CC       Claisen condensation of an acetyl-CoA and an acyl-CoA (often another
CC       acetyl-CoA), leading to the formation of an acyl-CoA that is longer
CC       by two carbon atoms.
CC   -!- The reaction starts with the acylation of a nucleophilic cysteine at
CC       the active site, usually by acetyl-CoA but potentially by a different
CC       acyl-CoA, with concomitant release of CoA.
CC   -!- In the second step the acyl group is transferred to an acetyl-CoA
CC       molecule. cf. EC 2.3.1.16.
