ID   2.3.1.16
DE   acetyl-CoA C-acyltransferase.
AN   3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase.
AN   beta-ketothiolase.
CA   an acyl-CoA + acetyl-CoA = a 3-oxoacyl-CoA + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in both eukaryotes and in prokaryotes, is involved
CC       in degradation pathways such as fatty acid beta-oxidation.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on 3-oxoacyl-CoAs to produce acetyl-CoA and an acyl-
CC       CoA shortened by two carbon atoms.
CC   -!- The reaction starts with the acylation of a nucleophilic cysteine at
CC       the active site by a 3-oxoacyl-CoA, with the concomitant release of
CC       acetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- In the second step the acyl group is transferred to CoA.
CC   -!- Most enzymes have a broad substrate range for the 3-oxoacyl-CoA. cf.
CC       EC 2.3.1.9.
