ID   2.3.1.39
DE   [acyl-carrier-protein] S-malonyltransferase.
AN   acyl carrier protein malonyltransferase.
AN   malonyl-CoA/dephospho-CoA acyltransferase.
AN   malonyl-CoA-acyl carrier protein transacylase.
AN   malonyl coenzyme A-acyl carrier protein transacylase.
AN   malonyl transacylase.
AN   malonyl transferase.
AN   MCAT.
CA   holo-[ACP] + malonyl-CoA = malonyl-[ACP] + CoA.
CC   -!- Essential, along with EC 2.3.1.38, for the initiation of fatty-acid
CC       biosynthesis in bacteria.
CC   -!- Also provides the malonyl groups for polyketide biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The product of the reaction, malonyl-ACP, is an elongation substrate
CC       in fatty-acid biosynthesis.
CC   -!- In Mycobacterium tuberculosis, holo-ACP (the product of EC 2.7.8.7)
CC       is the preferred substrate.
CC   -!- This enzyme also forms part of the multienzyme complexes EC 4.1.1.88
CC       and EC 4.1.1.89.
CC   -!- Malonylation of ACP is immediately followed by decarboxylation within
CC       the malonate-decarboxylase complex to yield acetyl-ACP,
CC       the catalytically active species of the decarboxylase.
CC   -!- In the enzyme from Klebsiella pneumoniae, methylmalonyl-CoA can also
CC       act as a substrate but acetyl-CoA cannot whereas the enzyme from
CC       Pseudomonas putida can use both as substrates.
CC   -!- The ACP subunit found in fatty-acid biosynthesis contains a
CC       pantetheine-4'-phosphate cofactor; that from malonate decarboxylase
CC       also contains pantetheine-4'-phosphate but in the form of a
CC       2'-(5-triphosphoribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA cofactor.
