ID   2.3.1.77
DE   triacylglycerol--sterol O-acyltransferase.
CA   a 3beta-hydroxysteroid + a triacylglycerol = a 3beta-hydroxysteroid ester
CA   + a diacylglycerol.
CC   -!- Tripalmitoylglycerol can act as donor, and, more slowly, other
CC       triacylglycerols containing C6 to C22 fatty acids.
CC   -!- The best acceptors are 3beta-hydroxysteroids with a planar ring
CC       system.
//
ID   2.3.1.78
DE   heparan-alpha-glucosaminide N-acetyltransferase.
CA   alpha-D-glucosaminyl-[heparan sulfate](n) + acetyl-CoA = N-acetyl-alpha-
CA   D-glucosaminyl-[heparan sulfate](n) + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Brings about the acetylation of glucosamine groups of heparan sulfate
CC       and heparin from which the sulfate has been removed.
CC   -!- Also acts on heparin.
CC   -!- Not identical with EC 2.3.1.3 or EC 2.3.1.4.
DR   Q68CP4, HGNAT_HUMAN;  Q3UDW8, HGNAT_MOUSE;
