ID   2.3.1.80
DE   cysteine-S-conjugate N-acetyltransferase.
CA   an S-substituted L-cysteine + acetyl-CoA = an N-acetyl-L-cysteine-S-
CA   conjugate + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- S-benzyl-L-cysteine and, in decreasing order of activity, S-butyl-L-
CC       cysteine, S-propyl-L-cysteine, O-benzyl-L-serine and S-ethyl-L-
CC       cysteine, can act as acceptor.
