ID   2.3.1.86
DE   fatty-acyl-CoA synthase system.
AN   fatty-acyl-CoA synthase.
AN   yeast fatty acid synthase.
CA   acetyl-CoA + n malonyl-CoA + 2n NADPH + 4n H(+) = a long-chain-acyl-CoA +
CA   n CoA + n CO2 + 2n NADP(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from yeasts (Ascomycota and Basidiomycota) is a multi-
CC       functional protein complex composed of two subunits.
CC   -!- One subunit catalyzes the reactions EC 1.1.1.100 and EC 2.3.1.41,
CC       while the other subunit catalyzes the reactions of EC 2.3.1.38,
CC       EC 2.3.1.39, EC 4.2.1.59, EC 1.3.1.10 and EC 1.1.1.279.
CC   -!- The enzyme differs from the animal enzyme (EC 2.3.1.85) in that the
CC       enoyl reductase domain requires FMN as a cofactor, and the ultimate
CC       product is an acyl-CoA (usually palmitoyl-CoA) instead of a free
CC       fatty acid.
