ID   2.3.1.97
DE   glycylpeptide N-tetradecanoyltransferase.
AN   peptide N-myristoyltransferase.
AN   peptide N-tetradecanoyltransferase.
CA   N-terminal glycyl-[protein] + tetradecanoyl-CoA = N-tetradecanoylglycyl-
CA   [protein] + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of myristic acid from myristoyl-CoA
CC       to the amino group of the N-terminal glycine residue in a variety of
CC       eukaryotic proteins.
CC   -!- It uses an ordered Bi Bi reaction in which myristoyl-CoA binds to the
CC       enzyme prior to the binding of the peptide substrate, and CoA release
CC       precedes the release of the myristoylated peptide.
CC   -!- The enzyme from yeast is profoundly affected by amino acids further
CC       from the N-terminus, and is particularly stimulated by a serine
CC       residue at position 5.
