ID   2.3.1.111
DE   mycocerosate synthase.
CA   (1) a long-chain fatty acyl-[mycocerosate synthase] + 3 (R)-
CA   methylmalonyl-CoA + 6 NADPH + 9 H(+) = trimethylated-mycocerosoyl-
CA   [mycocerosate synthase] + 3 CO2 + 6 NADP(+) + 3 CoA + 3 H2O.
CA   (2) a long-chain fatty acyl-[mycocerosate synthase] + 4 (R)-
CA   methylmalonyl-CoA + 8 NADPH + 12 H(+) = tetramethylated-mycocerosoyl-
CA   [mycocerosate synthase] + 4 CO2 + 8 NADP(+) + 4 CoA + 4 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from mycobacteria, is loaded with a long-
CC       chain acyl moiety by EC 6.2.1.49 and elongates it by incorporation of
CC       three or four methylmalonyl (but not malonyl) residues, to form tri-
CC       or tetramethyl-branched fatty-acids, respectively, such as 2,4,6,8-
CC       tetramethyloctacosanoate (C32-mycocerosate).
CC   -!- Since the enzyme lacks a thioesterase domain, the product remains
CC       bound and requires additional enzyme(s) for removal.
CC   -!- Even though the enzyme can accept C6 to C20 substrates in vitro,
CC       it prefers to act on C14-C20 substrates in vivo.
DR   Q02251, MCAS_MYCBO ;
