ID   2.3.1.125
DE   1-alkyl-2-acetylglycerol O-acyltransferase.
AN   1-hexadecyl-2-acetylglycerol acyltransferase.
CA   a 1-O-alkyl-2-acetyl-sn-glycerol + an acyl-CoA = a 1-O-alkyl-2-acetyl-3-
CA   acyl-sn-glycerol + CoA.
CC   -!- A number of acyl-CoAs can act as acyl donor; maximum activity is
CC       obtained with linoleoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- Not identical with EC 2.3.1.20.
//
ID   2.3.1.126
DE   isocitrate O-dihydroxycinnamoyltransferase.
CA   D-threo-isocitrate + (E)-caffeoyl-CoA = 2-[(E)-caffeoyl]-D-threo-
CA   isocitrate(3-) + CoA.
CC   -!- Feruloyl-CoA and 4-coumaroyl-CoA can also act as donors.
//
ID   2.3.1.127
DE   ornithine N-benzoyltransferase.
CA   2 benzoyl-CoA + L-ornithine = N(2),N(5)-dibenzoyl-L-ornithine + 2 CoA +
CA   2 H(+).
