ID   2.3.1.135
DE   phosphatidylcholine--retinol O-acyltransferase.
AN   lecithin retinol acyl transferase.
AN   lecithin-retinol acyltransferase.
AN   lecithin--retinol acyltransferase.
AN   retinyl ester synthase.
CA   all-trans-retinol--[retinol-binding protein] + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-
CA   phosphocholine = apo--[retinol-binding protein] + an all-trans-retinyl
CA   ester + a 2-acyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine.
CC   -!- A key enzyme in retinoid metabolism, catalyzing the transfer of an
CC       acyl group from the sn-1 position of phosphatidylcholine to retinol,
CC       forming retinyl esters which are then stored.
CC   -!- Recognizes the substrate both in free form and when bound to
CC       cellular-retinol-binding-protein, but has higher affinity for the
CC       bound form.
CC   -!- Can also esterify 11-cis-retinol.
DR   Q9BGL2, LRAT_BOVIN ;  O95237, LRAT_HUMAN ;  Q9JI60, LRAT_MOUSE ;
DR   Q9JI61, LRAT_RAT   ;
//
ID   2.3.1.136
DE   polysialic-acid O-acetyltransferase.
CA   (1) [N-acetyl-alpha-D-neuraminosyl-(2->8)](n) + n acetyl-CoA =
CA   [O(7),N-diacetyl-alpha-D-neuraminosyl-(2->8)](n) + n CoA.
CA   (2) [N-acetyl-alpha-D-neuraminosyl-(2->8)](n) + n acetyl-CoA = [N,O(9)-
CA   diacetyl-alpha-D-neuraminosyl-(2->8)](n) + n CoA.
CC   -!- Acts only on substrates containing more than 14 sialosyl residues.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the modification of capsular polysaccharides in some
CC       strains of Escherichia coli.
DR   A1ADJ6, NEUO_ECOK1 ;
//
ID   2.3.1.137
DE   carnitine O-octanoyltransferase.
CA   octanoyl-CoA + (R)-carnitine = O-octanoyl-(R)-carnitine + CoA.
CC   -!- Acts on a range of acyl-CoAs, with optimal activity with C6 or C8
CC       acyl groups. cf. EC 2.3.1.7 and EC 2.3.1.21.
DR   P52826, CACP_COLLI ;  P43155, CACP_HUMAN ;  P47934, CACP_MOUSE ;
