ID   2.3.1.138
DE   putrescine N-hydroxycinnamoyltransferase.
CA   (E)-caffeoyl-CoA + putrescine = N-caffeoylputrescine + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Feruloyl-CoA, cinnamoyl-CoA and sinapoyl-CoA can also act as donors,
CC       more slowly.
//
ID   2.3.1.139
DE   ecdysone O-acyltransferase.
CA   ecdysone + hexadecanoyl-CoA = ecdysone hexadecanoate + CoA.
//
ID   2.3.1.140
DE   rosmarinate synthase.
CA   (2R)-3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)lactate + (E)-caffeoyl-CoA = (R)-rosmarinate
CA   + CoA.
CC   -!- Involved with EC 1.1.1.237 in the biosynthesis of rosmarinic acid.
CC   -!- Characterized from the plant Melissa officinalis L. (lemon balm).
DR   G0LD36, RAS_MELOI  ;  A0PDV5, RAS_PLESU  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.141
DE   galactosylacylglycerol O-acyltransferase.
CA   a 2-acyl-3-O-(beta-D-galactosyl)-sn-glycerol + a fatty acyl-[ACP] =
CA   a 1,2-diacyl-3-O-(beta-D-galactosyl)-sn-glycerol + holo-[ACP].
CC   -!- Transfers long-chain acyl groups to the sn-1 position of the glycerol
CC       residues.
//
ID   2.3.1.142
DE   glycoprotein O-fatty-acyltransferase.
CA   palmitoyl-CoA + mucus glycoprotein = CoA + O-palmitoylglycoprotein.
//
ID   2.3.1.143
DE   beta-glucogallin--tetrakisgalloylglucose O-galloyltransferase.
CA   1,2,3,6-tetrakis-O-galloyl-beta-D-glucose + 1-O-galloyl-beta-D-glucose =
CA   1,2,3,4,6-pentakis-O-galloyl-beta-D-glucose + D-glucose + H(+).
//
ID   2.3.1.144
DE   anthranilate N-benzoyltransferase.
CA   anthranilate + benzoyl-CoA = N-benzoylanthranilate + CoA.
CC   -!- Cinnamoyl-CoA, 4-coumaroyl-CoA and salicyloyl-CoA can act as donors,
CC       more slowly.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of phytoalexins.
DR   O24645, HCBT1_DIACA;  O23917, HCBT2_DIACA;  O23918, HCBT3_DIACA;
//
ID   2.3.1.145
DE   piperidine N-piperoyltransferase.
CA   piperidine + (E,E)-piperoyl-CoA = piperine + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Pyrrolidine and 3-pyrroline can also act as acceptors, more slowly.
DR   P0DO57, PAS_PIPNI  ;  P0DO56, PS_PIPNI   ;
//
ID   2.3.1.146
DE   pinosylvin synthase.
AN   stilbene synthase.
CA   (E)-cinnamoyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 3 H(+) = (E)-pinosylvin + 4 CO2 +
CA   4 CoA.
CC   -!- Not identical with EC 2.3.1.74 or EC 2.3.1.95.
DR   P48407, DPS1_PINST ;  P48408, DPS2_PINST ;  Q02323, DPSS_PINSY ;
//
ID   2.3.1.147
DE   glycerophospholipid arachidonoyl-transferase (CoA-independent).
CA   a 1-alkyl-2-(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine
CA   + a 1-O-alkyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine = a 1-O-alkyl-2-
CA   (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine +
CA   a 1-O-alkyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the transfer of arachidonate and other polyenoic fatty
CC       acids from intact choline or ethanolamine-containing
CC       glycerophospholipids to the sn-2 position of a lyso-
CC       glycerophospholipid.
CC   -!- The organyl group on sn-1 of the donor or acceptor molecule can be
CC       alkyl, acyl or alk-1-enyl.
CC   -!- The term 'radyl' has sometimes been used to refer to such
CC       substituting groups.
CC   -!- Differs from EC 2.3.1.148 in not requiring CoA and in its specificity
CC       for poly-unsaturated acyl groups.
//
ID   2.3.1.148
DE   glycerophospholipid acyltransferase (CoA-dependent).
CA   a 1-O-alkyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine + a 1-O-alkyl-2-acyl-
CA   sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine = a 1-O-alkyl-2-acyl-sn-glycero-3-
CA   phosphoethanolamine + a 1-O-alkyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the transfer of fatty acids from intact choline- or
CC       ethanolamine-containing glycerophospholipids to the sn-2 position of
CC       a lyso-glycerophospholipid.
CC   -!- The organyl group on sn-1 of the donor or acceptor molecule can be
CC       alkyl, acyl or alk-1-enyl.
CC   -!- The term 'radyl' has sometimes been used to refer to such
CC       substituting groups.
CC   -!- Differs from EC 2.3.1.147 in requiring CoA and not favoring the
CC       transfer of polyunsaturated acyl groups.
//
ID   2.3.1.149
DE   platelet-activating factor acetyltransferase.
AN   PAF acetyltransferase.
CA   a 1-organyl-2-lyso-sn-glycero-3-phospholipid + a 1-O-alkyl-2-acetyl-
CA   sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine = a 1-organyl-2-acetyl-sn-glycero-3-
CA   phospholipid + a 1-O-alkyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the transfer of the acetyl group from 1-alkyl-2-acyl-
CC       sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine (platelet-activating factor) to the sn-2
CC       position of lyso-glycerophospholipids containing ethanolamine,
CC       choline, serine, inositol or phosphate groups at the sn-3 position as
CC       well as to sphingosine and long-chain fatty alcohols.
CC   -!- The organyl group can be alkyl, acyl or alk-1-enyl (sometimes also
CC       collectively referred to as 'radyl').
DR   P79106, PAFA2_BOVIN;  Q99487, PAFA2_HUMAN;  Q8VDG7, PAFA2_MOUSE;
DR   P83006, PAFA2_RAT  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.150
DE   salutaridinol 7-O-acetyltransferase.
CA   (7S)-salutaridinol + acetyl-CoA = (7S)-O-acetylsalutaridinol + CoA.
CC   -!- At higher pH values the product, 7-O-acetylsalutaridinol,
CC       spontaneously closes the 4->5 oxide bridge by allylic elimination to
CC       form the morphine precursor thebaine.
CC   -!- From the opium poppy plant, Papaver somniferum.
DR   Q94FT4, SALAT_PAPSO;
//
ID   2.3.1.151
DE   2,3',4,6-tetrahydroxybenzophenone synthase.
CA   3-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 2 H(+) = 2,3',4,6-
CA   tetrahydroxybenzophenone + 3 CO2 + 4 CoA.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of plant xanthones.
CC   -!- Benzoyl-CoA can replace 3-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA (cf. EC 2.3.1.220).
DR   Q8SAS8, TBSYN_HYPAN;
//
ID   2.3.1.152
DE   alcohol O-cinnamoyltransferase.
CA   1-O-(trans-cinnamoyl)-beta-D-glucose + an alcohol = an alkyl cinnamate +
CA   beta-D-glucose.
CC   -!- acceptor alcohols (ROH) include methanol, ethanol and propanol.
CC   -!- No cofactors are required as 1-O-trans-cinnamoyl-beta-D-glucopyranose
CC       itself is an 'energy-rich' (activated) acyl-donor, comparable to CoA-
CC       thioesters.
CC   -!- 1-O-trans-Cinnamoyl-beta-D-gentobiose can also act as the acyl donor,
CC       but with much less affinity.
//
ID   2.3.1.153
DE   anthocyanin 5-(6'''-hydroxycinnamoyltransferase).
CA   an anthocyanidin 3,5-di-O-beta-D-glucoside + (E)-4-coumaroyl-CoA =
CA   an anthocyanidin 3-O-beta-D-glucoside 5-O-beta-D-[(6-O-(E)-4-
CA   coumaroyl)glucoside] + CoA.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Gentiana triflora.
CC   -!- Transfers the hydroxycinnamoyl group only to the C-5 glucoside of
CC       anthocyanin.
CC   -!- Caffeoyl-CoA, but not malonyl-CoA, can substitute as an acyl donor.
DR   Q9ZWR8, ANTA_GENTR ;
