ID   2.3.1.158
DE   phospholipid:diacylglycerol acyltransferase.
AN   PDAT.
CA   a glycerophospholipid + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol =
CA   a monoacylglycerophospholipid + a triacyl-sn-glycerol.
CC   -!- This enzyme differs from EC 2.3.1.20 by synthesizing triacylglycerol
CC       using an acyl-CoA-independent mechanism.
CC   -!- The specificity of the enzyme for the acyl group in the phospholipid
CC       varies with species, e.g., the enzyme from castor bean (Ricinus
CC       communis) preferentially incorporates vernoloyl (12,13-epoxyoctadec-
CC       9-enoyl) groups into triacylglycerol, whereas that from the hawk's
CC       beard (Crepis palaestina) incorporates both ricinoleoyl
CC       (12-hydroxyoctadec-9-enoyl) and vernoloyl groups.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae specifically
CC       transfers acyl groups from the sn-2 position of the phospholipid to
CC       diacylglycerol, thus forming an sn-1-lysophospholipid.
DR   Q9FNA9, PDAT1_ARATH;  Q9FYC7, PDAT2_ARATH;  O94680, PDAT_SCHPO ;
DR   P40345, PDAT_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.3.1.159
DE   acridone synthase.
CA   N-methylanthraniloyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 3 H(+) = 1,3-dihydroxy-N-
CA   methylacridone + 3 CO2 + 4 CoA + H2O.
DR   Q9FSC0, ACS2_RUTGR ;  Q9FSC2, ACS3_RUTGR ;  Q9FSC1, ACS4_RUTGR ;
//
ID   2.3.1.160
DE   vinorine synthase.
CA   16-epivellosimine + acetyl-CoA = vinorine + CoA.
CC   -!- The reaction proceeds in two stages.
CC   -!- The indole nitrogen of 16-epivellosimine interacts with its aldehyde
CC       group giving an hydroxy-substituted new ring.
CC   -!- This alcohol is then acetylated.
CC   -!- Also acts on gardneral (11-methoxy-16-epivellosimine).
CC   -!- Generates the ajmalan skeleton, which forms part of the route to
CC       ajmaline.
DR   Q70PR7, VINSY_RAUSE;
//
ID   2.3.1.161
DE   lovastatin nonaketide synthase.
CA   holo-[lovastatin nonaketide synthase] + 9 malonyl-CoA + S-adenosyl-L-
CA   methionine + 11 NADPH + 19 H(+) = dihydromonacolin L-[lovastatin
CA   nonaketide synthase] + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 9 CO2 + 11 NADP(+) +
CA   9 CoA + 6 H2O.
CC   -!- This fungal enzyme system comprises a multi-functional polyketide
CC       synthase (PKS) and an enoyl reductase.
CC   -!- The PKS catalyzes many of the chain building reactions of
CC       EC 2.3.1.85, as well as a reductive methylation and a Diels-Alder
CC       reaction, while the reductase is responsible for three enoyl
CC       reductions that are necessary for dihydromonacolin L acid production.
DR   Q9Y8A5, LOVB_ASPTE ;  Q0C8M3, LOVB_ASPTN ;  Q9Y7D0, LOVC_ASPTE ;
DR   Q0C8M1, LOVC_ASPTN ;  Q3S2T9, MOKA_MONPI ;
//
ID   2.3.1.162
DE   taxadien-5alpha-ol O-acetyltransferase.
AN   taxa-4(20),11(12)-dien-5alpha-ol O-acetyltransferase.
AN   taxadienol acetyltransferase.
CA   taxa-4(20),11-dien-5alpha-ol + acetyl-CoA = taxa-4(20),11-dien-5alpha-yl
CA   acetate + CoA.
CC   -!- This is the third enzyme in the biosynthesis of the diterpenoid
CC       antineoplastic drug taxol (paclitaxel), which is widely used in the
CC       treatment of carcinomas, sarcomas and melanomas.
DR   Q8S9G6, T5AT_TAXCH ;  Q9M6F0, T5AT_TAXCU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.163
DE   10-hydroxytaxane O-acetyltransferase.
AN   acetyl coenzyme A:10-hydroxytaxane O-acetyltransferase.
CA   10-deacetyltaxuyunnanin C + acetyl-CoA = taxuyunnanin C + CoA.
CC   -!- Acts on a number of related taxane diterpenoids with a free 10-beta-
CC       hydroxy group.
CC   -!- May be identical to EC 2.3.1.167.
//
ID   2.3.1.164
DE   isopenicillin-N N-acyltransferase.
AN   acyl-coenzyme A:6-aminopenicillanic-acid-acyltransferase.
AN   acyl-coenzyme A:isopenicillin N acyltransferase.
AN   isopenicillin N:acyl-CoA acyltransferase.
CA   isopenicillin N + phenylacetyl-CoA + H2O = penicillin G + L-2-
CA   aminoadipate + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Proceeds by a two stage mechanism via 6-aminopenicillanic acid.
CC   -!- Different from EC 3.5.1.11.
DR   P21133, AATA_EMENI ;  P15802, AATA_PENCH ;  B6HLT9, AATA_PENRW ;
//
ID   2.3.1.165
DE   6-methylsalicylic acid synthase.
AN   6-MSAS.
AN   MSAS.
CA   3 malonyl-CoA + acetyl-CoA + NADPH + 3 H(+) = 6-methylsalicylate + 3 CO2
CA   + NADP(+) + 4 CoA + H2O.
CC   -!- A multienzyme complex with a 4'-phosphopantetheine cofactor on the
CC       acyl carrier protein.
CC   -!- It has a similar sequence to vertebrate type I fatty acid synthase.
CC   -!- Acetoacetyl-CoA can also act as a starter molecule.
DR   A0A1L9WN37, ACUA_ASPA1 ;  G1XU04, AR283_ARTOA;  Q0CJ59, ATX_ASPTN  ;
DR   A0A2P1DP91, MACA_PENTR ;  P22367, MSAS_PENPA ;  A1CFL8, PATK_ASPCL ;
DR   A0A075TRC0, PATK_PENEN ;  G3Y419, YANA_ASPNA ;
//
ID   2.3.1.166
DE   2alpha-hydroxytaxane 2-O-benzoyltransferase.
AN   2-debenzoyl-7,13-diacetylbaccatin III-2-O-benzoyl transferase.
AN   benzoyl-CoA:taxane 2alpha-O-benzoyltransferase.
CA   10-deacetyl-2-debenzoylbaccatin III + benzoyl-CoA = 10-deacetylbaccatin
CA   III + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme was studied using the semisynthetic substrate 2-debenzoyl-
CC       7,13-diacetylbaccatin III.
CC   -!- It will not acylate the hydroxy group at 1beta, 7beta, 10beta or
CC       13alpha of 10-deacetylbaccatin III, or at 2alpha or 5alpha of taxa-
CC       4(20),11-diene-2alpha,5alpha-diol.
DR   Q9FPW3, DBBT_TAXCU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.167
DE   10-deacetylbaccatin III 10-O-acetyltransferase.
CA   10-deacetylbaccatin III + acetyl-CoA = baccatin III + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme will not acylate the hydroxy group at 1beta, 7beta,
CC       13alpha of 10-deacetylbaccatin III, or at 5alpha of taxa-4(20),
CC       11-dien-5alpha-ol.
CC   -!- May be identical to EC 2.3.1.163.
DR   Q9M6E2, DBAT_TAXCU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.168
DE   dihydrolipoyllysine-residue (2-methylpropanoyl)transferase.
AN   dihydrolipoyl transacylase.
CA   N(6)-[(R)-dihydrolipoyl]-L-lysyl-[protein] + 2-methylpropanoyl-CoA =
CA   N(6)-[(R)-S(8)-2-methylpropanoyldihydrolipoyl]-L-lysyl-[protein] + CoA.
CC   -!- A multimer (24-mer) of this enzyme forms the core of the multienzyme
CC       3-methyl-2-oxobutanoate dehydrogenase complex, and binds tightly both
CC       EC 1.2.4.4 and EC 1.8.1.4.
CC   -!- The lipoyl group of this enzyme is reductively 2-methylpropanoylated
CC       by EC 1.2.4.4, and the only observed direction catalyzed by
CC       EC 2.3.1.168 is that where this 2-methylpropanoyl is passed to
CC       coenzyme A.
CC   -!- In addition to the 2-methylpropanoyl group, formed when EC 1.2.4.4
CC       acts on the oxoacid that corresponds with valine, this enzyme also
CC       transfers the 3-methylbutanoyl and S-2-methylbutanoyl groups, donated
CC       to it when EC 1.2.4.4 acts on the oxo acids corresponding with
CC       leucine and isoleucine.
DR   O06159, BKDC_MYCTU ;  Q9M7Z1, ODB2_ARATH ;  P37942, ODB2_BACSU ;
DR   P11181, ODB2_BOVIN ;  Q23571, ODB2_CAEEL ;  P11182, ODB2_HUMAN ;
DR   P53395, ODB2_MOUSE ;  Q9I1M0, ODB2_PSEAE ;  P09062, ODB2_PSEPU ;
