ID   2.3.1.179
DE   beta-ketoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] synthase II.
AN   3-oxoacyl-acyl carrier protein synthase I.
AN   beta-ketoacyl-ACP synthase II.
AN   KASII.
AN   KAS II.
CA   (9Z)-hexadecenoyl-[ACP] + malonyl-[ACP] + H(+) = 3-oxo-(11Z)-
CA   octadecenoyl-[ACP] + holo-[ACP] + CO2.
CC   -!- Involved in the dissociated (or type II) fatty acid biosynthesis
CC       system that occurs in plants and bacteria.
CC   -!- While the substrate specificity of this enzyme is very similar to
CC       that of EC 2.3.1.41, it differs in that palmitoleoyl-ACP is not a
CC       good substrate of EC 2.3.1.41 but is an excellent substrate of this
CC       enzyme.
CC   -!- The fatty-acid composition of Escherichia coli changes as a function
CC       of growth temperature, with the proportion of unsaturated fatty acids
CC       increasing with lower growth temperature.
CC   -!- Controls the temperature-dependent regulation of fatty-acid
CC       composition, with mutants lacking this acivity being deficient in the
CC       elongation of palmitoleate to cis-vaccenate at low temperatures.
