ID   2.3.1.180
DE   beta-ketoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] synthase III.
AN   3-ketoacyl-acyl carrier protein synthase III.
AN   3-oxoacyl:ACP synthase III.
AN   beta-ketoacyl (acyl carrier protein) synthase III.
AN   beta-ketoacyl-ACP synthase III.
AN   beta-ketoacyl-acyl carrier protein synthase III.
AN   KASIII.
AN   KAS III.
CA   malonyl-[ACP] + acetyl-CoA + H(+) = 3-oxobutanoyl-[ACP] + CO2 + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is responsible for initiating straight-chain fatty acid
CC       biosynthesis by the dissociated (or type II) fatty-acid biosynthesis
CC       system that occurs in plants and bacteria.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 2.3.1.41 and EC 2.3.1.179, this enzyme specifically
CC       uses short-chain acyl-CoA thioesters (preferably acetyl-CoA) rather
CC       than acyl-[acp] as its substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the reaction of EC 2.3.1.38, but to a
CC       much lesser extent.
CC   -!- The enzymes from some organisms (e.g. the Gram-positive bacterium
CC       Streptococcus pneumoniae) can accept branched-chain acyl-CoAs in
CC       addition to acetyl-CoA (cf. EC 2.3.1.300).
