ID   2.3.1.185
DE   tropine acyltransferase.
AN   TAT.
AN   tropine acetyltransferase.
AN   tropine tigloyltransferase.
CA   tropine + an acyl-CoA = an O-acyltropine + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Exhibits absolute specificity for the endo/3alpha configuration found
CC       in tropine as pseudotropine (tropan-3beta-ol; see EC 2.3.1.186) is
CC       not a substrate.
CC   -!- Acts on a wide range of aliphatic acyl-CoA derivatives, with tigloyl-
CC       CoA and acetyl-CoA being the best substrates.
CC   -!- It is probably involved in the formation of the tropane alkaloid
CC       littorine, which is a precursor of hyoscyamine.
//
ID   2.3.1.186
DE   pseudotropine acyltransferase.
AN   PAT.
AN   pseudotropine acetyltransferase.
AN   pseudotropine tigloyltransferase.
CA   pseudotropine + an acyl-CoA = an O-acylpseudotropine + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Exhibits absolute specificity for the exo/3beta configuration found
CC       in pseudotropine as tropine (tropan-3alpha-ol; see EC 2.3.1.185) and
CC       nortropine are not substrates.
CC   -!- Acts on a wide range of aliphatic acyl-CoA derivatives, including
CC       acetyl-CoA, beta-methylcrotonyl-CoA and tigloyl-CoA.
//
ID   2.3.1.187
DE   acetyl-S-ACP:malonate ACP transferase.
AN   ACP transferase.
AN   malonate/acetyl-CoA transferase.
CA   acetyl-[ACP] + malonate = malonyl-[ACP] + acetate.
CC   -!- This is the first step in the catalysis of malonate decarboxylation
CC       and involves the exchange of an acetyl thioester residue bound to the
CC       activated acyl-carrier protein (ACP) subunit of the malonate
CC       decarboxylase complex for a malonyl thioester residue.
CC   -!- This enzyme forms the alpha subunit of the multienzyme complexes
CC       EC 4.1.1.88 and EC 7.2.4.4.
CC   -!- Can also use acetyl-CoA as a substrate but more slowly.
DR   O06924, MADA_MALRU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.188
DE   omega-hydroxypalmitate O-feruloyl transferase.
AN   HHT.
AN   hydroxycinnamoyl-CoA omega-hydroxypalmitic acid
AN   O-hydroxycinnamoyltransferase.
CA   16-hydroxyhexadecanoate + (E)-feruloyl-CoA =
CA   16-feruloyloxyhexadecanoate + CoA.
CC   -!- p-Coumaroyl-CoA and sinapoyl-CoA also act as substrates.
CC   -!- The enzyme is widely distributed in roots of higher plants.
DR   Q94CD1, HHT1_ARATH ;
//
ID   2.3.1.189
DE   mycothiol synthase.
CA   1D-myo-inositol 2-(L-cysteinylamino)-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranoside +
CA   acetyl-CoA = mycothiol + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the last step in the biosynthesis of mycothiol,
CC       the major thiol in most actinomycetes, including Mycobacterium.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a member of a large family of GCN5-related
CC       N-acetyltransferases (GNATs).
CC   -!- The enzyme has been purified from Mycobacterium tuberculosis H37Rv.
CC   -!- Acetyl-CoA is the preferred CoA thioester but propionyl-CoA is also a
CC       substrate.
