//
ID   2.3.1.190
DE   acetoin dehydrogenase system.
AN   acetoin dehydrogenase.
CA   acetoin + NAD(+) + CoA = acetaldehyde + acetyl-CoA + NADH + H(+).
CC   -!- Requires thiamine diphosphate.
CC   -!- It belongs to the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase system family, which also
CC       includes EC 1.2.1.104, EC 1.2.1.105, EC 1.2.1.25 and EC 1.4.1.27.
CC   -!- With the exception of the glycine cleavage system, which contains 4
CC       components, the 2-oxoacid dehydrogenase systems share a common
CC       structure, consisting of three main components, namely a 2-oxoacid
CC       dehydrogenase (E1), a dihydrolipoamide acyltransferase (E2),
CC       and dihydrolipoamide dehydrogenase (E3).
//
ID   2.3.1.191
DE   UDP-3-O-(3-hydroxymyristoyl)glucosamine N-acyltransferase.
AN   UDP-3-O-[3-hydroxymyristoyl]-D-glucosamine N-acyltransferase.
AN   UDP-3-O-acyl-glucosamine N-acyltransferase.
CA   a UDP-3-O-[(3R)-3-hydroxyacyl]-alpha-D-glucosamine + a (3R)-hydroxyacyl-
CA   [ACP] = a UDP-2-N,3-O-bis[(3R)-3-hydroxyacyl]-alpha-D-glucosamine + holo-
CA   [ACP] + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes a step of lipid A biosynthesis.
CC   -!- LpxD from Escherichia coli prefers (3R)-3-hydroxytetradecanoyl-[acyl-
CC       carrier protein], but it does not an absolute specificity for
CC       14-carbon hydroxy fatty acids, as it can transfer other fatty acids,
CC       including odd-chain fatty acids, if they are available to the
CC       organism.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.1.n1.
