ID   2.3.1.195
DE   (Z)-3-hexen-1-ol acetyltransferase.
CA   (3Z)-hex-3-en-1-ol + acetyl-CoA = (3Z)-hex-3-en-1-yl acetate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is resonsible for the production of (3Z)-hex-3-en-1-yl
CC       acetate, the major volatile compound released upon mechanical
CC       wounding of the leaves of Arabidopsis thaliana.
DR   Q9SRQ2, CHAT_ARATH ;
//
ID   2.3.1.196
DE   benzyl alcohol O-benzoyltransferase.
CA   benzyl alcohol + benzoyl-CoA = benzyl benzoate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in volatile benzenoid and benzoic acid
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Petunia hybrida also catalyzes the formation of
CC       2-phenylethyl benzoate from benzoyl-CoA and 2-phenylethanol.
CC   -!- The apparent catalytic efficiency of the enzyme from Petunia hybrida
CC       with benzoyl-CoA is almost 6-fold higher than with acetyl-CoA.
DR   Q3ZPN4, ACMAT_VITLA;  Q6E593, BEBT1_PETHY;  Q8GT21, BEBT_CLABR ;
DR   Q8GT20, BEBT_TOBAC ;
