ID   2.3.1.199
DE   very-long-chain 3-oxoacyl-CoA synthase.
AN   condensing enzyme.
AN   very-long-chain 3-ketoacyl-CoA synthase.
AN   very-long-chain beta-ketoacyl-CoA synthase.
CA   a very-long-chain acyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + H(+) = a very-long-chain
CA   3-oxoacyl-CoA + CO2 + CoA.
CC   -!- This is the first component of the elongase, a microsomal protein
CC       complex responsible for extending palmitoyl-CoA and stearoyl-CoA (and
CC       modified forms thereof) to very-long-chain acyl CoAs.
CC   -!- Multiple forms exist with differing preferences for the substrate,
CC       and thus the specific form expressed determines the local composition
CC       of very-long-chain fatty acids.
CC   -!- For example, the FAE1 form from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana
CC       accepts only 16 and 18 carbon substrates, with oleoyl-CoA (18:1)
CC       being the preferred substrate, while CER6 from the same plant prefers
CC       substrates with chain length of C22 to C32. cf. EC 1.1.1.330,
CC       EC 1.3.1.93 and EC 4.2.1.134.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.1.119 and EC 2.3.1.n8.
