ID   2.3.1.207
DE   beta-ketodecanoyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] synthase.
CA   octanoyl-CoA + malonyl-[ACP] + H(+) = 3-oxodecanoyl-[ACP] + CO2 + CoA.
CC   -!- This enzyme, which has been characterized from the bacterium
CC       Pseudomonas aeruginosa PAO1, catalyzes the condensation of octanoyl-
CC       CoA, obtained from exogenously supplied fatty acids via beta-
CC       oxidation, with malonyl-[acp], forming 3-oxodecanoyl-[acp],
CC       an intermediate of the fatty acid elongation cycle.
CC   -!- The enzyme provides a shunt for beta-oxidation degradation
CC       intermediates into de novo fatty acid biosynthesis.
DR   Q9HYV7, BEKAS_PSEAE;
//
ID   2.3.1.208
DE   4-hydroxycoumarin synthase.
CA   2-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA = 4-hydroxycoumarin + CO2 + 2 CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, a polyketide synthase, can also accept benzoyl-CoA as
CC       substrate, which it condenses with 3 malonyl-CoA molecules to form
CC       3,5-dihydroxybiphenyl (cf. EC 2.3.1.177).
DR   D2DRC4, BIPS2_SORAU;  D2DRC5, BIPS3_SORAU;
//
ID   2.3.1.209
DE   dTDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-D-glucose acyltransferase.
CA   dTDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose + acetyl-CoA = dTDP-4-acetamido-
CA   4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The non-activated product, 4-acetamido-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose,
CC       is part of the O antigens of Shigella dysenteriae type 7 and
CC       Escherichia coli O7.
DR   Q9XCW3, VIOB_ECOLX ;
//
ID   2.3.1.210
DE   dTDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-D-galactose acyltransferase.
AN   TDP-fucosamine acetyltransferase.
CA   dTDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-galactose + acetyl-CoA = dTDP-4-
CA   acetamido-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-galactose + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The product, TDP-4-acetamido-4,6-dideoxy-D-galactose, is utilized in
CC       the biosynthesis of Enterobacterial Common Antigen (ECA).
DR   Q8FBQ3, WECD_ECOL6 ;  P27832, WECD_ECOLI ;
//
ID   2.3.1.211
DE   bisdemethoxycurcumin synthase.
AN   curcuminoid synthase.
CA   2 4-coumaroyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + H2O + H(+) = bisdemethoxycurcumin +
CA   2 CO2 + 3 CoA.
CC   -!- A polyketide synthase characterized from the plant Oryza sativa
CC       (rice) that catalyzes the formation of the C6-C7-C6 diarylheptanoid
CC       scaffold of bisdemethoxycurcumin.
CC   -!- Unlike the process in the plant Curcuma longa (turmeric), where the
CC       conversion is carried out via a diketide intermediate by two
CC       different enzymes, the diketide intermediate formed by this enzyme
CC       remains within the enzyme's cavity and is not released to the
CC       environment.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.1.n9.
DR   Q8LIL0, CUS_ORYSJ  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.212
DE   benzalacetone synthase.
CA   4-coumaroyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + H2O + H(+) = 4-hydroxybenzalacetone +
CA   2 CO2 + 2 CoA.
CC   -!- A polyketide synthase that catalyzes the C6-C4 skeleton of
CC       phenylbutanoids in higher plants.
DR   Q94FV7, BAS_RHEPA  ;  B0LDU5, PKS4_RUBID ;
//
ID   2.3.1.213
DE   cyanidin 3-O-(6-O-glucosyl-2-O-xylosylgalactoside) 6'''-O-
DE   hydroxycinnamoyltransferase.
CA   cyanidin 3-O-(6-O-glucosyl-2-O-xylosylgalactoside) betaine + 1-O-[(E)-4-
CA   coumaroyl]-beta-D-glucose = cyanidin 3-O-[6-O-(6-O-4-hydroxycinnamoyl-
CA   beta-D-glucosyl)-2-O-beta-D-xylosyl-beta-D-galactoside] + beta-D-glucose
CA   + H(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Daucus carota (Afghan cultivar carrot).
CC   -!- In addition to 1-O-(4-hydroxycinnamoyl)-beta-D-glucose, the enzyme
CC       can use the 1-O-sinapoyl- and 1-O-feruloyl- derivatives of beta-D-
CC       glucose.
//
ID   2.3.1.214
DE   pelargonidin 3-O-(6-caffeoylglucoside) 5-O-(6-O-malonylglucoside)
DE   4'''-malonyltransferase.
CA   4'''-demalonylsalvianin + malonyl-CoA = salvianin + CoA.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Salvia splendens (scarlet sage).
DR   Q6TXD2, 5MAT2_SALSN;
//
ID   2.3.1.215
DE   anthocyanidin 3-O-glucoside 6''-O-acyltransferase.
CA   an anthocyanidin 3-O-beta-D-glucoside + (E)-4-coumaroyl-CoA =
CA   an anthocyanidin 3-O-[6-O-(4-hydroxycinnamoyl)-beta-D-glucoside] + CoA +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the plants Perilla frutescens and Gentiana triflora
CC       (clustered gentian).
CC   -!- Acts on a range of anthocyanidin 3-O-glucosides, 3,5-di-O-glucosides
CC       and cyanidin 3-rutinoside.
CC   -!- It did not act on delphinidin 3,3',7-tri-O-glucoside.
CC   -!- Recombinant Perilla frutescens enzyme could utilize caffeoyl-CoA but
CC       not malonyl-CoA as alternative acyl donor.
DR   Q9MBC1, 3AT_PERFR  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.216
DE   5,7-dihydroxy-2-methylchromone synthase.
AN   pentaketide chromone synthase.
CA   5 malonyl-CoA + 4 H(+) = 5,7-dihydroxy-2-methyl-4H-chromen-4-one + 5 CO2
CA   + 5 CoA + H2O.
CC   -!- A polyketide synthase from the plant Aloe arborescens (aloe).
DR   Q58VP7, PCS_ALOAR  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.217
DE   curcumin synthase.
CA   (E)-feruloylacetyl-CoA + (E)-feruloyl-CoA + H2O = curcumin + CO2 + 2 CoA.
CC   -!- A polyketide synthase from the plant Curcuma longa (turmeric).
CC   -!- Three isoforms exist, CURS1, CURS2 and CURS3.
CC   -!- While CURS1 and CURS2 prefer feruloyl-CoA as a starter substrate,
CC       CURS3 can accept 4-coumaroyl-CoA equally well (see EC 2.3.1.219).
DR   C0SVZ6, CURS1_CURLO;  C6L7V8, CURS2_CURLO;  C6L7V9, CURS3_CURLO;
//
ID   2.3.1.218
DE   phenylpropanoylacetyl-CoA synthase.
AN   phenylpropanoyl-diketide-CoA synthase.
CA   (1) (E)-feruloyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + H(+) = (E)-feruloylacetyl-CoA +
CA   CO2 + CoA.
CA   (2) 4-coumaroyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + H(+) = (4-coumaroyl)acetyl-CoA +
CA   CO2 + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from the plant Curcuma longa
CC       (turmeric).
CC   -!- It prefers feruloyl-CoA, and has no activity with cinnamoyl-CoA.
DR   C0SVZ5, DCS_CURLO  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.219
DE   demethoxycurcumin synthase.
CA   (1) (E)-feruloylacetyl-CoA + (E)-4-coumaroyl-CoA + H2O =
CA   demethoxycurcumin + CO2 + 2 CoA.
CA   (2) (4-coumaroyl)acetyl-CoA + 4-coumaroyl-CoA + H2O =
CA   bisdemethoxycurcumin + CO2 + 2 CoA.
CC   -!- A polyketide synthase from the plant Curcuma longa (turmeric).
CC   -!- Three isoforms exist, CURS1, CURS2 and CURS3.
CC   -!- While CURS1 and CURS2 prefer feruloyl-CoA as a starter substrate (cf.
CC       EC 2.3.1.217), CURS3 can accept 4-coumaroyl-CoA equally well.
DR   C6L7V9, CURS3_CURLO;
//
ID   2.3.1.220
DE   2,4,6-trihydroxybenzophenone synthase.
AN   benzophenone synthase.
CA   benzoyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 2 H(+) = 2,4,6-trihydroxybenzophenone +
CA   3 CO2 + 4 CoA.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of plant xanthones.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the plant Hypericum androsaemum L can use
CC       3-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA instead of benzoyl-CoA, but with lower activity
CC       (cf. EC 2.3.1.151).
DR   L7NCQ3, TBSYN_GARMA;  Q8SAS8, TBSYN_HYPAN;
//
ID   2.3.1.221
DE   noranthrone synthase.
AN   norsolorinic acid anthrone synthase.
AN   polyketide synthase A.
CA   hexanoyl-[ACP] + 7 malonyl-CoA + 6 H(+) = noranthrone + holo-[ACP] +
CA   7 CO2 + 7 CoA + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- A multi-domain polyketide synthase involved in the synthesis of
CC       aflatoxins in the fungus Aspergillus parasiticus.
CC   -!- The hexanoyl starter unit is provided to the acyl-carrier protein
CC       (ACP) domain by a dedicated fungal fatty acid synthase.
DR   Q12053, AFLC_ASPPU ;  Q30DW5, PKSA_DOTSE ;  M2XHZ5, PKSA_DOTSN ;
DR   Q12397, STCA_EMENI ;
//
ID   2.3.1.222
DE   phosphate propanoyltransferase.
CA   propanoyl-CoA + phosphate = propanoyl phosphate + CoA.
CC   -!- Part of the degradation pathway for 1,2-propanediol.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.1.n10.
DR   A6TJX7, PDUL_ALKMQ ;  B1VB71, PDUL_CITFR ;  A8AEM8, PDUL_CITK8 ;
DR   D2TPR5, PDUL_CITRI ;  Q187N2, PDUL_CLOD6 ;  A0Q2W0, PDUL_CLONN ;
DR   Q834M4, PDUL_ENTFA ;  B7LTW5, PDUL_ESCF3 ;  A6TDD9, PDUL_KLEP7 ;
