ID   2.3.1.226
DE   carboxymethylproline synthase.
CA   (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate + malonyl-CoA + H2O + H(+) = (2S,5S)-5-
CA   carboxymethylproline + CO2 + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the carbapenem beta-
CC       lactam antibiotic (5R)-carbapen-2-em-3-carboxylate in the bacterium
CC       Pectobacterium carotovorum.
DR   Q9XB60, CARB_PECCC ;
//
ID   2.3.1.227
DE   GDP-perosamine N-acetyltransferase.
AN   GDP-alpha-D-perosamine N-acetyltransferase.
CA   GDP-alpha-D-perosamine + acetyl-CoA = GDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-perosamine +
CA   CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- D-Perosamine is one of several dideoxy sugars found in the O-antigen
CC       component of the outer membrane lipopolysaccharides of Gram-negative
CC       bacteria.
DR   Q7DBF7, PERB_ECO57 ;
//
ID   2.3.1.228
DE   isovaleryl-homoserine lactone synthase.
AN   IV-HSL synthase.
CA   3-methylbutanoyl-CoA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N-isovaleryl-L-
CA   homoserine lactone + S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in the bacterium Bradyrhizobium japonicum, does not
CC       accept isovaleryl-[acyl-carrier protein] as acyl donor (cf.
CC       EC 2.3.1.184).
DR   Q89VI2, BJAI_BRADU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.229
DE   4-coumaroyl-homoserine lactone synthase.
AN   p-coumaryl-homoserine lactone synthase.
CA   4-coumaroyl-CoA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = N-(4-coumaroyl)-L-homoserine
CA   lactone + S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in the bacterium Rhodopseudomonas palustris,
CC       which produces N-(4-coumaroyl)-L-homoserine lactone as a quorum-
CC       sensing signal.
DR   Q6NCZ6, RPAI_RHOPA ;
//
ID   2.3.1.230
DE   2-heptyl-4(1H)-quinolone synthase.
CA   (2-aminobenzoyl)acetate + octanoyl-CoA + H(+) = 2-heptyl-4(1H)-quinolone
CA   + CO2 + CoA + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa,
CC       is a heterodimeric complex.
CC   -!- The PqsC subunit acquires an octanoyl group from octanoyl-CoA and
CC       attaches it to an internal cysteine residue.
CC   -!- Together with the PqsB subunit, the proteins catalyze the coupling of
CC       the octanoyl group with (2-aminobenzoyl)acetate, leading to
CC       decarboxylation and dehydration events that result in closure of the
CC       quinoline ring.
DR   Q9I4X1, PQSC_PSEAE ;
//
ID   2.3.1.231
DE   tRNA(Phe) {7-[3-amino-3-(methoxycarbonyl)propyl]wyosine(37)-N}-
DE   methoxycarbonyltransferase.
AN   tRNA-yW synthesizing enzyme-4.
CA   7-[(3S)-(3-amino-3-methoxycarbonyl)propyl]wyosine(37) in tRNA(Phe) +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + CO2 = wybutosine(37) in tRNA(Phe) + S-adenosyl-
CA   L-homocysteine + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is found only in eukaryotes, where it is involved in the
CC       biosynthesis of wybutosine, a hypermodified tricyclic base found at
CC       position 37 of certain tRNAs.
CC   -!- The modification is important for translational reading-frame
CC       maintenance.
CC   -!- In some species that produce hydroxywybutosine the enzyme uses
CC       7-[2-hydroxy-3-amino-3-(methoxycarbonyl)propyl]wyosine(37) in
CC       tRNA(Phe) as substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme also has the activity of EC 2.1.1.290.
DR   Q4WVD1, TYW4_ASPFU ;  Q2U6D4, TYW4_ASPOR ;  Q5A931, TYW4_CANAL ;
DR   Q6FXA5, TYW4_CANGA ;  Q5BH52, TYW4_EMENI ;  Q75AW4, TYW4_EREGS ;
DR   Q4IER0, TYW4_GIBZE ;  O60294, TYW4_HUMAN ;  Q8BYR1, TYW4_MOUSE ;
DR   Q9P3K9, TYW4_NEUCR ;  Q5XIA3, TYW4_RAT   ;  O60157, TYW4_SCHPO ;
DR   Q6C3P4, TYW4_YARLI ;  Q08282, TYW4_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.3.1.232
DE   methanol O-anthraniloyltransferase.
CA   anthraniloyl-CoA + methanol = O-methyl anthranilate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Concord grape (Vitis labrusca) is solely responsible
CC       for the production of O-methyl anthranilate, an important aroma and
CC       flavor compound in the grape.
CC   -!- The enzyme has a broad substrate specificity, and can use a range of
CC       alcohols with substantial activity, the best being butanol, benzyl
CC       alcohol, iso-pentanol, octanol and 2-propanol.
CC   -!- It can use benzoyl-CoA and acetyl-CoA as acyl donors with lower
CC       efficiency.
CC   -!- In addition to O-methyl anthranilate, the enzyme might be responsible
CC       for the production of ethyl butanoate, methyl-3-hydroxy butanoate and
CC       ethyl-3-hydroxy butanoate, which are present in large quantities in
CC       the grapes.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes EC 2.3.1.196.
DR   Q3ZPN4, ACMAT_VITLA;
//
ID   2.3.1.233
DE   1,3,6,8-tetrahydroxynaphthalene synthase.
AN   THNS.
CA   5 malonyl-CoA + 5 H(+) = naphthalene-1,3,6,8-tetrol + 5 CO2 + 5 CoA +
CA   H2O.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Colletotrichum lagenarium, and the bacteria
CC       Streptomyces coelicolor and Streptomyces peucetius.
CC   -!- It only uses malonyl-CoA, without invovement of acetyl-CoA.
DR   B0FYK7, RPPA_STRC0 ;  Q9FCA7, RPPA_STRCO ;  Q54240, RPPA_STRGR ;
//
ID   2.3.1.234
DE   N(6)-L-threonylcarbamoyladenine synthase.
AN   t6A synthase.
CA   L-threonylcarbamoyladenylate + adenosine(37) in tRNA = N(6)-L-
CA   threonylcarbamoyladenosine(37) in tRNA + AMP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the synthesis of N(6)-
CC       threonylcarbamoyladenosine(37) in tRNAs, which is found in tRNAs with
CC       the anticodon NNU, i.e. tRNA(Ile), tRNA(Thr), tRNA(Asn), tRNA(Lys),
CC       tRNA(Ser) and tRNA(Arg).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.6.99.4.
