//
ID   2.3.1.235
DE   tetracenomycin F2 synthase.
CA   10 malonyl-CoA + 8 H(+) = tetracenomycin F2 + 10 CO2 + 10 CoA + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- A multi-domain polyketide synthase involved in the synthesis of
CC       tetracenomycin in the bacterium Streptomyces glaucescens.
CC   -!- It involves a ketosynthase complex, an acyl carrier protein,
CC       a malonyl CoA:ACP acyltransferase, and a cyclase.
CC   -!- A malonyl-CoA molecule is initially bound to the acyl carrier protein
CC       and decarboxylated to form an acetyl starter unit.
CC   -!- Additional two-carbon units are added from nine more malonyl-CoA
CC       molecules.
DR   P16558, TCMJ_STRGA ;  P16538, TCMK_STRGA ;  P16539, TCML_STRGA ;
DR   P12884, TCMM_STRGA ;  P16559, TCMN_STRGA ;
//
ID   2.3.1.236
DE   5-methylnaphthoic acid synthase.
CA   5 malonyl-CoA + acetyl-CoA + 3 NADPH + 7 H(+) = 5-methyl-1-naphthoate +
CA   5 CO2 + 3 NADP(+) + 6 CoA + 4 H2O.
CC   -!- A multi-domain polyketide synthase involved in the synthesis of
CC       azinomycin B in the bacterium Streptomyces griseofuscus.
DR   B4XYB8, AZIB_STREG ;
//
ID   2.3.1.237
DE   neocarzinostatin naphthoate synthase.
AN   naphthoic acid synthase.
CA   5 malonyl-CoA + acetyl-CoA + 2 NADPH + 6 H(+) = 2-hydroxy-5-methyl-1-
CA   naphthoate + 5 CO2 + 2 NADP(+) + 6 CoA + 3 H2O.
CC   -!- A multi-domain polyketide synthase involved in the synthesis of
CC       neocarzinostatin in the bacterium Streptomyces carzinostaticus.
DR   Q84HC6, NCSB_STRCZ ;
//
ID   2.3.1.238
DE   monacolin J acid methylbutanoate transferase.
CA   monacolin J carboxylate + (S)-2-methylbutanoyl-[2-methylbutanoate
CA   polyketide synthase] = lovastatin carboxylate + holo-[2-methylbutanoate
CA   polyketide synthase].
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the ultimate reaction in the lovastatin
CC       biosynthesis pathway of the filamentous fungus Aspergillus terreus.
DR   Q9Y7D1, LOVD_ASPTE ;  Q0C8M0, LOVD_ASPTN ;  Q3S2U2, MOKF_MONPI ;
//
ID   2.3.1.239
DE   10-deoxymethynolide syntase.
AN   (2S)-methylmalonyl-CoA:malonyl-CoA malonyltransferase
AN   (10-deoxymethynolide forming).
CA   5 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + 5 NADPH + 11 H(+) =
CA   10-deoxymethynolide + 6 CO2 + 5 NADP(+) + 6 CoA + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The product, 10-deoxymethynolide, contains a 12-membered ring and is
CC       an intermediate in the biosynthesis of methymycin in the bacterium
CC       Streptomyces venezuelae.
CC   -!- The enzyme also produces narbonolide (see EC 2.3.1.240).
CC   -!- The enzyme has 29 active sites arranged in four polypeptides (pikAI -
CC       pikAIV) with a loading domain, six extension modules and a terminal
CC       thioesterase domain.
CC   -!- Each extension module contains a ketosynthase (KS), keto reductase
CC       (KR), an acyltransferase (AT) and an acyl-carrier protein (ACP).
CC   -!- Not all active sites are used in the biosynthesis.
DR   Q9ZGI5, PIKA1_STRVZ;  Q9ZGI4, PIKA2_STRVZ;  Q9ZGI3, PIKA3_STRVZ;
DR   Q9ZGI2, PIKA4_STRVZ;
//
ID   2.3.1.240
DE   narbonolide synthase.
AN   pikromycin PKS.
CA   6 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + 5 NADPH + 12 H(+) = narbonolide +
CA   7 CO2 + 5 NADP(+) + 7 CoA + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The product, narbonolide, contains a 14-membered ring and is an
CC       intermediate in the biosynthesis of narbonomycin and pikromycin in
CC       the bacterium Streptomyces venezuelae.
CC   -!- The enzyme also produces 10-deoxymethynolide (see EC 2.3.1.239).
CC   -!- The enzyme has 29 active sites arranged in four polypeptides (pikAI -
CC       pikAIV) with a loading domain, six extension modules and a terminal
CC       thioesterase domain.
CC   -!- Each extension module contains a ketosynthase (KS), keto reductase
CC       (KR), an acyltransferase (AT) and an acyl-carrier protein (ACP).
CC   -!- Not all active sites are used in the biosynthesis.
DR   Q9ZGI5, PIKA1_STRVZ;  Q9ZGI4, PIKA2_STRVZ;  Q9ZGI3, PIKA3_STRVZ;
DR   Q9ZGI2, PIKA4_STRVZ;
//
ID   2.3.1.241
DE   Kdo2-lipid IVA acyltransferase.
AN   (Kdo)2-lipid IVA lauroyltransferase.
AN   alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-(2->6)-lipid IVA lauroyltransferase.
AN   Kdo2-lipid IVA lauroyltransferase.
CA   an alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-lipid IVA + a fatty acyl-[ACP] =
CA   an alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-(acyl)-lipid IVA + holo-[ACP].
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the phosphorylated
CC       outer membrane glycolipid lipid A.
CC   -!- It transfers an acyl group to the 3-O position of the 3R-hydroxyacyl
CC       already attached to the nitrogen of the non-reducing glucosamine
CC       molecule.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli is specific for lauryl
CC       (C12) acyl groups, giving the enzyme its previous accepted name.
CC   -!- However, enzymes from different species accept highly variable
CC       substrates.
DR   P0ACV1, LPXL_ECO57 ;  P0ACV0, LPXL_ECOLI ;  P45239, LPXL_HAEIN ;
//
ID   2.3.1.242
DE   Kdo2-lipid IVA palmitoleoyltransferase.
AN   (Kdo)2-lipid IVA palmitoleoyltransferase.
AN   alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-(2->6)-lipid IVA palmitoleoyltransferase.
AN   cold-induced palmitoleoyl transferase.
AN   palmitoleoyl-acyl carrier protein-dependent acyltransferase.
CA   (9Z)-hexadecenoyl-[ACP] + alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-lipid IVA (E.
CA   coli) = (9Z)-hexadecenoyl-(Kdo)2-lipid IVA (E. coli) + holo-[ACP].
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli,
CC       is induced upon cold shock and is involved in the formation of a
CC       cold-adapted variant of the outer membrane glycolipid lipid A.
DR   P0ACV2, LPXP_ECOLI ;  P0ACV3, LPXP_SHIFL ;
//
ID   2.3.1.243
DE   acyl-Kdo2-lipid IVA acyltransferase.
AN   acyl-Kdo2-lipid IVA myristoyltransferase.
AN   myristoyl-[acyl-carrier protein]:alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-
AN   (dodecanoyl)-lipid IVA O-myristoyltransferase.
CA   an alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-(acyl)-lipid IVA + a fatty acyl-
CA   [ACP] = an alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-lipid A + holo-[ACP].
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the phosphorylated
CC       outer membrane glycolipid lipid A.
CC   -!- It transfers an acyl group to the 3-O position of the 3R-hydroxyacyl
CC       already attached at the 2-O position of the non-reducing glucosamine
CC       molecule.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli is specific for
CC       myristoyl (C14) acyl groups, giving the enzyme its previous accepted
CC       name.
CC   -!- However, enzymes from different species accept highly variable
CC       substrates.
DR   P59198, LPXM1_SHIFL;  O06659, LPXM2_SHIFL;  P24205, LPXM_ECOLI ;
DR   P44567, LPXM_HAEIN ;
//
ID   2.3.1.244
DE   2-methylbutanoate polyketide synthase.
CA   holo-[2-methylbutanoate polyketide synthase] + 2 malonyl-CoA +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + 2 NADPH + 3 H(+) = (S)-2-methylbutanoyl-
CA   [2-methylbutanoate polyketide synthase] + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   2 CO2 + 2 NADP(+) + 2 CoA + H2O.
CC   -!- This polyketide synthase enzyme forms the (S)-2-methylbutanoate side
CC       chain during lovastatin biosynthesis by the filamentous fungus
CC       Aspergillus terreus.
CC   -!- The overall reaction comprises a single condensation reaction
CC       followed by alpha-methylation, beta-ketoreduction, dehydration,
CC       and alpha,beta enoyl reduction.
DR   Q9Y7D5, LOVF_ASPTE ;  Q0C8L6, LOVF_ASPTN ;  Q8J0F5, MLCB_PENCI ;
DR   Q3S2U6, MOKB_MONPI ;
//
ID   2.3.1.245
DE   3-hydroxy-5-phosphooxypentane-2,4-dione thiolase.
AN   3-hydroxy-5-phosphonooxypentane-2,4-dione thiolase.
CA   dihydroxyacetone phosphate + acetyl-CoA = 3-hydroxy-2,4-dioxopentyl
CA   phosphate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in a degradation pathway of the bacterial
CC       quorum-sensing autoinducer molecule AI-2.
DR   A7ZLX4, LSRF_ECO24 ;  Q8XAZ1, LSRF_ECO57 ;  B1XEA5, LSRF_ECODH ;
DR   A8A070, LSRF_ECOHS ;  B1IRU3, LSRF_ECOLC ;  P76143, LSRF_ECOLI ;
