ID   2.3.1.271
DE   L-glutamate-5-semialdehyde N-acetyltransferase.
CA   L-glutamate 5-semialdehyde + acetyl-CoA = N-acetyl-L-glutamate
CA   5-semialdehyde + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae
CC       Sigma1278b, N-acetylates L-glutamate-5-semialdehyde, an L-proline
CC       biosynthesis/utilization intermediate, into N-acetyl-L-glutamate
CC       5-semialdehyde, an intermediate of L-arginine biosynthesis, under
CC       oxidative stress conditions.
CC   -!- Its activity results in conversion of L-proline to L-arginine,
CC       and reduction in the concentration of L-glutamate 5-semialdehyde and
CC       its equilibrium partner, (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate, which has
CC       been linked to production of reactive oxygen species stress.
CC   -!- The enzyme also acts on (S)-1-acetylazetidine-2-carboxylate, a toxic
CC       L-proline analog produced by some plants, resulting in its
CC       detoxification and conferring resistance on the yeast.
DR   Q09927, ACA1_SCHPO ;  E9P8D2, MPR1_YEASX ;
//
ID   2.3.1.272
DE   2-acetylphloroglucinol acetyltransferase.
AN   MAPG ATase.
CA   2 2-acetylphloroglucinol = 2,4-diacetylphloroglucinol + 1,3,5-
CA   trihydroxybenzene + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas sp. YGJ3 is composed of
CC       three subunits named PhlA, PhlB and PhlC.
CC   -!- Production of 2,4-diacetylphloroglucinol, which has antibiotic
CC       activity, is strongly inhibited by chloride ions.
//
ID   2.3.1.273
DE   diglucosylglycerate octanoyltransferase.
AN   DGG octanoyltransferase.
CA   (2R)-2-O-[alpha-D-glucopyranosyl-(1->6)-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl]-glycerate
CA   + octanoyl-CoA = (2R)-2-O-[6-O-octanoyl-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl-(1->6)-
CA   alpha-D-glucopyranosyl]-glycerate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from mycobacteria, is involved in the
CC       biosynthesis of methylglucose lipopolysaccharide (MGLP).
CC   -!- The enzyme can also act on 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate,
CC       but with lower activity.
DR   K5BJH8, OCTT_MYCHD ;  A0R109, OCTT_MYCS2 ;  P71725, OCTT_MYCTU ;
