ID   2.3.1.276
DE   galactosamine-1-phosphate N-acetyltransferase.
CA   alpha-D-galactosamine 1-phosphate + acetyl-CoA = N-acetyl-alpha-D-
CA   galactosamine 1-phosphate + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Sulfolobus tokodaii,
CC       is also active toward alpha-D-glucosamine 1-phosphate (cf.
CC       EC 2.3.1.157).
CC   -!- In addition, that enzyme contains a second domain that catalyzes the
CC       activities of EC 2.7.7.23, EC 2.7.7.24, and EC 2.7.7.83.
DR   Q975F9, S1PNA_SULTO;
//
ID   2.3.1.277
DE   phosphorylated butenolide synthase.
AN   2-oxo-3-(phosphooxy)propyl 3-oxoalkanoate synthase.
CA   a medium-chain 3-oxoacyl-[ACP] + dihydroxyacetone phosphate =
CA   a (4-alkanoyl-5-oxo-2,5-dihydrofuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate + holo-[ACP] +
CA   H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the first committed step in the biosynthesis of
CC       gamma-butyrolactone, as well as 2-alkyl-4-hydroxymethylfuran-3-
CC       carboxylate (methylenomycin furan) autoregulators that control
CC       secondary metabolism and morphological development in Streptomyces
CC       bacteria.
DR   B1VN93, AFSA_STRGG ;  P18394, AFSA_STRGR ;  O24738, BARX_STRVG ;
DR   Q7AKF0, SCBA_STRCO ;
//
ID   2.3.1.278
DE   mycolipenoyl-CoA--2-(long-chain-fatty acyl)-trehalose
DE   mycolipenoyltransferase.
CA   a mycolipenoyl-CoA + a 2-O-(long-chain fatty acyl)-alpha,alpha-trehalose
CA   = a 2-O-(long-chain fatty acyl)-3-O-mycolipenoyl-trehalose + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mycobacterium
CC       tuberculosis, participates in the biosynthesis of polyacyltrehalose
CC       (PAT), a pentaacylated, trehalose-based glycolipid found in the cell
CC       wall of pathogenic strains.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes two successive activities - it first transfers
CC       an acyl (often palmitoyl) group to position 2 (see EC 2.3.1.279),
CC       followed by the transfer of a mycolipenyl group to position 3.
DR   P9WIK4, PAPA3_MYCTO;  P9WIK5, PAPA3_MYCTU;
//
ID   2.3.1.279
DE   long-chain-acyl-CoA--trehalose acyltransferase.
CA   a long-chain fatty acyl-CoA + alpha,alpha-trehalose = a 2-O-(long-chain
CA   fatty acyl)-alpha,alpha-trehalose + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mycobacterium
CC       tuberculosis, participates in the biosynthesis of polyacyltrehalose
CC       (PAT), a pentaacylated, trehalose-based glycolipid found in the cell
CC       wall of pathogenic strains.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes two successive activities - it first transfers
CC       an acyl (often palmitoyl) group to position 2, followed by the
CC       transfer of a mycolipenyl group to position 3 (see EC 2.3.1.278).
DR   P9WIK4, PAPA3_MYCTO;  P9WIK5, PAPA3_MYCTU;
//
ID   2.3.1.280
DE   (aminoalkyl)phosphonate N-acetyltransferase.
CA   aminomethylphosphonate + acetyl-CoA = 2-N-acetamidomethylphosphonate +
CA   CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli,
CC       is able to acetylate a range of (aminoalkyl)phosphonic acids.
CC   -!- Requires a divalent metal ion for activity.
DR   P16691, PHNO_ECOLI ;  Q8ZKE6, PHNO_SALTY ;
//
ID   2.3.1.281
DE   coelimycin P1 polyketide synthase.
CA   6 malonyl-CoA + NADH + 5 NADPH + 12 H(+) = (2E,5S,6E,8E,10E)-5-
CA   hydroxydodeca-2,6,8,10-tetraenal + 6 CO2 + NAD(+) + 5 NADP(+) + 6 CoA +
CA   4 H2O.
CC   -!- This polyketide synthase enzyme, characterized from the bacterium
CC       Streptomyces coelicolor A3(2), catalyzes the first reaction in the
CC       biosynthesis of coelimycin P1.
CC   -!- The enzyme is made of three proteins which together comprise six
CC       modules that contain a total of 28 domains.
CC   -!- An NADH-dependent terminal reductase domain at the C-terminus of the
CC       enzyme catalyzes the reductive release of the product.
//
ID   2.3.1.282
DE   phenolphthiocerol/phthiocerol/phthiodiolone dimycocerosyl transferase.
CA   (1) 2 a mycocerosyl-[mycocerosic acid synthase] + a phthiocerol =
CA   a dimycocerosyl phthiocerol + 2 holo-[mycocerosic acid synthase].
CA   (2) 2 a mycocerosyl-[mycocerosic acid synthase] + a phthiodiolone =
CA   a dimycocerosyl phthiodiolone + 2 holo-[mycocerosic acid synthase].
CA   (3) 2 a mycocerosyl-[mycocerosic acid synthase] + a phenolphthiocerol =
CA   a dimycocerosyl phenolphthiocerol + 2 holo-[mycocerosic acid synthase].
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in certain pathogenic species of mycobacteria,
CC       catalyzes the transfer of mycocerosic acids to the two hydroxyl
CC       groups at the common lipid core of phthiocerol, phthiodiolone,
CC       and phenolphthiocerol, forming dimycocerosate esters.
CC   -!- The fatty acid precursors of mycocerosic acids are activated by
CC       EC 6.2.1.49, which loads them onto EC 2.3.1.111.
CC   -!- That enzyme extends the precursors to form mycocerosic acids that
CC       remain attached until transferred by EC 2.3.1.282.
DR   Q02279, PAPA5_MYCBO;  A1KMT4, PAPA5_MYCBP;  Q49939, PAPA5_MYCLE;
DR   A3Q0G0, PAPA5_MYCSJ;  A1UGV8, PAPA5_MYCSK;  Q1B849, PAPA5_MYCSS;
DR   A5U6U6, PAPA5_MYCTA;  P9WIN4, PAPA5_MYCTO;  P9WIN5, PAPA5_MYCTU;
DR   A0PQ31, PAPA5_MYCUA;  A1T9S1, PAPA5_MYCVP;
//
ID   2.3.1.283
DE   2'-acyl-2-O-sulfo-trehalose (hydroxy)phthioceranyltransferase.
CA   a (hydroxy)phthioceranyl-[(hydroxy)phthioceranic acid synthase] +
CA   2'-palmitoyl/stearoyl-2-O-sulfo-alpha,alpha-trehalose =
CA   a 3'-(hydroxy)phthioceranyl-2'-palmitoyl/stearoyl-2-O-sulfo-alpha,alpha-
CA   trehalose + holo-[(hydroxy)phthioceranic acid synthase].
CC   -!- This mycobacterial enzyme catalyzes the acylation of
CC       2'-palmitoyl/stearoyl-2-O-sulfo-alpha,alpha-trehalose at the 3'
CC       position by a (hydroxy)phthioceranoyl group during the biosynthesis
CC       of mycobacterial sulfolipids.
DR   Q7TVK9, PAPA1_MYCBO;  A1KQF9, PAPA1_MYCBP;  A5U9F3, PAPA1_MYCTA;
DR   P9WIK8, PAPA1_MYCTO;  P9WIK9, PAPA1_MYCTU;
//
ID   2.3.1.284
DE   3'-(hydroxy)phthioceranyl-2'-palmitoyl(stearoyl)-2-O-sulfo-trehalose
DE   (hydroxy)phthioceranyltransferase.
CA   3 3'-(hydroxy)phthioceranyl-2'-palmitoyl(stearoyl)-2-O-sulfo-alpha,alpha-
CA   trehalose = 3,6,6'-tris-(hydroxy)phthioceranyl-2-palmitoyl(stearoyl)-
CA   2'-sulfo-alpha-alpha-trehalose + 2 2'-palmitoyl/stearoyl-2-O-sulfo-
CA   alpha,alpha-trehalose.
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in mycobacteria, catalyzes the ultimate step in
CC       the biosynthesis of mycobacterial sulfolipids.
CC   -!- It catalyzes two successive transfers of a (hydroxy)phthioceranyl
CC       group from two diacylated intermediates to third diacylated
CC       intermediate, generating the tetraacylated sulfolipid.
DR   O07801, CHP1_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.285
DE   (13S,14R)-1,13-dihydroxy-N-methylcanadine 13-O-acetyltransferase.
CA   (13S,14R)-1,13-dihydroxy-N-methylcanadine + acetyl-CoA = (13S,14R)-13-O-
CA   acetyl-1-hydroxy-N-methylcanadine + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Papaver somniferum (opium
CC       poppy), participates in the biosynthesis of the isoquinoline alkaloid
CC       noscapine.
DR   I3PLR4, AT1_PAPSO  ;
//
ID   2.3.1.286
DE   protein acetyllysine N-acetyltransferase.
AN   NAD(+)-dependent protein deacetylase.
AN   protein lysine deacetylase.
CA   N(6)-acetyl-L-lysyl-[protein] + NAD(+) + H2O = 2''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose
CA   + nicotinamide + L-lysyl-[protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in all domains of life, is involved in gene
CC       regulation by deacetylating proteins.
CC   -!- Some of the 2''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose converts non-enzymically to
CC       3''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose.
