ID   2.3.1.287
DE   phthioceranic/hydroxyphthioceranic acid synthase.
AN   PKS2.
CA   (1) hexadecanoyl-[(hydroxy)phthioceranic acid synthase] + 8 (S)-
CA   methylmalonyl-CoA + 16 NADPH + 24 H(+) = C40-phthioceranyl-
CA   [(hydroxy)phthioceranic acid synthase] + 8 CO2 + 16 NADP(+) + 8 CoA +
CA   8 H2O.
CA   (2) hexadecanoyl-[(hydroxy)phthioceranic acid synthase] + 7 (S)-
CA   methylmalonyl-CoA + 14 NADPH + 21 H(+) = C37-phthioceranyl-
CA   [(hydroxy)phthioceranic acid synthase] + 7 CO2 + 14 NADP(+) + 7 CoA +
CA   7 H2O.
CC   -!- This mycobacterial polyketide enzyme produces the hepta- and octa-
CC       methylated fatty acids known as phthioceranic acids, and presumably
CC       their hydroxylated versions.
CC   -!- Formation of hepta- and octamethylated products depends on whether
CC       the enzyme incorporates seven or eight methylmalonyl-CoA extender
CC       units, respectively.
CC   -!- Formation of hydroxylated products may result from the enzyme
CC       skipping the dehydratase (DH) and enoylreductase (ER) domains during
CC       the first cycle of condensation.
DR   Q7TVK8, PHAS_MYCBO ;  A1KQG0, PHAS_MYCBP ;  A5U9F4, PHAS_MYCTA ;
DR   P9WQE8, PHAS_MYCTO ;  P9WQE9, PHAS_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.288
DE   2-O-sulfo trehalose long-chain-acyltransferase.
CA   (1) 2-O-sulfo-alpha,alpha-trehalose + octadecanoyl-CoA = 2-O-sulfo-2'-O-
CA   octadecanoyl-alpha,alpha-trehalose + CoA.
CA   (2) 2-O-sulfo-alpha,alpha-trehalose + hexadecanoyl-CoA = 2-O-sulfo-2'-O-
CA   hexadecanoyl-alpha,alpha-trehalose + CoA.
CC   -!- This mycobacterial enzyme catalyzes the acylation of 2-O-sulfo-
CC       alpha,alpha-trehalose at the 2' position by a C16 or C18 fatty acyl
CC       group during the biosynthesis of mycobacterial sulfolipids.
DR   Q7TVL3, PAPA2_MYCBO;  A1KQF4, PAPA2_MYCBP;  A5U9E9, PAPA2_MYCTA;
DR   P9WIK6, PAPA2_MYCTO;  P9WIK7, PAPA2_MYCTU;
//
ID   2.3.1.289
DE   aureothin polyketide synthase system.
AN   aureothin polyketide synthase complex.
CA   4-nitrobenzoyl-CoA + 4 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + 4 NADPH +
CA   8 H(+) = demethylluteothin + 5 CO2 + 4 NADP(+) + 6 CoA + 3 H2O.
CC   -!- This polyketide synthase, characterized from the bacterium
CC       Streptomyces thioluteus, generates the backbone of the antibiotic
CC       aureothin.
CC   -!- It is composed of 4 modules that total 18 domains and is encoded by
CC       three genes.
CC   -!- The enzyme accepts the unusual starter unit 4-nitrobenzoyl-CoA and
CC       extends it by 4 molecules of (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA and a single
CC       molecule of malonyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The first module (encoded by aurA) is used twice in an iterative
CC       fashion, so that the five Claisen condensation reactions are
CC       catalyzed by only four modules.
CC   -!- The iteration becomes possible by the transfer of the [acp]-bound
CC       polyketide intermediate back to the ketosynthase (KS) domain on the
CC       opposite polyketide synthase strand (polyketides are homodimeric).
//
ID   2.3.1.290
DE   spectinabilin polyketide synthase system.
AN   spectinabilin polyketide synthase complex.
CA   4-nitrobenzoyl-CoA + 6 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + malonyl-CoA + 6 NADPH +
CA   12 H(+) = demethyldeoxyspectinabilin + 7 CO2 + 6 NADP(+) + 8 CoA + 5 H2O.
CC   -!- This polyketide synthase, characterized from the bacteria
CC       Streptomyces orinoci and Streptomyces spectabilis, generates the
CC       backbone of the antibiotic spectinabilin.
CC   -!- It is composed of 6 modules that total 28 domains and is encoded by
CC       four genes.
CC   -!- The enzyme accepts the unusual starter unit 4-nitrobenzoyl-CoA and
CC       extends it by 6 molecules of (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA and a single
CC       molecule of malonyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The first module (encoded by norA) is used twice in an iterative
CC       fashion, so that the seven Claisen condensation reactions are
CC       catalyzed by only six modules.
CC   -!- The iteration becomes possible by the transfer of the [acp]-bound
CC       polyketide intermediate back to the ketosynthase (KS) domain on the
CC       opposite polyketide synthase strand (polyketides are homodimeric).
DR   B4ER95, NORA2_STRON;  B4ER92, NORA_STRON ;  B4ER96, NORB_STRON ;
DR   B4ER97, NORC_STRON ;
//
ID   2.3.1.291
DE   sphingoid base N-palmitoyltransferase.
AN   mammalian ceramide synthase 5.
CA   a sphingoid base + hexadecanoyl-CoA = an N-hexadecanoyl-sphingoid base +
CA   CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Mammals have six ceramide synthases that exhibit relatively strict
CC       specificity regarding the chain-length of their acyl-CoA substrates.
CC   -!- Ceramide synthase 5 (CERS5) is specific for palmitoyl-CoA as the acyl
CC       donor.
CC   -!- It can use multiple sphingoid bases including sphinganine,
CC       sphingosine, and phytosphingosine.
DR   Q8N5B7, CERS5_HUMAN;  Q9D6K9, CERS5_MOUSE;  Q6ZMG9, CERS6_HUMAN;
DR   Q8C172, CERS6_MOUSE;  Q9LJK3, LOH2_ARATH ;
//
ID   2.3.1.292
DE   (phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone synthase.
CA   (1) icosanoyl-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone synthase] + 2 (S)-
CA   methylmalonyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 5 NADPH + 10 H(+) = C32-
CA   carboxyphthiodiolenone-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone synthase] + 5 CO2
CA   + 5 NADP(+) + 5 CoA + 2 H2O.
CA   (2) docosanoyl-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone synthase] + 2 (S)-
CA   methylmalonyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 5 NADPH + 10 H(+) = C34-
CA   carboxyphthiodiolenone-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone synthase] + 5 CO2
CA   + 5 NADP(+) + 5 CoA + 2 H2O.
CA   (3) 19-(4-hydroxyphenyl)nonadecanoyl-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone
CA   synthase] + 2 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 5 NADPH + 10 H(+) =
CA   C37-(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone
CA   synthase] + 5 CO2 + 5 NADP(+) + 5 CoA + 2 H2O.
CA   (4) 17-(4-hydroxyphenyl)heptadecanoyl-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone
CA   synthase] + 2 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + 3 malonyl-CoA + 5 NADPH + 10 H(+) =
CA   C35-(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone-[(phenol)carboxyphthiodiolenone
CA   synthase] + 5 CO2 + 5 NADP(+) + 5 CoA + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is a complex of five polyketide synthase proteins,
CC       is involved in the synthesis of the lipid core common to phthiocerols
CC       and phenolphthiocerols.
CC   -!- The first protein, PpsA, can accept either a C18 or C20 long-chain
CC       fatty acyl, or a (4-hydroxyphenyl)-C17 or C19 fatty acyl.
CC   -!- The substrates must first be adenylated by EC 6.2.1.59, which also
CC       loads them onto PpsA.
CC   -!- PpsA then extends them using a malonyl-CoA extender unit.
CC   -!- The PpsB protein adds the next malonyl-CoA extender unit.
CC   -!- The absence of a dehydratase and an enoyl reductase domains in the
CC       PpsA and PpsB modules results in the formation of the diol portion of
CC       the phthiocerol moiety.
CC   -!- PpsC adds a third malonyl unit (releasing a water molecule due to its
CC       dehydratase domain), PpsD adds an (R)-methylmalonyl unit, releasing a
CC       water molecule, and PpsE adds a second (R)-methylmalonyl unit,
CC       without releasing a water molecule.
CC   -!- The incorporation of the methylmalonyl units results in formation of
CC       two branched methyl groups in the elongated product.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not contain a thioesterase domain, and release of the
CC       products requires the tesA-encoded type II thioesterase.
DR   Q7TXM0, PPSA_MYCBO ;  P9WQE6, PPSA_MYCTO ;  P9WQE7, PPSA_MYCTU ;
DR   Q7TXL9, PPSB_MYCBO ;  P9WQE4, PPSB_MYCTO ;  P9WQE5, PPSB_MYCTU ;
DR   Q7TXL8, PPSC_MYCBO ;  P96202, PPSC_MYCTU ;  Q7TXL7, PPSD_MYCBO ;
DR   P9WQE2, PPSD_MYCTO ;  P9WQE3, PPSD_MYCTU ;  Q7TXL6, PPSE_MYCBO ;
DR   P9WQE0, PPSE_MYCTO ;  P9WQE1, PPSE_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.293
DE   meromycolic acid 3-oxoacyl-(acyl carrier protein) synthase I.
AN   beta-ketoacyl-acyl carrier protein synthase KasA.
CA   an ultra-long-chain mono-unsaturated fatty acyl-[ACP] + malonyl-[ACP] +
CA   H(+) = a 3-oxo-ultra-long-chain mono-unsaturated fatty acyl-[ACP] + holo-
CA   [ACP] + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of the fatty acid synthase (FAS) II system of
CC       mycobacteria, which extends modified products of the FAS I system,
CC       eventually forming meromycolic acids that are incorporated into
CC       mycolic acids.
CC   -!- Meromycolic acids consist of a long chain, typically 50-60 carbons,
CC       which is functionalized by different groups.Two 3-oxoacyl-(acyl
CC       carrier protein) synthases function within the FAS II system, encoded
CC       by the kasA and kasB genes.
CC   -!- The two enzymes share some sequence identity but function
CC       independently on separate sets of substrates.
CC   -!- KasA differs from KasB (EC 2.3.1.294), by preferring shorter (C-22 to
CC       C-36) and more saturated (only one double bond) substrates.
DR   P63455, KASA_MYCBO ;  Q9CBS7, KASA_MYCLE ;  H8ESN0, KASA_MYCTE ;
DR   P9WQD8, KASA_MYCTO ;  P9WQD9, KASA_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.294
DE   meromycolic acid 3-oxoacyl-(acyl carrier protein) synthase II.
AN   beta-ketoacyl-acyl carrier protein synthase KasB.
CA   an ultra-long-chain di-unsaturated fatty acyl-[ACP] + malonyl-[ACP] +
CA   H(+) = a 3-oxo-ultra-long-chain di-unsaturated fatty acyl-[ACP] + holo-
CA   [ACP] + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of the fatty acid synthase (FAS) II system of
CC       mycobacteria, which extends modified products of the FAS I system,
CC       eventually forming meromycolic acids that are incorporated into
CC       mycolic acids.
CC   -!- Meromycolic acids consist of a long chain, typically 50-60 carbons,
CC       which is functionalized by different groups.Two 3-oxoacyl-(acyl
CC       carrier protein) synthases function within the FAS II system, encoded
CC       by the kasA and kasB genes.
CC   -!- The two enzymes share some sequence identity but function
CC       independently on separate sets of substrates.
CC   -!- KasB differs from KasA (EC 2.3.1.293), by preferring longer
CC       substrates (closer to the upper limit), which also contain two double
CC       bonds.
DR   P63457, KASB_MYCBO ;  O69473, KASB_MYCLE ;  P9WQD6, KASB_MYCTO ;
DR   P9WQD7, KASB_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.295
DE   mycoketide-CoA synthase.
CA   a medium-chain fatty acyl-CoA + 5 (S)-methylmalonyl-CoA + 5 malonyl-CoA +
CA   22 NADPH + 32 H(+) = a mycoketide-CoA + 10 CO2 + 22 NADP(+) + 10 CoA +
CA   11 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in mycobacteria, is involved in the synthesis of
CC       beta-D-mannosyl phosphomycoketides.
CC   -!- It is a very large polyketide synthase that contains two complete
CC       sets of FAS-like fatty acid synthase modules.
CC   -!- It binds an acyl-CoA with 5-9 carbons as a starter unit, and extends
CC       it by five rounds of alternative additions of malonyl-CoA and
CC       methylmalonyl-CoA extender units.
CC   -!- Depending on the starter unit, the enzyme forms mycoketide-CoAs of
CC       different lengths.
DR   I6XD69, PKS12_MYCTU;
//
ID   2.3.1.296
DE   omega-hydroxyceramide transacylase.
CA   an N-(omega-hydroxy-ultra-long chain fatty acyl)-sphingoid base +
CA   a (9Z,12Z)-octadecadienoyl-containing triacyl-sn-glycerol = an N-[omega-
CA   (9Z,12Z-octadecadienoyloxy)-O-ultra-long chain fatty acyl]-sphingoid base
CA   + a diacylglycerol.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the production of acylceramides in the
CC       stratum corneum, the outermost layer of the epidermis.
CC   -!- Acylceramides are crucial components of the skin permeability
CC       barrier.
DR   Q8N8W4, PLPL1_HUMAN;  Q3V1D5, PLPL1_MOUSE;
//
ID   2.3.1.297
DE   very-long-chain ceramide synthase.
AN   mammalian ceramide synthase 2.
AN   sphingoid base N-very-long-chain fatty acyl-CoA transferase.
CA   a very long-chain fatty acyl-CoA + a sphingoid base = an N-(very-long-
CA   chain fatty acyl)-sphingoid base + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- This entry describes ceramide synthase enzymes that are specific for
CC       very-long-chain fatty acyl-CoA substrates.
CC   -!- The two isoforms from yeast and the plant LOH1 and LOH3 isoforms
CC       transfer 24:0 and 26:0 acyl chains preferentially and use
CC       phytosphingosine as the preferred sphingoid base.
CC   -!- The mammalian CERS2 isoform is specific for acyl donors of 20-26
CC       carbons, which can be saturated or unsaturated.
CC   -!- The mammalian CERS3 isoform catalyzes this activity, but has a
CC       broader substrate range and also catalyzes the activity of
CC       EC 2.3.1.298.
CC   -!- Both mammalian enzymes can use multiple sphingoid bases, including
CC       sphinganine, sphingosine, and phytosphingosine.
DR   Q3ZBF8, CERS2_BOVIN;  Q96G23, CERS2_HUMAN;  Q924Z4, CERS2_MOUSE;
DR   Q8IU89, CERS3_HUMAN;  Q1A3B0, CERS3_MOUSE;  G5ED45, HYL1_CAEEL ;
DR   Q7Z139, HYL2_CAEEL ;  P28496, LAC1_YEAST ;  P38703, LAG1_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.3.1.298
DE   ultra-long-chain ceramide synthase.
AN   mammalian ceramide synthase 3.
AN   sphingoid base N-ultra-long-chain fatty acyl-CoA transferase.
CA   an ultra-long-chain fatty acyl-CoA + a sphingoid base = an N-(ultra-long-
CA   chain-acyl)-sphingoid base + CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Mammals have six ceramide synthases that exhibit relatively strict
CC       specificity regarding the chain-length of their acyl-CoA substrates.
CC   -!- Ceramide synthase 3 (CERS3) is the only enzyme that is active with
CC       ultra-long-chain acyl-CoA donors (C28 or longer).
CC   -!- It is active in the epidermis, where its products are incorporated
CC       into acylceramides.
CC   -!- CERS3 also accepts (2R)-2-hydroxy fatty acids and omega-hydroxy fatty
CC       acids, and can accept very-long-chain acyl-CoA substrates (see
CC       EC 2.3.1.297).
CC   -!- It can use multiple sphingoid bases including sphinganine,
CC       sphingosine, phytosphingosine, and (6R)-6-hydroxysphingosine.
DR   Q8IU89, CERS3_HUMAN;  Q1A3B0, CERS3_MOUSE;
//
ID   2.3.1.299
DE   sphingoid base N-stearoyltransferase.
AN   mammalian ceramide synthase 1.
CA   a sphingoid base + octadecanoyl-CoA = an N-octadecanoyl-sphingoid base +
CA   CoA + H(+).
CC   -!- Mammals have six ceramide synthases that exhibit relatively strict
CC       specificity regarding the chain-length of their acyl-CoA substrates.
CC   -!- Ceramide synthase 1 (CERS1) is structurally and functionally
CC       distinctive from all other CERS enzymes, and is specific for
CC       stearoyl-CoA as the acyl donor.
CC   -!- It can use multiple sphingoid bases including sphinganine,
CC       sphingosine, and phytosphingosine.
DR   P27544, CERS1_HUMAN;  P27545, CERS1_MOUSE;
//
ID   2.3.1.300
DE   branched-chain beta-ketoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] synthase.
CA   (1) 3-methylbutanoyl-CoA + malonyl-[ACP] + H(+) = 5-methyl-3-oxohexanoyl-
CA   [ACP] + CO2 + CoA.
CA   (2) 2-methylpropanoyl-CoA + malonyl-[ACP] + H(+) = 4-methyl-3-
CA   oxopentanoyl-[ACP] + CO2 + CoA.
CA   (3) (2S)-2-methylbutanoyl-CoA + malonyl-[ACP] + H(+) = (4S)-4-methyl-3-
CA   oxohexanoyl-[ACP] + CO2 + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is responsible for initiating branched-chain fatty acid
CC       biosynthesis by the dissociated (or type II) fatty-acid biosynthesis
CC       system (FAS-II) in some bacteria, using molecules derived from
CC       degradation of the branched-chain amino acids L-leucine, L-valine,
CC       and L-isoleucine to form the starting molecules for elongation by the
CC       FAS-II system.
CC   -!- In some organisms the enzyme is also able to use acetyl-CoA, leading
CC       to production of a mix of branched-chain and straight-chain fatty
CC       acids (cf. EC 2.3.1.180).
DR   O34746, FABH1_BACSU;  P72392, FABH1_STRCO;  O07600, FABH2_BACSU;
