ID   2.3.2.1
DE   D-glutamyltransferase.
AN   D-glutamyl transpeptidase.
CA   (1) D-glutamine + D-glutamate = gamma-D-glutamyl-D-glutamate + NH4(+).
CA   (2) L(or D)-glutamine + (gamma-D-glutamyl)n-[peptide] = NH3 + (gamma-D-
CA   glutamyl)n+1-[peptide].
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes two reactions; the first is the transfer of a
CC       glutamyl residue from L- or D-glutamine to D-glutamate via a gamma
CC       linkage, forming gamma-glutamyl-D-glutamate, and the second is the
CC       transfer of additional glutamyl residues to the peptide, extending
CC       the polypeptide chain.
