//
ID   2.3.2.24
DE   (E3-independent) E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme.
AN   E3-independent ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme E2.
CA   S-ubiquitinyl-[E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme]-L-cysteine + [acceptor
CA   protein]-L-lysine = [E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme]-L-cysteine + N(6)-
CA   monoubiquitinyl-[acceptor protein]-L-lysine.
CC   -!- The enzyme transfers a single ubiquitin directly from an
CC       ubiquitinated E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme to itself, and on to a
CC       lysine residue of the acceptor protein without involvement of E3
CC       ubiquitin transferases (cf. EC 2.3.2.26, EC 2.3.2.27).
CC   -!- It forms a labile ubiquitin adduct in the presence of E1, ubiquitin,
CC       and Mg(2+)-ATP and catalyzes the conjugation of ubiquitin to protein
CC       substrates, independently of E3.
CC   -!- This transfer has only been observed with small proteins.
CC   -!- In vitro a transfer to small acceptors (e.g. L-lysine, N-acetyl-L-
CC       lysine methyl ester) has been observed.
