ID   2.3.2.27
DE   RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase.
AN   RING E3 ligase.
AN   ubiquitin transferase RING E3.
CA   S-ubiquitinyl-[E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme]-L-cysteine + [acceptor
CA   protein]-L-lysine = [E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme]-L-cysteine + N(6)-
CA   ubiquitinyl-[acceptor protein]-L-lysine.
CC   -!- RING E3 ubiquitin transferases serve as mediators bringing the
CC       ubiquitin-charged E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme (EC 2.3.2.23) and
CC       an acceptor protein together to enable the direct transfer of
CC       ubiquitin through the formation of an isopeptide bond between the
CC       C-terminal glycine residue of ubiquitin and the epsilon-amino group
CC       of an L-lysine residue of the acceptor protein.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 2.3.2.26 the RING-E3 domain does not form a catalytic
CC       thioester intermediate with ubiquitin.
CC   -!- Many members of the RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase family are not
CC       able to bind a substrate directly, and form a complex with a cullin
CC       scaffold protein and a substrate recognition module (the complexes
CC       are named CRL for Cullin-RING-Ligase).
CC   -!- In these complexes, the RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase provides
CC       an additional function, mediating the transfer of a NEDD8 protein
CC       from a dedicated E2 carrier to the cullin protein (see EC 2.3.2.32).
CC       cf. EC 2.3.2.31.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.2.19 and EC 6.3.2.21.
