ID   2.3.2.34
DE   E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme.
AN   NEDD8-carrier-protein E2.
AN   NEDD8-conjugating enzyme E2.
CA   [E1 NEDD8-activating enzyme]-S-[NEDD8 protein]-yl-L-cysteine + [E2 NEDD8-
CA   conjugating enzyme]-L-cysteine = [E1 NEDD8-activating enzyme]-L-cysteine
CA   + [E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme]-S-[NEDD8-protein]-yl-L-cysteine.
CC   -!- Some RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferases (EC 2.3.2.27) are not able
CC       to bind a substrate protein directly.
CC   -!- Instead, they form complexes with a cullin scaffold protein and a
CC       substrate recognition module, which are known as CRL (Cullin-RING-
CC       Ligase) complexes.
CC   -!- The cullin protein needs to be activated by the ubiquitin-like
CC       protein NEDD8 in a process known as neddylation.
CC   -!- Like ubiquitin, the NEDD8 protein ends with two glycine residues.
CC   -!- EC 6.2.1.64 activates NEDD8 in an ATP-dependent reaction by forming a
CC       high-energy thioester intermediate between NEDD8 and one of its
CC       cysteine residues.
CC   -!- The activated NEDD8 is subsequently transferred to a cysteine residue
CC       of an E2 NEDD8-conjugating enzyme, and is eventually conjugated to a
CC       lysine residue of specific substrates in the presence of the
CC       appropriate E3 transferase (EC 2.3.2.32).
