ID   2.4.1.4
DE   amylosucrase.
AN   sucrose--glucan glucosyltransferase.
CA   [(1->4)-alpha-D-glucosyl](n) + sucrose = [(1->4)-alpha-D-glucosyl](n+1) +
CA   D-fructose.
CC   -!- The glucansucrases transfer a D-glusosyl residue from sucrose to a
CC       glucan chain.
CC   -!- They are classified based on the linkage by which they attach the
CC       transferred residue.
CC   -!- In some cases, in which the enzyme forms more than one linkage type,
CC       classification relies on the relative proportion of the linkages that
CC       are generated.
CC   -!- This enzyme extends the glucan chain by an alpha(1->4) linkage.
