ID   2.4.1.19
DE   cyclomaltodextrin glucanotransferase.
AN   Bacillus macerans amylase.
AN   cyclodextrin glucanotransferase.
AN   cyclodextrin glycosyltransferase.
CA   Cyclizes part of a (1->4)-alpha-D-glucan chain by formation of a (1->4)-
CA   alpha-D-glucosidic bond.
CC   -!- Cyclomaltodextrins (Schardinger dextrins) of various sizes (6, 7,
CC       8, etc. glucose units) are formed reversibly from starch and similar
CC       substrates.
CC   -!- Also disproportionates linear maltodextrins without cyclizing (cf.
CC       EC 2.4.1.25).
