CA   galactosamine = an N-acetyl-beta-D-galactosaminyl-(1->4)-N-acetyl-beta-D-
CA   glucosaminyl derivative + UDP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from human can transfer N-acetyl-D-galactosamine (GalNAc)
CC       to N-glycan and O-glycan substrates that have N-acetyl-D-glucosamine
CC       (GlcNAc) but not D-glucuronic acid (GlcUA) at their non-reducing end.
CC   -!- The N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl group is normally on a core
CC       oligosaccharide although benzyl glycosides have been used in enzyme-
CC       characterization experiments.
CC   -!- Some glycohormones, e.g. lutropin and thyrotropin contain the
CC       N-glycan structure containing the N-acetyl-beta-D-galactosaminyl-
