ID   2.4.2.29
DE   tRNA-guanosine(34) preQ1 transglycosylase.
AN   guanine insertion enzyme.
AN   Q-insertase.
AN   TGT.
AN   tRNA guanine(34) transglycosidase.
AN   tRNA transglycosylase.
CA   7-aminomethyl-7-carbaguanine + guanosine(34) in tRNA = 7-aminomethyl-7-
CA   carbaguanosine(34) in tRNA + guanine.
CC   -!- Certain prokaryotic and eukaryotic tRNAs contain the modified base
CC       queuine at position 34.
CC   -!- In eubacteria, which produce queuine de novo, the enzyme catalyzes
CC       the exchange of guanine with the queuine precursor preQ1, which is
CC       ultimately modified to queuosine.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use an earlier intermediate, preQ0, to replace
CC       guanine in unmodified tRNA(Tyr) and tRNA(Asn).
CC   -!- This enzyme acts after EC 1.7.1.13 in the queuine-biosynthesis
CC       pathway. cf. EC 2.4.2.64.
