//
ID   2.4.99.18
DE   dolichyl-diphosphooligosaccharide--protein glycotransferase.
CA   a di-trans,poly-cis-dolichyl diphosphooligosaccharide + L-asparaginyl-
CA   [protein] = N(4)-(oligosaccharide-(1->4)-N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-
CA   (1->4)-N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl)-L-asparaginyl-[protein] +
CA   a di-trans,poly-cis-dolichyl diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- Occurs in eukaryotes that form a glycoprotein by the transfer of a
CC       glucosyl-mannosyl-glucosamine polysaccharide to the side-chain of an
CC       L-asparagine residue in the sequence -Asn-Xaa-Ser- or -Asn-Xaa-Thr-
CC       (Xaa not Pro) in nascent polypeptide chains.
CC   -!- The basic oligosaccharide is the tetradecasaccharide Glc3Man9GlcNAc2.
CC   -!- However, smaller oligosaccharides derived from it and
CC       oligosaccharides with additional monosaccharide units attached may be
CC       involved.
CC   -!- Man3GlcNAc2 seems to be common for all of the oligosaccharides
CC       involved with the terminal N-acetylglucosamine linked to the protein
CC       L-asparagine.
CC   -!- Occurs on the lumenal face of the endoplasmic reticulum.
CC   -!- The dolichol involved normally has 14-21 isoprenoid units with two
CC       trans double-bonds at the omega end, and the rest of the double-bonds
CC       in cis form.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.4.1.119.
