ID   2.4.99.19
DE   undecaprenyl-diphosphooligosaccharide--protein glycotransferase.
CA   tritrans,heptacis-undecaprenyl diphosphooligosaccharide + [protein]-L-
CA   asparagine = tritrans,heptacis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + a glycoprotein
CA   with the oligosaccharide chain attached by N-beta-D-glycosyl linkage to
CA   protein L-asparagine.
CC   -!- A bacterial enzyme that has been isolated from Campylobacter jejuni
CC       and Campylobacter lari.
CC   -!- It forms a glycoprotein by the transfer of a glucosyl-N-
CC       acetylgalactosaminyl-N,N'-diacetylbacillosamine
CC       (GalNAc2(Glc)GalNAc3diNAcBac) polysaccharide and related
CC       oligosaccharides to the side-chain of an L-asparagine residue in the
CC       sequence -Asp/Glu-Xaa-Asn-Xaa'-Ser/Thr- (Xaa and Xaa' not Pro) in
CC       nascent polypeptide chains.
CC   -!- Occurs on the external face of the plasma membrane.
CC   -!- The polyprenol involved is normally tritrans,heptacis-undecaprenol
CC       but a decaprenol is used by some species.
DR   Q0P9C8, PGLB_CAMJE ;  Q5HTX9, PGLB_CAMJR ;  B9KDD4, PGLB_CAMLR ;
//
ID   2.4.99.20
DE   2'-phospho-ADP-ribosyl cyclase/2'-phospho-cyclic-ADP-ribose transferase.
AN   diphosphopyridine nucleosidase.
CA   nicotinate + NADP(+) = NAADP(+) + nicotinamide.
CC   -!- This multiunctional enzyme catalyzes both the removal of nicotinamide
CC       from NADP(+), forming 2'-phospho-cyclic ADP-ribose, and the addition
CC       of nicotinate to the cyclic product, forming NAADP(+), a calcium
CC       messenger that can mobilize intracellular Ca(2+) stores and activate
CC       Ca(2+) influx to regulate a wide range of physiological processes.
CC   -!- In addition, the enzyme also catalyzes EC 3.2.2.6.
DR   P28907, CD38_HUMAN ;  Q5VAN0, CD38_MACFA ;  P56528, CD38_MOUSE ;
DR   Q9MZ03, CD38_RABIT ;  Q64244, CD38_RAT   ;  P29241, NADA_APLCA ;
DR   Q27312, NADA_APLKU ;
//
ID   2.4.99.21
DE   dolichyl-phosphooligosaccharide-protein glycotransferase.
AN   archaeal oligosaccharyl transferase.
AN   dolichyl-monophosphooligosaccharide-protein glycotransferase.
CA   an archaeal dolichyl phosphooligosaccharide + [protein]-L-asparagine =
CA   an archaeal dolichyl phosphate + a glycoprotein with the oligosaccharide
CA   chain attached by N-beta-D-glycosyl linkage to a protein L-asparagine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaea Methanococcus voltae and
CC       Haloferax volcanii, transfers a glycan component from dolichyl
CC       phosphooligosaccharide to external proteins.
CC   -!- It is different from EC 2.4.99.18 which uses dolichyl diphosphate as
CC       carrier compound in bacteria and eukaryotes.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the N-glycosylation of proteins in some
CC       archaea.
CC   -!- Dolichol used by archaea is different from that used by eukaryotes;
CC       it is much shorter (C55-C60), it is alpha,omega-saturated and it may
CC       have additional unsaturated positions in the chain.
DR   O29918, AGLB1_ARCFU;  Q8U4D2, AGLB1_PYRFU;  O74088, AGLB1_PYRHO;
DR   O30195, AGLB2_ARCFU;  Q8U3P6, AGLB2_PYRFU;  O58981, AGLB2_PYRHO;
DR   O29867, AGLB3_ARCFU;  D4GYH4, AGLB_HALVD ;  Q58920, AGLB_METJA ;
DR   Q2EMT4, AGLB_METVO ;
