ID   2.4.99.26
DE   O-antigen ligase.
CA   a lipid-linked O antigen + a lipid A-core oligosaccharide =
CA   a lipopolysaccharide + a polyisoprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- This Gram-negative bacterial enzyme attaches the polymerized O
CC       antigen molecule to the outer core region of the lipid A-core
CC       oligosaccharide, finalizing the biosynthesis of the
CC       lipopolysaccharide.
CC   -!- Prior to the reaction the two substrates are attached to the
CC       periplasmic-facing side of the inner membrane, and the enzyme
CC       transfers the O-antigen from its polyprenyl diphosphate membrane
CC       anchor (usually ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl diphosphate) to a
CC       terminal sugar of the lipid A-core oligosaccharide.
CC   -!- Despite the popular name 'ligase', the enzyme is not a real ligase,
CC       as the reaction does not involve the hydrolysis of a phosphate bond
CC       in a triphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is embedded in the inner membrane and often has 12 trans-
CC       membrane segments.
CC   -!- It is a metal-independent inverting glycosyltransferase, and in some
CC       cases it can attach surface polymers other than O-antigens to the
CC       lipid A-core oligosaccharide.
DR   P27243, WAAL_ECOLI ;  Q9HUG6, WAAL_PSEAE ;  P26471, WAAL_SALTY ;
//
ID   2.4.99.27
DE   O-antigen polymerase Wzy.
AN   Wzy O-antigen polymerase.
AN   Wzy polymerase.
CA   n lipid-linked O-antigen repeat units = a lipid-linked O antigen + (n-1)
CA   polyisoprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The Wzy-type polymerase polymerizes O antigen repeat unit
CC       oligosaccharides that are anchored to the periplasmic face of the
CC       inner membrane, forming an O antigen polysaccharide that is still
CC       anchored to the membrane.
CC   -!- A Wzz chain length regulator (sometimes referred to as an O-antigen
CC       co-polymerase) normally interacts with Wzy to confer a distinctive
CC       modal chain length distribution.
CC   -!- The resultant polysaccharide is transferred from the membrane anchor
CC       to the lipid A-core oligosaccharide by EC 2.4.99.26 forming a
CC       complete lipopolysaccharide structure.
CC   -!- There is an enormous diversity of O antigen polymerases with
CC       different specificities, reflecting the variability in the structure
CC       and composition of O-antigens.
DR   Q58YW1, WZY_ECOLX  ;  G3XCW3, WZY_PSEAE  ;  Q00474, WZY_SALMU  ;
DR   P0A236, WZY_SALTI  ;  P0A235, WZY_SALTY  ;  Q03584, WZY_SHIDY  ;
DR   P37784, WZY_SHIFL  ;
//
ID   2.4.99.28
DE   peptidoglycan glycosyltransferase.
AN   peptidoglycan TGase.
AN   peptidoglycan transglycosylase.
AN   PG-II.
CA   [GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)](n)-
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + beta-D-GlcNAc-(1->4)-
CA   Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)-di-trans,octa-
CA   cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate = [GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-
CA   Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)](n+1)-di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate +
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme also works when the lysine residue is replaced by meso-
CC       2,6-diaminoheptanedioate (meso-2,6-diaminopimelate, A2pm) combined
CC       with adjacent residues through its L-center, as it is in Gram-
CC       negative and some Gram-positive organisms.
CC   -!- The undecaprenol involved is ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol.
CC   -!- Involved in the synthesis of cell-wall peptidoglycan.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.4.1.129.
