ID   2.5.1.21
DE   squalene synthase.
AN   farnesyl-diphosphate farnesyltransferase.
AN   farnesyltransferase.
AN   presqualene-diphosphate synthase.
AN   presqualene synthase.
AN   squalene synthetase.
CA   (1) 2 (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + NADPH + H(+) = squalene +
CA   2 diphosphate + NADP(+).
CA   (2) 2 (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + NADH + H(+) = squalene +
CA   2 diphosphate + NAD(+).
CC   -!- This microsomal enzyme catalyzes the first committed step in the
CC       biosynthesis of sterols.
CC   -!- In the absence of NAD(P)H, presqualene diphosphate (PSPP) is
CC       accumulated.
CC   -!- When NAD(P)H is present, presqualene diphosphate does not dissociate
CC       from the enzyme during the synthesis of squalene from farnesyl
CC       diphosphate (FPP).
CC   -!- High concentrations of FPP inhibit the production of squalene but not
CC       of PSPP.
