ID   2.5.1.39
DE   4-hydroxybenzoate polyprenyltransferase.
AN   COQ2.
AN   p-hydroxybenzoate polyprenyltransferase.
CA   an all-trans-polyprenyl diphosphate + 4-hydroxybenzoate = a 4-hydroxy-3-
CA   (all-trans-polyprenyl)benzoate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, involved in the biosynthesis of ubiquinone, attaches a
CC       polyprenyl side chain to a 4-hydroxybenzoate ring, producing the
CC       first ubiquinone intermediate that is membrane bound.
CC   -!- The number of isoprenoid subunits in the side chain varies in
CC       different species.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not have any specificity concerning the length of the
CC       polyprenyl tail, and accepts tails of various lengths with similar
CC       efficiency.
