ID   2.5.1.41
DE   phosphoglycerol geranylgeranyltransferase.
AN   (S)-3-O-geranylgeranylglyceryl phosphate synthase.
AN   GGGPS.
AN   GGGP synthase.
CA   sn-glycerol 1-phosphate + (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = sn-3-
CA   O-(geranylgeranyl)glycerol 1-phosphate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the first pathway-specific step in the biosynthesis of the
CC       core membrane diether lipids in archaebacteria.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the alkylation of the primary hydroxy group in
CC       sn-glycerol 1-phosphate by geranylgeranyl diphosphate (GGPP) in a
CC       prenyltransfer reaction where a hydroxy group is the nucleophile in
CC       the acceptor substrate.
CC   -!- The other enzymes involved in the biosynthesis of polar lipids in
CC       archaea are EC 1.1.1.261, EC 2.5.1.42 and EC 2.7.7.67, which lead to
CC       the formation of CDP-unsaturated archaeol.
CC   -!- The final step in the pathway involves the addition of L-serine, with
CC       concomitant removal of CMP, leading to the production of unsaturated
CC       archaetidylserine.
