ID   2.5.1.44
DE   homospermidine synthase.
CA   (1) 2 putrescine = sym-homospermidine + NH4(+).
CA   (2) putrescine + spermidine = sym-homospermidine + propane-1,3-diamine.
CC   -!- The reaction of this bacterial enzyme occurs in three steps, with
CC       some of the intermediates presumably remaining enzyme-bound:
CC       (1) NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation of either putrescine or
CC       spermidine.
CC       (2) Attack by water forming 4-aminobutanal (and releasing ammonia or
CC       propane-1,3-diamine, respectively).
CC       (3) Condensation of 4-aminobutanal with putrescine, which forms
CC       homospermidine and restores NAD(+).
CC   -!- Differs from the eukaryotic enzyme EC 2.5.1.45, which cannot use
CC       putrescine as donor of the aminobutyl group.
DR   O32323, HSS_BLAVI  ;  Q98H64, HSS_RHILO  ;
//
ID   2.5.1.45
DE   homospermidine synthase (spermidine-specific).
CA   putrescine + spermidine = sym-homospermidine + propane-1,3-diamine.
CC   -!- A eukaryotic enzyme found in plants.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in three steps, with some of the intermediates
CC       presumably remaining enzyme-bound:
CC       (1) NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation of spermidine to
CC       dehydrospermidine.
CC       (2) Attack by water forming 4-aminobutanal (and releasing propane-
CC       1,3-diamine).
CC       (3) Condensation of 4-aminobutanal with purescine, which forms
CC       homospermidine and restores NAD(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme is more specific than EC 2.5.1.44, which is found in
CC       bacteria, as it cannot use putrescine as donor of the 4-aminobutyl
CC       group.
CC   -!- Forms part of the biosynthetic pathway of the poisonous pyrrolizidine
CC       alkaloids of the ragworts (Senecio).
DR   Q9SC13, HSS1_SENVE ;  Q9M4B0, HSS1_SENVU ;  P60038, HSS2_SENVE ;
