ID   2.5.1.58
DE   protein farnesyltransferase.
AN   CAAX farnesyltransferase.
AN   FTase.
CA   L-cysteinyl-[protein] + (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = S-(2E,6E)-
CA   farnesyl-L-cysteinyl-[protein] + diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, along with EC 2.5.1.59 and EC 2.5.1.60, constitutes the
CC       protein prenyltransferase family of enzymes.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the formation of a thioether linkage between the C-1 of an
CC       isoprenyl group and a cysteine residue fourth from the C-terminus of
CC       the protein.
CC   -!- These protein acceptors have the C-terminal sequence CA(1)A(2)X,
CC       where the terminal residue, X, is preferably serine, methionine,
CC       alanine or glutamine; leucine makes the protein a substrate for
CC       EC 2.5.1.59.
CC   -!- The enzymes are relaxed in specificity for A(1), but cannot act if
CC       A(2) is aromatic.
CC   -!- Substrates of the prenyltransferases include Ras, Rho, Rab, other
CC       Ras-related small GTP-binding proteins, gamma-subunits of
CC       heterotrimeric G-proteins, nuclear lamins, centromeric proteins and
CC       many proteins involved in visual signal transduction.
