ID   2.5.1.61
DE   hydroxymethylbilane synthase.
AN   (4-[2-carboxyethyl]-3-[carboxymethyl]pyrrol-2-yl)methyltransferase
AN   (hydrolyzing).
AN   HMB-synthase.
AN   porphobilinogen deaminase.
AN   pre-uroporphyrinogen synthase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen I synthase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen I synthetase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen synthase.
AN   uroporphyrinogen synthetase.
CA   4 porphobilinogen + H2O = hydroxymethylbilane + 4 NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme works by stepwise addition of pyrrolylmethyl groups until
CC       a hexapyrrole is present at the active center.
CC   -!- The terminal tetrapyrrole is then hydrolyzed to yield the product,
CC       leaving a cysteine-bound dipyrrole on which assembly continues.
CC   -!- In the presence of a second enzyme, EC 4.2.1.75, which is often
CC       called cosynthase, the product is cyclized to form uroporphyrinogen
CC       III.
CC   -!- If EC 4.2.1.75 is absent, the hydroxymethylbilane cyclizes
CC       spontaneously to form uroporphyrinogen I.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.1.8.
