//
ID   2.5.1.62
DE   chlorophyll synthase.
CA   phytyl diphosphate + chlorophyllide a + H(+) = chlorophyll a +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is modified by binding of the first substrate, phytyl
CC       diphosphate, before reaction of the modified enzyme with the second
CC       substrate, chlorophyllide a, can occur.
CC   -!- The reaction also occurs when phytyl diphosphate is replaced by
CC       geranylgeranyl diphosphate.
DR   Q38833, CHLG_ARATH ;  Q9M3W5, CHLG_AVESA ;  Q5W6H5, CHLG_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   2.5.1.63
DE   adenosyl-fluoride synthase.
AN   fluorinase.
CA   fluoride + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 5'-deoxy-5'-fluoroadenosine +
CA   L-methionine.
DR   A0A1G9FQX8, FLA_ACTMZ  ;  R4LHX8, FLA_ACTS9  ;  W8JNL4, FLA_NOCB7  ;
DR   Q70GK9, FLA_STRCT  ;  W0W999, FLA_STRSQ  ;
//
ID   2.5.1.64
DE   Transferred entry: 2.2.1.9 and 4.2.99.20.
//
ID   2.5.1.65
DE   O-phosphoserine sulfhydrylase.
AN   O-phosphoserine(thiol)-lyase.
CA   O-phospho-L-serine + hydrogen sulfide + H(+) = L-cysteine + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Aeropyrum pernix acts on both O-phospho-L-serine and
CC       O(3)-acetyl-L-serine, in contrast with EC 2.5.1.47, which acts only
CC       on O(3)-acetyl-L-serine.
DR   Q79FV4, CYSK2_MYCTU;  Q9YBL2, CYSO_AERPE ;
//
ID   2.5.1.66
DE   N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)arginine synthase.
AN   CEAS.
AN   CEA synthetase.
AN   N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)arginine synthetase.
CA   D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate + L-arginine = N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)-L-
CA   arginine + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- Requires thiamine diphosphate and catalyzes the first step in the
CC       clavulanic-acid biosynthesis pathway.
CC   -!- The 2-hydroxy-3-oxo group transferred from glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate
CC       is isomerized during transfer to form the 2-carboxyethyl group.
DR   Q9LCV9, CEAS_STRCL ;
//
ID   2.5.1.67
DE   chrysanthemyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   CPPase.
CA   2 dimethylallyl diphosphate = (R,R)-chrysanthemyl diphosphate +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- Chrysanthemyl diphosphate is a monoterpene with a non-head-to-tail
CC       linkage; it is unlike most monoterpenoids, which are derived from
CC       geranyl diphosphate and have isoprene units that are linked head-
CC       to-tail.
CC   -!- The mechanism of its formation is similar to that of the early steps
CC       of squalene and phytoene biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Chrysanthemyl diphosphate is the precursor of chrysanthemic acid,
CC       the acid half of the pyrethroid insecticides found in chrysanthemums.
DR   Q7XYS8, CHRDS_ARTSI;  P0C565, CHRYS_TANCI;
//
ID   2.5.1.68
DE   (2Z,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   (Z)-farnesyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   Z-farnesyl diphosphate synthase.
CA   isopentenyl diphosphate + (2E)-geranyl diphosphate = (2Z,6E)-farnesyl
CA   diphosphate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The product of this reaction is an intermediate in the synthesis of
CC       decaprenyl phosphate, which plays a central role in the biosynthesis
CC       of most features of the mycobacterial cell wall, including
CC       peptidoglycan, linker unit galactan and arabinan.
CC   -!- Neryl diphosphate can also act as substrate.
DR   A0A386JVA3, FPPS_NEZVI ;  Q7U0P8, ZFPP_MYCBO ;  Q9CB36, ZFPP_MYCLE ;
DR   A0R2W4, ZFPP_MYCS2 ;  P9WFF4, ZFPP_MYCTO ;  P9WFF5, ZFPP_MYCTU ;
DR   Q47SS3, ZFPP_THEFY ;
//
ID   2.5.1.69
DE   lavandulyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   FDS-5.
CA   2 dimethylallyl diphosphate = (R)-lavandulyl diphosphate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Lavandulyl diphosphate is a monoterpene with a non-head-to-tail
CC       linkage; it is unlike most monoterpenoids, which are derived from
CC       geranyl diphosphate and have isoprene units that are linked head-
CC       to-tail.
CC   -!- When this enzyme is incubated with prenyl diphosphate and isopentenyl
CC       diphosphate, it also forms the regular monoterpene geranyl
CC       diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Artemisia tridentata (big sagebrush) forms both
CC       lavandulyl diphosphate and chrysanthemyl diphosphate (see
CC       EC 2.5.1.67) when prenyl diphosphate is the sole substrate.
DR   Q7XYS8, CHRDS_ARTSI;
//
ID   2.5.1.70
DE   naringenin 8-dimethylallyltransferase.
AN   N8DT.
CA   (2S)-naringenin + dimethylallyl diphosphate = sophoraflavanone B +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- In addition to naringenin, the enzyme can prenylate several other
CC       flavanones at the C-8 position, but more slowly.
CC   -!- Along with EC 1.14.14.142 and EC 2.5.1.71, this enzyme forms part of
CC       the sophoraflavanone-G biosynthesis pathway.
DR   B1B3P3, N8DT1_SOPFL;  B1B5P4, N8DT2_SOPFL;
//
ID   2.5.1.71
DE   leachianone-G 2''-dimethylallyltransferase.
AN   leachianone G 2''-dimethylallyltransferase.
AN   LG 2''-dimethylallyltransferase.
AN   LGDT.
CA   leachianone G + dimethylallyl diphosphate = sophoraflavanone G +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- The reaction forms the lavandulyl sidechain of sophoraflavanone G by
CC       transferring a prenyl group to the 2'' position of another prenyl
CC       group attached at postiion 8 of leachianone G.
CC   -!- The enzyme is specific for prenyl diphosphate as the prenyl donor,
CC       as it cannot be replaced by isopentenyl diphosphate or geranyl
CC       diphosphate.
CC   -!- Euchrenone a7 (a 5-deoxy derivative of leachianone G) and kenusanone
CC       I (a 7-methoxy derivative of leachianone G) can also act as
CC       substrates, but more slowly.
CC   -!- Along with EC 1.14.14.142 and EC 2.5.1.70, this enzyme forms part of
CC       the sophoraflavanone-G biosynthesis pathway.
//
ID   2.5.1.72
DE   quinolinate synthase.
AN   quinolinate synthetase.
CA   iminosuccinate + dihydroxyacetone phosphate = quinolinate + phosphate +
CA   2 H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- Quinolinate synthase catalyzes the second step in the de novo
CC       biosynthesis of NAD(+) from aspartate in some bacteria, with
CC       EC 1.4.3.16 catalyzing the first step and EC 2.4.2.19 the third step.
