ID   2.5.1.73
DE   O-phospho-L-seryl-tRNA:Cys-tRNA synthase.
AN   SepCysS.
AN   Sep-tRNA:Cys-tRNA synthase.
CA   O-phospho-L-seryl-tRNA(Cys) + hydrogen sulfide + H(+) = L-cysteinyl-
CA   tRNA(Cys) + phosphate.
CC   -!- In organisms like Archaeoglobus fulgidus lacking EC 6.1.1.16 for the
CC       direct Cys-tRNA(Cys) formation, Cys-tRNA(Cys) is produced by an
CC       indirect pathway, in which EC 6.1.1.27 ligates O-phosphoserine to
CC       tRNA(Cys), and EC 2.5.1.73 converts the produced O-phospho-L-seryl-
CC       tRNA(Cys) to Cys-tRNA(Cys).
CC   -!- The SepRS/SepCysS pathway is the sole route for cysteine biosynthesis
CC       in the organism.
CC   -!- Methanosarcina mazei can use both pathways, the direct route using
CC       EC 6.1.1.16 and the indirect pathway with EC 6.1.1.27 and
CC       EC 2.5.1.73.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.n3.
