ID   2.5.1.130
DE   2-carboxy-1,4-naphthoquinone phytyltransferase.
AN   1,4-diketo-2-naphthoate phytyltransferase.
AN   1,4-dioxo-2-naphthoate phytyltransferase.
CA   2-carboxy-1,4-naphthoquinone + phytyl diphosphate + H(+) =
CA   demethylphylloquinone + CO2 + diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, founds in plant and cyanobacteria, catalyzes a step in
CC       the synthesis of phylloquinone (vitamin K1), an electron carrier
CC       associated with photosystem I.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of the phytyl chain synthesized by
CC       EC 1.3.1.83 to 2-carboxy-1,4-naphthoquinone.
DR   Q0WUA3, MENA_ARATH ;  P73962, MENA_SYNY3 ;
//
ID   2.5.1.131
DE   (4-{4-[2-(gamma-L-glutamylamino)ethyl]phenoxymethyl}furan-2-
DE   yl)methanamine synthase.
CA   gamma-L-glutamyltyramine + [5-(aminomethyl)furan-3-yl]methyl diphosphate
CA   = (4-{4-[2-(gamma-L-glutamylamino)ethyl]phenoxymethyl}furan-2-
CA   yl)methanamine + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the archaeon Methanocaldococcus jannaschii,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the methanofuran cofactor.
DR   Q58250, MFNF_METJA ;  Q50834, MFNF_METVA ;
//
ID   2.5.1.132
DE   3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-nononate 9-phosphate synthase.
AN   2-keto-3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-9-phosphonononic acid synthase.
AN   KDN 9-P synthase.
CA   aldehydo-D-mannose 6-phosphate + phosphoenolpyruvate + H2O = 3-deoxy-D-
CA   glycero-beta-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate 9-phosphate + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of the sialic acid
CC       3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-nononate (KDN).
CC   -!- The human sialic acid synthase (EC 2.5.1.57) is also able to catalyze
CC       the reaction.
CC   -!- KDN is abundant in extracellular glycoconjugates of lower vertebrates
CC       such as fish and amphibians, but is also found in the capsular
CC       polysaccharides of bacteria that belong to the Bacteroides genus.
DR   Q9VG74, SIAS_DROME ;  Q9NR45, SIAS_HUMAN ;
//
ID   2.5.1.133
DE   bacteriochlorophyll a synthase.
CA   bacteriochlorophyllide a + (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate + H(+)
CA   = geranylgeranyl-bacteriochlorophyllide a + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the addition of a geranylgeranyl hydrophobic
CC       chain to bacteriochlorophyllide a via an ester bond with the
CC       17-propionate residue.
CC   -!- The side chain is later modified to a phytyl chain, resulting in
CC       bacteriochlorophyll a.
//
ID   2.5.1.134
DE   cystathionine beta-synthase (O-acetyl-L-serine).
AN   O-acetylserine dependent cystathionine beta-synthase.
CA   O-acetyl-L-serine + L-homocysteine = L,L-cystathionine + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, purified from the bacterium Bacillus subtilis, also has a
CC       low activity with L-serine (cf. EC 4.2.1.22).
DR   O05393, MCCA_BACSU ;
//
ID   2.5.1.135
DE   validamine 7-phosphate valienyltransferase.
CA   validamine 7-phosphate + GDP-valienol = validoxylamine A 7'-phosphate +
CA   GDP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from several Streptomyces strains,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of the antifungal agent validamycin
CC       A.
DR   H2K885, VALL_STRHJ ;  Q15JG1, VLDE_STRHL ;
//
ID   2.5.1.136
DE   2-acylphloroglucinol 4-prenyltransferase.
AN   aromatic prenyltransferase.
CA   a 2-acylphloroglucinol + dimethylallyl diphosphate = a 2-acyl-4-
CA   prenylphloroglucinol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from hop (Humulus lupulus), acts on
CC       phlorisovalerophenone, phlormethylbutanophenone,
CC       and phlorisobutanophenone during the synthesis of bitter acids.
CC   -!- It also acts with much lower activity on naringenin chalcone.
CC   -!- Forms a complex with EC 2.5.1.137 which catalyzes additional
CC       prenylation reactions.
DR   A0A0B5A051, PT1L_HUMLU ;  E5RP65, PT1_HUMLU  ;
//
ID   2.5.1.137
DE   2-acyl-4-prenylphloroglucinol 6-prenyltransferase.
AN   aromatic prenyltransferase.
CA   (1) a 2-acyl-4-prenylphloroglucinol + dimethylallyl diphosphate =
CA   a 2-acyl-4,6-diprenylphloroglucinol + diphosphate.
CA   (2) a 2-acyl-4,6-diprenylphloroglucinol + dimethylallyl diphosphate =
CA   a 2-acyl-4,6,6-triprenylphloroglucinol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from hop (Humulus lupulus), catalyzes two
CC       successive prenylations of a 2-acyl-4-prenylphloroglucinol during the
CC       synthesis of bitter acids.
CC   -!- Forms a complex with EC 2.5.1.136 which catalyzes the initial
CC       prenylation of the substrates.
DR   A0A0B4ZTQ2, PT2_HUMLU  ;
//
ID   2.5.1.138
DE   coumarin 8-geranyltransferase.
CA   (1) umbelliferone + (2E)-geranyl diphosphate = 8-geranylumbelliferone +
CA   diphosphate.
CA   (2) esculetin + (2E)-geranyl diphosphate = 8-geranylesculetin +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Citrus limon, is specific
CC       for geranyl diphosphate as a prenyl donor.
CC   -!- It also has low activity with the coumarins 5,7-dihydroxycoumarin and
CC       5-methoxy-7-hydroxycoumarin.
DR   A0A077K8G3, CGT1A_CITLI;  A0A077K9K6, CGT1B_CITLI;
//
ID   2.5.1.139
DE   umbelliferone 6-dimethylallyltransferase.
CA   umbelliferone + dimethylallyl diphosphate = demethylsuberosin +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from parsley (Petroselinum crispum) is specific for
CC       umbelliferone and dimethylallyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- A minor product is osthenol, which is produced by transfer of the
CC       dimethylallyl group to C-8 of umbelliferone.
DR   W0SKS3, U6DT_PETCR ;
//
ID   2.5.1.140
