DE   4-hydroxyglutamate transaminase.
AN   4-hydroxyglutamate aminotransferase.
CA   (4S)-4-hydroxy-L-glutamate + 2-oxoglutarate = (4R)-4-hydroxy-2-
CA   oxoglutarate + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in a degradation pathway of trans-4-hydroxy-
CC       L-proline, a compound that contributes to the stability of the
CC       collagen triple helix.
CC   -!- Oxaloacetate can replace 2-oxoglutarate.
CC   -!- This enzyme may be identical with EC 2.6.1.1.
//
ID   2.6.1.24
