ID   2.6.1.85
DE   aminodeoxychorismate synthase.
AN   4-amino-4-deoxychorismate synthase.
AN   ADC synthase.
CA   chorismate + L-glutamine = 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is composed of two parts, a glutaminase (PabA in
CC       Escherichia coli) and an aminotransferase (PabB).
CC   -!- In the absence of PabA and glutamine (but in the presence of Mg(2+)),
CC       PabB can convert ammonia and chorismate into 4-amino-4-
CC       deoxychorismate.
CC   -!- PabA converts glutamine into glutamate only in the presence of
CC       stoichiometric amounts of PabB.
CC   -!- In many organisms, including plants, the genes encoding the two
CC       proteins have fused to encode a single bifunctional protein. This
CC       enzyme is coupled with EC 4.1.3.38 to form 4-aminobenzoate. cf.
CC       EC 2.6.1.123.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.5.8.
