CA   UDP-2-acetamido-2,6-dideoxy-beta-L-arabino-hex-4-ulose + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme transfers the primary amino group of L-glutamate to C-4''
CC       of UDP-4-dehydro sugars, forming a C-N bond in a stereo configuration
CC       opposite to that of UDP.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Bacillus cereus has been shown to act
CC       on UDP-2-acetamido-2,6-dideoxy-beta-L-arabino-hex-4-ulose, UDP-beta-
CC       L-threo-pentapyranos-4-ulose, UDP-4-dehydro-6-deoxy-D-glucose,
CC       and UDP-2-acetamido-2,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-xylo-hex-4-ulose. cf.
CC       EC 2.6.1.34, which catalyzes a similar reaction, but forms the C-N
CC       bond in the same stereo configuration as that of UDP.
