//
ID   2.7.1.8
DE   glucosamine kinase.
CA   D-glucosamine + ATP = D-glucosamine 6-phosphate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is specific for glucosamine and has only a minor activity
CC       with D-glucose.
CC   -!- Two unrelated enzymes with this activityn have been described.
CC   -!- One type was studied in the bacterium Vibrio cholerae, where it
CC       participates in a chitin degradation pathway.
CC   -!- The other type has been described from actinobacteria, where it is
CC       involved in the incorporation of environmental glucosamine into
CC       antibiotic biosynthesis pathways. cf. EC 2.7.1.147.
DR   I7FJX8, GLCNK_MYCS2;  A0A1H7TQR5, GLCNK_STRJI;  Q9KUA9, GSPK_VIBCH ;
//
ID   2.7.1.9
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   2.7.1.10
DE   phosphoglucokinase.
AN   glucose-phosphate kinase.
CA   alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate + ATP = alpha-D-glucose 1,6-bisphosphate +
CA   ADP + H(+).
//
ID   2.7.1.11
DE   6-phosphofructokinase.
AN   phosphofructokinase I.
AN   phosphohexokinase.
CA   beta-D-fructose 6-phosphate + ATP = beta-D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate +
CA   ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from rabbit muscle displays absolute stereoselectivity for
CC       the beta-anomer of D-fructofuranose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- D-tagatose 6-phosphate and sedoheptulose 7-phosphate can act as
CC       acceptors.
CC   -!- UTP, CTP and ITP can act as donors.
CC   -!- Not identical with EC 2.7.1.105.
