ID   2.7.1.26
DE   riboflavin kinase.
AN   flavokinase.
AN   RFK.
CA   riboflavin + ATP = FMN + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The cofactors FMN and FAD participate in numerous processes in all
CC       organisms, including mitochondrial electron transport,
CC       photosynthesis, fatty-acid oxidation, and metabolism of vitamin B6,
CC       vitamin B12 and folates.
CC   -!- While monofunctional riboflavin kinase is found in eukaryotes, some
CC       bacteria have a bifunctional enzyme that exhibits both this activity
CC       and that of EC 2.7.7.2.
CC   -!- In Bacillus subtilis, ATP can be replaced by other phosphate donors
CC       but with decreasing enzyme activity in the order ATP > dATP > CTP >
CC       UTP.
