//
ID   2.7.1.61
DE   acyl-phosphate--hexose phosphotransferase.
CA   a D-hexose + an acyl phosphate = a D-hexose phosphate + a carboxylate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Phosphorylates D-glucose and D-mannose on O-6, and D-fructose on O-1
CC       or O-6.
//
ID   2.7.1.62
DE   phosphoramidate--hexose phosphotransferase.
CA   phosphoramidate + a D-hexose + H(+) = alpha-D-hexose 1-phosphate +
CA   NH4(+).
CC   -!- Activity is observed with several hexoses; of these glucose is the
CC       best substrate and the product from it is alpha-D-glucose
CC       1-phosphate.
CC   -!- The phosphoramidate donor can be replaced by N-phosphoglycine and by
CC       an N-phosphohistidine.
CC   -!- May be identical with EC 3.1.3.9.
//
ID   2.7.1.63
DE   polyphosphate--glucose phosphotransferase.
AN   polyphosphate glucokinase.
CA   [phosphate](n) + D-glucose = [phosphate](n-1) + D-glucose 6-phosphate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Requires a neutral salt, e.g. KCl, for maximum activity.
CC   -!- Also acts on glucosamine.
DR   Q49988, PPGK_MYCLE ;  A5U654, PPGK_MYCTA ;  P9WIN0, PPGK_MYCTO ;
DR   P9WIN1, PPGK_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.7.1.64
DE   inositol 3-kinase.
AN   inositol 1-kinase.
AN   myo-inositol 1-kinase.
AN   myoinositol kinase.
CA   myo-inositol + ATP = 1D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate + ADP + H(+).
DR   Q93Z01, MIK_ARATH  ;  Q5GA22, MIK_MAIZE  ;  Q84R36, MIK_ORYSJ  ;
//
ID   2.7.1.65
DE   scyllo-inosamine 4-kinase.
CA   1-amino-1-deoxy-scyllo-inositol + ATP = 1-amino-1-deoxy-scyllo-inositol
CA   4-phosphate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on streptamine, 2-deoxystreptamine and 1D-1-guanidino-3-
CC       amino-1,3-dideoxy-scyllo-inositol.
//
ID   2.7.1.66
DE   undecaprenol kinase.
AN   C55-isoprenoid alcohol kinase.
AN   isoprenoid-alcohol kinase.
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenol + ATP = di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl
CA   phosphate + ADP + H(+).
