ID   2.7.1.169
DE   pantoate kinase.
CA   (R)-pantoate + ATP = (R)-4-phosphopantoate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The conversion of (R)-pantoate to (R)-4'-phosphopantothenate is part
CC       of the pathway leading to biosynthesis of 4'-phosphopantetheine,
CC       an essential cofactor of coenzyme A and acyl-carrier protein.
CC   -!- In bacteria and eukaryotes this conversion is performed by
CC       condensation with beta-alanine, followed by phosphorylation
CC       (EC 6.3.2.1 and EC 2.7.1.33, respectively).
CC   -!- In archaea the order of these two steps is reversed,
CC       and phosphorylation precedes condensation with beta-alanine.
DR   Q2FUB2, POK_METHJ  ;  Q58379, POK_METJA  ;  Q5JHF1, POK_THEKO  ;
//
ID   2.7.1.170
DE   anhydro-N-acetylmuramic acid kinase.
AN   anhMurNAc kinase.
CA   1,6-anhydro-N-acetyl-beta-muramate + ATP + H2O = N-acetyl-D-muramate
CA   6-phosphate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, along with EC 4.2.1.126, is required for the utilization
CC       of anhydro-N-acetylmuramic acid in proteobacteria.
CC   -!- The substrate is either imported from the medium or derived from the
CC       bacterium's own cell wall murein during cell wall recycling.
CC   -!- The product N-acetylmuramate 6-phosphate is produced as a 7:1 mixture
CC       of the alpha- and beta-anomers.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.n1.
