//
ID   2.7.1.224
DE   cytidine diphosphoramidate kinase.
CA   cytidine 5'-diphosphoramidate + ATP = cytidine 3'-phospho-
CA   5'-diphosphoramidate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Campylobacter jejuni,
CC       is involved in formation of a unique O-methyl phosphoramidate
CC       modification on specific sugar residues within the bacterium&#8217;s
CC       capsular polysaccharides.
DR   Q0P8J9, CDK_CAMJE  ;
//
ID   2.7.1.225
DE   L-serine kinase (ATP).
CA   L-serine + ATP = O-phospho-L-serine + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of L-2,3-diaminopropanoate, which is
CC       used by that organism as a precursor for the biosynthesis of the
CC       siderophore staphyloferrin B.
