//
ID   2.7.1.226
DE   L-serine kinase (ADP).
CA   L-serine + ADP = O-phospho-L-serine + AMP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized in the hyperthermophilic archaeon
CC       Thermococcus kodakarensis, participates in L-cysteine biosynthesis.
DR   Q5JD03, SERK_THEKO ;
//
ID   2.7.1.227
DE   inositol phosphorylceramide synthase.
CA   an N-(2R-hydroxy-very-long-chain fatty acyl)-(R)-4-hydroxysphingoid base
CA   + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) = a 1D-myo-
CA   inositol-1-phospho-N-[(R)-2-hydroxy-very-long-chain fatty acyl]-(R)-4-
CA   hydroxysphingoid base + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from yeast, attaches a phosphoinositol
CC       headgroup to alpha-hydroxyphytoceramides, generating a very-long-
CC       chain inositol phospho-alpha hydroxyphytoceramide (IPC), the simplest
CC       of the three complex sphingolipids produced by yeast.
DR   P36107, AUR1_YEAST ;  Q84WB7, GINT1_ARATH;  Q9SH93, IPCS2_ARATH;
//
ID   2.7.1.228
DE   mannosyl-inositol-phosphoceramide inositolphosphotransferase.
CA   an alpha-D-mannosyl-(1<->6)-1D-myo-inositol-1-phospho-N-[(R)-2-hydroxy-
CA   very-long-chain fatty acyl]-(R)-4-hydroxysphingoid base + a 1,2-diacyl-
CA   sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) = an alpha-D-mannosyl-6-(1D-myo-
CA   inositol phospho)-(1<->6)-1D-myo-inositol-1-phospho-N-[(R)-2-hydroxy-
CA   very-long-chain fatty acyl]-(R)-4-hydroxysphingoid base + a 1,2-diacyl-
CA   sn-glycerol.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the ultimate reaction in the yeast sphingolipid
CC       biosynthesis pathway.
CC   -!- It transfers a second phosphoinositol group to mannosyl-inositol-
CC       phospho-alpha-hydroxyphytoceramide (MIPC), forming the final and most
CC       abundant yeast sphingolipid, mannosyl-diphosphoinositol-ceramide
CC       (MIP2C).
DR   P38954, IPT1_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.7.1.229
DE   deoxyribokinase.
CA   2-deoxy-D-ribose + ATP = 2-deoxy-D-ribose 5-phosphate + ADP + H(+).
