//
ID   2.7.2.12
DE   acetate kinase (diphosphate).
AN   Acetate kinase (pyrophosphate).
CA   acetate + diphosphate = acetyl phosphate + phosphate.
//
ID   2.7.2.13
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   2.7.2.14
DE   branched-chain-fatty-acid kinase.
AN   isobutyrate kinase.
CA   2-methylpropanoate + ATP = 2-methylpropanoyl phosphate + ADP.
CC   -!- 3-methylbutanoate, 2-methylbutanoate, pentanoate, butanoate,
CC       and propanoate can also act as acceptors (cf. EC 2.7.2.7).
//
ID   2.7.2.15
DE   propionate kinase.
AN   propionate/acetate kinase.
CA   propanoate + ATP = propanoyl phosphate + ADP.
CC   -!- Both propanoate and acetate can act as a substrate.
CC   -!- Involved in the anaerobic degradation of L-threonine in bacteria.
CC   -!- Both this enzyme and EC 2.7.2.1 play important roles in the
CC       production of propanoate.
