ID   2.7.4.29
DE   Kdo2-lipid A phosphotransferase.
AN   lipid A undecaprenyl phosphotransferase.
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + alpha-Kdo-(2->4)-alpha-
CA   Kdo-(2->6)-lipid A (E. coli) = (Kdo)2-lipid A 1-diphosphate +
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl phosphate.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme can use diacylglycerol 3-diphosphate as the
CC       phosphate donor.
DR   P76445, LPXT_ECOLI ;
//
ID   2.7.4.30
DE   Transferred entry: 2.7.8.43.
//
ID   2.7.4.31
DE   [5-(aminomethyl)furan-3-yl]methyl phosphate kinase.
CA   [5-(aminomethyl)-3-furyl]methyl phosphate + ATP = [5-(aminomethyl)furan-
CA   3-yl]methyl diphosphate + ADP.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the archaeon Methanocaldococcus jannaschii,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the methanofuran cofactor.
DR   Q57900, MFNE_METJA ;
//
ID   2.7.4.32
DE   farnesyl phosphate kinase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl phosphate + CTP = CDP + (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in plants and animals, is specific for CTP as
CC       phosphate donor.
CC   -!- It does not use farnesol as substrate (cf. EC 2.7.1.216).
//
ID   2.7.4.33
DE   AMP-polyphosphate phosphotransferase.
AN   PPK2D.
CA   [phosphate](n) + ADP = [phosphate](n+1) + AMP.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Acinetobacter johnsonii
CC       and Pseudomonas aeruginosa, transfers a phosphate group from
CC       polyphosphates to nucleotide monophosphates.
CC   -!- The highest activity is achieved with AMP, but the enzyme can also
CC       phosphorylate GMP, dAMP, dGMP, IMP, and XMP.
CC   -!- The reverse reactions were not detected.
DR   Q83XD3, PK22_ACIJO ;  Q9HYF1, PK22_PSEAE ;  Q886D9, PK22_PSESM ;
//
ID   2.7.4.34
DE   GDP-polyphosphate phosphotransferase.
AN   polyphosphate kinase 2.
CA   [phosphate](n) + GTP = [phosphate](n+1) + GDP.
CC   -!- Polyphosphate kinase 2, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas
CC       aeruginosa, uses inorganic polyphosphate as a donor to convert GDP to
CC       GTP.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also act on ADP (cf. EC 2.7.4.1), but with lower
CC       activity.
CC   -!- The enzyme has only a trivial activity in the opposite direction
CC       (synthesizing polyphosphate from GTP).
CC   -!- The GTP that is produced is believed to be consumed by EC 2.7.7.13.
DR   Q9I6Z1, PK21A_PSEAE;
