ID   2.7.7.23
DE   UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase.
AN   N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphate uridyltransferase.
AN   UDP-N-acetylglucosamine pyrophosphorylase.
CA   N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine 1-phosphate + UTP + H(+) = UDP-N-acetyl-
CA   alpha-D-glucosamine + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Part of the pathway for acetamido sugar biosynthesis in bacteria and
CC       archaea.
CC   -!- The enzyme from several bacteria (e.g., Escherichia coli, Bacillus
CC       subtilis and Haemophilus influenzae) has been shown to be
CC       bifunctional and also to possess the activity of EC 2.3.1.157.
CC   -!- The enzyme from plants and animals is also active toward N-acetyl-
CC       alpha-D-galactosamine 1-phosphate (cf. EC 2.7.7.83), while the
CC       bacterial enzyme shows low activity toward that substrate.
