ID   2.7.7.34
DE   glucose-1-phosphate guanylyltransferase.
AN   GDP-glucose diphosphorylase.
AN   GDP-glucose pyrophosphorylase.
CA   alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate + GTP + H(+) = GDP-D-glucose + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Also acts, more slowly, on D-mannose 1-phosphate.
//
ID   2.7.7.35
DE   ADP ribose phosphorylase.
AN   ADP-ribose phosphorylase.
AN   ribose-5-phosphate adenylyltransferase.
CA   D-ribose 5-phosphate + ADP + H(+) = ADP-D-ribose + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the single-celled alga Euglena
CC       gracilis, catalyzes an irreversible reaction in the direction of ADP
CC       formation. cf. EC 2.7.7.96.
//
ID   2.7.7.36
DE   aldose-1-phosphate adenylyltransferase.
AN   ADP-aldose phosphorylase.
AN   ADP-sugar phosphorylase.
AN   sugar-1-phosphate adenylyltransferase.
CA   ADP + alpha-D-aldose 1-phosphate = phosphate + ADP-aldose.
//
ID   2.7.7.37
DE   aldose-1-phosphate nucleotidyltransferase.
AN   NDP-aldose phosphorylase.
AN   NDP-sugar phosphorylase.
AN   sugar-1-phosphate nucleotidyltransferase.
CA   NDP + alpha-D-aldose 1-phosphate = phosphate + NDP-aldose.
CC   -!- The enzyme works on a variety of alpha-D-aldose 1-phosphates and
CC       beta-L-aldose 1-phosphates (which have the same anomeric
CC       configuration as the former).
//
