ID   2.7.7.61
DE   citrate lyase holo-[acyl-carrier protein] synthase.
AN   2'-(5''-phosphoribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA transferase.
AN   holo-ACP synthase.
AN   holo-citrate lyase synthase.
CA   apo-[citrate lyase ACP] + 2'-(5''-triphospho-alpha-D-ribosyl)-
CA   3'-dephospho-CoA = holo-[citrate lyase ACP] + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The gamma-subunit of EC 4.1.3.6 serves as an acyl-carrier protein
CC       (ACP) and contains the cofactor 2'-(5-triphosphoribosyl)-
CC       3'-dephospho-CoA.
CC   -!- Synthesis and attachment of the cofactor requires the concerted
CC       action of this enzyme and EC 2.4.2.52.
CC   -!- In the enzyme from Escherichia coli, the cofactor is attached to
CC       serine-14 of the ACP via a phosphodiester bond.
