DE   GDP-L-galactose/GDP-D-glucose: hexose 1-phosphate guanylyltransferase.
AN   GDP-L-galactose phosphorylase.
CA   (1) GDP-beta-L-galactose + alpha-D-mannose 1-phosphate = beta-L-galactose
CA   1-phosphate + GDP-alpha-D-mannose.
CA   (2) GDP-alpha-D-glucose + alpha-D-mannose 1-phosphate = alpha-D-glucose
CA   1-phosphate + GDP-alpha-D-mannose.
CC   -!- This plant enzyme catalyzes the conversion of GDP-beta-L-galactose
CC       and GDP-alpha-D-glucose to beta-L-galactose 1-phosphate and alpha-D-
CC       glucose 1-phosphate, respectively.
CC   -!- The enzyme can use inorganic phosphate as the cosubstrate,
CC       but several hexose 1-phosphates, including alpha-D-mannose
CC       1-phosphate, alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate, and alpha-D-galactose
CC       1-phosphate, are better guanylyl acceptors.
CC   -!- The enzyme's activity on GDP-beta-L-galactose is crucial for the
CC       biosynthesis of L-ascorbate.
