ID   2.7.7.79
DE   tRNA(His) guanylyltransferase.
AN   histidine tRNA guanylyltransferase.
CA   a 5'-end ribonucleotide-tRNA(His) + GTP + ATP + H2O = a 5'-end phospho-
CA   guanosine-ribonucleotide-tRNA(His) + AMP + 2 diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- In eukarya an additional guanosine residue is added post-
CC       transcriptionally to the 5'-end of tRNA(His) molecules.
CC   -!- The addition occurs opposite a universally conserved adenosine(73)
CC       and is thus the result of a non-templated 3'-5' addition reaction.
CC   -!- The additional guanosine residue is an important determinant for
CC       aminoacylation by EC 6.1.1.21.
CC   -!- The enzyme requires a divalent cation for activity.
CC   -!- ATP activation is not required when the substrate contains a
CC       5'-triphosphate (ppp-tRNA(His)).
