ID   2.7.7.108
DE   protein adenylyltransferase.
AN   AMPylase.
CA   (1) L-seryl-[protein] + ATP = 3-O-(5'-adenylyl)-L-seryl-[protein] +
CA   diphosphate.
CA   (2) L-threonyl-[protein] + ATP = 3-O-(5'-adenylyl)-L-threonyl-[protein] +
CA   diphosphate.
CA   (3) L-tyrosyl-[protein] + ATP = O-(5'-adenylyl)-L-tyrosyl-[protein] +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, commonly referred to as AMPylase, transfers an adenylyl
CC       (adenosine 5'-phosphate) group from ATP to L-serine, L-threonine,
CC       and L-tyrosine residues in its target protein substrates.
CC   -!- AMPylation is found in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes.
CC   -!- In bacteria AMPylases are abundant enzymes that either regulate the
CC       function of endogenous bacterial proteins or are translocated into
CC       host cells to hijack host cell signaling processes.
