ID   2.7.8.43
DE   lipid A phosphoethanolamine transferase.
AN   lipid A PEA transferase.
CA   (1) lipid A (E. coli) + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine +
CA   H(+) = lipid A hexaacyl 1-(2-aminoethyl diphosphate) (E. coli) + a 1,2-
CA   diacyl-sn-glycerol.
CA   (2) lipid A (E. coli) + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine +
CA   H(+) = lipid A 4'-(2-aminoethyl diphosphate) (E. coli) + a 1,2-diacyl-
CA   sn-glycerol.
CA   (3) lipid A hexaacyl 1-(2-aminoethyl diphosphate) (E. coli) + a 1,2-
CA   diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine + H(+) = lipid A
CA   1,4'-bis(2-aminoethyl diphosphate) (E. coli) + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol.
CC   -!- The enzyme adds one or two ethanolamine phosphate groups to lipid A
CC       giving a diphosphate, sometimes in combination with EC 2.4.2.43
CC       giving products with 4-amino-4-deoxy-beta-L-arabinose groups at the
CC       phosphates of lipid A instead of diphosphoethanolamine groups.
CC   -!- It will also act on lipid IVA and Kdo2-lipid A.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.4.30.
DR   A0A0R6L508, MCR1_ECOLX ;  A0A1C3NEV1, MCR2_ECOLX ;
