ID   2.7.9.4
DE   alpha-glucan, water dikinase.
AN   alpha-glucan,water dikinase.
AN   starch-related R1 protein.
CA   [(1->4)-alpha-D-glucosyl](n) + n ATP + n H2O = [(1->4)-6-phospho-alpha-D-
CA   glucosyl](n) + n AMP + n phosphate + 2n H(+).
CC   -!- ATP appears to be the only phosphate donor.
CC   -!- No activity could be detected using GTP, UTP, phosphoenolpyruvate or
CC       diphosphate.
CC   -!- The protein phosphorylates glucans exclusively at O-6 of glucosyl
CC       residues.
CC   -!- The protein phosphorylates itself with the beta-phosphate of ATP,
CC       which is then transferred to the glucan.
DR   Q9SAC6, GWD1_ARATH ;  Q8LPT9, GWD1_CITRE ;  Q9AWA5, GWD1_SOLTU ;
DR   Q9STV0, GWD2_ARATH ;
//
ID   2.7.9.5
DE   phosphoglucan, water dikinase.
CA   [(1->4)-6-phospho-alpha-D-glucosyl](n) + n ATP + n H2O = [(1->4)-3,6-
CA   bisphospho-alpha-D-glucosyl](n) + n AMP + n phosphate + 2n H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme phosphorylates granular starch that has previously been
CC       phosphorylated by EC 2.7.9.4; there is no activity with
CC       unphosphorylated glucans.
CC   -!- It transfers the beta-phosphate of ATP to the phosphoglucan, whereas
CC       the gamma-phosphate is transferred to water.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 2.7.9.4, which phosphorylates the glucose groups in
CC       glucans predominantly on O-6, this enzyme phosphorylates glucose
CC       groups in phosphorylated starch predominantly on O-3.
CC   -!- The protein phosphorylates itself with the beta-phosphate of ATP,
CC       which is then transferred to the glucan.
DR   Q6ZY51, PWD_ARATH  ;  Q2QTC2, PWD_ORYSJ  ;
//
ID   2.7.9.6
DE   rifampicin phosphotransferase.
CA   rifampicin + ATP + H2O = 21-phosphorifampicin + AMP + phosphate + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from a diverse collection of Gram-positive
CC       bacteria, inactivates the antibiotic rifampicin by phosphorylating it
CC       at position 21.
CC   -!- The enzyme comprises three domains: two substrate-binding domains
CC       (ATP-grasp and rifampicin-binding domains) and a smaller phosphate-
CC       carrying L-histidine swivel domain that transits between the
CC       spatially distinct substrate-binding sites during catalysis.
DR   Q81BR3, RPH_BACCR  ;  O34309, RPH_BACSU  ;  A0A0X1KHF9, RPH_LISMF  ;
DR   A0A059WGE7, RPH_STRSQ  ;  B5I920, RPH_STRX2  ;
