ID   2.7.11.13
DE   protein kinase C.
AN   calcium/phospholipid dependent protein kinase.
AN   calcium-dependent protein kinase C.
AN   calcium-independent protein kinase C.
AN   cPKC.
AN   nPKC.
AN   PKC.
CA   (1) L-seryl-[protein] + ATP = O-phospho-L-seryl-[protein] + ADP + H(+).
CA   (2) L-threonyl-[protein] + ATP = O-phospho-L-threonyl-[protein] + ADP +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- A family of serine- and threonine-specific protein kinases that
CC       depend on lipids for activity.
CC   -!- They can be activated by calcium but have a requirement for the
CC       second messenger diacylglycerol.
CC   -!- Members of this group of enzymes phosphorylate a wide variety of
CC       protein targets and are known to be involved in diverse cell-
CC       signaling pathways.
CC   -!- Members of the protein kinase C family also serve as major receptors
CC       for phorbol esters, a class of tumor promoters.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.37.
