CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme associates with the spindle pole during mitosis and is
CC       thought to play an important role in the dynamic function of the
CC       mitotic spindle during chromosome segregation.
CC   -!- The human form of the enzyme, Plk1, does not phosphorylate histone
CC       H1, enolase and phosvitin but it can phosphorylate myelin basic
CC       protein and microtubule-associated protein MAP-2, although to a
CC       lesser extent than casein.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.37.
