ID   2.7.11.30
DE   receptor protein serine/threonine kinase.
AN   activin receptor kinase.
AN   receptor serine/threonine protein kinase.
AN   receptor type II serine/threonine protein kinase.
AN   receptor type I serine/threonine protein kinase.
AN   TGF-beta kinase.
CA   (1) L-seryl-[receptor-protein] + ATP = O-phospho-L-seryl-[receptor-
CA   protein] + ADP + H(+).
CA   (2) L-threonyl-[receptor-protein] + ATP = O-phospho-L-threonyl-[receptor-
CA   protein] + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The transforming growth factor beta (TGF-beta) family of cytokines
CC       regulates cell proliferation, differentiation, recognition and death.
CC   -!- Signaling occurs by the binding of ligand to the type II receptor,
CC       which is the constitutively active kinase.
CC   -!- Bound TGF-beta is then recognized by receptor I, which is
CC       phosphorylated and can propagate the signal to downstream substrates.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.37.
