ID   2.8.1.7
DE   cysteine desulfurase.
AN   cysteine desulfurylase.
CA   (sulfur carrier)-H + L-cysteine = (sulfur carrier)-SH + L-alanine.
CC   -!- The sulfur from free L-cysteine is first transferred to a cysteine
CC       residue in the active site, and then passed on to various other
CC       acceptors.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of iron-sulfur clusters,
CC       thio-nucleosides in tRNA, thiamine, biotin, lipoate and pyranopterin
CC       (molybdopterin).
CC   -!- In Azotobacter vinelandii, this sulfur provides the inorganic sulfide
CC       required for nitrogenous metallocluster formation.
