ID   2.8.1.11
DE   molybdopterin synthase sulfurtransferase.
AN   molybdopterin synthase sulfurylase.
CA   [molybdopterin-synthase sulfur-carrier protein]-C-terminal Gly-Gly-AMP +
CA   S-sulfanyl-L-cysteinyl-[cysteine desulfurase] + AH2 = [molybdopterin-
CA   synthase sulfur-carrier protein]-C-terminal-Gly-aminoethanethioate +
CA   L-cysteinyl-[cysteine desulfurase] + A + AMP + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme transfers sulfur to form a thiocarboxylate moiety on the
CC       C-terminal glycine of the small subunit of EC 2.8.1.12.
CC   -!- In the human, the reaction is catalyzed by the rhodanese-like
CC       C-terminal domain (cf. EC 2.8.1.1) of the MOCS3 protein,
CC       a bifunctional protein that also contains EC 2.7.7.80 at the
CC       N-terminal domain.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.8.1.n1.
