DR   O13947, MTU1_SCHPO ;  Q12093, MTU1_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.8.1.15
DE   tRNA-5-methyluridine(54) 2-sulfurtransferase.
CA   [TtuB sulfur-carrier protein]-C-terminal-Gly-aminoethanethioate +
CA   5-methyluridine(54) in tRNA + ATP + H2O = [TtuB sulfur-carrier protein]-
CA   C-terminal Gly-Gly + 5-methyl-2-thiouridine(54) in tRNA + AMP +
CA   diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in thermophilic bacteria such as Thermus
CC       thermophilus and archaea such as Pyrococcus horikoshii, modifies the
CC       ribothymidine (5-methyluridine) residue at position 54 of tRNAs.
DR   Q72LF3, TTUA_THET2 ;
//
ID   2.8.1.16
DE   L-aspartate semialdehyde sulfurtransferase.
CA   L-aspartate 4-semialdehyde + reduced 2[4Fe-4S]-[ferredoxin] + hydrogen
CA   sulfide + 3 H(+) = oxidized 2[4Fe-4S]-[ferredoxin] + L-homocysteine +
CA   H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Methanosarcina
CC       acetivorans, participates in an L-methionine biosysnthetic pathway
CC       found in most of the methanogenic archaea.
DR   Q8TPT4, ASST_METAC ;  Q57564, ASST_METJA ;
