DE   [ribosomal protein uS12] (aspartate(89)-C(3))-methylthiotransferase.
AN   [ribosomal protein S12] (aspartate-C(3))-methylthiotransferase.
CA   L-aspartate(89)-[ribosomal protein uS12]-hydrogen + (sulfur carrier)-SH +
CA   AH2 + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3-methylsulfanyl-L-aspartate(89)-
CA   [ribosomal protein uS12]-hydrogen + (sulfur carrier)-H +
CA   5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + A + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme binds two [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- A bridge of five sulfur atoms is formed between the free Fe atoms of
CC       the two [4Fe-4S] clusters.
CC   -!- In the first reaction the enzyme transfers a methyl group from AdoMet
CC       to the external sulfur ion of the sulfur bridge.
CC   -!- In the second reaction the enzyme catalyzes the reductive
CC       fragmentation of a second molecule of AdoMet, yielding a
CC       5'-deoxyadenosine radical, which then attacks the methylated sulfur
CC       atom of the polysulfide bridge, resulting in the transfer of a
CC       methylsulfanyl group to aspartate(89) (Escherichia coli numbering).
CC   -!- The enzyme is a member of the superfamily of S-adenosyl-L-methionine-
CC       dependent radical (radical AdoMet) enzymes.
