ID   2.8.4.5
DE   tRNA (N(6)-L-threonylcarbamoyladenosine(37)-C(2))-methylthiotransferase.
AN   methylthio-threonylcarbamoyl-adenosine transferase B.
CA   N(6)-L-threonylcarbamoyladenosine(37) in tRNA + (sulfur carrier)-SH +
CA   AH2 + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 2-methylsulfanyl-N(6)-L-
CA   threonylcarbamoyladenosine(37) in tRNA + (sulfur carrier)-H +
CA   5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + A + S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is a member of the S-adenosyl-L-methionine-
CC       dependent radical (radical AdoMet) enzymes superfamily, binds two
CC       [4Fe-4S] clusters as well as the transferred sulfur.
CC   -!- The sulfur donor is believed to be one of the [4Fe-4S] clusters,
CC       which is sacrificed in the process, so that in vitro the reaction is
CC       a single turnover.
CC   -!- The identity of the electron donor is not known.
DR   O29021, AMTAB_ARCFU;  Q58277, AMTAB_METJA;  O26914, AMTAB_METTH;
DR   Q9UXX9, AMTAB_PYRAB;  O59545, AMTAB_PYRHO;  Q8MXQ7, CDKAL_CAEEL;
