DR   Q9Z874, MTAB_CHLPN ;  Q49573, MTAB_MALIO ;  Q9ZDB6, MTAB_RICPR ;
DR   Q9WZT7, MTAB_THEMA ;  O83293, MTAB_TREPA ;
//
ID   2.8.4.6
DE   S-methyl-1-thioxylulose 5-phosphate methylthiotransferase.
AN   1-methylthioxylulose 5-phosphate sulfurylase.
CA   S-methyl-1-thio-D-xylulose 5-phosphate + glutathione =
CA   S-(methylsulfanyl)glutathione + 1-deoxy-D-xylulose 5-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Rhodospirillum rubrum,
CC       belongs to the cupin superfamily and contains a manganese ion.
CC   -!- It participates in an anaerobic salvage pathway that restores
CC       methionine from S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine.
CC   -!- The enzyme was assayed in vitro using L-dithiothreitol instead of
CC       glutathione.
DR   Q2RSU5, CUPIN_RHORT;
//
ID   2.8.5.1
DE   S-sulfo-L-cysteine synthase (3-phospho-L-serine-dependent).
CA   O-phospho-L-serine + thiosulfate = S-sulfo-L-cysteine + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has been characterized from the bacterium
CC       Mycobacterium tuberculosis, has no activity with O-acetyl-L-serine.
CC       cf. EC 2.5.1.144.
DR   Q79FV4, CYSK2_MYCTU;
//
ID   2.8.5.2
DE   L-cysteine S-thiosulfotransferase.
CA   (1) L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein] + thiosulfate + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome c] =
CA   S-sulfosulfanyl-L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein] + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] +
CA   2 H(+).
CA   (2) S-sulfanyl-L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein] + thiosulfate + 2 Fe(III)-
CA   [cytochrome c] = S-(2-sulfodisulfanyl)-L-cysteinyl-[SoxY protein] +
CA   2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome c] + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of the Sox enzyme system, which participates in a
CC       bacterial thiosulfate oxidation pathway that produces sulfate.
CC   -!- It catalyzes two reactions in the pathway - early in the pathway it
CC       attaches a thiosulfate molecule to the sulfur atom of an L-cysteine
CC       of a SoxY protein; later it transfers a second thiosulfate molecule
CC       to a sulfane group that is already attached to the same cysteine
CC       residue.
DR   D3DJG4, SOXA1_HYDTT;  D3DJG5, SOXA2_HYDTT;  Q1W3E4, SOXA_ALLVI ;
DR   D7A6E5, SOXA_ANCN5 ;  Q8KDM7, SOXA_CHLTE ;  Q8RLX0, SOXA_CHLTI ;
DR   Q08IS0, SOXA_HYDTE ;  O33434, SOXA_PARPN ;  Q9K4M4, SOXA_PSESE ;
DR   Q939U1, SOXA_RHOSU ;
//
ID   2.9.1.1
DE   L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) selenium transferase.
AN   cysteinyl-tRNA(Sec)-selenium transferase.
AN   cysteinyl-tRNA(Sel)-selenium transferase.
AN   L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec) synthase.
AN   L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sel) synthase.
AN   selenocysteine synthase.
CA   L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) + selenophosphate + H(+) = L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec)
CA   + phosphate.
CC   -!- Recognizes specifically tRNA(Sec)-species.
CC   -!- Binding of tRNA(Sec) also occurs in the absence of the seryl group.
CC   -!- 2-Aminoacryloyl-tRNA, bound to the enzyme as an imine with the
CC       pyridoxal phosphate, is an intermediate in the reaction.
