ID   2.9.1.2
DE   O-phospho-L-seryl-tRNA(Sec):L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA synthase.
AN   O-phosphoseryl-tRNA:selenocysteinyl-tRNA synthase.
AN   O-phosphoseryl-tRNA(Sec) selenium transferase.
AN   SepSecS.
CA   O-phospho-L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) + selenophosphate + H2O = L-selenocysteinyl-
CA   tRNA(Sec) + 2 phosphate.
CC   -!- In archaea and eukarya selenocysteine formation is achieved by a two-
CC       step process: EC 2.7.1.164 phosphorylates the endogenous L-seryl-
CC       tRNA(Sec) to O-phospho-L-seryl-tRNA(Sec), and then this misacylated
CC       amino acid-tRNA species is converted to L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec)
CC       by Sep-tRNA:Sec-tRNA synthase.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.9.1.n1.
