ID   2.9.1.3
DE   tRNA 2-selenouridine synthase.
CA   5-methylaminomethyl-2-thiouridine(34) in tRNA + selenophosphate + (2E)-
CA   geranyl diphosphate + H2O + H(+) = 5-methylaminomethyl-2-
CA   selenouridine(34) in tRNA + (2E)-thiogeraniol + phosphate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme converts 5-methylaminomethyl-2-uridine and
CC       5-carboxymethylaminomethyl-2-uridine to the respective selenouridine
CC       forms in a two-step process that involves geranylation and subsequent
CC       phosphoselenation of the resulting geranylated intermediates.
CC   -!- The resultant seleno-phosphorylated uridine intermediates further
CC       react with a water molecule to release a phosphate anion and
CC       2-selenouridine tRNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a rhodanese domain.
