ID   3.1.1.3
DE   triacylglycerol lipase.
AN   lipase.
AN   tributyrase.
AN   triglyceride lipase.
CA   a triacylglycerol + H2O = a diacylglycerol + a fatty acid + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in diverse organisms including animals, plants,
CC       fungi, and bacteria.
CC   -!- It hydrolyzes triglycerides into diglycerides and subsequently into
CC       monoglycerides and free fatty acids.
CC   -!- The enzyme is highly soluble in water and acts at the surface of oil
CC       droplets.
CC   -!- Access to the active site is controlled by the opening of a lid,
CC       which, when closed, hides the hydrophobic surface that surrounds the
CC       active site.
CC   -!- The lid opens when the enzyme contacts an oil-water interface
CC       (interfacial activation).
CC   -!- The pancreatic enzyme requires a protein cofactor, namely colipase,
CC       to counteract the inhibitory effects of bile salts.
