ID   3.1.1.29
DE   peptidyl-tRNA hydrolase.
AN   aminoacyl-transfer ribonucleate hydrolase.
AN   aminoacyl-tRNA hydrolase.
AN   N-substituted aminoacyl transfer RNA hydrolase.
CA   an N-acyl-L-alpha-aminoacyl-tRNA + H2O = an N-acyl-L-amino acid + a tRNA
CA   + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on premature protein synthesis products that
CC       dissociate from stalled ribosomes, cleaving the peptidyl chains and
CC       restoring functionality to the tRNA.
CC   -!- In most organisms mutants with limited Pth activity accumulate
CC       peptidyl-tRNAs, reducing the availability of uncharged tRNAs below
CC       the limit that is necessary for protein synthesis and impairing cell
CC       growth.
CC   -!- Two distinct classes of the enzyme, Pth and Pth2, have been
CC       identified.
CC   -!- While most enzymes can recognize and cleave N-acylated aminoacyl-
CC       tRNAs, they are not able to act on N-formyl-methionyl-tRNA.
