//
ID   3.1.1.40
DE   orsellinate-depside hydrolase.
AN   lecanorate hydrolase.
CA   o-orsellinate depside + H2O = 2 orsellinate + H(+).
CC   -!- Will only hydrolyze those substrates based on the 2,4-dihydroxy-6-
CC       methylbenzoate structure that also have a free hydroxyl ortho to the
CC       depside linkage.
//
ID   3.1.1.41
DE   cephalosporin-C deacetylase.
CA   cephalosporin C + H2O = deacetylcephalosporin C + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- Hydrolyzes the acetyl ester bond on the 10-position of the antibiotic
CC       cephalosporin C.
