//
ID   3.1.1.50
DE   wax-ester hydrolase.
CA   a long-chain alcohol wax ester + H2O = a long chain fatty alcohol +
CA   a long-chain fatty acid + H(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on long-chain acylglycerol, but not diacyl- or
CC       triacylglycerols.
//
ID   3.1.1.51
DE   phorbol-diester hydrolase.
AN   diacylphorbate 12-hydrolase.
CA   phorbol 12,13-dibutanoate + H2O = phorbol 13-butanoate + butanoate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- Hydrolyzes the 12-ester bond in a variety of 12,13-diacylphorbols
CC       (phorbol is a diterpenoid).
CC   -!- This reaction inactivates tumor promoter 12-O-tetradecanoylphorbol-
CC       13-acetate from croton oil.
//
ID   3.1.1.52
DE   phosphatidylinositol deacylase.
AN   Phosphatidylinositol phospholipase A2.
CA   a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + H2O = a 1-acyl-
CA   sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + a fatty acid + H(+).
//
ID   3.1.1.53
DE   sialate O-acetylesterase.
CA   (1) N-acetyl-9-O-acetylneuraminate + H2O = N-acetylneuraminate + acetate
CA   + H(+).
CA   (2) N-acetyl-4-O-acetylneuraminate + H2O = N-acetylneuraminate + acetate
CA   + H(+).
CC   -!- Acts on free and glycosidically-bound N-acetyl- or
CC       N-glycoloylneuraminic acid.
CC   -!- Acts mainly on 4-O- and 9-O-acetyl groups.
CC   -!- Also acts on some other O-acetyl esters, both cyclic and acyclic
