ID   3.1.1.90
DE   all-trans-retinyl ester 13-cis isomerohydrolase.
CA   an all-trans-retinyl ester + H2O = 13-cis-retinol + a fatty acid + H(+).
CC   -!- all-trans-retinyl esters, which are a storage form of vitamin A,
CC       are generated by the activity of EC 2.3.1.135.
CC   -!- They can be hydrolyzed to 11-cis-retinol by EC 3.1.1.64, or to
CC       13-cis-retinol by this enzyme.
DR   A9C3R9, RP65B_DANRE;  A9C3R8, RP65C_DANRE;
//
ID   3.1.1.91
DE   2-oxo-3-(5-oxofuran-2-ylidene)propanoate lactonase.
CA   2-oxo-3-(5-oxofuran-2-ylidene)propanoate + H2O = 3-maleylpyruvate + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, characterized from the soil bacterium Bradyrhizobium sp.
CC       JS329, is involved in the pathway of 5-nitroanthranilate degradation.
DR   F8QQ74, NAAC_BRASZ ;
//
ID   3.1.1.92
DE   4-sulfomuconolactone hydrolase.
CA   4-sulfomuconolactone + H2O = maleylacetate + sulfite + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme was isolated from the bacteria Hydrogenophaga intermedia
CC       and Agrobacterium radiobacter S2.
CC   -!- It catalyzes a step in the degradation of 4-sulfocatechol.
DR   A6XIG7, SLMH_AGRRD ;  A6XIG6, SLMH_HYDIT ;
//
ID   3.1.1.93
DE   mycophenolic acid acyl-glucuronide esterase.
AN   AcMPAG deglucuronidase.
AN   mycophenolic acid acyl-glucuronide deglucuronidase.
CA   mycophenolic acid O-acyl-beta-D-glucuronide + H2O = mycophenolate +
CA   D-glucuronate + H(+).
CC   -!- This liver enzyme deglucuronidates mycophenolic acid O-acyl-
CC       glucuronide, a metabolite of the immunosuppressant drug mycophenolate
CC       that is thought to be immunotoxic.
DR   Q5E9H9, ABHDA_BOVIN;  Q9NUJ1, ABHDA_HUMAN;  Q6PE15, ABHDA_MOUSE;
DR   Q5REX5, ABHDA_PONAB;  Q5I0K5, ABHDA_RAT  ;
//
ID   3.1.1.94
DE   versiconal hemiacetal acetate esterase.
AN   VHA esterase.
CA   (1) (2S,3S)-versiconal hemiacetal acetate + H2O = (2S-3S)-versiconal
CA   hemiacetal + acetate + H(+).
CA   (2) (3S)-versiconol acetate + H2O = (S)-versiconol + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the mold Aspergillus parasiticus.
CC   -!- Involved in a metabolic grid that leads to aflatoxin biosynthesis.
DR   Q6UEG5, AFLJ_ASPPU ;  M2YJ38, EST1_DOTSN ;  Q00675, STCI_EMENI ;
//
ID   3.1.1.95
DE   aclacinomycin methylesterase.
AN   aclacinomycin methyl esterase.
CA   aclacinomycin T + H2O = 15-demethylaclacinomycin T + methanol.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the modification of the aklavinone skeleton
CC       in the biosynthesis of anthracyclines in Streptomyces species.
DR   Q54528, RDMC_STREF ;
//
ID   3.1.1.96
DE   D-aminoacyl-tRNA deacylase.
AN   D-tyrosyl-tRNA(Tyr) aminoacylhydrolase.
AN   D-Tyr-tRNA(Tyr) deacylase.
CA   (1) a D-aminoacyl-tRNA + H2O = a tRNA + a D-alpha-amino acid + H(+).
CA   (2) glycyl-tRNA(Ala) + H2O = tRNA(Ala) + glycine + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in all domains of life, can cleave mischarged
CC       glycyl-tRNA(Ala).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli can cleave D-tyrosyl-tRNA(Tyr),
CC       D-aspartyl-tRNA(Asp) and D-tryptophanyl-tRNA(Trp).
CC   -!- Whereas the enzyme from the archaeon Pyrococcus abyssi is a zinc
CC       protein, the enzyme from Escherichia coli does not carry any zinc.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.n1.
