ID   3.1.1.99
DE   6-deoxy-6-sulfogluconolactonase.
AN   SGL lactonase.
CA   6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-glucono-1,5-lactone + H2O = 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate
CA   + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas putida SQ1,
CC       participates in a sulfoquinovose degradation pathway.
DR   P0DOV6, SGL_PSEPU  ;
//
ID   3.1.1.100
DE   chlorophyllide a hydrolase.
AN   bciC (gene name).
CA   chlorophyllide a + H2O + H(+) = 8-ethyl-12-methyl-3-
CA   vinylbacteriochlorophyllide d + methanol + CO2.
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae) and green
CC       filamentous bacteria (Chloroflexaceae), catalyzes the first committed
CC       step in the biosynthesis of bacteriochlorophylls c, d and e,
CC       the removal of the C-13(2)-methylcarboxyl group from chlorophyllide
CC       a.
CC   -!- The reaction is very similar to the conversion of pheophorbide a to
CC       pyropheophorbide a during chlorophyll a degradation, which is
CC       catalyzed by EC 3.1.1.82.
//
ID   3.1.1.101
DE   poly(ethylene terephthalate) hydrolase.
AN   PETase.
AN   PET hydrolase.
CA   (ethylene terephthalate)(n) + H2O = (ethylene terephthalate)(n-1) +
CA   4-[(2-hydroxyethoxy)carbonyl]benzoate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Ideonella sakaiensis, also
CC       produces small amounts of terephthalate (cf. EC 3.1.1.102).
CC   -!- The reaction takes place on PET-film placed in solution.
DR   D4Q9N1, PETH1_THEAE;  E9LVH8, PETH1_THECS;  G8GER6, PETH1_THEFU;
DR   Q47RJ7, PETH1_THEFY;  F7IX06, PETH2_THEAE;  E9LVH9, PETH2_THECS;
DR   Q6A0I4, PETH2_THEFU;  Q47RJ6, PETH2_THEFY;  A0A0K8P6T7, PETH_PISS1 ;
DR   G9BY57, PETH_UNKP  ;
//
ID   3.1.1.102
DE   mono(ethylene terephthalate) hydrolase.
AN   MHETase.
AN   MHET hydrolase.
CA   4-[(2-hydroxyethoxy)carbonyl]benzoate + H2O = terephthalate + ethylene
CA   glycol + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Ideonella sakaiensis, has no
CC       activity with poly(ethylene terephthalate) PET (cf. EC 3.1.1.101).
DR   A0A0K8P8E7, MHETH_PISS1;
//
ID   3.1.1.103
DE   teichoic acid D-alanine hydrolase.
CA   [(4-D-Ala)-(2-GlcNAc)-Rib-ol-P]n-[Gro-P]m-beta-D-ManNAc-(1->4)-alpha-D-
CA   GlcNAc-P-peptidoglycan + n H2O = [(2-GlcNAc)-Rib-ol-P]n-[Gro-P]m-beta-D-
CA   ManNAc-(1->4)-alpha-D-GlcNAc-P-peptidoglycan + n D-alanine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus,
CC       removes D-alanine groups from the teichoic acid produced by this
CC       organism, thus modulating the electrical charge of the bacterial
CC       surface.
CC   -!- The activity greatly increases methicillin resistance in MRSA
CC       strains.
DR   Q2FZK3, FMTA_STAA8 ;  Q5HH27, FMTA_STAAC ;  Q7A2T0, FMTA_STAAM ;
DR   Q7A6A2, FMTA_STAAN ;  Q6GI27, FMTA_STAAR ;  Q6GAF6, FMTA_STAAS ;
DR   O50608, FMTA_STAAU ;  Q7A185, FMTA_STAAW ;
//
ID   3.1.1.104
DE   5-phospho-D-xylono-1,4-lactonase.
CA   (1) D-xylono-1,4-lactone 5-phosphate + H2O = 5-phospho-D-xylonate + H(+).
CA   (2) L-arabino-1,4-lactone 5-phosphate + H2O = 5-phospho-L-arabinonate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Mycoplasma spp., contains a binuclear
CC       metal center with two zinc cations.
CC   -!- The enzyme is specific for the phosphorylated forms, and is unable to
CC       hydrolyze non-phosphorylated 1,4-lactones.
DR   A5IZ80, PFLAC_MYCAP;  Q4A724, PFLAC_MYCS5;
//
ID   3.1.1.105
DE   3-O-acetylpapaveroxine carboxylesterase.
CA   3-O-acetylpapaveroxine + H2O = narcotine hemiacetal + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Papaver somniferum (opium
CC       poppy), participates in the biosynthesis of the isoquinoline alkaloid
CC       noscapine.
DR   I3PLR2, CXE1_PAPSO ;  A0A0A1EQ07, CXE2_PAPSO ;
//
ID   3.1.1.106
DE   O-acetyl-ADP-ribose deacetylase.
CA   (1) 3''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose + H2O = ADP-D-ribose + acetate + H(+).
CA   (2) 2''-O-acetyl-ADP-D-ribose + H2O = ADP-D-ribose + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli and
CC       from human cells, removes the acetyl group from either the 2'' or 3''
CC       position of O-acetyl-ADP-ribose, which are formed by the action of
CC       EC 2.3.1.286.
CC   -!- The human enzyme can also remove ADP-D-ribose from phosphorylated
CC       double stranded DNA adducts.
DR   Q2KHU5, MACD1_BOVIN;  Q9BQ69, MACD1_HUMAN;  Q922B1, MACD1_MOUSE;
DR   Q8K4G6, MACD1_RAT  ;  E1SDF1, YMDB1_PANVC;  E1PL40, YMDB2_PANVC;
DR   A8AI35, YMDB_CITK8 ;  D2TT52, YMDB_CITRI ;  A7MG20, YMDB_CROS8 ;
DR   C9Y0V8, YMDB_CROTZ ;  P0A8D8, YMDB_ECO57 ;  P0A8D7, YMDB_ECOL6 ;
DR   P0A8D6, YMDB_ECOLI ;  A4W960, YMDB_ENT38 ;  D5CE05, YMDB_ENTCC ;
DR   B7LT90, YMDB_ESCF3 ;  B5XXK9, YMDB_KLEV3 ;  D3RKJ0, YMDB_KLEVT ;
DR   B5F961, YMDB_SALA4 ;  B5RBF3, YMDB_SALG2 ;  B4T2X8, YMDB_SALNS ;
DR   P67342, YMDB_SALTI ;  P67341, YMDB_SALTY ;  Q32E73, YMDB_SHIDS ;
DR   Q0T5Z6, YMDB_SHIF8 ;
