ID   3.1.1.107
DE   apo-salmochelin esterase.
CA   (1) enterobactin + H2O = N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine trimer.
CA   (2) triglucosyl-enterobactin + H2O = [N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]3 + H(+).
CA   (3) diglucosyl-enterobactin + H2O = N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-
CA   [N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]2 + H(+).
CA   (4) monoglucosyl-enterobactin + H2O = [N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-
CA   seryl]2-N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme is present in pathogenic Salmonella species,
CC       uropathogenic and avian pathogenic Escherichia coli strains,
CC       and certain Klebsiella strains.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.1.1.108, which acts only on enterobactin, this enzyme can
CC       also act on the C-glucosylated forms known as salmochelins.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.1.1.109, (IroD), IroE prefers apo siderophores as
CC       substrates, and is assumed to act before the siderophores are
CC       exported out of the cell.
CC   -!- It hydrolyzes the trilactone only once, producing linearized trimers.
DR   A0A0H2V871, IROE_ECOL6 ;
//
ID   3.1.1.108
DE   iron(III) enterobactin esterase.
CA   Fe(III)-enterobactin + 3 H2O + H(+) = Fe(III)-[N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-
CA   L-serine] + 2 N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Escherichia coli, allows the
CC       bacterium to grow in limited iron conditions.
CC   -!- It can also act on enterobactin (with no complexed iron) and the
CC       aluminum(III) analog of iron(III) enterobactin.
CC   -!- The trimer formed is further hydrolyzed to form the dimer and the
CC       monomer.
DR   O51900, FES_DICD3  ;  A0A0H2V760, FES_ECOL6  ;  P13039, FES_ECOLI  ;
DR   Q56855, FES_YEREN  ;  Q9I0F2, PFEE_PSEAE ;
//
ID   3.1.1.109
DE   iron(III) salmochelin esterase.
CA   (1) Fe(III)-di(C-5-deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl)-enterobactin + H2O = Fe(III)-
CA   {N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-[N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]2} + H(+).
CA   (2) Fe(III)-C-5-deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl-enterobactin + H2O = Fe(III)-
CA   {di[N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl]-N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine} + H(+).
CA   (3) Fe(III)-{N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-[N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-
CA   glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]2} + H2O + H(+) = Fe(III)-
CA   [N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]2 +
CA   N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.
CA   (4) Fe(III)-{N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-[N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-
CA   glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine]2} + H2O + H(+) = Fe(III)-
CA   {N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine} + N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.
CA   (5) Fe(III)-{di[N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl]-N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-
CA   glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine} + H2O + H(+) = Fe(III)-{N-(2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-seryl-N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine} + N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.
CA   (6) Fe(III)-[N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-
CA   serine]2 + H2O + H(+) = Fe(III)-[N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine] + N-(C-5-[deoxy-beta-D-glucosyl]-2,3-
CA   dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme is present in pathogenic Salmonella species,
CC       uropathogenic and avian pathogenic Escherichia coli strains,
CC       and certain Klebsiella strains.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on iron(III)-bound enterobactin and C-glucosylated
CC       derivatives known as salmochelins.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.1.1.107, (IroE), IroD prefers iron(III)-bound
CC       siderophores as substrates, and is assumed to act after the iron-
CC       siderophore complexes are imported into the cell.
CC   -!- It catalyzes several hydrolytic reactions, producing a mixture of
CC       iron(III)-[N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine] complex and salmochelin
CC       SX.
DR   A0A0H2V660, IROD_ECOL6 ;
//
ID   3.1.1.110
DE   xylono-1,5-lactonase.
AN   D-xylono-1,5-lactone lactonase.
CA   D-xylono-1,5-lactone + H2O = D-xylonate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in bacteria, participates in the degradation of
CC       D-xylose. cf. EC 3.1.1.68.
DR   Q9A9Z1, XYLC_CAUVC ;
//
ID   3.1.1.111
DE   phosphatidylserine sn-1 acylhydrolase.
AN   phosphatidylserine-specific phospholipase A1.
CA   (1) a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-L-serine + H2O = a 2-acyl-
CA   sn-glycero-3-phospho-L-serine + a fatty acid + H(+).
CA   (2) a 1-acyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-L-serine + H2O = sn-glycero-3-phospho-
CA   L-serine + a fatty acid + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has described from mammals, is specific for
CC       phosphatidylserine and 2-lysophosphatidylserine, and does not act on
CC       phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylethanolamine, phosphatidic acid or
CC       phosphatidylinositol.
DR   Q9H3Z7, ABHGB_HUMAN;  Q80YU0, ABHGB_MOUSE;  Q5XIL6, ABHGB_RAT  ;
DR   O46606, DDHD1_BOVIN;  Q8NEL9, DDHD1_HUMAN;  Q80YA3, DDHD1_MOUSE;
DR   Q5E9H0, PLA1A_BOVIN;  Q53H76, PLA1A_HUMAN;  Q8VI78, PLA1A_MOUSE;
DR   Q5RBQ5, PLA1A_PONAB;  P97535, PLA1A_RAT  ;  G5EEM9, PLA1_CAEEL ;
//
ID   3.1.1.112
DE   isoamyl acetate esterase.
CA   3-methylbutyl acetate + H2O = 3-methylbutan-1-ol + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae,
CC       hydrolyzes acetate esters.
CC   -!- It acts preferentially on 3-methylbutyl acetate, a major determinant
CC       of sake flavor.
DR   O74648, IAH1_SCHPO ;  P41734, IAH1_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.1.1.113
DE   ethyl acetate hydrolase.
CA   ethyl acetate + H2O = ethanol + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Pseudomonas strains, is involved in
CC       degradation of short chain alkyl methyl ketones.
