ID   3.1.3.78
DE   phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate 4-phosphatase.
AN   PtdIns-4,5-P2 4-phosphatase.
CA   a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol-4,5-bisphosphate) +
CA   H2O = a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol-5-phosphate) +
CA   phosphate.
CC   -!- Two pathways exist in mammalian cells to degrade 1-phosphatidyl-
CC       1D-myo-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate [PtdIns(4,5)P2].
CC   -!- One is catalyzed by this enzyme and the other by EC 3.1.3.36, where
CC       the product is PtdIns4P.
CC   -!- The enzyme from human is specific for PtdIns(4,5)P2 as substrate,
CC       as it cannot use PtdIns(3,4,5)P3, PtdIns(3,4)P2, PtdIns(3,5)P2,
CC       PtdIns5P, PtdIns4P or PtdIns3P.
CC   -!- In humans, the enzyme is localized to late endosomal/lysosomal
CC       membranes.
CC   -!- It can control nuclear levels of PtdIns5P and thereby control p53-
CC       dependent apoptosis.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.3.n3.
DR   Q07566, IPGD_SHIFL ;  Q55286, IPGD_SHISO ;  Q86T03, PP4P1_HUMAN;
DR   Q4R6W2, PP4P1_MACFA;  Q3TWL2, PP4P1_MOUSE;  Q5PPM8, PP4P1_RAT  ;
DR   Q5XKA6, PP4P1_XENLA;  Q3SZ48, PP4P2_BOVIN;  Q8N4L2, PP4P2_HUMAN;
DR   Q9CZX7, PP4P2_MOUSE;  Q4V888, PP4P2_RAT  ;  Q5EAU3, PP4P2_XENLA;
