ID   3.1.3.85
DE   glucosyl-3-phosphoglycerate phosphatase.
CA   (2R)-2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-3-phospho-glycerate + H2O = (2R)-2-
CA   O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-glycerate + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of 2-O-(alpha-D-
CC       glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate via the two-step pathway in which
CC       EC 2.4.1.266 catalyzes the conversion of GDP-glucose and 3-phospho-D-
CC       glycerate into 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-3-phospho-D-glycerate,
CC       which is then converted to 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate
CC       by glucosyl-3-phosphoglycerate phosphatase.
CC   -!- In vivo the enzyme catalyzes the dephosphorylation of 2-O-(alpha-D-
CC       mannopyranosyl)-3-phospho-D-glycerate with lower efficiency.
CC   -!- Divalent metal ions (Mg(2+), Mn(2+) or Co(2+)) stimulate activity.
