ID   3.1.3.100
DE   thiamine phosphate phosphatase.
CA   thiamine phosphate + H2O = thiamine + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the thiamine biosynthesis pathway in
CC       eukaryotes and a few prokaryotes.
CC   -!- These organisms lack EC 2.7.4.16 and need to convert thiamine
CC       phosphate to thiamine diphosphate, the active form of the vitamin,
CC       by first removing the phosphate group, followed by diphosphorylation
CC       by EC 2.7.6.2.
