ID   3.1.3.108
DE   nocturnin.
AN   nocturnin (curled).
CA   (1) NADPH + H2O = phosphate + NADH.
CA   (2) NADP(+) + H2O = phosphate + NAD(+).
CC   -!- The mammalian mitochondrial enzyme is a rhythmically expressed
CC       protein that regulates metabolism under the control of circadian
CC       clock.
CC   -!- It has a slight preference for NADPH over NADP(+).
CC   -!- The archaeal enzyme, identified in Methanocaldococcus jannaschii,
CC       is bifunctional acting as NAD kinase (EC 2.7.1.23) and NADP
CC       phosphatase with a slight preference for NADP(+) over NADPH.
DR   Q9UK39, NOCT_HUMAN ;  O35710, NOCT_MOUSE ;  Q9ET55, NOCT_RAT   ;
//
ID   3.1.3.109
DE   ribulose-1,5-bisphosphate 5-phosphatase.
AN   RuBP 5-phosphatase.
CA   D-ribulose 1,5-bisphosphate + H2O = D-ribulose 1-phosphate + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the halophilic archaeon Halopiger
CC       xanaduensis, participates in a non-carboxylating pentose bisphosphate
CC       pathway for nucleoside degradation, which is found in some halophilic
CC       archaea.
CC   -!- The enzyme requires both monovalent and divalent ions for optimal
CC       activity.
DR   F8D9F4, RUBPP_HALXS;
//
ID   3.1.3.110
DE   4'-phosphopantetheine phosphatase.
CA   (R)-4'-phosphopantetheine + H2O = (R)-pantetheine + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from mammals and from the bacterium
CC       Streptantibioticus cattleyicolor.
CC   -!- In mammals it hydrolyzes excess 4'-phosphopantetheine to prevent cell
CC       damage.
CC   -!- In S. cattleyicolor it participates in the biosynthesis of the beta-
CC       lactam antibiotic thienamycin.
//
ID   3.1.3.111
