ID   3.1.4.61
DE   cyclic 2,3-diphosphoglycerate hydrolase.
CA   cyclic (2R)-2,3-bisphosphoglycerate + H2O = (2R)-2,3-bisphosphoglycerate
CA   + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme degrades cyclic 2,3-bisphosphoglycerate,
CC       a thermoprotectant that is produced by certain archaeal genera.
CC   -!- Two different enzymes that catalyze this activity, one soluble and
CC       one membrane-bound, have been characterized from the archaeon
CC       Methanothermobacter thermautotrophicus.
