ID   3.1.6.1
DE   arylsulfatase (type I).
AN   aryl-sulfate sulphohydrolase.
AN   sulfatase.
CA   an aryl sulfate + H2O = a phenol + sulfate + H(+).
CC   -!- Sulfatase enzymes are classified as type I, in which the key
CC       catalytic residue is 3-oxo-L-alanine, type II, which are non-heme
CC       iron-dependent dioxygenases, or type III, whose catalytic domain
CC       adopts a metallo-beta-lactamase fold and binds two zinc ions as
CC       cofactors.
CC   -!- Arylsulfatases are type I enzymes, found in both prokaryotes and
CC       eukaryotes, with rather similar specificities.
CC   -!- The key catalytic residue 3-oxo-L-alanine initiates the reaction
CC       through a nucleophilic attack on the sulfur atom in the substrate.
CC   -!- This residue is generated by post-translational modification of a
CC       conserved cysteine or serine residue by EC 1.8.3.7, EC 1.1.98.7,
CC       or EC 1.8.98.7.
DR   P54793, ARSF_HUMAN ;  Q32KH9, ARSG_CANLF ;  Q96EG1, ARSG_HUMAN ;
