ID   3.1.21.2
DE   deoxyribonuclease IV.
AN   deoxyribonuclease IV (phage T4-induced).
AN   endodeoxyribonuclease IV (phage T4-induced).
AN   endonuclease II.
AN   endonuclease IV.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage to 5'-phosphooligonucleotide end-products.
CC   -!- The enzyme is an apurinic/apyrimidinic (AP) site endonuclease that
CC       primes DNA repair synthesis at AP sites.
CC   -!- It specifically cleaves the DNA backbone at AP sites and also removes
CC       3' DNA-blocking groups such as 3' phosphates, 3' phosphoglycolates,
CC       and 3' alpha,beta-unsaturated aldehydes that arise from oxidative
CC       base damage and the activity of combined glycosylase/lyase enzymes.
CC   -!- It is also the only known repair enzyme that is able to cleave the
CC       DNA backbone 5' of the oxidative lesion alpha-deoxyadenosine.
CC   -!- The enzyme has a strong preference for single-stranded DNA.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.4.30.
