ID   3.1.21.3
DE   type I site-specific deoxyribonuclease.
AN   type I restriction enzyme.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of DNA to give random double-stranded fragments
CA   with terminal 5'-phosphates, ATP is simultaneously hydrolyzed.
CC   -!- Large group of enzymes that have an absolute requirement for ATP (or
CC       dATP) and S-adenosyl-L-methionine.
CC   -!- They recognize specific short DNA sequences and cleave at sites
CC       remote from the recognition sequence.
CC   -!- Multifunctional proteins which also catalyze the reactions of
CC       EC 2.1.1.72 and EC 2.1.1.73, with similar site specificity.
CC   -!- See the REBASE database for a complete list of these enzymes:
CC       http://rebase.neb.com/rebase/
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.24.1 and EC 3.1.24.2.
