ID   3.1.21.5
DE   type III site-specific deoxyribonuclease.
AN   type III restriction enzyme.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of DNA to give specific double-stranded
CA   fragments with terminal 5'-phosphates.
CC   -!- Has an absolute requirement for ATP, but does not hydrolyze it;
CC       S-adenosyl-L-methionine stimulates the reaction, but is not
CC       absolutely required.
CC   -!- Recognize specific short DNA sequences and cleave a short distance
CC       away from the recognition sequence.
CC   -!- Exist as complexes with enzymes of similar specificity listed under
CC       EC 2.1.1.72 or EC 2.1.1.73.
CC   -!- See the REBASE database for a complete list of these enzymes:
CC       http://rebase.neb.com/rebase/
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.24.3 and EC 3.1.24.4.
DR   P25241, T3RE_BACC1 ;  P08764, T3RE_BPP1  ;  Q5ZND2, T3RE_ECOLX ;
DR   P40815, T3RE_SALTY ;  P44105, T3RH_HAEIN ;
//
ID   3.1.21.6
DE   CC-preferring endodeoxyribonuclease.
AN   5'-CC-3'-preferring endodeoxyribonuclease.
AN   Streptomyces glaucescens exocytoplasmic endodeoxyribonuclease.
AN   Streptomyces glaucescens exocytoplasmic endonuclease.
CA   endonucleolytic cleavage to give 5'-phosphooligonucleotide end-products,
CA   with a preference for cleavage within the sequence CC.
CC   -!- Prefers CC sites in double-stranded circular and linear DNA.
CC   -!- Greater affinity for double-stranded than single-stranded DNA.
CC   -!- Produces nicks, generating double-stranded fragments with 5'- and/or
CC       3'-protruding single-stranded tails.
//
