//
ID   3.1.21.8
DE   T4 deoxyribonuclease II.
AN   T4 endonuclease II.
CA   Endonucleolytic nicking and cleavage of cytosine-containing double-
CA   stranded DNA.
CC   -!- This phage T4 enzyme is involved in degradation of host DNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme primarily catalyzes nicking of the bottom strand of double
CC       stranded DNA between the first and second base pair to the right of a
CC       top-strand CCGC motif.
CC   -!- Double-stranded breaks are produced 5- to 10-fold less frequently.
CC   -!- It does not cleave the T4 native DNA, which contains
CC       5-hydroxymethylcytosine instead of cytosine.
DR   P07059, END2_BPT4  ;
//
ID   3.1.21.9
DE   T4 deoxyribonuclease IV.
AN   T4 endonuclease IV.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of the 5' phosphodiester bond of deoxycytidine
CA   in single-stranded DNA.
CC   -!- This phage T4 enzyme is involved in degradation of host DNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not cleave double-stranded DNA or native T4 DNA,
CC       which contains 5-hydroxymethylcytosine instead of cytosine.
DR   P39250, END4_BPT4  ;
//
ID   3.1.21.10
DE   crossover junction endodeoxyribonuclease.
AN   crossover junction endoribonuclease.
AN   cruciform-cutting endonuclease.
AN   endonuclease RuvC.
AN   endonuclease VII.
AN   endonuclease X3.
AN   endo X3.
AN   Hje endonuclease.
AN   Holliday junction-cleaving endonuclease.
AN   Holliday junction endonuclease CCE1.
AN   Holliday junction nuclease.
AN   Holliday junction resolvase.
AN   Holliday junction-resolving endoribonuclease.
AN   resolving enzyme CCE1.
AN   RusA endonuclease.
AN   RusA Holliday junction resolvase.
AN   RuvC endonuclease.
AN   SpCCe1 Holliday junction resolvase.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage at a junction such as a reciprocal single-
CA   stranded crossover between two homologous DNA duplexes (Holliday
CA   junction).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Saccharomyces cerevisiae has no endonuclease or
CC       exonuclease activity on single-stranded or double-stranded DNA
CC       molecules that do not contain Holliday junctions.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.22.4.
