//
ID   3.1.26.5
DE   ribonuclease P.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of RNA, removing 5'-extranucleotides from tRNA
CA   precursor.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is found in archaea, bacteria and eukaryotes,
CC       is essential for tRNA processing.
CC   -!- It generates 5'-termini or mature tRNA molecules.
CC   -!- The enzyme from most sources has been shown to have an RNA chain and
CC       a one or more polypeptide chains, but since the RNA chain can act
CC       alone as a catalyst in vitro the enzyme should be considered to be a
CC       ribozyme.
CC   -!- Human mitochondrial RNase P has been shown to be a protein that does
CC       not require RNA for activity. Spinach chloroplast RNase P has also
CC       been shown to function without an RNA component.
