ID   3.1.26.9
DE   ribonuclease [poly-(U)-specific].
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of poly(U) to fragments terminated by 3'-hydroxy
CA   and 5'-phosphate groups.
CC   -!- Forms oligonucleotides with chain length 6-12.
//
ID   3.1.26.10
DE   ribonuclease IX.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of poly(U) or poly(C) to fragments terminated by
CA   3'-hydroxy and 5'-phosphate groups.
CC   -!- Acts on poly(U) and poly(C), with a higher affinity for poly(C),
CC       but does not act on poly(A) or poly(G).
//
ID   3.1.26.11
DE   ribonuclease Z.
AN   3 tRNase.
AN   RNase Z.
AN   tRNA 3 endonuclease.
AN   tRNase Z.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of RNA, removing extra 3' nucleotides from tRNA
CA   precursor, generating 3' termini of tRNAs. A 3'-hydroxy group is left at
CA   the tRNA terminus and a 5'-phosphoryl group is left at the trailer
CA   molecule.
CC   -!- No cofactor requirements.
