ID   3.2.1.20
DE   alpha-glucosidase.
AN   acid maltase.
AN   glucoinvertase.
AN   glucosidosucrase.
AN   lysosomal alpha-glucosidase.
AN   maltase.
AN   maltase-glucoamylase.
CA   Hydrolysis of terminal, non-reducing (1->4)-linked alpha-D-glucose
CA   residues with release of alpha-D-glucose.
CC   -!- Group of enzymes whose specificity is directed mainly toward the
CC       exohydrolysis of 1,4-alpha-glucosidic linkages, and that hydrolyze
CC       oligosaccharides rapidly, relative to polysaccharides, which are
CC       hydrolyzed relatively slowly, or not at all.
CC   -!- The intestinal enzyme also hydrolyzes polysaccharides, catalyzing the
CC       reactions of EC 3.2.1.3, and, more slowly, hydrolyzes 1,6-alpha-D-
CC       glucose links.
