ID   3.2.1.33
DE   amylo-alpha-1,6-glucosidase.
AN   amylo-1,6-glucosidase.
AN   dextrin 6-alpha-D-glucosidase.
CA   Hydrolysis of (1->6)-alpha-D-glucosidic branch linkages in glycogen
CA   phosphorylase limit dextrin.
CC   -!- This enzyme hydrolyzes an unsubstituted glucose unit linked by an
CC       alpha(1->6) bond to an alpha(1->4) glucose chain.
CC   -!- The enzyme activity found in mammals and Saccharomyces cerevisiae is
CC       in a polypeptide chain containing two active centers.
CC   -!- The other activity is similar to that of EC 2.4.1.25, which acts on
CC       the glycogen phosphorylase limit dextrin chains to expose the single
CC       glucose residues, which the 6-alpha-glucosidase activity can then
CC       hydrolyze.
CC   -!- Together, these two activities constitute the glycogen debranching
CC       system.
DR   Q2PQH8, GDE_CANLF  ;  A8BQB4, GDE_HORSE  ;  P35573, GDE_HUMAN  ;
