ID   3.2.1.40
DE   alpha-L-rhamnosidase.
CA   Hydrolysis of terminal non-reducing alpha-L-rhamnose residues in alpha-L-
CA   rhamnosides.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in animal tissues, plants, yeasts, fungi and
CC       bacteria, utilizes an inverting mechanism of hydrolysis, releasing
CC       beta-L-rhamnose.
CC   -!- Substrates include naringin, rutin, quercitrin, hesperidin, dioscin,
CC       terpenyl glycosides and many other natural glycosides containing
