ID   3.2.1.155
DE   xyloglucan-specific endo-processive beta-1,4-glucanase.
AN   [(1->6)-alpha-D-xylo]-(1->4)-beta-D-glucan exo-glucohydrolase.
AN   xyloglucan-specific exo-beta-1,4-glucanase.
CA   Hydrolysis of (1->4)-D-glucosidic linkages in xyloglucans so as to
CA   successively remove oligosaccharides from the newly-formed chain end
CA   after endo-initiation on a polymer molecule.
CC   -!- The enzyme removes branched oligosaccharides, containing
CC       preferentially four glucoside residues in the main chain, from
CC       xyloglucan molecules in a processive manner after the initial endo-
CC       type attack on a polysaccharide.
CC   -!- Hydrolysis occurs at either the unsubstituted D-glucopyranose residue
CC       in the main backbone and/or the D-glucopyranose residue bearing a
CC       xylosyl group.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not display activity, or shows very low activity,
CC       toward other beta-D-glucans.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.2.1.160.
DR   Q7Z9M8, XG74_HYPJQ ;
