ID   3.2.2.23
DE   DNA-formamidopyrimidine glycosylase.
AN   Fapy-DNA glycosylase.
AN   formamidopyrimidine-DNA glycosylase.
CA   Hydrolysis of DNA containing ring-opened 7-methylguanine residues,
CA   releasing 2,6-diamino-4-hydroxy-5-(N-methyl)formamidopyrimidine.
CC   -!- May play a significant role in processes leading to recovery from
CC       mutagenesis and/or cell death by alkylating agents.
CC   -!- Also involved in the GO system responsible for removing an
CC       oxidatively damaged form of guanine (7,8-dihydro-8-oxoguanine) from
CC       DNA.
