ID   3.2.2.31
DE   adenine glycosylase.
AN   A/G-specific adenine glycosylase.
CA   Hydrolyzes free adenine bases from 7,8-dihydro-8-oxoguanine:adenine
CA   mismatched double-stranded DNA, leaving an apurinic site.
CC   -!- The enzyme serves as a mismatch repair enzyme that works to correct
CC       7,8-dihydro-8-oxoguanine:adenine mispairs that arise in DNA when
CC       error-prone synthesis occurs past 7,8-dihydro-8-oxoguanine (GO)
CC       lesions in DNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme excises the adenine of the mispair, producing an apurinic
CC       site sensitive to AP endonuclease activity.
CC   -!- After removing the undamaged adenine the enzyme remains bound to the
CC       site to prevent EC 3.2.2.23 (MutM) from removing the GO lesion, which
CC       could lead to a double strand break.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme is also active with adenine:guanine,
CC       adenine:cytosine, and adenine:7,8-dihydro-8-oxoadenine (AO) mispairs,
CC       removing the adenine in all cases.
