ID   3.4.11.13
DE   clostridial aminopeptidase.
AN   Clostridium histolyticum aminopeptidase.
CA   Release of any N-terminal amino acid, including proline and
CA   hydroxyproline, but no cleavage of Xaa-|-Pro.
CC   -!- A secreted enzyme from Clostridium histolyticum.
//
ID   3.4.11.14
DE   cytosol alanyl aminopeptidase.
AN   aminopolypeptidase.
AN   arylamidase.
AN   cytosol aminopeptidase III.
AN   liver aminopeptidase.
AN   puromycin-sensitive aminopeptidase.
AN   soluble alanyl aminopeptidase.
CA   Release of an N-terminal amino acid, preferentially alanine, from a wide
CA   range of peptides, amides and arylamides.
CC   -!- A puromycin-sensitive, cobalt-activated zinc-sialoglycoprotein that
CC       is generally cytosolic.
CC   -!- Multiple forms are widely distributed in mammalian tissues and body
CC       fluids.
DR   Q8H0S9, PSA_ARATH  ;  Q4TT88, PSA_CAEEL  ;  P55786, PSA_HUMAN  ;
DR   Q11011, PSA_MOUSE  ;  B7EA73, PSA_ORYSJ  ;
//
ID   3.4.11.15
DE   aminopeptidase Y.
AN   aminopeptidase (cobalt-activated).
AN   aminopeptidase Co.
AN   lysyl aminopeptidase.
CA   Preferentially, release of N-terminal lysine.
CC   -!- Inhibited by Zn(2+) and Mn(2+).
CC   -!- Hydrolyzes L-lysyl-4-nitroanilide and, more slowly, L-arginyl-4-
CC       nitroanilide.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M28B.
DR   Q8TZW4, AMPK_PYRFU ;  P37302, APE3_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.4.11.16
DE   Xaa-Trp aminopeptidase.
AN   aminopeptidase W.
AN   aminopeptidase X-Trp.
AN   X-Trp aminopeptidase.
CA   Release of a variety of N-terminal residues (especially glutamate and
CA   leucine) from peptides, provided tryptophan (or at least phenylalanine or
CA   tyrosine) is the penultimate residue. Also acts on Glu-|-Trp, Leu-|-Trp
CA   and a number of other dipeptides.
//
ID   3.4.11.17
DE   tryptophanyl aminopeptidase.
AN   tryptophan aminopeptidase.
CA   an N-terminal L-tryptophanyl-L-alpha-aminoacyl-[peptide] + H2O =
CA   an N-terminal L-alpha-aminoacyl-[peptide] + L-tryptophan.
CC   -!- Also acts on L-tryptophanamide.
CC   -!- From Trichosporon cutaneum.
DR   Q4WYG3, 7DMAW_ASPFU;  Q4WB07, CDNPT_ASPFU;  D1D8L6, CDNTP_ASPFM;
DR   Q4WZ67, EASL_ASPFU ;  Q4WAW7, FTMB_ASPFU ;  B0XWK7, HASE_ASPFC ;
//
ID   3.4.11.18
DE   methionyl aminopeptidase.
AN   methionine aminopeptidase.
AN   peptidase M.
CA   Release of N-terminal amino acids, preferentially methionine, from
CA   peptides and arylamides.
CC   -!- This membrane-bound enzyme, which is present in both prokaryotes and
CC       eukaryotes, releases the initiator methionine from nascent peptides.
CC   -!- The activity is dependent on the identity of the second, third and
CC       fourth amino acid residues of the target protein, but in general the
CC       enzyme acts only when the penultimate residue is small and uncharged
CC       (e.g. Gly, Ala, Cys, Ser, Thr, and Val).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M24A.
