ID   3.4.11.20
DE   aminopeptidase Ey.
CA   Differs from other aminopeptidases in broad specificity for amino acids
CA   in the P1 position and the ability to hydrolyze peptides of four or five
CA   residues that contain Pro in the P1' position.
CC   -!- From the plasma fraction of chicken egg yolk.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M1.
DR   O57579, AMPN_CHICK ;
//
ID   3.4.11.21
DE   aspartyl aminopeptidase.
CA   Release of an N-terminal aspartate or glutamate from a peptide, with a
CA   preference for aspartate.
CC   -!- Aminoacyl-arylamides are poor substrates.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M18.
