ID   3.4.13.21
DE   dipeptidase E.
AN   aspartyl dipeptidase.
AN   PepE gene product (Salmonella typhimurium).
AN   peptidase E.
CA   Dipeptidase E catalyzes the hydrolysis of dipeptides Asp-|-Xaa. It does
CA   not act on peptides with N-terminal Glu, Asn or Gln, nor does it cleave
CA   isoaspartyl peptides.
CC   -!- A free carboxy group is not absolutely required in the substrate
CC       since Asp-Phe-NH2 and Asp-Phe-OMe are hydrolyzed somewhat more slowly
CC       than dipeptides with free C-termini.
CC   -!- No peptide larger than a C-blocked dipeptide is known to be a
CC       substrate.
CC   -!- Asp-NH-Np is hydrolyzed and is a convenient substrate for routine
CC       assay.
CC   -!- The enzyme is most active near pH 7.0, and is not inhibited by
CC       di-isopropylfluorophosphate or phenylmethanesulfonyl fluoride.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S51.
