AN   TPP.
CA   Hydrolysis of Xaa-Xaa-Pro-|-Yaa- releasing the N-terminal tripeptide of a
CA   peptide with Pro as the third residue (position P1) and where Yaa is not
CA   proline.
CC   -!- This cell-surface-associated serine exopeptidase is found in the
CC       Gram-negative, anaerobic bacterium Porphyromonas gingivalis, which
CC       has been implicated in adult periodontal disease.
CC   -!- The enzyme releases tripeptides from the free amino terminus of
CC       peptides and small proteins, such as interleukin-6.
CC   -!- The enzyme possesses an absolute requirement for a proline residue at
CC       the P1 position but is completely inactivated by a proline residue at
CC       the P1' position.
CC   -!- The size of the peptide does not affect the rate of reaction.
DR   B2RJX3, PTP_PORG3  ;  Q7MUW6, PTP_PORGI  ;
//
ID   3.4.14.13
DE   gamma-D-glutamyl-L-lysine dipeptidyl-peptidase.
CA   The enzyme releases L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu dipeptides from cell wall peptides
CA   via cleavage of an L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-|-L-Lys bond.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacillus subtilis,
CC       is involved in the recycling of the murein peptide.
DR   Q736M3, YKFC_BACC1 ;  O35010, YKFC_BACSU ;
//
ID   3.4.14.14
DE   [mycofactocin precursor peptide] peptidase.
CA   [mycofactocin precursor peptide]-C-terminal glycyl-N-
CA   {5-[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-4,4-dimethyl-2-oxopyrrolidin-3-yl}acetamide
CA   + H2O = [mycofactocin precursor peptide]-C-terminal glycine + 3-amino-5-
CA   [(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-4,4-dimethyl-2-pyrrolidin-2-one.
CC   -!- Requires Fe(2+) ad Zn(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of the enzyme cofactor
CC       mycofactocin.
CC   -!- It catalyzes cleavage of the mycofactocin precursor peptide following
CC       its modification by MftC to liberate its final two residues, which
CC       consist of a cross-linked valine-tyramine dipeptide.
