CA   L-alpha-aminoacyl-[tubulin] + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- This is a subfamily of enzymes that cleave C-terminal and/or side
CC       chain amino acids from tubulins.
CC   -!- The dual-specificity enzymes can cleave both alpha- and gamma-linked
CC       L-glutamate from tubulins, removing the post-translationally added
CC       polyglutamyl side chains from the C-terminal regions.
CC   -!- In addition, the enzyme removes two glutamate residues from the
CC       C-terminus of beta-tubulin and detyrosinated alpha-tubulin (from
CC       which the C-terminal L-tyrosine has been removed by EC 3.4.17.17).
CC   -!- The latter is cleaved to Delta2-tubulin and further to Delta3-
CC       tubulin.
