ID   3.4.19.6
DE   pyroglutamyl-peptidase II.
AN   PAP-II.
AN   pyroglutamyl aminopeptidase II.
AN   thyroliberinase.
AN   thyrotropin-releasing hormone degrading ectoenzyme.
AN   TRH-DE.
AN   TRH-degrading ectoenzyme.
AN   TRH-specific aminopeptidase.
CA   Release of the N-terminal pyroglutamyl group from pGlu-|-His-Xaa
CA   tripeptides and pGlu-|-His-Xaa-Gly tetrapeptides.
CC   -!- Highly specific for thyrotropin releasing hormone (pyroglutamyl-
CC       histidyl-prolylamide).
CC   -!- Will not cleave the pyroglutamyl-histidyl bond of luteinizing hormone
CC       releasing hormone.
CC   -!- Found in serum and brain.
CC   -!- Inhibited by metal chelators.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M1.
DR   Q9UKU6, TRHDE_HUMAN;  Q8K093, TRHDE_MOUSE;  Q10836, TRHDE_RAT  ;
//
ID   3.4.19.7
DE   N-formylmethionyl-peptidase.
AN   (fMet)-releasing enzyme.
CA   Release of an N-terminal, formyl-methionyl residue from a polypeptide.
CC   -!- Highly specific for N-formylmethionyl-peptides.
CC   -!- Will not cleave methionyl peptides or N-formyl derivatives of amino
CC       acids other than methionine.
CC   -!- Isolated from liver.
CC   -!- Inhibited by heavy metals and activated by chloride.
//
ID   3.4.19.8
DE   Transferred entry: 3.4.17.21.
//
ID   3.4.19.9
DE   folate gamma-glutamyl hydrolase.
AN   carboxypeptidase G.
AN   conjugase.
AN   folate conjugase.
AN   gamma-glutamyl hydrolase.
AN   gamma-Glu-X carboxypeptidase.
AN   lysosomal gamma-glutamyl carboxypeptidase.
AN   pteroyl-poly-alpha-glutamate hydrolase.
AN   tetrahydropteroyl-poly-gamma-glutamyl gamma-glutamyl hydrolase.
CA   (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolyl-(gamma-L-Glu)(n) + (n-1) H2O = (6S)-5,6,7,8-
CA   tetrahydrofolate + (n-1) L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which occurs only in animals and plants, can be either
CC       endo- and/or exopeptidase.
CC   -!- It acts on tetrahydropteroyl polyglutamates and their modified forms,
CC       as well as the polyglutamates of the folate breakdown product
CC       N-(4-aminobenzoyl)-L-glutamate (pABA-Glu).
CC   -!- The initial cleavage may release either monoglutamate or poly-gamma-
CC       glutamate of two or more residues, depending on the specific enzyme.
CC   -!- For example, GGH1 from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana cleaves
CC       pentaglutamates, mainly to di- and triglutamates, whereas GGH2 from
CC       the same organism yields mainly monoglutamates.
CC   -!- The enzyme is lysosomal (and secreted) in animals and vacuolar in
CC       plants.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C26.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.12.10 and EC 3.4.22.12.
DR   Q9SYL6, GGH1_ARATH ;  O65355, GGH2_ARATH ;  Q9ZV85, GGH3_ARATH ;
