ID   3.4.19.11
DE   gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-diaminopimelate peptidase.
AN   endopeptidase I.
AN   gamma-D-glutamyl-L-diamino acid endopeptidase I.
AN   gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-diaminopimelate peptidase I.
CA   Hydrolysis of gamma-D-glutamyl bonds to the L-terminus (position 7) of
CA   meso-diaminopimelic acid (meso-A2pm) in 7-(L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu)-meso-A2pm
CA   and 7-(L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu)-7-(D-Ala)-meso-A2pm. It is required that the
CA   D-terminal amino and carboxy groups of meso-A2pm are unsubstituted.
CC   -!- Metallopeptidase from Bacillus sphaericus, the substrates being
CC       components of the bacterial spore wall.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M14.
DR   O31852, CWLS_BACSU ;  Q03415, ENP1_LYSSH ;  Q9I2Q1, TSE1_PSEAE ;
//
ID   3.4.19.12
DE   ubiquitinyl hydrolase 1.
AN   ubiquitin C-terminal hydrolase.
AN   ubiquitin thiolesterase.
CA   Thiol-dependent hydrolysis of ester, thioester, amide, peptide and
CA   isopeptide bonds formed by the C-terminal Gly of ubiquitin (a 76-residue
CA   protein attached to proteins as an intracellular targeting signal).
CC   -!- Links to polypeptides smaller than 60 residues are hydrolyzed more
CC       readily than those to larger polypeptides.
CC   -!- Isoforms exist with quantitatively different specificities among the
CC       best known being UCH-L1 and UCH-L3, major proteins of the brain of
CC       mammals.
CC   -!- Inhibited by ubiquitin aldehyde (in which Gly76 is replaced by
CC       aminoacetaldehyde).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C12.
