ID   3.4.19.13
DE   glutathione gamma-glutamate hydrolase.
AN   gamma-glutamyltranspeptidase.
AN   glutathionase.
CA   (1) glutathione + H2O = L-cysteinylglycine + L-glutamate.
CA   (2) an S-substituted glutathione + H2O = an S-substituted
CA   L-cysteinylglycine + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- This is a bifunctional protein that also has the activity of
CC       EC 2.3.2.2.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds its substrate by forming an initial gamma-glutamyl-
CC       enzyme intermediate, releasing the L-cysteinylglycine part of the
CC       molecule.
CC   -!- The enzyme then reacts with either a water molecule or a different
CC       acceptor substrate (usually an L-amino acid or a dipeptide) to form
CC       L-glutamate or a product containing a new gamma-glutamyl isopeptide
CC       bond, respectively.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on glutathione, glutathione-S-conjugates, and, at a
CC       lower level, on other substrates with an N-terminal L-gamma-glutamyl
CC       residue.
CC   -!- It plays a crucial part in the glutathione-mediated xenobiotic
CC       detoxification pathway.
CC   -!- The enzyme consists of two chains that are created by the proteolytic
CC       cleavage of a single precursor polypeptide.
DR   Q05902, ECM38_YEAST;  Q8VYW6, GAGT1_ARATH;  Q680I5, GAGT2_ARATH;
