ID   3.4.19.15
DE   desampylase.
AN   SAMP-protein conjugate cleaving protease.
CA   an N(6)-[small archaeal modifier protein]-[protein]-L-lysine + H2O =
CA   a [protein]-L-lysine + a [small archaeal modifier protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Haloferax volcanii,
CC       specifically cleaves the ubiquitin-like small modifier proteins SAMP1
CC       and SAMP2 from protein conjugates, hydrolyzing the isopeptide bond
CC       between a lysine residue of the target protein and the C-terminal
CC       glycine of the modifier protein. cf. EC 3.4.19.12.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M67.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.24.88.
DR   D4GTS4, JAMM1_HALVD;  Q8U1Y4, JAMM1_PYRFU;
//
ID   3.4.19.16
DE   glucosinolate gamma-glutamyl hydrolase.
CA   (1) an S-[(1E)-1-(hydroxyimino)-omega-(methylsulfanyl)alkyl]-L-
CA   glutathione + H2O = an S-[(1E)-1-(hydroxyimino)-omega-
CA   (methylsulfanyl)alkyl]-L-cysteinylglycine + L-glutamate.
CA   (2) (E)-1-(glutathione-S-yl)-2-(1H-indol-3-yl)acetohydroximate + H2O =
CA   (E)-1-(glycyl-L-cystein-S-yl)-2-(1H-indol-3-yl)acetohydroximate +
CA   L-glutamate.
CA   (3) 2-(glutathion-S-yl)-2-(1H-indol-3-yl)acetonitrile + H2O = 2-(glycyl-
CA   L-cystein-S-yl)-2-(1H-indol-3-yl)acetonitrile + L-glutamate.
CA   (4) (Z)-1-(glutathione-S-yl)-2-phenylacetohydroximate + H2O = (Z)-1-
CA   (glycyl-L-cystein-S-yl)-2-phenylacetohydroximate + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, characterized from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the plant defense compounds
CC       glucosinolates and camalexin.
CC   -!- It is the only known plant enzyme capable of hydrolyzing the gamma-
CC       glutamyl residue of glutathione in the cytosol.
DR   Q9M0A7, GGP1_ARATH ;  Q9M0A6, GGP2_ARATH ;  Q9M0A5, GGP3_ARATH ;
