ID   3.4.21.35
DE   tissue kallikrein.
AN   glandular kallikrein.
AN   kininogenin.
CA   Preferential cleavage of Arg-|-Xaa bonds in small molecule substrates.
CA   Highly selective action to release kallidin (lysyl-bradykinin) from
CA   kininogen involves hydrolysis of Met-|-Xaa or Leu-|-Xaa.
CC   -!- Formed from tissue prokallikrein by activation with trypsin.
CC   -!- A large number of tissue kallikrein-related sequences have been
CC       reported for rats and mice, though fewer seem to exist in other
CC       mammals.
CC   -!- The few that have been isolated and tested on substrates include
CC       mouse EC 3.4.21.54, submandibular proteinase a, epidermal growth-
CC       factor-binding protein, nerve growth factor gamma-subunit, rat tonin,
CC       submaxillary proteinases A and B, T-kininogenase, kallikreins K7 and
CC       K8.
CC   -!- The rat enzyme is unusual in liberating bradykinin directly from
CC       autologous kininogens by cleavage at two Arg-|-Xaa bonds.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.21.8.
