ID   3.4.21.54
DE   gamma-renin.
CA   Cleavage of the Leu-|-Leu bond in synthetic tetradecapeptide renin
CA   substrate, to produce angiotensin I, but not active on natural
CA   angiotensinogen. Also hydrolyzes Bz-Arg-p-nitroanilide.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.4.23.15, does not act on natural angiotensinogen.
CC   -!- A member of the tissue kallikrein family, from submandibular glands
CC       of male mice.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   P04071, K1B16_MOUSE;
//
ID   3.4.21.55
DE   venombin AB.
AN   Bitis gabonica serine proteinase.
AN   gabonase.
CA   Preferential cleavage: Arg-|-Xaa bonds in fibrinogen to form fibrin and
CA   release fibrinopeptides A and B.
CC   -!- From the venom of the Gaboon viper Bitis gabonica.
CC   -!- Activates factor XIII.
CC   -!- Not inhibited by antithrombin III/heparin or hirudin, unlike
CC       EC 3.4.21.5.
DR   P0C577, VSPG_BITGA ;
