ID   3.4.21.59
DE   tryptase.
AN   lung tryptase.
AN   mast cell protease II.
AN   mast cell tryptase.
AN   pituitary tryptase.
AN   skin tryptase.
CA   Preferential cleavage: Arg-|-Xaa, Lys-|-Xaa, but with more restricted
CA   specificity than trypsin.
CC   -!- Occurs as a tetrameric molecule with high affinity for heparin,
CC       in mast cell granules.
CC   -!- Not inhibited by alpha-1-proteinase inhibitor of alpha-2-
CC       macroglobulin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   Q15661, TRYB1_HUMAN;  Q02844, TRYB1_MOUSE;  P27435, TRYB1_RAT  ;
DR   P20231, TRYB2_HUMAN;  P21845, TRYB2_MOUSE;  P50343, TRYB2_RAT  ;
