ID   3.4.21.60
DE   scutelarin.
AN   taipan activator.
CA   Selective cleavage of Arg-|-Thr and Arg-|-Ile in prothrombin to form
CA   thrombin and two inactive fragments.
CC   -!- From the venom of the Taipan snake (Oxyuranus scutellatus).
CC   -!- Converts prothrombin to thrombin.
CC   -!- Specificity is similar to that of Factor Xa (EC 3.4.21.6).
CC   -!- However, unlike Factor Xa this enzyme can cleave its target in the
CC       absence of coagulation Factor Va.
CC   -!- Activity is potentiated by phospholipid and Ca(2+) which binds via
CC       gamma-carboxyglutamic acid residues.
CC   -!- Similar enzymes are known from the venom of other Australian elapid
CC       snakes, including Pseudonaja textilis textilis, Oxyuranus
CC       microlepidotus and Demansia nuchalis affinis.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.99.28.
//
ID   3.4.21.61
DE   kexin.
AN   paired-basic endopeptidase.
AN   prohormone-processing endoprotease.
AN   proteinase yscF.
AN   yeast KEX2 protease.
CA   Cleavage of -Lys-Arg-|-Xaa- and -Arg-Arg-|-Xaa- bonds to process yeast
CA   alpha-factor pheromone and killer toxin precursors.
CC   -!- Calcium activated.
CC   -!- Inhibited by p-mercuribenzoate.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S8.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.22.23.
DR   O13359, KEX2_CANAW ;  P13134, KEX2_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.4.21.62
DE   subtilisin.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity for peptide bonds, and a
CA   preference for a large uncharged residue in P1. Hydrolyzes peptide
CA   amides.
CC   -!- Subtilisin is a serine endopeptidase that evolved independently of
CC       chymotrypsin.
CC   -!- It contains no cysteine residues (although these are found in
CC       homologous enzymes).
CC   -!- Species variants include subtilisin BPN' (also subtilisin B,
CC       subtilopeptidase C, nagarse, nagarse proteinase, subtilisin Novo,
CC       bacterial proteinase Novo) and subtilisin Carlsberg (subtilisin A,
CC       subtilopeptidase A, alcalase Novo).
CC   -!- Similar enzymes are produced by various Bacillus subtilis strains and
CC       other Bacillus species.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S8.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.16 and EC 3.4.21.14.
DR   P09230, AEP_YARLI  ;  A0A509AKI1, PIMM2_PLABA;  A0A509AM03, SUB1_PLABA ;
