ID   3.4.21.65
DE   thermomycolin.
AN   thermomycolase.
CA   Rather non-specific hydrolysis of proteins. Preferential cleavage:
CA   -Ala-|-Xaa-, -Tyr-|-Xaa-, -Phe-|-Xaa- in small molecular substrates.
CC   -!- From the thermophilic fungus Malbranchea pulchella var. sulfurea.
CC   -!- Contains Cys, but not inhibited by p-mercuribenzoate.
CC   -!- Very thermostable.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S8.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.16 and EC 3.4.21.14.
DR   P13858, THEM_MALCI ;
//
ID   3.4.21.66
DE   thermitase.
AN   thermophilic Streptomyces serine protease.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins, including collagen.
CC   -!- From Thermoactinomyces vulgaris containing a single Cys, near the
CC       active site His, and inhibited by p-mercuribenzoate.
CC   -!- The N-terminal extension of the polypeptide chain relative to
CC       subtilisin contributes to calcium-binding and the high
CC       thermostability.
CC   -!- The amino acid composition and properties of the thermostable enzyme
CC       from Streptomyces rectus var. proteolyticus are closely similar.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S8.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.16.
DR   P04072, THET_THEVU ;
//
ID   3.4.21.67
DE   endopeptidase So.
AN   E.coli cytoplasmic proteinase.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins, but not Bz-Tyr-OEt, Ac-Phe-beta-naphthylester,
CA   or Bz-Arg-OEt.
CC   -!- Cytoplasmic peptidase.
CC   -!- Inhibited by Tos-Phe-CH2Cl, but not by Tos-Lys-CH2Cl.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.16 and EC 3.4.21.14.
//
ID   3.4.21.68
DE   t-plasminogen activator.
AN   tissue plasminogen activator.
AN   tissue-type plasminogen activator.
AN   tPA.
CA   Specific cleavage of Arg-|-Val bond in plasminogen to form plasmin.
CC   -!- From a wide variety of mammalian tissues, especially endothelial
CC       cells.
CC   -!- Secreted as a single chain precursor which is cleaved to a two-chain
CC       form by plasmin.
CC   -!- Activity is considerably enhanced by fibrin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.21.31 and EC 3.4.99.26.
