ID   3.4.21.69
DE   activated protein C (thrombin-activated peptidase).
AN   activated blood coagulation factor XIV.
AN   autoprothrombin IIA.
AN   protein C (activated).
CA   Degradation of blood coagulation factors Va and VIIIa.
CC   -!- One of the gamma-carboxyglutamic acid-containing coagulation factors.
CC   -!- The enzyme plays an important role in regulating anticoagulation,
CC       inflammation, and cell death by proteolytically inactivating the
CC       blood coagulation factors factor Va and factor VIIIa.
CC   -!- Formed from protein C, the proenzyme that circulates in plasma,
CC       by the action of a complex of thrombin with thrombomodulin.
CC   -!- Protein C can also be activated by serine endopeptidases present in
CC       several snake venoms.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   P00745, PROC_BOVIN ;  Q28278, PROC_CANLF ;  Q28315, PROC_CAPHI ;
DR   Q28412, PROC_FELCA ;  Q28380, PROC_HORSE ;  P04070, PROC_HUMAN ;
DR   Q28506, PROC_MACMU ;  P33587, PROC_MOUSE ;  Q9GLP2, PROC_PIG   ;
DR   Q28661, PROC_RABIT ;  P31394, PROC_RAT   ;
