ID   3.4.21.72
DE   IgA-specific serine endopeptidase.
AN   IgA protease.
AN   immunoglobulin A1 protease.
CA   Cleavage of immunoglobulin A molecules at certain Pro-|-Xaa bonds in the
CA   hinge region. No small molecule substrates are known.
CC   -!- Species variants differing slightly in specificity are secreted by
CC       Gram-negative bacteria Neisseria gonorrhoeae and Haemophilus
CC       influenzae.
CC   -!- Some other bacterial endopeptidases with similar specificity are of
CC       metallotype (see EC 3.4.24.13).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S6.
DR   P44969, IGA0_HAEIN ;  P42782, IGA1_HAEIF ;  P45384, IGA2_HAEIF ;
DR   P45385, IGA3_HAEIF ;  P45386, IGA4_HAEIF ;  P09790, IGA_NEIGO  ;
//
ID   3.4.21.73
DE   u-plasminogen activator.
AN   cellular plasminogen activator.
AN   urinary plasminogen activator.
AN   urokinase.
CA   Specific cleavage of Arg-|-Val bond in plasminogen to form plasmin.
CC   -!- Formed from the inactive precursor by action of plasmin or plasma
CC       kallikrein.
CC   -!- Differs in structure from EC 3.4.21.68, and does not bind to fibrin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.21.31 and EC 3.4.99.26.
