ID   3.4.21.74
DE   venombin A.
CA   Selective cleavage of Arg-|-Xaa bond in fibrinogen, to form fibrin,
CA   and release fibrinopeptide A. The specificity of further degradation of
CA   fibrinogen varies with species origin of the enzyme.
CC   -!- A somewhat thrombin-like enzyme from venoms of snakes of the
CC       viper/rattlesnake group.
CC   -!- Species variants of the enzyme include ancrod from Agkistrodon
CC       rhodostoma (Malayan pit viper), batroxobin from Bothrops atrox (South
CC       American pit viper) and crotalase from Crotalus adamanteus (Eastern
CC       diamondback rattlesnake).
CC   -!- Does not require activation by calcium.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.21.28, EC 3.4.21.29 and EC 3.4.21.30.
