ID   3.4.21.78
DE   granzyme A.
AN   cytotoxic T-lymphocyte proteinase 1.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins, including fibronectin, type IV collagen and
CA   nucleolin. Preferential cleavage: -Arg-|-Xaa-, -Lys-|-Xaa- >> -Phe-|-
CA   Xaa- in small molecule substrates.
CC   -!- From cytotoxic T lymphocyte granules.
CC   -!- The human enzyme does not cleave Phe-|-Xaa.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   Q7YRZ7, GRAA_BOVIN ;  P12544, GRAA_HUMAN ;  P11032, GRAA_MOUSE ;
//
ID   3.4.21.79
DE   granzyme B.
AN   cytotoxic t-lymphocyte proteinase 2.
CA   Preferential cleavage: -Asp-|-Xaa- >> -Asn-|-Xaa- > -Met-|-Xaa-,
CA   -Ser-|-Xaa-.
CC   -!- From cytotoxic T lymphocyte granules.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   P10144, GRAB_HUMAN ;  P04187, GRAB_MOUSE ;  P18291, GRAB_RAT   ;
//
ID   3.4.21.80
DE   streptogrisin A.
AN   pronase enzyme A.
AN   SGPA.
AN   Streptomyces protease A.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with specificity similar to chymotrypsin.
CC   -!- Not inhibited by Tos-Phe-CH2Cl or ovomucoid.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1E.
DR   P00776, PRTA_STRGR ;
//
ID   3.4.21.81
DE   streptogrisin B.
AN   pronase enzyme B.
AN   SGPB.
AN   Streptomyces protease B.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with trypsin-like specificity.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1E.
DR   P00777, PRTB_STRGR ;
//
ID   3.4.21.82
DE   glutamyl endopeptidase II.
AN   GluSGP.
AN   glutamic acid-specific protease.
CA   Preferential cleavage: -Glu-|-Xaa- >> -Asp-|-Xaa-. Preference for Pro or
CA   Leu at P2 and Phe at P3. Cleavage of -Glu-|-Asp- and -Glu-|-Pro- bonds is
CA   slow.
CC   -!- Inhibited by (18-Leu->Glu) modified turkey ovomucoid third domain.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1E.
DR   Q07006, GLUP_STRGR ;
//
ID   3.4.21.83
DE   oligopeptidase B.
AN   protease II.
CA   Hydrolysis of -Arg-|-Xaa- and -Lys-|-Xaa- bonds in oligopeptides, even
CA   when P1' residue is proline.
CC   -!- Inhibited by Tos-Lys-CH2Cl.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S9A.
DR   P24555, PTRB_ECOLI ;  Q59536, PTRB_MORLA ;
//
ID   3.4.21.84
DE   limulus clotting factor C.
CA   Selective cleavage of 103-Arg-|-Ser-104 and 124-Ile-|-Ile-125 bonds in
CA   Limulus clotting factor B to form activated factor B. Cleavage of -Pro-
CA   Arg-|-Xaa- bonds in synthetic substrates.
CC   -!- From the hemocyte granules of the horseshoe crabs Limulus and
CC       Tachypleus.
CC   -!- Factor C is activated by Gram-negative bacterial lipopolysaccharides
CC       and chymotrypsin.
CC   -!- Inhibited by antithrombin III.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   P28175, CFC_TACTR  ;  Q26422, LFC_CARRO  ;
//
ID   3.4.21.85
DE   limulus clotting factor B.
CA   Selective cleavage of 98-Arg-|-Ile-99 bond in Limulus proclotting enzyme
CA   to form active clotting enzyme.
CC   -!- From the hemocyte granules of the horseshoe crabs Limulus and
CC       Tachypleus.
CC   -!- Factor B is activated by factor C.
DR   Q27081, CFB_TACTR  ;  Q27083, CFGB_TACTR ;
//
ID   3.4.21.86
DE   limulus clotting enzyme.
CA   Selective cleavage of 18-Arg-|- and 47-Arg-|- bonds in coagulogen to form
CA   coagulin and fragments.
CC   -!- From the hemocyte granules of the horseshoe crabs Limulus and
CC       Tachypleus.
CC   -!- Limulus clotting enzyme is activated by factor B.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
DR   P21902, PCE_TACTR  ;
//
ID   3.4.21.87
DE   Transferred entry: 3.4.23.49.
//
ID   3.4.21.88
DE   repressor LexA.
CA   Hydrolysis of Ala-|-Gly bond in repressor LexA.
CC   -!- In the presence of single-stranded DNA, the RecA protein interacts
CC       with LexA causing an autocatalytic cleavage which disrupts the DNA-
CC       binding part of LexA, leading to derepression of the SOS regulon and
CC       eventually DNA repair.
CC   -!- The activity was previously attributed to the RecA protein (formerly
CC       EC 3.4.99.37).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S24.
