ID   3.4.21.92
DE   endopeptidase Clp.
AN   caseinolytic protease.
AN   endopeptidase Ti.
AN   protease Ti.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins to small peptides in the presence of ATP and
CA   magnesium. alpha-casein is the usual test substrate. In the absence of
CA   ATP, only oligopeptides shorter than five residues are hydrolyzed (such
CA   as succinyl-Leu-Tyr-|-NHMec, and Leu-Tyr-Leu-|-Tyr-Trp, in which cleavage
CA   of the -Tyr-|-Leu- and -Tyr-|-Trp bonds also occurs).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S14.
