ID   3.4.21.102
DE   C-terminal processing peptidase.
AN   photosystem II D1 protein processing peptidase.
AN   protease Re.
AN   tail-specific protease.
AN   Tsp protease.
CA   The enzyme shows specific recognition of a C-terminal tripeptide, Xaa-
CA   Yaa-Zaa, in which Xaa is preferably Ala or Leu, Yaa is preferably Ala or
CA   Tyr, and Zaa is preferably Ala, but then cleaves at a variable distance
CA   from the C-terminus. A typical cleavage is -Ala-Ala-|-Arg-Ala-Ala-
CA   Lys-Glu-Asn-Tyr-Ala-Leu-Ala-Ala.
CC   -!- In the plant chloroplast, the enzyme removes the C-terminal extension
CC       of the D1 polypeptide of photosystem II; this proteolytic processing
CC       is necessary to allow the light-driven assembly of the tetranuclear
CC       manganese cluster, which is responsible for photosynthetic water
CC       oxidation.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S41.
