DE   HtrA2 peptidase.
AN   high temperature requirement protein A2.
AN   HtrA2 protease.
AN   Omi stress-regulated endoprotease.
AN   serine proteinase OMI.
CA   Cleavage of non-polar aliphatic amino-acids at the P1 position, with a
CA   preference for Val, Ile and Met. At the P2 and P3 positions, Arg is
CA   selected most strongly with a secondary preference for other hydrophilic
CA   residues.
CC   -!- Up-regulated in mammalian cells in response to stress induced by both
CC       heat shock and tunicamycin treatment.
CC   -!- Can induce apoptosis in a caspase-independent manner through its
CC       peptidase activity and in a caspase-dependent manner by disrupting
CC       the interaction between caspase and the inhibitor of apoptosis (IAP).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1B.
