CC   -!- The polyprotein of noncytopathogenic pestiviruses is cleaved co- and
CC       post-translationally into at least 11 proteins (N(pro), C, E(rns),
CC       E1, E2, p7, NS2-3, NS4A, NS4B, NS5A, and NS5B).
CC   -!- The genomes of cytopathogenic pestivirus strains express at least one
CC       additional protein, called NS3 (p80).
CC   -!- This enzyme, which resides in the N-terminal region of NS3 (non-
CC       structural protein 3), is essential for generation of its own
CC       C-terminus and for processing of the downstream cleavage sites,
