ID   3.4.22.44
DE   nuclear-inclusion-a endopeptidase.
AN   potyvirus NIa protease.
CA   Hydrolyzes glutaminyl bonds, and activity is further restricted by
CA   preferences for the amino acids in P6 - P1' that vary with the species of
CA   potyvirus, e.g. Glu-Xaa-Xaa-Tyr-Xaa-Gln-|-(Ser or Gly) for the enzyme
CA   from tobacco etch virus. The natural substrate is the viral polyprotein,
CA   but other proteins and oligopeptides containing the appropriate consensus
CA   sequence are also cleaved.
CC   -!- The potyviruses cause diseases in plants, and inclusion bodies appear
CC       in the host cell nuclei, protein a of these being the endopeptidase.
CC   -!- The enzyme finds practical use when encoded in vectors for the
CC       artificial expression of recombinant fusion proteins, since it can
CC       confer on them the capacity for autolytic cleavage.
CC   -!- It is also reported that transgenic plants expressing the enzyme are
CC       resistant to viral infection.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C4.
