ID   3.4.22.57
DE   caspase-4.
AN   CASP-4.
AN   ICErelII.
AN   ICErel-II.
AN   Ich-2.
CA   Strict requirement for Asp at the P1 position. It has a preferred
CA   cleavage sequence of Tyr-Val-Ala-Asp-|- but also cleaves at Asp-Glu-Val-
CA   Asp-|-.
CC   -!- Part of the family of inflammatory-caspases, which also includes
CC       caspase-1 (EC 3.4.22.36) and caspase-5 (EC 3.4.22.58) in humans and
CC       caspase-11 (EC 3.4.22.64), caspase-12, caspase-13 and caspase-14 in
CC       mice.
CC   -!- Contains a caspase-recruitment domain (CARD) in its N-terminal
CC       prodomain, which plays a role in procaspase activation.
CC   -!- Able to cleave itself and the p30 caspase-1 precursor, but, unlike
CC       caspase-1, it is very inefficient at generating mature interleukin-
CC       1beta (IL-1beta) from pro-IL-1beta.
CC   -!- Both this enzyme and caspase-5 can cleave pro-caspase-3 to release
CC       the small subunit (p12) but not the large subunit (p17).
CC   -!- The caspase-1 inhibitor Ac-Tyr-Val-Ala-Asp-CHO can also inhibit this
CC       enzyme, but more slowly.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C14.
DR   Q5E9C1, CASP4_BOVIN;  P49662, CASP4_HUMAN;
