ID   3.4.22.65
DE   peptidase 1 (mite).
AN   allergen Der p 1.
AN   endopeptidase 1 (mite).
AN   major mite fecal allergen Der p 1.
CA   Broad endopeptidase specificity.
CC   -!- This enzyme, derived from the house dust mite, is a major component
CC       of the allergic immune response.
CC   -!- The substrate specificity of this enzyme is not altogether clear; it
CC       cleaves the low-affinity IgE receptor CD23 at 298-Glu-|-Ser-299 and
CC       155-Ser-|-Ser-156.
CC   -!- It also cleaves the pulmonary structural proteins occludin and
CC       claudin at Leu-|-Leu, Asp-|-Leu and at Gly-|-Thr bonds, and it can
CC       also cleave the alpha subunit of the interleukin-2 (IL-2) receptor
CC       (CD25).
CC   -!- Using a positional scanning combinatorial library, it was found that
CC       the major substrate-specificity determinant is for Ala in the P2
CC       position.
CC   -!- The enzyme shows only a slight preference for basic amino acids in
CC       the P1 and P3 positions and a preference for aliphatic amino acids
CC       such as Ile, Pro, Val, Leu and norleucine in the P4 position.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C1.
DR   P16311, PEPT1_DERFA;  P16312, PEPT1_DERMI;  P08176, PEPT1_DERPT;
DR   P25780, PEPT1_EURMA;  Q1EIQ3, PEPT1_PSOOV;
