ID   3.4.22.68
DE   Ulp1 peptidase.
AN   Smt3-protein conjugate proteinase.
AN   Ubl-specific protease 1.
AN   Ulp1.
AN   Ulp1 endopeptidase.
AN   Ulp1 protease.
CA   Hydrolysis of the alpha-linked peptide bond in the sequence Gly-
CA   Gly-|-Ala-Thr-Tyr at the C-terminal end of the small ubiquitin-like
CA   modifier (SUMO) propeptide, Smt3, leading to the mature form of the
CA   protein. A second reaction involves the cleavage of an epsilon-linked
CA   peptide bond between the C-terminal glycine of the mature SUMO and the
CA   lysine epsilon-amino group of the target protein.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Saccharomyces cerevisiae can also recognize small
CC       ubiquitin-like modifier 1 (SUMO-1) from human as a substrate in both
CC       SUMO-processing (alpha-linked peptide bonds) and SUMO-deconjugation
CC       (epsilon-linked peptide bonds) reactions.
CC   -!- Ulp1 has several functions, including an essential role in
CC       chromosomal segregation and progression of the cell cycle through the
CC       G2/M phase of the cell cycle.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C48.
DR   Q94F30, ESD4_ARATH ;  Q02724, ULP1_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.4.22.69
DE   SARS coronavirus main proteinase.
AN   3C-like protease.
AN   3cLpro.
AN   coronavirus 3C-like protease.
AN   SARS coronavirus main protease.
AN   SARS-CoV 3CLpro enzyme.
AN   severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus main protease.
CA   TSAVLQ-|-SGFRK-NH2 and SGVTFQ-|-GKFKK the two peptides corresponding to
CA   the two self-cleavage sites of the SARS 3C-like proteinase are the two
CA   most reactive peptide substrates. The enzyme exhibits a strong preference
CA   for substrates containing Gln at P1 position and Leu at P2 position.
CC   -!- SARS coronavirus main protease is the key enzyme in SARS coronavirus
CC       replicase polyprotein processing.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C30.
