ID   3.4.22.70
DE   sortase A.
CA   The enzyme catalyzes a cell wall sorting reaction in which a surface
CA   protein with a sorting signal containing a LPXTG motif is cleaved between
CA   the Thr and Gly residue. The resulting threonine carboxyl end of the
CA   protein is covalently attached to a pentaglycine cross-bridge of
CA   peptidoglycan.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C60.
DR   Q2FV99, SRTA_STAA8 ;  Q9XA14, SRTE1_STRCO;  Q9XA15, SRTE2_STRCO;
//
ID   3.4.22.71
DE   sortase B.
AN   SrtB.
CA   The enzyme catalyzes a cell wall sorting reaction in which a surface
CA   protein with a sorting signal containing a NPXTN motif is cleaved between
CA   the Thr and Asn residue. The resulting threonine carboxyl end of the
CA   protein is covalently attached to a pentaglycine cross-bridge of
CA   peptidoglycan.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C60.
DR   Q2FZE3, SRTB_STAA8 ;
