CA   of insulin.
CC   -!- Isolated from the imperfect fungus Scytalidium lignicolum.
CC   -!- Not inhibited by pepstatin-Ac, methyl 2-diazoacetamidohexanoate or
CC       1,2-epoxy-3-(p-nitrophenyl)propane.
CC   -!- A related enzyme from the same organism, proteinase C, is also
CC       insensitive to these inhibitors and has molecular weight 406 kDa.
//
ID   3.4.23.32
DE   scytalidopepsin B.
AN   Scytalidium aspartic proteinase B.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity, cleaving 24-Phe-|-Phe-25,
CA   but not 15-Leu-|-Tyr-16 and 25-Phe-|-Tyr-26 in the B chain of insulin.
CC   -!- Isolated from the imperfect fungus Scytalidium lignicolum.
CC   -!- A second endopeptidase from S.lignicolum (see scytalidopepsin A) that
CC       is insensitive to pepstatin and methyl 2-diazoacetamidohexanoate.
CC   -!- 1,2-epoxy-3-(p-nitrophenoxy)propane reacts with Glu-53, which
CC       replaces one of the aspartic residues at the active center.
CC   -!- One of the smallest aspartic endopeptidases active as the monomer,
CC       with molecular weight 22 kDa.
CC   -!- Similarly inhibitor-resistant endopeptidases are found in the
CC       basidiomycetes Lentinus edodes and Ganoderma lucidum, and in
CC       Polyporus tulipiferae (a second endopeptidase distinct from
CC       polyporopepsin), but these are of typical aspartic endopeptidase
CC       size.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family G1.
DR   P15369, PRTB_SCYLI ;
//
ID   3.4.23.33
DE   Transferred entry: 3.4.21.101.
//
ID   3.4.23.34
DE   cathepsin E.
AN   erythrocyte membrane aspartic proteinase.
AN   slow-moving proteinase.
CA   Similar to cathepsin D, but slightly broader specificity.
CC   -!- Found in stomach, spleen, erythrocyte membrane; not lysosomal.
CC   -!- Pro-cathepsin E is an 86 kDa disulfide-linked dimer; activation or
CC       reduction produces monomers.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
DR   Q805F3, CATEA_XENLA;  Q805F2, CATEB_XENLA;  Q800A0, CATE_AQUCT ;
DR   P25796, CATE_CAVPO ;  P14091, CATE_HUMAN ;  P70269, CATE_MOUSE ;
DR   P43159, CATE_RABIT ;  P16228, CATE_RAT   ;
//
ID   3.4.23.35
DE   barrierpepsin.
AN   Bar proteinase.
AN   extracellular 'barrier' protein.
CA   Selective cleavage of 6-Leu-|-Lys-7 bond in the pheromone alpha-mating
CA   factor.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
DR   P12630, BAR1_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.4.23.36
DE   signal peptidase II.
AN   bacterial leader peptidase I.
AN   lipoprotein signal peptidase.
AN   premurein-leader peptidase.
AN   prolipoprotein-signal peptidase.
AN   SPase II.
CA   Release of signal peptides from bacterial membrane prolipoproteins.
CA   Hydrolyzes -Xaa-Yaa-Zaa-|-(S,diacylglyceryl)Cys-, in which Xaa is
CA   hydrophobic (preferably Leu), and Yaa (Ala or Ser) and Zaa (Gly or Ala)
CA   have small, neutral side chains.
CC   -!- Inhibited by pepstatin and the antibiotic globomycin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A8.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.99.35.
