ID   3.4.23.38
DE   plasmepsin I.
AN   aspartic hemoglobinase I.
AN   PfAPG.
CA   Hydrolysis of the 33-Phe-|-Leu-34 bond in the alpha-chain of hemoglobin,
CA   leading to denaturation of molecule.
CC   -!- Inhibited by pepstatin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
DR   Q7KQM4, PLM1_PLAF7 ;  P39898, PLM1_PLAFX ;
//
ID   3.4.23.39
DE   plasmepsin II.
AN   aspartic hemoglobinase II.
AN   PfAPD.
CA   Hydrolysis of the bonds linking certain hydrophobic residues in
CA   hemoglobin or globin. Also cleaves small molecules substrates such as
CA   Ala-Leu-Glu-Arg-Thr-Phe-|-Phe(NO2)-Ser-Phe-Pro-Thr.
CC   -!- Inhibited by pepstatin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
DR   Q8I6V3, PLM2_PLAF7 ;  P46925, PLM2_PLAFX ;  Q8IM15, PLM3_PLAF7 ;
DR   Q9Y006, PLM3_PLAFX ;  Q8IM16, PLM4_PLAF7 ;  Q17SB3, PLM4_PLAFX ;
//
ID   3.4.23.40
DE   phytepsin.
CA   Prefers hydrophobic residues Phe, Val, Ile, Leu, and Ala at P1 and P1',
CA   but also cleaves -Phe-|-Asp- and -Asp-|-Asp- bonds in 2S albumin from
CA   plant seeds.
