DE   dactylysin.
AN   peptide hormone inactivating endopeptidase.
CA   Hydrolysis of peptides of at least six residues, with bulky hydrophobic
CA   residues in the P1' position. Shows a preference for hydrophobic doublets
CA   such as -Phe-|-Phe- and -Phe-|-Leu- in somatostatin-(1-14)-peptide and
CA   dynorphin A-(1-6)-peptide, respectively.
CC   -!- An endopeptidase of 100 kDa secreted from the skin of Xenopus laevis.
CC   -!- Resembles neprilysin in insensitivity to 1 uM captopril, but differs
CC       in being insensitive to thiorphan and unable to digest (5-Met)-
CC       enkephalin, (5-Leu)-enkephalin, oxytocin and substance P-(7-11)-
CC       peptide.
