ID   3.5.1.89
DE   N-acetylglucosaminylphosphatidylinositol deacetylase.
AN   acetylglucosaminylphosphatidylinositol deacetylase.
AN   GlcNAc-PI deacetylase.
AN   GlcNAc-PI de-N-acetylase.
AN   N-acetyl-D-glucosaminylphosphatidylinositol acetylhydrolase.
AN   N-acetylglucosaminylphosphatidylinositol de-N-acetylase.
CA   a 6-(N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosaminyl)-1-(1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho)-
CA   1D-myo-inositol + H2O = a 6-(alpha-D-glucosaminyl)-1-(1,2-diacyl-
CA   sn-glycero-3-phospho)-1D-myo-inositol + acetate.
CC   -!- Involved in the second step of glycosylphosphatidylinositol (GPI)
CC       anchor formation in all eukaryotes.
CC   -!- The enzyme appears to be composed of a single subunit (PIG-L in
CC       mammalian cells and GPI12 in Saccharomyces cerevisiae).
CC   -!- In some species, the long-chain sn-1-acyl group of the phosphatidyl
CC       group is replaced by a long-chain alkyl or alk-1-enyl group.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.1.69.
DR   D4B4K9, GPI12_ARTBC;  Q9HDW9, GPI12_SCHPO;  P23797, GPI12_YEAST;
DR   A6QQ24, PIGL_BOVIN ;  Q54C64, PIGL_DICDI ;  Q9Y2B2, PIGL_HUMAN ;
DR   Q5SX19, PIGL_MOUSE ;  O35790, PIGL_RAT   ;
//
ID   3.5.1.90
DE   adenosylcobinamide hydrolase.
AN   AdoCbi amidohydrolase.
AN   AdoCbi hydrolase.
CA   adenosylcob(III)inamide + H2O = (R)-1-aminopropan-2-ol +
CA   adenosylcob(III)yrate.
CC   -!- Involved in the salvage pathway of cobinamide in archaea.
CC   -!- Archaea convert adenosylcobinamide (AdoCbi) into adenosylcobinamide
CC       phosphate (AdoCbi-P) in two steps.
CC   -!- First, the amidohydrolase activity of CbiZ cleaves off the
CC       aminopropanol moiety of AdoCbi yielding adenosylcobyric acid
CC       (AdoCby); second, AdoCby is converted into AdoCbi-P by the action of
CC       EC 6.3.1.10 (CbiB).
DR   Q9HPK9, CBIZ_HALSA ;  Q8Q0G3, CBIZ_METMA ;
//
ID   3.5.1.91
DE   N-substituted formamide deformylase.
CA   N-benzylformamide + H2O = benzylamine + formate.
CC   -!- While N-benzylformamide is the best substrate, the enzyme from
CC       Arthrobacter pascens can also act on the N-substituted formamides
CC       N-butylformamide, N-allylformamide, N-[2-(cyclohex-1-
CC       enyl)ethyl]formamide and N-(1-phenylethyl)formamide, but much more
CC       slowly.
CC   -!- Amides of other acids do not act as substrates.
DR   Q68AP4, NFDA_ARTPS ;
//
ID   3.5.1.92
DE   pantetheine hydrolase.
AN   pantetheinase.
AN   vanin-1.
CA   (R)-pantetheine + H2O = cysteamine + (R)-pantothenate.
CC   -!- Hydrolyzes only one of the amide bonds of pantetheine.
CC   -!- The substrate analogs phosphopantetheine and CoA are not substrates.
CC   -!- Recycles pantothenate (vitamin B5) and produces cysteamine, a potent
CC       anti-oxidant.
DR   Q58CQ9, VNN1_BOVIN ;  Q9TSX8, VNN1_CANLF ;  O95497, VNN1_HUMAN ;
DR   Q9Z0K8, VNN1_MOUSE ;  Q9BDJ5, VNN1_PIG   ;  O95498, VNN2_HUMAN ;
//
ID   3.5.1.93
DE   glutaryl-7-aminocephalosporanic-acid acylase.
AN   7beta-(4-carboxybutanamido)cephalosporanic acid acylase.
AN   CA.
AN   cephalosporin acylase.
AN   cephalosporin C acylase.
AN   GA.
AN   GCA.
AN   GL-7-ACA acylase.
AN   glutaryl-7-ACA acylase.
AN   glutaryl-7-aminocephalosporanic acid acylase.
CA   (7R)-7-(4-carboxybutanamido)cephalosporanate + H2O = (7R)-7-
CA   aminocephalosporanate + glutarate.
CC   -!- Forms 7-aminocephalosporanic acid, a key intermediate in the
CC       synthesis of cephem antibiotics.
CC   -!- It reacts only weakly with cephalosporin C.
DR   Q9L5D6, G7AC_BREDI ;  P07662, G7AC_PSEU7 ;  P15557, PAC1_PSES3 ;
DR   Q05053, PAC1_PSESV ;
//
ID   3.5.1.94
DE   gamma-glutamyl-gamma-aminobutyrate hydrolase.
AN   gamma-glutamyl-GABA hydrolase.
CA   4-(gamma-L-glutamylamino)butanoate + H2O = 4-aminobutanoate +
CA   L-glutamate.
CC   -!- Forms part of a novel putrescine-utilizing pathway in Escherichia
CC       coli, in which it has been hypothesized that putrescine is first
CC       glutamylated to form gamma-glutamylputrescine, which is oxidized to
CC       4-(gamma-glutamylamino)butanal and then to 4-(gamma-
CC       glutamylamino)butanoate.
CC   -!- Also can catalyze the reactions of EC 3.5.1.35 and EC 3.5.1.65.
DR   Q8X7G2, PUUD_ECO57 ;  P76038, PUUD_ECOLI ;  Q83LB6, PUUD_SHIFL ;
DR   Q3Z146, PUUD_SHISS ;
//
ID   3.5.1.95
DE   N-malonylurea hydrolase.
AN   ureidomalonase.
CA   3-oxo-3-ureidopropanoate + H2O = malonate + urea + H(+).
CC   -!- Forms part of the oxidative pyrimidine-degrading pathway in some
CC       microorganisms, along with EC 1.17.99.4 and EC 3.5.2.1.
//
ID   3.5.1.96
DE   succinylglutamate desuccinylase.
AN   N(2)-succinylglutamate desuccinylase.
AN   SGDS.
CA   N-succinyl-L-glutamate + H2O = L-glutamate + succinate.
CC   -!- N(2)-acetylglutamate is not a substrate.
CC   -!- The final enzyme in the arginine succinyltransferase (AST) pathway
CC       for the catabolism of arginine.
CC   -!- This pathway converts the carbon skeleton of arginine into glutamate,
CC       with the concomitant production of ammonia and conversion of
CC       succinyl-CoA into succinate and CoA.
CC   -!- The five enzymes involved in this pathway are EC 2.3.1.109,
CC       EC 3.5.3.23, EC 2.6.1.11, EC 1.2.1.71 and EC 3.5.1.96.
DR   Q6FCP8, ASTE_ACIAD ;  B7GVV1, ASTE_ACIB3 ;  B7IA88, ASTE_ACIB5 ;
DR   B2HZS2, ASTE_ACIBC ;  B0VQ89, ASTE_ACIBS ;  A3M9D1, ASTE_ACIBT ;
