ID   3.5.1.123
DE   gamma-glutamylanilide hydrolase.
CA   N(5)-phenyl-L-glutamine + H2O = aniline + L-glutamate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Acinetobacter sp. YAA,
CC       catalyzes the opposite reaction from that catalyzed by EC 6.3.1.18,
CC       which is part of an aniline degradation pathway.
CC   -!- Its purpose is likely to maintain a low concentration of N(5)-phenyl-
CC       L-glutamine, which is potentially toxic.
DR   Q44250, ATDA2_ACISP;
