ID   3.5.1.124
DE   protein deglycase.
AN   glyoxylase III.
CA   (1) N(omega)-(1-hydroxy-2-oxopropyl)-L-arginyl-[protein] + H2O = lactate
CA   + L-arginyl-[protein] + H(+).
CA   (2) N(6)-(1-hydroxy-2-oxopropyl)-L-lysyl-[protein] + H2O = lactate +
CA   L-lysyl-[protein] + H(+).
CA   (3) S-(1-hydroxy-2-oxopropyl)-L-cysteinyl-[protein] + H2O = lactate +
CA   L-cysteinyl-[protein] + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, previously thought to be a glyoxalase, acts on glycated
CC       L-arginine, L-lysine, and L-cysteine residues within proteins that
CC       have been attacked and modified by glyoxal or 2-oxopropanal.
CC   -!- The attack forms hemithioacetal in the case of cysteines and
CC       aminocarbinols in the case of arginines and lysines.
CC   -!- The enzyme repairs the amino acids, releasing glycolate or lactate
CC       (70-80% (S)-lactate and 20-30% (R)-lactate), depending on whether the
CC       attacking agent was glyoxal or 2-oxopropanal, respectively.
