ID   3.5.3.23
DE   N-succinylarginine dihydrolase.
AN   arginine succinylhydrolase.
AN   N(2)-succinylarginine dihydrolase.
AN   SADH.
CA   N(2)-succinyl-L-arginine + 2 H2O + 2 H(+) = N(2)-succinyl-L-ornithine +
CA   2 NH4(+) + CO2.
CC   -!- Arginine, N(2)-acetylarginine and N(2)-glutamylarginine do not act as
CC       substrates.
CC   -!- The second enzyme in the arginine succinyltransferase (AST) pathway
CC       for the catabolism of arginine.
CC   -!- This pathway converts the carbon skeleton of arginine into glutamate,
CC       with the concomitant production of ammonia and conversion of
CC       succinyl-CoA into succinate and CoA.
CC   -!- The five enzymes involved in this pathway are EC 2.3.1.109,
CC       EC 3.5.3.23, EC 2.6.1.11, EC 1.2.1.71 and EC 3.5.1.96.
