ID   3.5.3.24
DE   N(1)-aminopropylagmatine ureohydrolase.
CA   N(1)-(3-aminopropyl)agmatine + H2O = urea + spermidine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has been characterized from the hyperthermophilic
CC       archaeon Pyrococcus kodakarensis and the thermophilic Gram-negative
CC       bacterium Thermus thermophilus, is involved in the biosynthesis of
CC       spermidine.
DR   P72703, APAUH_SYNY3;  Q5JI38, APAUH_THEKO;  Q72JK8, APAUH_THET2;
DR   Q5SJ85, APAUH_THET8;
//
ID   3.5.3.25
DE   N(omega)-hydroxy-L-arginine amidinohydrolase.
CA   N(omega)-hydroxy-L-arginine + H2O = hydroxyurea + L-ornithine.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the biosynthetic pathway of D-cycloserine,
CC       an antibiotic substance produced by several Streptomyces species.
DR   D2Z025, DCSB_STRLA ;
//
ID   3.5.3.26
DE   (S)-ureidoglycine aminohydrolase.
CA   (S)-2-ureidoglycine + H2O = (S)-ureidoglycolate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in plants and bacteria, is part of the ureide
CC       pathway, which enables the recycling of the nitrogen in purine
CC       compounds.
CC   -!- In plants it is localized in the endoplasmic reticulum.
DR   P75713, ALLE_ECOLI ;  Q8GXV5, UGHY_ARATH ;  Q7F1K9, UGHY_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   3.5.3.27
DE   arginine dihydrolase.
CA   L-arginine + 2 H2O + 2 H(+) = L-ornithine + 2 NH4(+) + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from different cyanobacterial species,
CC       is highly specific to arginine and does not require a metal cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Nostoc is bifunctional, and also catalyzes the
CC       activity of EC 4.3.1.12.
DR   Q8YMD9, AGRE_NOSS1 ;  P74535, ARGZ_SYNY3 ;
//
ID   3.5.4.1
DE   cytosine deaminase.
AN   Cytosine aminohydrolase.
CA   cytosine + H2O + H(+) = uracil + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on 5-methylcytosine.
DR   P25524, CODA_ECOLI ;  P78594, FCA1_CANAL ;  Q12178, FCY1_YEAST ;
DR   O59834, FCYS_SCHPO ;
//
