//
ID   3.5.4.17
DE   adenosine-phosphate deaminase.
CA   (1) AMP + H2O + H(+) = IMP + NH4(+).
CA   (2) ADP + H2O + H(+) = IDP + NH4(+).
CA   (3) ATP + H2O + H(+) = ITP + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Acts on AMP, ADP, ATP, NAD(+) and adenosine, in decreasing order of
CC       activity.
CC   -!- The bacterial enzyme can also accept the deoxy derivatives (cf.
CC       EC 3.5.4.6).
//
ID   3.5.4.18
DE   ATP deaminase.
CA   ATP + H2O + H(+) = ITP + NH4(+).
//
ID   3.5.4.19
DE   phosphoribosyl-AMP cyclohydrolase.
CA   1-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)-5'-AMP + H2O = 1-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)-
CA   5-[(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosylamino)methylideneamino]imidazole-4-
CA   carboxamide.
CC   -!- The Neurospora crassa enzyme also catalyzes the reactions of
CC       EC 1.1.1.23 and EC 3.6.1.31.
