CA   GTP + 3 H2O = 2-amino-5-formylamino-6-(5-phospho-D-
CA   ribosylamino)pyrimidin-4(3H)-one + 2 phosphate + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of the imidazole ring of
CC       guanosine 5'-triphosphate, N(7)-methylguanosine 5'-triphosphate or
CC       inosine 5'-triphosphate.
CC   -!- Xanthosine 5'-triphosphate and ATP are not substrates.
CC   -!- It also catalyzes the hydrolysis of diphosphate to form two
CC       equivalents of phosphate.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.5.4.25, this enzyme does not release formate, but does
CC       hydrolyze the diphosphate from GTP to phosphate.
