AN   phosphoglucosamine isomerase.
AN   phosphoglucosaminisomerase.
CA   alpha-D-glucosamine 6-phosphate + H2O = beta-D-fructose 6-phosphate +
CA   NH4(+).
CC   -!- Isomerization of the aldose-ketose type converts the -CH(-NH2)-CH=O
CC       group of glucosamine 6-phosphate into -C(=NH)-CH2-OH, forming
CC       2-deoxy-2-imino-D-arabino-hexitol which then hydrolyzes to yield
CC       fructose 6-phosphate and ammonia.
CC   -!- N-acetyl-D-glucosamine 6-phosphate, which is not broken down,
CC       activates the enzyme.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 5.3.1.10.
