ID   3.5.99.7
DE   1-aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate deaminase.
AN   1-aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate endolyase (deaminating).
AN   1-aminocyclopropane carboxylic acid deaminase.
AN   ACC deaminase.
CA   1-aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate + H2O = 2-oxobutanoate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in certain soil bacteria and fungi, catalyzes the
CC       ring opening of 1-aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate, the immediate
CC       precursor to ethylene, an important plant hormone that regulates
CC       fruit ripening and other processes.
CC   -!- The enzyme releases an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to
CC       an imine form, which undergoes spontaneous hydrolytic deamination.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been used to make fruit ripening dependent on
CC       externally added ethylene, as it removes the substrate for endogenous
CC       ethylene formation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.99.4.
DR   B9MGI8, 1A1D_ACIET ;  Q9AHF0, 1A1D_AGRTU ;  B9K206, 1A1D_ALLAM ;
DR   Q89XR6, 1A1D_BRADU ;  A5EJ46, 1A1D_BRASB ;  A4YUJ5, 1A1D_BRASO ;
