ID   3.5.99.8
DE   5-nitroanthranilic acid aminohydrolase.
AN   5NAA deaminase.
CA   5-nitroanthranilate + H2O + H(+) = 5-nitrosalicylate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the initial step in biodegradation of
CC       5-nitroanthranilic acid by Bradyrhizobium sp. strain JS329.
DR   D3WZ85, NAAA_BRASZ ;
//
ID   3.5.99.9
DE   2-nitroimidazole nitrohydrolase.
AN   2NI denitrase.
AN   2NI nitrohydrolase.
CA   2-nitroimidazole + H2O = 1,3-dihydro-2H-imidazol-2-one + nitrite + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the initial step in the biodegradation of
CC       2-nitroimidazole by the soil bacterium Mycobacterium sp. JS330.
DR   F4ZCI3, NNHA_MYCS0 ;
//
ID   3.5.99.10
DE   2-iminobutanoate/2-iminopropanoate deaminase.
AN   enamine/imine deaminase.
CA   (1) 2-iminobutanoate + H2O = 2-oxobutanoate + NH4(+).
CA   (2) 2-iminopropanoate + H2O = pyruvate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, which has been found in all species and tissues
CC       examined, catalyzes the hydrolytic deamination of imine intermediates
CC       formed by several types of pyridoxal-5'-phosphate-dependent
CC       dehydratases, such as EC 4.3.1.19 and EC 4.3.1.17.
CC   -!- The reactions, which can occur spontaneously, are accelerated to
CC       minimize the cellular damage that could be caused by these reactive
CC       intermediates.
DR   Q94JQ4, RIDA_ARATH ;  P37552, RIDA_BACSU ;  Q3T114, RIDA_BOVIN ;
DR   P80601, RIDA_CAPHI ;  A0A1J1DL12, RIDA_DERFA ;  P0AF94, RIDA_ECOL6 ;
DR   P0AF93, RIDA_ECOLI ;  P52758, RIDA_HUMAN ;  P52760, RIDA_MOUSE ;
DR   Q8U308, RIDA_PYRFU ;  P52759, RIDA_RAT   ;  Q7CP78, RIDA_SALTY ;
DR   P0AF95, RIDA_SHIFL ;
