ID   3.5.99.11
DE   2-aminomuconate deaminase (2-hydroxymuconate-forming).
CA   (2Z,4E)-2-aminomuconate + H2O = (2Z,4E)-2-hydroxyhexa-2,4-dienedioate +
CA   NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Comamonas testosteroni
CC       CNB-1, converts 2-aminomuconate to 2-hydroxyhexa-2,4-dienedioate,
CC       unlike the enzymes from Pseudomonas, which produce (3E)-2-oxohex-3-
CC       enedioate (see EC 3.5.99.5).
CC   -!- The enzyme also acts on 2-amino-5-chloromuconate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.5.1.120.
DR   Q09KQ6, CNBZ_COMTE ;
//
ID   3.5.99.12
DE   salsolinol synthase.
AN   Sal synthase.
CA   dopamine + acetaldehyde = (R)-salsolinol + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in mammalian brains, forms the catechol
CC       isoquinoline (R)-salsolinol.
CC   -!- This compound can be metabolized to (R)-N-methylsalsolinol,
CC       a 1-methyl-4-phenylpyridinium-like neurotoxin that impairs the
CC       function of dopaminergic neurons, causing the clinical symptoms of
CC       Parkinson's disease.
//
ID   3.5.99.13
DE   strictosidine synthase.
AN   STR.
AN   strictosidine synthetase.
CA   3alpha(S)-strictosidine + H2O = secologanin + tryptamine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes a Pictet-Spengler reaction between the aldehyde group of
CC       secologanin and the amino group of tryptamine.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of the monoterpenoid indole alkaloids.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.3.2.
DR   P92976, SSL11_ARATH;  P94111, SSL12_ARATH;  P18417, STSY_CATRO ;
DR   P68174, STSY_RAUMA ;  P68175, STSY_RAUSE ;
//
ID   3.5.99.14
DE   (S)-norcoclaurine synthase.
AN   (S)-norlaudanosoline synthase.
CA   (4-hydroxyphenyl)acetaldehyde + dopamine = (S)-norcoclaurine + H2O.
CC   -!- The reaction makes a six-membered ring by forming a bond between C-6
CC       of the 3,4-dihydroxyphenyl group of the dopamine and C-1 of the
CC       aldehyde in the imine formed between the substrates.
CC   -!- The product is the precursor of the benzylisoquinoline alkaloids in
CC       plants.
CC   -!- The enzyme, formerly known as (S)-norlaudanosoline synthase, will
CC       also catalyze the reaction of 4-(2-aminoethyl)benzene-1,2-diol +
CC       (3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)acetaldehyde to form (S)-norlaudanosoline,
CC       but this alkaloid has not been found to occur in plants.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.1.78.
DR   A2A1A0, NCS1_COPJA ;  Q4QTJ2, NCS1_PAPSO ;  A2A1A1, NCS2_COPJA ;
DR   Q4QTJ1, NCS2_PAPSO ;  Q67A25, NCS_THLFG  ;
//
ID   3.5.99.15
DE   deacetylisoipecoside synthase.
CA   deacetylisoipecoside + H2O = secologanin + dopamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the leaves of Alangium lamarckii differs in
CC       enantiomeric specificity from EC 3.5.99.16.
CC   -!- The product is rapidly converted to demethylisoalangiside.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.3.3.
//
ID   3.5.99.16
DE   deacetylipecoside synthase.
CA   deacetylipecoside + H2O = secologanin + dopamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the leaves of Alangium lamarckii differs in
CC       enantiomeric specificity from EC 3.5.99.15.
CC   -!- The product is rapidly converted to demethylalangiside.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.3.4.
//
