ID   3.6.1.9
DE   nucleotide diphosphatase.
AN   dinucleotide nucleotidohydrolase.
AN   nucleoside-triphosphate diphosphatase.
AN   nucleotide pyrophosphatase.
CA   (1) a ribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate + H2O = a ribonucleoside
CA   5'-phosphate + diphosphate + H(+).
CA   (2) a 2'-deoxyribonucleoside 5'-triphosphate + H2O =
CA   a 2'-deoxyribonucleoside 5'-phosphate + diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme preferentially hydrolyzes ATP, but can also hydrolyze
CC       other nucleoside 5' triphosphates such as GTP, CTP, TTP and UTP to
CC       their corresponding monophosphates.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme also acts as a nucleotidohydrolase on ADP,
CC       NAD(+), NADP(+), FAD, and CoA.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.19.
