ID   3.6.1.22
DE   NAD(+) diphosphatase.
AN   NADH pyrophosphatase.
AN   NADP pyrophosphatase.
AN   nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide pyrophosphatase.
CA   (1) NAD(+) + H2O = beta-nicotinamide D-ribonucleotide + AMP + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) NADH + H2O = reduced beta-nicotinamide D-ribonucleotide + AMP +
CA   2 H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, described from plants, animals, and bacteria, can act on
CC       both reduced and oxidized forms of its substrate, although enzymes
CC       from different organisms have different preferences.
CC   -!- Also acts on other dinucleotides, including NADP(H), FAD(H2), and the
CC       thionicotinamide analogs of NAD(+) and NADP(+).
