ID   3.6.1.58
DE   8-oxo-dGDP phosphatase.
CA   (1) 8-oxo-dGDP + H2O = 8-oxo-dGMP + phosphate + H(+).
CA   (2) 8-oxo-GDP + H2O = 8-oxo-GMP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of both 8-oxo-dGDP and 8-oxo-GDP
CC       thereby preventing translational errors caused by oxidative damage.
CC   -!- The preferred in vivo substrate is not known.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not degrade 8-oxo-dGTP and 8-oxo-GTP to the
CC       monophosphates (cf. EC 3.6.1.55).
CC   -!- Ribonucleotide diphosphates and deoxyribonucleotide diphosphates are
CC       hydrolyzed with broad specificity.
CC   -!- The bifunctional enzyme NUDT5 also hydrolyzes ADP-ribose to AMP and
CC       D-ribose 5-phosphate (cf. EC 3.6.1.13).
CC   -!- The human enzyme NUDT18 also hydrolyzes 8-oxo-dADP and 2-hydroxy-
CC       dADP, the latter at a slower rate.
DR   I6X235, ADPP_MYCTU ;  A0QUZ2, MUTT1_MYCS2;  Q568Q0, NUD18_DANRE;
