ID   3.6.1.69
DE   8-oxo-(d)GTP phosphatase.
CA   (1) 8-oxo-GTP + H2O = 8-oxo-GDP + phosphate + H(+).
CA   (2) 8-oxo-dGTP + H2O = 8-oxo-dGDP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Mycobacterium
CC       tuberculosis, catalyzes the hydrolysis of both 8-oxo-GTP and 8-oxo-
CC       dGTP, thereby preventing transcriptional and translational errors
CC       caused by oxidative damage.
CC   -!- The enzyme is highly specific.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.6.1.55, it removes only a single phosphate group.
CC   -!- The nucleoside diphosphate products are hydrolyzed further by
CC       EC 3.6.1.58.
DR   A0QUZ2, MUTT1_MYCS2;  P9WIY2, MUTT1_MYCTO;  P9WIY3, MUTT1_MYCTU;
DR   Q9RVK2, Y1025_DEIRA;
//
ID   3.6.1.70
DE   guanosine-5'-diphospho-5'-[DNA] diphosphatase.
AN   aprataxin.
AN   pp5'G5'DNA diphosphatase.
AN   pp5'G5'-DNA guanylate hydrolase.
CA   a 5'-end guanosine-5'-diphospho-5'-(2'-deoxyribonucleoside)-DNA + H2O =
CA   a 5'-end 5'-phospho-2'-deoxyribonucleoside-DNA + GMP + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Aprataxin is a DNA-binding protein that catalyzes (among other
CC       activities) the 5' decapping of Gpp-DNA (formed by homologs of RtcB3
CC       from the bacterium Myxococcus xanthus).
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the guanylate group to a histidine residue at its
CC       active site, forming a covalent enzyme-nucleotide phosphate
CC       intermediate, followed by the hydrolysis of the guanylate from the
CC       nucleic acid and eventual release.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a 5'-phospho terminus that can be efficiently joined
CC       by 'classical' ligases.
CC   -!- The enzyme also possesses the activity of EC 3.6.1.71 and
CC       EC 3.6.1.72.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.11.8.
//
ID   3.6.1.71
DE   adenosine-5'-diphospho-5'-[DNA] diphosphatase.
AN   5'-App5'-DNA adenylate hydrolase.
AN   aprataxin.
CA   (1) a 5'-end adenosine-5'-diphospho-5'-2'-deoxyribonucleoside-DNA + H2O =
CA   a 5'-end 5'-phospho-2'-deoxyribonucleoside-DNA + AMP + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) a 5'-end adenosine-5'-diphospho-5'-ribonucleoside-
CA   2'-deoxyribonucleotide-DNA + H2O = a 5'-end 5'-phospho-ribonucleoside-
CA   2'-deoxyribonucleotide-DNA + AMP + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Aprataxin is a DNA-binding protein involved in different types of DNA
CC       break repair.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts (among other activities) on abortive DNA ligation
CC       intermediates that contain an adenylate covalently linked to the
CC       5'-phosphate DNA terminus.
CC   -!- It also acts when the adenylate is covalently linked to the
CC       5'-phosphate of a ribonucleotide linked to a DNA strand, which is the
CC       result of abortive ligase activty on products of EC 3.1.26.4,
CC       an enzyme that cleaves RNA-DNA hybrids on the 5' side of the
CC       ribonucleotide found in the 5'-RNA-DNA-3' junction.
CC   -!- Aprataxin binds the adenylate group to a histidine residue within the
CC       active site, followed by its hydrolysis from the nucleic acid and
CC       eventual release, leaving a 5'-phosphate terminus that can be
CC       efficiently rejoined.
CC   -!- The enzyme also possesses the activities of EC 3.6.1.70 and
CC       EC 3.6.1.72.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.11.7.
