CA   a 3'-end 2'-deoxyribonucleotide 3'-phosphate-DNA + GMP + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- Aprataxin is a DNA-binding protein that catalyzes (among other
CC       activities) the 3' decapping of DNA-ppG (formed by EC 6.5.1.8).
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the guanylate group to a histidine residue at its
CC       active site, forming a covalent enzyme-nucleotide phosphate
