//
ID   3.6.5.1
DE   heterotrimeric G-protein GTPase.
CA   GTP + H2O = GDP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- This group comprises GTP-hydrolyzing systems, where GTP and GDP
CC       alternate in binding.
CC   -!- This group includes stimulatory and inhibitory G-proteins such as Gs,
CC       Gi, Go and Golf, targeting adenylate cyclase and/or K(+) and Ca(2+)
CC       channels; Gq stimulating phospholipase C; transducin activating cGMP
CC       phosphodiesterase; gustducin activating cAMP phosphodiesterase.
CC   -!- Golf is instrumental in odor perception, transducin in vision and
CC       gustducin in taste recognition.
CC   -!- At least 16 different alpha subunits (39-52 kDa), 5 beta subunits (36
CC       kDa) and 12 gamma subunits (6-9 kDa) are known.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.46.
//
ID   3.6.5.2
DE   small monomeric GTPase.
CA   GTP + H2O = GDP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- A family of about 50 enzymes with a molecular mass of 21 kDa that are
CC       distantly related to the alpha-subunit of EC 3.6.1.46.
CC   -!- Involved in cell-growth regulation (Ras subfamily), membrane vesicle
CC       traffic and uncoating (Rab and ARF subfamilies), nuclear protein
CC       import (Ran subfamily) and organization of the cytoskeleton (Rho and
CC       Rac subfamilies).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.47.
