ID   4.1.2.43
DE   3-hexulose-6-phosphate synthase.
AN   3-hexulosephosphate synthase.
AN   3-hexulose phosphate synthase.
AN   D-arabino-3-hexulose 6-phosphate formaldehyde-lyase.
AN   HPS.
CA   D-ribulose 5-phosphate + formaldehyde = D-arabino-hex-3-ulose
CA   6-phosphate.
CC   -!- Specific for formaldehyde and D-ribulose 5-phosphate as substrates.
CC   -!- Ribose 5-phosphate, xylulose 5-phosphate, allulose 6-phosphate and
CC       fructose 6-phosphate cannot act as substrate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, along with EC 5.3.1.27, plays a key role in the
CC       ribulose-monophosphate cycle of formaldehyde fixation, which is
CC       present in many microorganisms that are capable of utilizing
CC       C1-compounds.
CC   -!- The hyperthermophilic and anaerobic archaeon Pyrococcus horikoshii
CC       OT3 constitutively produces a bifunctional enzyme that sequentially
