ID   4.1.2.60
DE   dihydroneopterin triphosphate aldolase.
CA   7,8-dihydroneopterin 3'-triphosphate = glycolaldehyde triphosphate +
CA   6-hydroxymethyl-7,8-dihydropterin.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which participates in a pathway for folate biosynthesis,
CC       is found in the Stramenopiles, a large group that includes oomycetes,
CC       various microalgae and brown algae, as well as in several bacterial
CC       phyla.
CC   -!- It provides a bypass mechanism compensating for the lack of
CC       EC 4.1.2.25.
CC   -!- In the malaria parasite Plasmodium falciparum the enzyme is
CC       bifunctional and also catalyzes the activity of EC 4.2.3.12. cf.
CC       EC 4.1.2.59.
//
ID   4.1.2.61
DE   feruloyl-CoA hydratase/lyase.
CA   (E)-feruloyl-CoA + H2O = vanillin + acetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a member of the enoyl-CoA hydratase/isomerase
CC       superfamily.
CC   -!- It catalyzes a two-step process involving first the hydration of the
CC       double bond of feruloyl-CoA and then the cleavage of the resultant
CC       beta-hydroxy thioester by retro-aldol reaction.
CC   -!- (E)-caffeoyl-CoA and (E)-4-coumaroyl-CoA are also substrates.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.2.41 and EC 4.2.1.101.
