ID   4.1.3.27
DE   anthranilate synthase.
CA   chorismate + L-glutamine = anthranilate + pyruvate + L-glutamate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in plants, fungi and bacteria is composed of two
CC       parts, a glutaminase subunit and a lyase subunit.
CC   -!- The glutaminase produces ammonia that is channeled to the lyase
CC       subunit.
CC   -!- In the absence of the glutaminase, the lyase can convert ammonia and
CC       chorismate into anthranilate.
CC   -!- In some organisms, this enzyme is part of a multifunctional protein,
CC       together with one or more other components of the system for the
CC       biosynthesis of tryptophan (EC 2.4.2.18, EC 4.1.1.48, EC 4.2.1.20,
CC       and EC 5.3.1.24).
