ID   4.1.99.2
DE   tyrosine phenol-lyase.
AN   beta-tyrosinase.
CA   L-tyrosine + H2O = phenol + pyruvate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme cleaves a carbon-carbon bond, releasing phenol and an
CC       unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form, which
CC       undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and ammonia.
CC   -!- The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be
CC       catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.
CC   -!- The enzyme also slowly catalyzes similar reactions with D-tyrosine,
CC       S-methyl-L-cysteine, L-cysteine, L-serine and D-serine.
DR   P31013, TPL_CITFR  ;  P31012, TPL_CITIN  ;  Q897C2, TPL_CLOTE  ;
