ID   4.1.99.13
DE   (6-4)DNA photolyase.
AN   DNA photolyase.
CA   (6-4) photoproduct (in DNA) = 2 pyrimidine residues (in DNA).
CC   -!- The overall repair reaction consists of two distinct steps, one of
CC       which is light-independent and the other one light-dependent.
CC   -!- In the initial light-independent step, a 6-iminium ion is thought to
CC       be generated via proton transfer induced by two histidines highly
CC       conserved among the (6-4) photolyases.
CC   -!- This intermediate spontaneously rearranges to form an oxetane
CC       intermediate by intramolecular nucleophilic attack.
CC   -!- In the subsequent light-driven reaction, one electron is believed to
CC       be transferred from the fully reduced FAD cofactor (FADH(-)) to the
CC       oxetane intermediate thus forming a neutral FADH radical and an
CC       anionic oxetane radical, which spontaneously fractures.
CC   -!- The excess electron is then back-transferred to the flavin radical
CC       restoring the fully reduced flavin cofactor and a pair of pyrimidine
CC       bases.
DR   A9CH39, PHRB_AGRFC ;  O48652, UVR3_ARATH ;  Q0E2Y1, UVR3_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   4.1.99.14
DE   spore photoproduct lyase.
AN   SP lyase.
CA   (5R)-5,6-dihydro-5-(thymidin-7-yl)thymidine in DNA = a thymidine dimer in
CA   DNA.
CC   -!- This enzyme is a member of the 'AdoMet radical' (radical SAM) family.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster.
CC   -!- The cluster is coordinated by 3 cysteines and an exchangeable SAM
CC       molecule.
CC   -!- The 5'-deoxy-adenosine radical formed after electron transfer from
CC       the [4Fe-4S] cluster to the S-adenosyl-L-methionine, initiates the
CC       repair by abstracting the C-6 hydrogen of the spore photoproduct
CC       lesion.
CC   -!- During the second part of the repair process the SAM molecule is
CC       regenerated.
DR   Q97L63, SPLB_CLOAB ;  P37956, SPL_BACSU  ;  C9RZ55, SPL_GEOSY  ;
//
ID   4.1.99.15
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   4.1.99.16
DE   geosmin synthase.
CA   (1E,4S,5E,7R)-germacra-1(10),5-dien-11-ol + H2O = (-)-geosmin + acetone.
CC   -!- Geosmin is the cause of the characteristic smell of moist soil.
CC   -!- It is a bifunctional enzyme.
CC   -!- The N-terminal part of the enzyme is EC 4.2.3.22, germacradienol
CC       synthase, and forms germacradienol from FPP.
CC   -!- The C-terminal part of the enzyme catalyzes the conversion of
CC       germacradienol to geosmin via (1S,4aS,8aS)-8,10-dimethyl-
CC       1,2,3,4,4a,5,6,8a-octahydronaphthalene.
DR   Q9X839, CYC2_STRCO ;
//
ID   4.1.99.17
DE   phosphomethylpyrimidine synthase.
CA   5-amino-1-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)imidazole + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   4-amino-2-methyl-5-(phosphooxymethyl)pyrimidine + CO + 5'-deoxyadenosine
CA   + formate + L-methionine + 3 H(+).
CC   -!- Binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster that is coordinated by 3 cysteines and an
CC       exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-methionine molecule.
CC   -!- The first stage of catalysis is reduction of the S-adenosyl-L-
CC       methionine to produce L-methionine and a 5'-deoxyadenosin-5'-yl
CC       radical that is crucial for the conversion of the substrate.
CC   -!- Part of the pathway for thiamine biosynthesis.
