ID   4.1.99.19
DE   2-iminoacetate synthase.
CA   L-tyrosine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine + NADPH = 2-iminoacetate +
CA   4-methylphenol + 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + NADP(+).
CC   -!- Binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster that is coordinated by 3 cysteines and an
CC       exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-methionine molecule.
CC   -!- The first stage of catalysis is reduction of the S-adenosyl-L-
CC       methionine to produce methionine and a 5-deoxyadenosin-5-yl radical
CC       that is crucial for the conversion of the substrate.
CC   -!- Part of the pathway for thiamine biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.n2.
DR   P30140, THIH_ECOLI ;  Q9S498, THIH_SALTY ;
