//
ID   4.2.1.20
DE   tryptophan synthase.
AN   indoleglycerol phosphate aldolase.
AN   L-tryptophan synthetase.
AN   tryptophan desmolase.
AN   tryptophan synthetase.
CA   (1S,2R)-1-C-(indol-3-yl)glycerol 3-phosphate + L-serine =
CA   D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate + L-tryptophan + H2O.
CC   -!- The alpha-subunit catalyzes the conversion of 1-C-(indol-3-
CC       yl)glycerol 3-phosphate to indole and D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate
CC       (this reaction was listed formerly as EC 4.1.2.8).
CC   -!- The indole migrates to the beta-subunit where, in the presence of
CC       pyridoxal 5'-phosphate, it is combined with L-serine to form
CC       L-tryptophan.
CC   -!- In some organisms this enzyme is part of a multifunctional protein
CC       that also includes one or more of the enzymes EC 2.4.2.18,
CC       EC 4.1.1.48, EC 4.1.3.27 and EC 5.3.1.24.
CC   -!- In thermophilic organisms, where the high temperature enhances
CC       diffusion and causes the loss of indole, a protein similar to the
CC       beta subunit can be found (EC 4.2.1.122).
CC   -!- That enzyme cannot combine with the alpha unit of EC 4.2.1.20 to form
CC       a complex.
