ID   4.2.1.24
DE   porphobilinogen synthase.
AN   aminolevulinate dehydratase.
AN   delta-aminolevulinic acid dehydratase.
CA   2 5-aminolevulinate = porphobilinogen + 2 H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the asymmetric condensation and cyclization of
CC       two 5-aminolevulinate molecules, which is the first common step in
CC       the biosynthesis of tetrapyrrole pigments such as porphyrin,
CC       chlorophyll, vitamin B12, siroheme, phycobilin, and cofactor F430.
CC   -!- The enzyme is widespread, being essential in organisms that carry out
CC       respiration, photosynthesis, or methanogenesis.
CC   -!- In humans, the enzyme is a primary target for the environmental toxin
CC       Pb.
CC   -!- The enzymes from some organisms utilize a dynamic equilibrium between
CC       architecturally distinct multimeric assemblies as a means for
CC       allosteric regulation.
DR   Q9SFH9, HEM21_ARATH;  Q94LA4, HEM22_ARATH;  O67876, HEM2_AQUAE ;
