ID   4.2.1.27
DE   acetylenecarboxylate hydratase.
AN   acetylenemonocarboxylate hydratase.
AN   alkynoate hydratase.
AN   malonate-semialdehyde dehydratase.
CA   3-oxopropanoate = propynoate + H2O.
CC   -!- The reaction is effectively irreversible, favoring oxopropanoate
CC       (malonic semialdehyde) and its tautomers.
CC   -!- Also acts on but-3-ynoate forming acetoacetate.
CC   -!- The mechanism appears to involve hydration of the acetylene to
CC       3-hydroxypropenoate, which will spontaneously tautomerize to
CC       3-oxopropanoate.
CC   -!- It is thus analogous to EC 4.1.1.78 in its mechanism.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.1.71.
//
ID   4.2.1.28
DE   propanediol dehydratase.
CA   propane-1,2-diol = propanal + H2O.
CC   -!- Two different forms of the enzyme have been described.
CC   -!- One form requires a cobamide cofactor, while the other is a glycyl
CC       radical enzyme.
CC   -!- The cobamide-dependent enzyme has been shown to also dehydrate
CC       ethylene glycol to acetaldehyde.
DR   P0DUM7, PDUC_CITFR ;  P37450, PDUC_SALTY ;  P0DUM8, PDUD_CITFR ;
DR   O31041, PDUD_SALTY ;  P0DUM9, PDUE_CITFR ;  O31042, PDUE_SALTY ;
