ID   4.2.1.80
DE   2-oxopent-4-enoate hydratase.
AN   2-keto-4-pentenoate hydratase.
AN   OEH.
CA   (S)-4-hydroxy-2-oxopentanoate = (2Z)-2-hydroxypenta-2,4-dienoate + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the catechol meta-cleavage pathway, a major
CC       mechanism for degradation of aromatic compounds.
CC   -!- Also acts, more slowly, on cis-2-oxohex-4-enoate, but not on the
CC       trans-isomer.
CC   -!- The enzyme was named when it was thought that the substrate is
CC       2-oxopent-4-enoate.
CC   -!- However, it was later found that the actual substrate is its tautomer
CC       (2Z)-2-hydroxypenta-2,4-dienoate.
CC   -!- In some organisms the enzyme forms a complex with EC 4.1.1.77.
DR   Q9KWS4, AMNF_PSESP ;  Q47HM0, MHPD1_DECAR;  Q400K2, MHPD1_PSEPU;
