DE   cyanase.
AN   cyanate aminohydrolase.
AN   cyanate C-N-lyase.
AN   cyanate hydratase.
AN   cyanate hydrolase.
AN   cyanate lyase.
CA   cyanate + hydrogencarbonate + 3 H(+) = NH4(+) + 2 CO2.
CC   -!- This enzyme, which is found in bacteria and plants, is used to
CC       decompose cyanate, which can be used as the sole source of nitrogen.
CC   -!- The reaction can be considered as the reverse of 'carbamate = cyanate
CC       + H2O', where this is assisted by reaction with bicarbonate and
CC       carbon dioxide, and hence is classified in sub-subclass 4.2.1.
CC   -!- Bicarbonate functions as a recycling substrate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.5.5.3 and EC 4.3.99.1.
