ID   4.2.1.119
DE   enoyl-CoA hydratase 2.
AN   2-enoyl-CoA hydratase 2.
AN   D-3-hydroxyacyl-CoA hydro-lyase.
AN   D-specific 2-trans-enoyl-CoA hydratase.
AN   ECH2.
CA   a (3R)-3-hydroxyacyl-CoA = a (2E)-enoyl-CoA + H2O.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a hydration step in peroxisomal beta-oxidation.
CC   -!- The human multifunctional enzyme type 2 (MFE-2) is a 79000 Da enzyme
CC       composed of three functional units: (3R)-hydroxyacyl-CoA
CC       dehydrogenase, 2-enoyl-CoA hydratase 2 and sterol carrier protein
CC       2-like units.
CC   -!- The enzymes from Aeromonas caviae and Arabidopsis thaliana are
CC       monofunctional enzymes.
CC   -!- 2-enoyl-CoA hydratase 3 from Candida tropicalis is a part from
CC       multifunctional enzyme type 2.
DR   Q9VXJ0, DHB4_DROME ;  P51659, DHB4_HUMAN ;  P51660, DHB4_MOUSE ;
DR   P97852, DHB4_RAT   ;  Q8VYI3, ECH2_ARATH ;  P22414, FOX2_CANTR ;
DR   Q01373, FOX2_NEUCR ;  Q02207, FOX2_YEAST ;  O53664, HTDX_MYCTU ;
DR   I6YBZ8, HTDY_MYCTU ;  Q7U2S5, HTDZ_MYCBO ;  P9WNP2, HTDZ_MYCTO ;
DR   P9WNP3, HTDZ_MYCTU ;  Q54XZ0, MFEB_DICDI ;  O32472, PHAJ_AERCA ;
DR   Q2RQ36, PHAJ_RHORT ;
//
ID   4.2.1.120
DE   4-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA dehydratase.
CA   4-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA = (2E)-butenoyl-CoA + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from several microorganisms,
CC       including Clostridium kluyveri, where it participates in succinate
CC       fermentation, Clostridium aminobutyricum, where it participates in
CC       4-aminobutyrate degradation, and Metallosphaera sedula, where it
CC       participates in the 3-hydroxypropionate/4-hydroxybutyrate cycle,
CC       an autotrophic CO2 fixation pathway found in some thermoacidophilic
CC       archaea.
DR   P55792, HDVD_CLOAM ;
