CC   -!- The enzyme, found in some amino acid-fermenting anaerobic bacteria,
CC       participates in the fermentation pathways of L-phenylalanine,
CC       L-tyrosine, and L-tryptophan.
CC   -!- It is a heterodimeric protein consisting of the FldB and
CC       FldC polypeptides, both of which contain an [4Fe-4S] cluster,
CC       and forms a complex with EC 2.8.3.17.
CC   -!- In order to catalyze the reaction, the enzyme requires one high-
CC       energy electron that transiently reduces the electrophilic thiol
CC       ester carbonyl of the substrate to a nucleophilic ketyl radical
CC       anion, facilitating the elimination of the hydroxyl group.
CC   -!- This electron, which is provided by by EC 5.6.1.9, needs to be
CC       supplied only once, before the first reaction takes place, as it is
CC       regenerated at the end of each reaction cycle.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on (R)-3-(aryl)lactoyl-CoAs produced by FldA,
CC       and regenerates the CoA donors used by that enzyme.
