ID   4.2.3.94
DE   gamma-curcumene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = gamma-curcumene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- One of five sesquiterpenoid synthases in Pogostemon cablin
CC       (patchouli).
DR   Q6JD73, TPS4A_MAIZE;  Q6JD70, TPS5A_MAIZE;  Q49SP7, TPSCS_POGCB;
//
ID   4.2.3.95
DE   (-)-alpha-cuprenene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (-)-alpha-cuprenene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Coprinus cinereus produces (-)-alpha-cuprenene with
CC       high selectivity.
DR   Q4KSH9, BARS_ARATH ;
//
ID   4.2.3.96
DE   avermitilol synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H2O = avermitilol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The recombinent enzyme gives avermitilol (85%) plus traces of
CC       germacrene A, germacrene B and viridiflorol.
CC   -!- The (1S)-hydrogen of farnesyl diphosphate is retained.
DR   Q82RR7, TPC1_STRAW ;
//
ID   4.2.3.97
DE   (-)-delta-cadinene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (-)-delta-cadinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The cyclization mechanism involves an intermediate nerolidyl
CC       diphosphate leading to a helminthogermacradienyl cation.
CC   -!- Following a 1,3-hydride shift of the original 1-pro-S hydrogen of
CC       (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate, cyclization and deprotonation gives
CC       (-)-delta-cadinene.
DR   B5GS26, DCADS_STRCL;
//
ID   4.2.3.98
DE   (+)-T-muurolol synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H2O = (+)-T-muurolol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The cyclization mechanism involves an intermediate nerolidyl
CC       diphosphate leading to a helminthogermacradienyl cation.
CC   -!- After a 1,3-hydride shift of the original 1-pro-S hydrogen of
CC       farnesyl diphosphate, cyclization and deprotonation result in (+)-T-
CC       muurolol.
DR   A0A8H8CMW1, CUBA_PSICU ;  A7NH01, TMUUS_ROSCS;  B5GW45, TMUUS_STRCL;
//
ID   4.2.3.99
DE   labdatriene synthase.
CA   9alpha-copalyl diphosphate = (12E)-9alpha-labda-8(17),12,14-triene +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from rice (Oryza sativa), expressed in Escherichia coli,
CC       also produces ent-sandaracopimara-8(14),15-diene from ent-copalyl
CC       diphosphate, another naturally occurring copalyl isomer in rice (cf.
CC       EC 4.2.3.29).
DR   Q2QQJ5, KSL10_ORYSJ;
//
ID   4.2.3.100
DE   bicyclogermacrene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = bicyclogermacrene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from oregano (Origanum vulgare) gives mainly
CC       bicyclogermacrene with Mn(2+) as a cofactor.
CC   -!- With Mg(2+) a more complex mixture is produced.
DR   E2E2N7, BCGS_ORIVU ;  U3LVL5, GERDS_LAVAN;  A0A348B782, STS6_POSPM ;
DR   J7LMP2, TPS5_PHYDL ;  A0A0A2JP58, TS4_PENEN  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.101
DE   7-epi-sesquithujene synthase.
AN   TPS4-B73.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = 7-epi-sesquithujene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Zea mays, variety B73, gives mainly 7-epi-
CC       sesquithujene with (S)-beta-bisabolene and traces of other
CC       sesquiterpenoids, cf. EC 4.2.3.55.
CC   -!- The product ratio is dependent on which metal ion is present.
CC   -!- 7-epi-sesquithujene is an attractant for the emerald ash borer
CC       beetle.
DR   Q6JD73, TPS4A_MAIZE;
//
ID   4.2.3.102
DE   sesquithujene synthase.
AN   TPS5-Del1.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = sesquithujene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Zea mays, variety Delprim, gives mainly sesquithujene
CC       with (S)-beta-bisabolene and (E)-beta-farnesene plus traces of other
CC       sesquiterpenoids, cf. EC 4.2.3.55 and EC 4.2.3.47.
CC   -!- The exact product ratio is dependent on which metal ion is present.
DR   Q6JD70, TPS5A_MAIZE;
//
ID   4.2.3.103
DE   ent-isokaurene synthase.
AN   ent-isokaur-15-ene synthase.
CA   ent-copalyl diphosphate = ent-isokaurene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Two enzymes of the rice sub-species Oryza sativa subsp. indica,
CC       OsKSL5 and OsKSL6, produce ent-isokaurene.
CC   -!- A variant of OsKSL5 from the sub-species Oryza sativa subsp. japonica
CC       produces ent-pimara-8(14),15-diene instead (cf. EC 4.2.3.30).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.3.n8.
DR   A5A8G0, CPSKS_PHYPA;  A4KAG7, KSL5_ORYSI ;  A4KAG8, KSL6_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   4.2.3.104
DE   alpha-humulene synthase.
AN   ZSS1.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = alpha-humulene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Zingiber zerumbet, shampoo ginger, also gives traces
CC       of beta-caryophyllene.
DR   F2XF97, AHUMS_PICGL;  A0A2U8U2L5, ASR6_SARSH ;  E2E2N5, BCPSD_ORIVU;
DR   E2E2N4, BCPSF_ORIVU;  Q4U3F6, CS_HELAN   ;  A0A8H7XP09, CUBC_PSICU ;
DR   A0A4P8GFV8, EUPE_PHOSX ;  Q84UU4, HUMS_ARATH ;  B6SCF5, STS1_HUMLU ;
DR   A0A5S9I252, TATC6_HYPAT;  G8H5M8, TPS12_SOLHA;  D5KXD2, TPS12_SOLLC;
DR   A0A1V0E492, TPS1_PIPNI ;  I7H727, TPS2_TOOSI ;  A0A1V0QSG6, TS4FN_CANSA;
DR   A0A7J6HK32, TS9FN_CANSA;  B1B1U3, ZSS1_ZINZE ;
//
ID   4.2.3.105
DE   tricyclene synthase.
CA   (2E)-geranyl diphosphate = tricyclene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Solanum lycopersicum (tomato) gives a mixture of
CC       tricyclene, camphene, beta-myrcene, limonene, and traces of several
CC       other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.117, EC 4.2.3.15 and EC 4.2.3.16.
DR   R9QMY8, CAMPS_PINCO;  Q84NC8, TPS1_ANTMA ;  Q84ND0, TPS2_ANTMA ;
