//
ID   4.2.3.214
DE   dolasta-1(15),8-diene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = (5R,12R,14S)-dolasta-1(15),8-
CA   diene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Colletotrichum gloeosporioides, a pathogenic fungus
CC       that causes bitter rot in variety of crops.
DR   P9WEV7, CGDS_COLGL ;
//
ID   4.2.3.215
DE   delta-araneosene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = delta-araneosene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Colletotrichum gloeosporioidea.
CC   -!- delta-Araneosene may be involved in the biosynthesis of dolasta-
CC       1(15),8-diene (see EC 4.2.3.214) and cycloaraneosene (see
CC       EC 4.2.3.191).
DR   P9WEV7, CGDS_COLGL ;
//
ID   4.2.3.216
DE   somaliensene A synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E,14E)-geranylfarnesyl diphosphate = somaliensene A +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- A sesterterpenoid synthase enzyme isolated from the bacterium
CC       Streptomyces somaliensis.
CC   -!- The enzyme also produces somalensene B (cf. EC 4.2.3.217).
DR   P0DXD5, STSC_STRE0 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.217
DE   somaliensene B synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E,14E)-geranylfarnesyl diphosphate = (-)-somaliensene B +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- A sesterterpenoid synthase enzyme isolated from the bacterium
CC       Streptomyces somaliensis.
CC   -!- The enzyme also produces somaliensene A (cf. EC 4.2.3.216).
DR   P0DXD5, STSC_STRE0 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.218
DE   variediene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = variediene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- A diterpenoid synthase enzyme isolated from the fungus Aspergillus
CC       stellatus.
DR   A0A0P0ZD79, EVVS_EMEVA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.219
DE   (2E)-alpha-cericerene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E,14E)-geranylfarnesyl diphosphate = (R,2E)-alpha-cericerene +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- A sesterterpenoid synthase enzyme isolated from the fungus
CC       Aspergillus stellatus.
DR   A0A0P0ZD79, EVVS_EMEVA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.220
DE   talaropentaene synthase.
CA   all-trans-hexaprenyl diphosphate = talaropentaene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Talaromyces verruculosus.
DR   P9WER5, TVTS_TALVE ;
//
ID   4.2.3.221
DE   macrophomene synthase.
CA   all-trans-hexaprenyl diphosphate = macrophomene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Macrophomina phaseolina, a pathogenic fungus that
CC       causes damping off, seedling blight, collar rot, stem rot, charcoal
CC       rot, basal stem rot, and root rot on many plant species.
CC   -!- The 22-membered ring in macrophomene represents the largest
CC       macrocycle discovered in terpenes so far.
DR   K2SUY0, MPMS_MACPH ;
//
ID   4.2.3.222
DE   phomopsene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = phomopsene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- A diterpene synthase from the fungus Diaporthe amygdali.
CC   -!- Phomopsene synthase has also been isolated from the bacteria Nocardia
CC       testacea, Nocardia rhamnosiphila, and Allokutzneria albata.
CC   -!- The Allokutzneria albata enzyme also generates allokutznerene
CC       (EC 4.2.3.224) and traces of (-)-spiroviolene (EC 4.2.3.158).
DR   A0A1G9VRW7, PMS_ALLAB  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.223
DE   bonnadiene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = bonnadiene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- A diterpene synthase isolated from the bacterium Allokutzneria
CC       albata.
DR   A0A1G9UQQ0, BDS_ALLAB  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.224
DE   allokutznerene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = allokutznerene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- A diterpene synthase isolated from the bacterium Allokutzneria
CC       albata.
CC   -!- It also produces phomopsene (EC 4.2.3.222) and traces of (-)-
CC       spiroviolene (EC 4.2.3.158).
DR   A0A1G9VRW7, PMS_ALLAB  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.225
DE   cattleyene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E)-geranylgeranyl diphosphate = cattleyene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- A diterpene synthase isolated from the bacterium Streptantibioticus
CC       cattleyicolor.
DR   F8JK18, CYS_STREN  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.226
DE   (+)-2-epi-prezizaene synthase.
CA   (2Z,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (+)-2-epi-prezizaene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme occurs in plants.
CC   -!- The initial cyclization product is a (7R)-beta-bisabolyl cation.
CC   -!- The major final product is (+)-2-epi-prezizaene.
CC   -!- Other products are (-)-alpha-cedrene (cf. EC 4.2.3.227), small
CC       amounts of (-)-beta-curcumene, and other sesquiterpenes with less
CC       than 10% yield.
CC   -!- The enzyme also catalyzes the reaction of EC 4.2.3.61.
DR   Q40577, 5EAS_TOBAC ;
//
ID   4.2.3.227
DE   (-)-alpha-cedrene synthase.
CA   (2Z,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (-)-alpha-cedrene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme occurs in plants.
CC   -!- The initial cyclization product is a (7R)-beta-bisabolyl cation.
CC   -!- (-)-alpha-cedrene is one of the major products.
CC   -!- Other products are (+)-2-epi-prezizaene (cf. EC 4.2.3.226), small
CC       amounts of (+)-beta-curcumene, and other sesquiterpenes with less
CC       than 10% yield.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Nicotiana tabacum (tobacco) also catalyzes the
CC       reaction of EC 4.2.3.61.
DR   Q40577, 5EAS_TOBAC ;
//
ID   4.2.3.228
DE   (Z)-beta-ocimene synthase.
CA   (2E)-geranyl diphosphate = (Z)-beta-ocimene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme found in flowers (pistillate inflorescences) of Cannabis
CC       sativa produces 94% (Z)-beta-ocimene from geranyl diphosphate. cf.
CC       EC 4.2.3.106.
DR   A0A8H7XP09, CUBC_PSICU ;  A0A1V0QSG1, T13PK_CANSA;  A0A1V0QSH1, TS6FN_CANSA;
//
ID   4.2.3.229
DE   ent-beyerene synthase.
CA   ent-copalyl diphosphate = ent-beyerene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been shown to occur in castor bean (Ricinus communis)
CC       and rice (Oryza sativa).
CC   -!- ent-beyerene is also a product of EC 4.2.3.19 of the moss
CC       Physcomitrella patens.
DR   A5A8G0, CPSKS_PHYPA;  Q0JA81, KSL2_ORYSJ ;  B9SIM3, KSL4_RICCO ;
//
ID   4.2.3.230
DE   2-deoxy-4-epi-scyllo-inosose synthase.
CA   D-mannose 6-phosphate = 2-deoxy-4-epi-scyllo-inosose + phosphate.
CC   -!- Requires Co(2+) or Ni(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from the cyanobacterium Nostoc
CC       punctiforme and the Gram-negative cellulose degrading bacterium
CC       Sporocytophaga myxococcoides.
CC   -!- cf. EC 4.2.3.124.
