ID   4.2.99.21
DE   isochorismate lyase.
AN   isochorismate pyruvate lyase.
CA   isochorismate = salicylate + pyruvate.
CC   -!- This enzyme is part of the pathway of salicylate formation from
CC       chorismate, and forms an integral part of pathways that produce
CC       salicylate-derived siderophores, such as pyochelin and
CC       yersiniabactin.
DR   Q7TYQ1, MBTI_MYCBO ;  Q73XV3, MBTI_MYCPA ;  P9WFX0, MBTI_MYCTO ;
DR   P9WFX1, MBTI_MYCTU ;  Q51507, PCHB_PSEAE ;
//
ID   4.2.99.22
DE   tuliposide A-converting enzyme.
AN   6-O-(4 -hydroxy-2 -methylenebutyryl)-D-glucose acyltransferase (lactone-
AN   forming).
AN   tuliposide-converting enzyme.
CA   6-tuliposide A = tulipalin A + D-glucose.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Tulipa gesneriana (tulip).
CC   -!- The reaction is an intramolecular transesterification producing the
CC       lactone.
CC   -!- The enzyme also has a weak activity with 6-tuliposide B and 6-O-
CC       benzoyl-D-glucose.
DR   R4X244, TCAB1_TULGE;  R4X4V6, TCAB2_TULGE;  R4X5P0, TCAB3_TULGE;
DR   R4X247, TCAB4_TULGE;  I4DST8, TCEA1_TULGE;  I4DST9, TCEA2_TULGE;
//
ID   4.2.99.23
DE   tuliposide B-converting enzyme.
CA   6-tuliposide B = tulipalin B + D-glucose.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from pollen of the plant Tulipa gesneriana
CC       (tulip), catalyzes the intramolecular transesterification of
CC       6-tuliposide B to form the antibiotic aglycon tulipalin B as a sole
CC       product.
CC   -!- It does not catalyze the hydrolysis of 6-tuliposide B to form a
CC       hydroxy acid.
CC   -!- The enzyme has marginal activity with 6-tuliposide A. cf.
CC       EC 4.2.99.22.
DR   A0A0H5BMX5, TCEB1_TULGE;
//
ID   4.2.99.24
DE   thebaine synthase.
AN   THS.
CA   (7S)-O-acetylsalutaridinol = thebaine + acetate + H(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Papaver somniferum (opium poppy).
CC   -!- The reaction occurs spontaneously when the pH is between 8-9, but the
CC       enzyme is required at the physiological pH, which is close to 7.
DR   A0A2U9GHG9, THS1_PAPSO ;  A0A2U9GGW3, THS2_PAPSO ;
//
ID   4.2.99.25
DE   unsaturated pyranuronate lyase.
CA   (1) 4-deoxy-L-erythro-hex-4-enopyranuronate = (4S,5S)-4,5-dihydroxy-2,6-
CA   dioxohexanoate.
CA   (2) 4-deoxy-L-threo-hex-4-enopyranuronate = 5-dehydro-4-deoxy-D-
CA   glucuronate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in bacteria and archaea, is involved in the
CC       degradation of polysaccharides such as alginate and pectin.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes a pyranose ring-opening reaction followed by
CC       enol-keto tautomerization.
//
ID   4.2.99.n1
DE   Transferred entry: 4.2.99.20.
