ID   4.3.1.13
DE   carbamoyl-serine ammonia-lyase.
AN   O-carbamoyl-L-serine deaminase.
CA   O-carbamoyl-L-serine + H2O + H(+) = pyruvate + 2 NH4(+) + CO2.
CC   -!- The enzyme cleaves a carbon-oxygen bond, releasing CO2, ammonia,
CC       and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form,
CC       which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and a
CC       second ammonia molecule.
CC   -!- The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be
CC       catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.
//
ID   4.3.1.14
DE   3-aminobutyryl-CoA ammonia-lyase.
AN   L-3-aminobutyryl-CoA deaminase.
CA   (3S)-3-aminobutanoyl-CoA = (2E)-butenoyl-CoA + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Hydroxylamine can replace ammonia as a substrate.
CC   -!- Crotonoyl-pantetheine can replace crotonoyl-CoA but it is a poorer
CC       substrate.
DR   E3PRK1, KAL_ACESD  ;  Q8RHX1, KAL_FUSNN  ;
