ID   4.3.1.22
DE   3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine reductive deaminase.
AN   DOPARDA.
AN   DOPA-reductive deaminase.
AN   reductive deaminase.
CA   L-dopa + NADH + H(+) = 3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)propanoate + NH4(+) +
CA   NAD(+).
CC   -!- Forms part of the L-phenylalanine-catabolism pathway in the
CC       anoxygenic phototrophic bacterium Rhodobacter sphaeroides OU5.
CC   -!- NADPH is oxidized more slowly than NADH.
//
ID   4.3.1.23
DE   tyrosine ammonia-lyase.
AN   L-tyrosine ammonia-lyase.
AN   TAL.
AN   tyrase.
CA   L-tyrosine = (E)-4-coumarate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- Member of the aromatic amino acid lyase family, other members of
CC       which are EC 4.3.1.3, EC 4.3.1.24 and EC 4.3.1.25.
CC   -!- Far more active with tyrosine than with phenylalanine as substrate,
CC       but the substrate specificity can be switched by mutation of a single
CC       amino acid (H89F) in the enzyme from the bacterium Rhodobacter
CC       sphaeroides.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.1.5.
