ID   4.3.1.29
DE   D-glucosaminate-6-phosphate ammonia lyase.
CA   2-amino-2-deoxy-D-gluconate 6-phosphate = 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-6-phospho-D-
CA   gluconate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, from the bacterium Salmonella typhimurium, is involved in
CC       the degradation pathway of 2-amino-2-deoxy-D-gluconate.
DR   D0ZLR3, DGAE_SALT1 ;
//
ID   4.3.1.30
DE   dTDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-D-glucose ammonia-lyase.
CA   dTDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose + AH2 + S-adenosyl-L-methionine
CA   = dTDP-3-dehydro-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-glucose + 5'-deoxyadenosine +
CA   L-methionine + A + NH4(+) + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is a member of the 'AdoMet radical' (radical SAM)
CC       family, is involved in biosynthesis of TDP-alpha-D-desosamine.
CC   -!- The reaction starts by the transfer of an electron from the reduced
CC       form of the enzyme's [4Fe-4S] cluster to S-adenosyl-L-methionine,
CC       spliting it into methionine and the radical 5-deoxyadenosin-5'-yl,
CC       which attacks the sugar substrate.
DR   Q9ZGH1, DESII_STRVZ;
//
ID   4.3.1.31
DE   L-tryptophan ammonia lyase.
CA   L-tryptophan = (E)-3-(indol-3-yl)acrylate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Rubrivivax
CC       benzoatilyticus JA2, requires no cofactors.
CC   -!- It acts on L-phenylalanine and L-glutamate with about 60% of the
CC       activity with L-tryptophan, and on L-tyrosine, glycine, and L-alanine
CC       with about 30% of the activity.
//
ID   4.3.1.32
DE   7,8-didemethyl-8-hydroxy-5-deazariboflavin synthase.
AN   F0-synthase.
AN   FO synthase.
CA   5-amino-5-(4-hydroxybenzyl)-6-(D-ribitylimino)-5,6-dihydrouracil +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 7,8-didemethyl-8-hydroxy-5-deazariboflavin +
CA   5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + NH4(+) + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme produces the 7,8-didemethyl-8-hydroxy-5-deazariboflavin
CC       (F0) precursor of factor 420 (coenzyme F420), a metabolite found in
CC       methanogens and in various actinobacteria.
CC   -!- F0 is also produced by some cyanobacteria and eukaryotes.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which forms a complex with EC 2.5.1.147, is a radical SAM
CC       enzyme that uses the 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical to catalyze the
CC       condensation reaction.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.77.
