//
ID   4.3.2.9
DE   gamma-glutamylcyclotransferase.
AN   GGCT.
CA   an alpha-(gamma-L-glutamyl)-L-amino acid = 5-oxo-L-proline + an L-alpha-
CA   amino acid.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in animals and plants, acts on derivatives of
CC       L-glutamate, L-2-aminobutanoate, L-alanine and glycine.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts as a cyclotransferase, cleaving the amide bond via
CC       transamidation using the alpha-amine of the L-glutamyl residue,
CC       releasing it as the cyclic 5-oxo-L-proline.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.2.4.
DR   Q2UPC2, ACLK_ASPOR ;  A0A0M8N9Q3, ETPK_ESCWE ;  Q8GY54, GCT21_ARATH;
DR   Q84MC1, GCT22_ARATH;  Q32LE4, GGCT_BOVIN ;  O75223, GGCT_HUMAN ;
