ID   4.3.2.10
DE   imidazole glycerol-phosphate synthase.
AN   IGP synthase.
CA   5-[(5-phospho-1-deoxy-D-ribulos-1-ylimino)methylamino]-1-(5-phospho-beta-
CA   D-ribosyl)imidazole-4-carboxamide + L-glutamine = D-erythro-1-(imidazol-
CA   4-yl)glycerol 3-phosphate + 5-amino-1-(5-phospho-beta-D-
CA   ribosyl)imidazole-4-carboxamide + L-glutamate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in histidine biosynthesis, as well as purine
CC       nucleotide biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzymes from archaea and bacteria are heterodimeric.
CC   -!- A glutaminase component (cf. EC 3.5.1.2) produces an ammonia molecule
CC       that is transferred by a 25 A tunnel to a cyclase component, which
CC       adds it to the imidazole ring, leading to lysis of the molecule and
CC       cyclization of one of the products.
CC   -!- The glutminase subunit is only active within the dimeric complex.
CC   -!- In fungi and plants the two subunits are combined into a single
CC       polypeptide.
