//
ID   4.3.2.11
DE   (3R)-3-[(carboxylmethyl)amino]fatty acid synthase.
CA   a (3R)-3-[(carboxymethyl)amino]fatty acid + holo-[ACP] + H(+) = a (2E)-
CA   enoyl-[ACP] + glycine + H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in some actinobacterial species, participates in
CC       the biosynthesis of isonitrile-containing lipopeptides.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the formation of (3R)-3-[(carboxylmethyl)amino]fatty
CC       acid by the addition of glycine and the release of the product from
CC       the acyl-carrier protein.
DR   P64686, INLPD_MYCBO;  B2HKM2, INLPD_MYCMM;  P9WM66, INLPD_MYCTO;
DR   P9WM67, INLPD_MYCTU;  P0DX13, INLPD_STRC4;
//
ID   4.3.3.1
DE   3-ketovalidoxylamine C-N-lyase.
CA   4-nitrophenyl-3-ketovalidamine = 5D-(5/6)-5-C-(hydroxymethyl)-2,6-
CA   dihydroxycyclohex-2-en-1-one + 4-nitroaniline.
CC   -!- Eliminates 4-nitroaniline from 4-nitrophenyl-3-ketovalidamine or
CC       4-nitrophenol from 4-nitrophenyl-alpha-D-3-dehydroglucoside.
CC   -!- Involved in the degradation of the fungicide validamycin A by
CC       Flavobacterium saccharophilum.
//
ID   4.3.3.2
DE   Transferred entry: 3.5.99.13.
//
ID   4.3.3.3
DE   Transferred entry: 3.5.99.15.
//
ID   4.3.3.4
DE   Transferred entry: 3.5.99.16.
//
ID   4.3.3.5
DE   4'-demethylrebeccamycin synthase.
AN   arcyriaflavin A N-glycosyltransferase.
CA   4'-demethylrebeccamycin + H2O = dichloroarcyriaflavin A + beta-D-glucose.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a step in the biosynthesis of rebeccamycin,
CC       an indolocarbazole alkaloid produced by the bacterium Lechevalieria
CC       aerocolonigenes.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a glycosylase, and acts in the reverse direction to
CC       that shown.
CC   -!- It has a wide substrate range, and was shown to glycosylate several
CC       substrates, including the staurosporine aglycone, EJG-III-108A,
CC       J-104303, 6-N-methyl-arcyriaflavin C and indolo-[2,3-a]-carbazole.
DR   Q8KHE4, REBG_LENAE ;
//
ID   4.3.3.6
DE   pyridoxal 5'-phosphate synthase (glutamine hydrolyzing).
CA   aldehydo-D-ribose 5-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate +
CA   L-glutamine = pyridoxal 5'-phosphate + L-glutamate + phosphate + 3 H2O +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- The ammonia is provided by the glutaminase subunit and channeled to
CC       the active site of the lyase subunit by a 100 A tunnel.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use ribulose 5-phosphate and dihydroxyacetone
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme complex is found in aerobic bacteria, archeae, fungi and
CC       plants.
