ID   4.3.3.8
DE   mimosinase.
AN   mimosine amidohydrolase.
CA   L-mimosine + H2O = 3-hydroxy-4H-pyrid-4-one + pyruvate + NH4(+).
CC   -!- A pyridoxal 5'-phosphate protein.
CC   -!- The enzyme degrades the toxic amino acid L-mimosine.
CC   -!- It cleaves a carbon-nitrogen bond, releasing 3-hydroxy-4H-pyrid-4-one
CC       and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form,
CC       which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and
CC       ammonia.
CC   -!- It is thought to have evolved from EC 4.4.1.13.
CC   -!- It has been described in both mimosine-producing plants and some
CC       bacteria.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.5.1.61.
DR   A8CEI3, MIMOS_LEULE;  U6BYK3, MIMOS_MIMPU;
//
ID   4.3.3.9
DE   indigoidine synthase.
CA   2 FMN + 2 L-glutamine + 2 ATP + O2 = indigoidine + 2 FMNH2 + 2 AMP +
CA   2 diphosphate + 2 H2O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in a number of bacterial strains, is a non-
CC       ribosomal peptide synthase (NRPS).
CC   -!- The enzyme forms 3-amino-1,5-dihydropyridine-2,6-dione, which
CC       undergoes spontaneous oxidation to form the blue pigment indigoidine.
DR   Q9L391, INDGS_DICD3;  Q1MWN4, INDGS_STRLA;
