ID   4.6.1.14
DE   glycosylphosphatidylinositol diacylglycerol-lyase.
AN   (glycosyl)phosphatidylinositol-specific phospholipase C.
AN   6-(alpha-D-glucosaminyl)-1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol diacylglycerol-
AN   lyase (1,2-cyclic-phosphate-forming).
AN   glycosyl inositol phospholipid anchor-hydrolyzing enzyme.
AN   glycosylphosphatidylinositol-phospholipase C.
AN   glycosylphosphatidylinositol-specific phospholipase C.
AN   GPI-PLC.
AN   GPI-specific phospholipase C.
AN   variant-surface-glycoprotein phospholipase C.
AN   VSG-lipase.
CA   a 6-(alpha-D-glucosaminyl)-1-(1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho)-1D-myo-
CA   inositol = 6-(alpha-D-glucosaminyl)-1D-myo-inositol 1,2-cyclic phosphate
CA   + a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol.
CC   -!- This enzyme is also active when O-4 of the glucosamine is substituted
CC       by carrying the oligosaccharide that can link a protein to the
CC       structure.
CC   -!- It therefore cleaves proteins from the lipid part of the
CC       glycosylphostphatidylinositol (GPI) anchors.
CC   -!- In some cases, the long-chain acyl group at the sn-1 position of
CC       glycerol is replaced by an alkyl or alk-1-enyl group.
CC   -!- In other cases, the diacylglycerol is replaced by ceramide.
CC   -!- The only characterized enzyme with this specificity is from
CC       Trypanosoma brucei, where the acyl groups are myristoyl, but the
CC       function of the trypanosome enzyme is unknown.
CC   -!- Substitution on O-2 of the inositol blocks action of this enzyme.
CC   -!- It is not identical with EC 3.1.4.50.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.4.47.
DR   P09194, PHLC_TRYBB ;  O15886, PHLC_TRYCR ;
//
ID   4.6.1.15
DE   FAD-AMP lyase (cyclizing).
AN   FMN cyclase.
CA   FAD = riboflavin cyclic-4',5'-phosphate + AMP + H(+).
CC   -!- While FAD was the best substrate tested the enzyme also splits
CC       ribonucleoside diphosphate-X compounds in which X is an acyclic or
CC       cyclic monosaccharide or derivative bearing an X-OH group that is
CC       able to attack internally the proximal phosphorus with the geometry
CC       necessary to form a P=X product; either a five-atom monocyclic
CC       phosphodiester or a cis-bicyclic phosphodiester-pyranose fusion.
CC   -!- The reaction is strongly inhibited by ADP or ATP but is unaffected by
CC       the presence of the product, cFMN.
DR   Q58DK4, TKFC_BOVIN ;  Q3LXA3, TKFC_HUMAN ;  Q8VC30, TKFC_MOUSE ;
DR   F1RKQ4, TKFC_PIG   ;  Q4KLZ6, TKFC_RAT   ;
//
ID   4.6.1.16
DE   tRNA-intron lyase.
AN   tRNA splicing endonuclease.
CA   pretRNA = a 3'-half-tRNA molecule with a 5'-OH end + a 5'-half-tRNA
CA   molecule with a 2',3'-cyclic phosphate end + an intron with a
CA   2',3'-cyclic phosphate and a 5'-hydroxyl terminus.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the final stage in the maturation of tRNA
CC       molecules.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.27.9.
