ID   4.6.1.18
DE   pancreatic ribonuclease.
AN   pancreatic RNase.
AN   ribonuclease I.
AN   RNase.
AN   RNase A.
AN   RNase I.
CA   (1) an [RNA] containing cytidine + H2O = an [RNA]-3'-cytidine-
CA   3'-phosphate + a 5'-hydroxy-ribonucleotide-3'-[RNA].
CA   (2) an [RNA] containing uridine + H2O = an [RNA]-3'-uridine-3'-phosphate
CA   + a 5'-hydroxy-ribonucleotide-3'-[RNA].
CC   -!- Specifically cleaves at the 3'-side of pyrimidine (uracil or
CC       cytosine) phosphate bonds in RNA.
CC   -!- The reaction takes place in two steps, with the 2',3'-cyclic
CC       phosphodiester intermediates released from the enzyme at the
CC       completion of the first step.
CC   -!- Hydrolysis of these cyclic compounds occurs at a much slower rate
CC       through a reversal of the first step, in which the -OH group of water
CC       substitutes for the 2'-OH group of the ribose used in the first step,
CC       and does not take place until essentially all the susceptible
CC       3',5'-phosphodiester bonds have been cyclised.
CC   -!- The enzyme can act as an endo- or exo ribonuclease.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.7.16, EC 3.1.4.22 and EC 3.1.27.5.
DR   Q9WUR3, RNAS1_ABRJE;  Q9WTT5, RNAS1_ACOCA;  P07847, RNAS1_AEPME;
DR   P00667, RNAS1_ALCAA;  P00668, RNAS1_ANTAM;  Q8SQ06, RNAS1_ATEGE;
DR   P87351, RNAS1_AXIPR;  P00673, RNAS1_BALAC;  P61824, RNAS1_BISBI;
DR   P07849, RNAS1_BOSTR;  P61823, RNAS1_BOVIN;  P00657, RNAS1_BUBBU;
