ID   4.6.1.19
DE   ribonuclease T2.
AN   ribonuclease II.
CA   a ribonucleotidyl-ribonucleotide-RNA + H2O = a 3'-end 3'-phospho-
CA   ribonucleotide-RNA + a 5'-end dephospho-ribonucleoside-RNA + H(+).
CC   -!- A widely distributed family of related enzymes found in protozoans,
CC       plants, bacteria, animals and viruses that cleave ssRNA 3'-phosphate
CC       group with little base specificity.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes a two-stage endonucleolytic cleavage.
CC   -!- The first reaction produces 5'-hydroxy-phosphooligonucletides and
CC       3'-phosphooligonucleotides ending with a 2',3'-cyclic phosphodiester,
CC       which are released from the enzyme.
CC   -!- The enzyme then hydrolyzes the cyclic products in a second reaction
CC       that takes place only when all the susceptible 3',5'-phosphodiester
CC       bonds have been cyclised.
CC   -!- The second reaction is a reversal of the first reaction using the
CC       hydroxyl group of water instead of the 5'-hydroxyl group of ribose.
CC   -!- The overall process is that of a phosphorus-oxygen lyase followed by
CC       hydrolysis to form the 3'-nucleotides.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.7.17, EC 3.1.4.23 and EC 3.1.27.1.
