ID   4.99.1.3
DE   sirohydrochlorin cobaltochelatase.
AN   anaerobic cobalt chelatase.
AN   cobaltochelatase.
CA   (1) Co-sirohydrochlorin + 2 H(+) = sirohydrochlorin + Co(2+).
CA   (2) Co-precorrin-2 + 3 H(+) = precorrin-2 + Co(2+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, which forms part of the anaerobic (early cobalt
CC       insertion) cobalamin biosynthesis pathway, is a type II chelatase.
CC   -!- It is ATP-independent and exists as either a monomer (CbiX) or a
CC       homodimer (CibK).
CC   -!- CbiK from Salmonella enterica uses precorrin-2 as the substrate to
CC       yield cobalt-precorrin-2.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains two histidines at the active site that are
CC       thought to be involved in the deprotonation of the tetrapyrrole
CC       substrate as well as in metal binding.
CC   -!- CbiX from Bacillus megaterium inserts cobalt at the level of
CC       sirohydrochlorin (factor-II) rather than precorrin-2.
CC   -!- See EC 6.6.1.2 for the cobaltochelatase that participates in the
CC       aerobic cobalamin biosynthesis pathway.
DR   Q72CB8, CBIKC_NITV2;  Q72EC8, CBIKP_NITV2;  Q05592, CBIK_SALTY ;
DR   O29537, CBIX_ARCFU ;  Q9HQM3, CBIX_HALSA ;  O87690, CBIX_PRIMG ;
