//
ID   5.1.1.14
DE   nocardicin-A epimerase.
CA   (1) isonocardicin C = nocardicin C.
CA   (2) isonocardicin A = nocardicin A.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Nocardia uniformis,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of the monolactam antibiotic
CC       nocardicin A.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the epimerization of the amino group at position 9' from
CC       (S) configuration to (R).
CC   -!- The enzyme can act on both isonocardicin A and isonocardicin C,
CC       but the in vivo substrate appears to be the latter.
DR   Q5J1R2, NOCJ_NOCUT ;
//
ID   5.1.1.15
DE   2-aminohexano-6-lactam racemase.
AN   2-amino-hexano-6-lactam racemase.
AN   alpha-amino-epsilon-caprolactam racemase.
CA   L-2-aminohexano-6-lactam = D-2-aminohexano-6-lactam.
CC   -!- Also interconverts 2-aminopentano-5-lactam (alpha-amino-delta-
CC       valerolactam) and 2-amino-4-thiahexano-6-lactam (where S replaces CH2
CC       of C-4).
CC   -!- It does not catalyze the racemisation of alpha-amino acids but has
CC       some transaminase activity with them.
DR   Q7M181, ACLR_ACHOB ;
//
ID   5.1.1.16
DE   protein-serine epimerase.
AN   protein-serine racemase.
CA   L-seryl-[protein] = D-seryl-[protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme specifically interconverts the configuration of Ser-46 of
CC       the peptide omega-agatoxin-KT, found in the venom of the funnel web
CC       spider, Agelenopsis aperta, but not that of the other serine residue,
CC       Ser-28.
//
ID   5.1.1.17
DE   isopenicillin-N epimerase.
CA   isopenicillin N = penicillin N.
CC   -!- Epimerization at C-5 of the 5-amino-5-carboxypentanoyl group to form
CC       penicillin N is required to make a substrate for EC 1.14.20.1,
CC       to produce cephalosporins.
CC   -!- Forms part of the penicillin biosynthesis pathway.
DR   Q8J0E9, CEFD1_HAPCH;  Q8J0F0, CEFD2_HAPCH;  Q03046, CEFD_AMYLA ;
DR   P18549, CEFD_STRCL ;
//
ID   5.1.1.18
DE   serine racemase.
CA   L-serine = D-serine.
CC   -!- Highly selective for L-serine as substrate.
CC   -!- D-Serine is found in type-II astrocytes in mammalian brain, where it
CC       appears to be an endogenous ligand of the glycine site of N-methyl-D-
CC       aspartate (NMDA) receptors.
CC   -!- The reaction can also occur in the reverse direction but does so more
CC       slowly at physiological serine concentrations.
DR   Q2PGG3, SRR_ARATH  ;  A0JNI4, SRR_BOVIN  ;  Q54HH2, SRR_DICDI  ;
DR   Q9GZT4, SRR_HUMAN  ;  Q9QZX7, SRR_MOUSE  ;  A2XWA9, SRR_ORYSI  ;
DR   Q7XSN8, SRR_ORYSJ  ;  Q76EQ0, SRR_RAT    ;  O59791, SRR_SCHPO  ;
//
ID   5.1.1.19
DE   O-ureido-serine racemase.
CA   O-ureido-L-serine = O-ureido-D-serine.
CC   -!- The enzyme employs a two-base mechanism, with a thiolate-thiol pair
CC       in the active site.
CC   -!- It participates in the biosynthetic pathway of D-cycloserine,
CC       an antibiotic substance produced by several Streptomyces species.
DR   D2Z026, DCSC_STRLA ;
//
ID   5.1.1.20
DE   L-Ala-D/L-Glu epimerase.
AN   AE epimerase.
CA   L-alanyl-L-glutamate = L-alanyl-D-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Escherichia coli and
CC       Bacillus subtilis, is involved in the recycling of the murein
CC       peptide, of which L-Ala-D-Glu is a component.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme from E.coli epimerizes several L-Ala-L-X
CC       dipeptides with broader specificity than the enzyme from B.subtilis.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 5.1.1.n1.
DR   O34508, AEEP_BACSU ;  Q8A861, AEEP_BACTN ;  Q97MK4, AEEP_CLOAB ;
DR   P51981, AEEP_ECOLI ;  A0Q5S7, AEEP_FRATN ;  Q9WXM1, AEEP_THEMA ;
//
ID   5.1.1.21
DE   isoleucine 2-epimerase.
AN   BCAA racemase.
CA   L-isoleucine = D-allo-isoleucine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Lactobacillus buchneri,
CC       specifically catalyzes racemization of nonpolar amino acids at the
CC       C-2 position.
DR   M1GRN3, ILE2E_LENBU;
//
ID   5.1.1.22
DE   4-hydroxyproline betaine 2-epimerase.
CA   (1) trans-4-hydroxy-L-proline betaine = cis-4-hydroxy-D-proline betaine.
CA   (2) L-proline betaine = D-proline betaine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Pelagibaca bermudensis
CC       and Paracoccus denitrificans, specifically catalyzes racemization of
CC       trans-4-hydroxy-L-proline betaine and L-proline betaine at the C-2
CC       position.
DR   A1B198, HPBD_PARDP ;  Q0FPQ4, HPBD_SALBH ;
//
ID   5.1.1.23
DE   UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramoyl-L-alanyl-L-glutamate epimerase.
AN   UDP-MurNAc-L-Ala-L-Glu epimerase.
CA   UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramoyl-L-alanyl-L-glutamate + ATP + H2O = UDP-N-
CA   acetyl-alpha-D-muramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamate + AMP + diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Xanthomonas oryzae,
CC       catalyzes epimerization of the terminal L-glutamate in UDP-N-acetyl-
CC       alpha-D-muramoyl-L-alanyl-L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The reaction proceeds only in one direction and involves an
CC       adenylated intermediate.
CC   -!- The combined activity of this enzyme and EC 6.3.2.53 provides an
CC       alternative route for incorporating D-glutamate into peptidoglycan,
CC       replacing the more common combination of EC 5.1.1.3 and EC 6.3.2.9.
DR   C4RJF8, MURL_MICS3 ;  A4X982, MURL_SALTO ;  P0DQD8, MURL_XANOM ;
//
ID   5.1.1.24
DE   histidine racemase.
CA   L-histidine = D-histidine.
