ID   5.1.3.17
DE   heparosan-N-sulfate-glucuronate 5-epimerase.
CA   [heparosan-N-sulfate](n) = [heparan-N-sulfate](n).
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on D-glucosyluronate residues in N-sulfated heparosan
CC       polymers, converting them to L-iduronate, thus modifying the polymer
CC       to heparan-N-sulfate.
CC   -!- The enzyme requires that at least the N-acetylglucosamine residue
CC       linked to C-4 of the substrate has been deacetylated and N-sulfated,
CC       and activity is highest with fully N-sulfated substrate.
CC   -!- It does not act on glucuronate residues that are O-sulfated or are
CC       adjacent to N-acetylglucosamine residues that are O-sulfated at the 6
CC       position.
CC   -!- Thus the epimerization from D-glucuronate to L-iduronate occurs after
CC       N-sulfation of glucosamine residues but before O-sulfation.
CC   -!- Not identical with EC 5.1.3.19 or with EC 5.1.3.36.
DR   F1QR43, GLCEB_DANRE;  O18756, GLCE_BOVIN ;  P46555, GLCE_CAEEL ;
DR   O94923, GLCE_HUMAN ;  Q9EPS3, GLCE_MOUSE ;
//
ID   5.1.3.18
DE   GDP-mannose 3,5-epimerase.
CA   (1) GDP-alpha-D-mannose = GDP-beta-L-gulose.
CA   (2) GDP-beta-L-gulose = GDP-beta-L-galactose.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyze the formation of the stable intermediate GDP-
CC       beta-L-gulose as well as GDP-beta-L-galactose.
CC   -!- The reaction proceeds by C4' oxidation of GDP-alpha-D-mannose
CC       followed by epimerization of the C5' position to give GDP-beta-L-4-
CC       dehydro-gulose.
CC   -!- This intermediate is either reduced to give GDP-beta-L-gulose or the
CC       C3' position is epimerized to give GDP-beta-L-4-dehydro-galactose,
CC       followed by C4' reduction to yield GDP-beta-L-galactose.
CC   -!- Both products serve as intermediates in two different variants of
CC       plant L-ascorbate biosynthesis pathways.
DR   A2Z7B3, GME1_ORYSI ;  A3C4S4, GME1_ORYSJ ;  Q2R1V8, GME2_ORYSJ ;
DR   Q93VR3, GME_ARATH  ;
