ID   5.3.1.3
DE   D-arabinose isomerase.
AN   arabinose isomerase.
AN   L-fucose isomerase.
CA   D-arabinose = D-ribulose.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the closed form of the sugar and catalyzes ring
CC       opening to generate a form of open-chain conformation that
CC       facilitates the isomerization reaction, which proceeds via an ene-
CC       diol mechanism.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the aldose-ketose isomerization of several
CC       sugars.
CC   -!- Most enzymes also catalyze the reaction of EC 5.3.1.25.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Falsibacillus pallidus also converts
CC       D-altrose to D-psicose. cf. EC 5.3.1.4.
DR   P69922, FUCI_ECOLI ;
//
ID   5.3.1.4
DE   L-arabinose isomerase.
AN   L-arabinose ketol-isomerase.
CA   beta-L-arabinopyranose = L-ribulose.
CC   -!- Requires a divalent metal ion (the enzyme from the bacterium
CC       Escherichia coli prefers Mn(2+)).
CC   -!- The enzyme binds beta-L-arabinopyranose and catalyzes ring opening to
CC       generate a form of open-chain conformation that facilitates the
CC       isomerization reaction, which proceeds via an ene-diol mechanism.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also convert alpha-D-galactose to D-tagatose with
CC       lower efficiency.
DR   Q65GC0, ARAA1_BACLD;  Q97JE4, ARAA1_CLOAB;  Q65J10, ARAA2_BACLD;
