ID   5.3.1.5
DE   xylose isomerase.
AN   D-xylose aldose-ketose-isomerase.
AN   D-xylose isomerase.
AN   D-xylose ketoisomerase.
AN   D-xylose ketol-isomerase.
CA   alpha-D-xylose = alpha-D-xylulofuranose.
CC   -!- Contains two divalent metal ions, preferably magnesium, located at
CC       different metal-binding sites within the active site.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the interconversion of aldose and ketose sugars
CC       with broad substrate specificity.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the closed form of its sugar substrate (in the case
CC       of xylose and glucose, only the alpha anomer) and catalyzes ring
CC       opening to generate a form of open-chain conformation that is
CC       coordinated to one of the metal sites.
CC   -!- Isomerization proceeds via a hydride-shift mechanism.
