ID   5.3.3.8
DE   Delta(3)-Delta(2)-enoyl-CoA isomerase.
AN   3,2-trans-enoyl-CoA isomerase.
AN   acetylene-allene isomerase.
AN   Delta(3),Delta(2)-enoyl-CoA isomerase.
AN   Delta(3)-cis-Delta(2)-trans-enoyl-CoA isomerase.
AN   dodecenoyl-CoA Delta-isomerase.
AN   dodecenoyl-CoA isomerase.
CA   (1) a (3Z)-enoyl-CoA = a 4-saturated (2E)-enoyl-CoA.
CA   (2) a (3E)-enoyl-CoA = a 4-saturated (2E)-enoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the beta-oxidation of fatty acids with
CC       double bonds at an odd position.
CC   -!- Processing of these substrates via the beta-oxidation system results
CC       in intermediates with a cis- or trans-double bond at position C3,
CC       which cannot be processed further by the regular enzymes of the beta-
CC       oxidation system.
CC   -!- This enzyme isomerizes the bond to a trans bond at position C2, which
CC       can be processed further.
CC   -!- The reaction rate is ten times higher for the (3Z) isomers than for
CC       (3E) isomers.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the isomerization of 3-acetylenic fatty
CC       acyl thioesters to 2,3-dienoyl fatty acyl thioesters.
