ID   5.3.3.21
DE   Delta(3,5)-Delta(2,4)-dienoyl-CoA isomerase.
AN   3,5-tetradecadienoyl-CoA isomerase.
CA   a (3E,5Z)-dienoyl-CoA = a (2E,4E)-(5,6-saturated)-dienoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in an alternative degradation route of fatty
CC       acids with cis-double bonds on odd-number carbons such as oleate and
CC       linoleate.
CC   -!- The main physiological substrate is (3E,5Z)-tetradeca-3,5-dienoyl-
CC       CoA, but other (3E,5Z)-dienoyl-CoAs with varying carbon chain lengths
CC       are also substrates.
DR   Q9FHR8, DCI1_ARATH ;  G4NCP4, DCI1_PYRO7 ;  Q08558, DCI1_YEAST ;
DR   Q13011, ECH1_HUMAN ;  O35459, ECH1_MOUSE ;  Q5RFG0, ECH1_PONAB ;
DR   Q62651, ECH1_RAT   ;
//
ID   5.3.3.22
DE   lutein isomerase.
AN   meso-zeaxanthin isomerase.
CA   lutein = (3R,3'S)-zeaxanthin.
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE) of
CC       vertebrates.
CC   -!- It also has the activity of EC 3.1.1.64.
DR   Q6PBW5, RP65A_DANRE;  A9C3R9, RP65B_DANRE;  A9C3R8, RP65C_DANRE;
DR   Q9YI25, RPE65_AMBTI;  Q28175, RPE65_BOVIN;  Q9TVB8, RPE65_CANLF;
