//
ID   5.4.2.10
DE   phosphoglucosamine mutase.
CA   alpha-D-glucosamine 1-phosphate = D-glucosamine 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the pathway for bacterial cell-wall
CC       peptidoglycan and lipopolysaccharide biosyntheses, being an essential
CC       step in the pathway for UDP-N-acetylglucosamine biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli is activated by phosphorylation and
CC       can be autophosphorylated in vitro by alpha-D-glucosamine 1,6-
CC       bisphosphate, which is an intermediate in the reaction, alpha-D-
CC       glucose 1,6-bisphosphate or ATP.
CC   -!- It can also catalyze the interconversion of alpha-D-glucose
CC       1-phosphate and alpha-D-glucose 6-phosphate, although at a much lower
CC       rate.
