//
ID   5.4.2.12
DE   phosphoglycerate mutase (2,3-diphosphoglycerate-independent).
AN   2,3-diphosphoglycerate-independent phosphoglycerate mutase.
AN   cofactor independent phosphoglycerate mutase.
AN   phosphoglycerate phosphomutase.
AN   phosphoglyceromutase.
CA   (2R)-2-phosphoglycerate = (2R)-3-phosphoglycerate.
CC   -!- The enzymes from higher plants, algae, some fungi, nematodes,
CC       sponges, coelenterates, myriapods, arachnids, echinoderms, archaea
CC       and some bacteria (particularly Gram-positive) have maximum activity
CC       in the absence of 2,3-bisphospho-D-glycerate. cf. EC 5.4.2.11.
CC   -!- The reaction involves a phosphotransferase reaction to serine
CC       followed by transfer back to the glycerate at the other position.
CC   -!- Both metal ions are involved in the reaction.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.5.3 and EC 5.4.2.1.
