//
ID   5.4.3.9
DE   glutamate 2,3-aminomutase.
CA   L-glutamate = 3-aminopentanedioate.
CC   -!- This enzyme is a member of the 'AdoMet radical' (radical SAM) family.
CC   -!- It contains pyridoxal phosphate and a [4Fe-4S] cluster, which is
CC       coordinated by 3 cysteines and binds an exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-
CC       methionine molecule.
CC   -!- During the reaction cycle, the AdoMet forms a 5'-deoxyadenosyl
CC       radical, which is regenerated at the end of the reaction.
DR   Q185C5, EAM_CLOD6  ;
//
ID   5.4.3.10
DE   phenylalanine aminomutase (L-beta-phenylalanine forming).
CA   L-phenylalanine = (3R)-beta-phenylalanine.
CC   -!- cf. EC 5.4.3.11.
DR   P9WEN6, CCTP1_TALIS;  Q6GZ04, PAM_TAXCA  ;  Q68G84, PAM_TAXCH  ;
//
ID   5.4.3.11
DE   phenylalanine aminomutase (D-beta-phenylalanine forming).
CA   L-phenylalanine = (S)-3-amino-3-phenylpropanoate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Pantoea agglomerans produces D-beta-
CC       phenylalanine, an intermediate in the biosynthesis of the polyketide
CC       non-ribosomal antibiotic andrimid. cf. EC 5.4.3.10.
//
ID   5.4.4.1
DE   (hydroxyamino)benzene mutase.
AN   HAB mutase.
AN   hydroxylaminobenzene hydroxymutase.
AN   hydroxylaminobenzene mutase.
CA   N-phenylhydroxylamine = 2-aminophenol.
DR   O52214, HABA_ECTOL ;  O52216, HABB_ECTOL ;
//
ID   5.4.4.2
DE   isochorismate synthase.
AN   isochorismate mutase.
AN   isochorismate synthetase.
CA   chorismate = isochorismate.
CC   -!- The reaction is reversible.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 5.4.99.6.
DR   P23300, AMOA_AERHY ;  P45744, DHBC_BACSU ;  P0AEJ3, ENTC_ECO57 ;
DR   P0AEJ2, ENTC_ECOLI ;  Q9S7H8, ICS1_ARATH ;  Q9M9V6, ICS2_ARATH ;
DR   Q9ZPC0, ICS_CATRO  ;  Q7TYQ1, MBTI_MYCBO ;  Q73XV3, MBTI_MYCPA ;
DR   P9WFX0, MBTI_MYCTO ;  P9WFX1, MBTI_MYCTU ;  P23973, MENF_BACSU ;
DR   P38051, MENF_ECOLI ;  P44613, MENF_HAEIN ;  P9WFW8, MENF_MYCTO ;
DR   P9WFW9, MENF_MYCTU ;  Q9CPI5, MENF_PASMU ;  Q51508, PCHA_PSEAE ;
DR   O07898, VIBC_VIBCH ;
//
ID   5.4.4.3
DE   3-(hydroxyamino)phenol mutase.
AN   3HAP mutase.
AN   3-hydroxylaminophenol mutase.
CA   3-hydroxyaminophenol = aminohydroquinone.
DR   Q46ZL2, 3HAPM_CUPPJ;
//
ID   5.4.4.4
DE   geraniol isomerase.
CA   (2E)-geraniol = (S)-linalool.
CC   -!- In absence of oxygen the bifunctional linalool dehydratase-isomerase
CC       can catalyze in vitro two reactions, the isomerization of (3S)-
CC       linalool to geraniol and the hydration of myrcene to (3S)-linalool,
CC       the latter activity being classified as EC 4.2.1.127.
DR   E1XUJ2, LDI_CASD6  ;
//
ID   5.4.4.5
DE   9,12-octadecadienoate 8-hydroperoxide 8R-isomerase.
AN   (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxy-9,12-octadecadienoate mutase ((5S,8R,9Z,12Z)-
AN   5,8-dihydroxy-9,12-octadecadienoate-forming).
CA   (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate = (5S,8R,9Z,12Z)-5,8-
CA   dihydroxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate.
CC   -!- The bifunctional enzyme from Aspergillus nidulans uses different heme
CC       domains to catalyze two separate reactions.
CC   -!- Linoleic acid is oxidized within the N-terminal heme peroxidase
CC       domain to (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate (cf.
CC       EC 1.13.11.60), which is subsequently isomerized to (5S,8R,9Z,12Z)-
CC       5,8-dihydroxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate within the C-terminal P450 heme
CC       thiolate domain.
DR   B0Y6R2, PPOA_ASPFC ;  Q4WPX2, PPOA_ASPFU ;  Q6RET3, PPOA_EMEND ;
DR   G5EB19, PPOA_EMENI ;
//
ID   5.4.4.6
DE   9,12-octadecadienoate 8-hydroperoxide 8S-isomerase.
AN   (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxy-9,12-octadecadienoate mutase ((7S,8S,9Z,12Z)-
AN   5,8-dihydroxy-9,12-octadecadienoate-forming).
CA   (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate = (7S,8S,9Z,12Z)-7,8-
CA   dihydroxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate.
CC   -!- The bifunctional enzyme from Gaeumannomyces graminis catalyzes the
CC       oxidation of linoleic acid to (8R,9Z,12Z)-8-hydroperoxyoctadeca-9,12-
CC       dienoate (cf. EC 1.13.11.60), which is then isomerized to
CC       (7S,8S,9Z,12Z)-5,8-dihydroxyoctadeca-9,12-dienoate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.13.11.44.
DR   Q9UUS2, LIDS_GAEGR ;  G4N4J5, LIDS_PYRO7 ;
//
ID   5.4.4.7
DE   hydroperoxy icosatetraenoate isomerase.
AN   epidermal lipoxygenase-3.
CA   a hydroperoxyeicosatetraenoate = a hydroxy-epoxy-eicosatetraenoate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from mammals accepts a range of hydroperoxy
CC       icosatetraenoates producing one or several different hydroxy epoxy
CC       icosatrienoates.
CC   -!- The human enzyme has highest activity with (12R)-HPETE producing
CC       (5Z,8R,9E,11R,12R,14Z)-8-hydroxy-11,12-epoxyicosa-5,9,14-trienoate,
CC       followed by (12S)-HPETE producing (5Z,8Z,10R,11S,12S,14Z)-10-hydroxy-
CC       11,12-epoxyicosa-5,8,14-trienoate and (5Z,8R,9E,11S,12S,14Z)-8-
CC       hydroxy-11,12-epoxyicosa-5,9,14-trienoate.
CC   -!- The mouse enzyme has highest activity with (8S)-HPETE, producing
CC       (5Z,8S,9S,10R,11Z,14Z)-10-hydroxy-8,9-epoxyicosa-5,11,14-trienoate.
CC   -!- The enzymes also have the activity of EC 4.2.1.152.
DR   P51589, CP2J2_HUMAN;  Q9BYJ1, LOXE3_HUMAN;  Q9WV07, LOXE3_MOUSE;
DR   D3ZKX9, LOXE3_RAT  ;
//
ID   5.4.4.8
DE   linalool isomerase.
AN   3,1-hydroxyl-Delta(1)-Delta(2)-mutase (linalool isomerase).
CA   linalool = (2E)-geraniol.
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Thauera linaloolentis grown on (RS)-
CC       linalool as the sole source of carbon.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 5.4.4.4, which only acts on (S)-linalool, this enzyme acts
CC       equally well on both enantiomers.
DR   N6Z5E2, LIS_THAL4  ;
