ID   5.4.99.54
DE   beta-seco-amyrin synthase.
CA   (S)-2,3-epoxysqualene = beta-seco-amyrin.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Arabidopsis thaliana is multifunctional and produces
CC       about equal amounts of alpha- and beta-seco-amyrin.
CC   -!- See EC 5.4.99.52.
DR   Q9SYN1, PEN6_ARATH ;
//
ID   5.4.99.55
DE   delta-amyrin synthase.
CA   (S)-2,3-epoxysqualene = delta-amyrin.
CC   -!- The enzyme from tomato (Solanum lycopersicum) gives 48% delta-amyrin,
CC       18% alpha-amyrin, 13% beta-amyrin and traces of three or four other
CC       triterpenoid alcohols.
CC   -!- See also EC 5.4.99.40 and EC 5.4.99.39.
DR   E7DN64, DAMS_SOLLC ;
//
ID   5.4.99.56
DE   tirucalladienol synthase.
CA   (S)-2,3-epoxysqualene = tirucalla-7,24-dien-3beta-ol.
CC   -!- The product from Arabidopsis thaliana is 85% tirucalla-7,24-dien-
CC       3beta-ol with trace amounts of other triterpenoids.
DR   A0A5B8NBN0, OSC1_AZAIN ;  A0A067ECN5, OSC1_CITSI ;  A0A5B8NBE6, OSC1_MELAZ ;
DR   P0DXI2, OSC2_AILAL ;  Q9LVY2, PEN3_ARATH ;
//
ID   5.4.99.57
DE   baruol synthase.
AN   BARS1.
CA   (S)-2,3-epoxysqualene = baruol.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Arabidopsis thaliana also produces traces of 22 other
CC       triterpenoids.
DR   O23390, BARS1_ARATH;
//
ID   5.4.99.58
DE   methylornithine synthase.
CA   L-lysine = (3R)-3-methyl-D-ornithine.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a member of the superfamily of S-adenosyl-L-methionine-
CC       dependent radical (radical AdoMet) enzymes.
CC   -!- Binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster that is coordinated by 3 cysteines and an
CC       exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-methionine molecule.
CC   -!- The reaction is part of the biosynthesis pathway of pyrrolysine,
CC       a naturally occurring amino acid found in some archaeal
CC       methyltransferases.
DR   Q8TUB9, PYLB_METAC ;  Q46E78, PYLB_METBF ;
//
ID   5.4.99.59
DE   dTDP-fucopyranose mutase.
CA   dTDP-alpha-D-fucose = dTDP-alpha-D-fucofuranose.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the Escherichia coli
CC       O52 O antigen.
DR   Q6E7F1, FCF2_ECOLX ;
//
ID   5.4.99.60
DE   cobalt-precorrin-8 methylmutase.
CA   Co-precorrin-8X = cob(II)yrinate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which participates in the anaerobic (early cobalt
CC       insertion) adenosylcobalamin biosynthesis pathway, catalyzes the
CC       conversion of cobalt-precorrin-8 to cobyrinate by methyl
CC       rearrangement.
CC   -!- The equivalent enzyme in the aerobic pathway is EC 5.4.99.61.
DR   Q8EXP7, CBIC_LEPIN ;  Q58340, CBIC_METJA ;  O26329, CBIC_METTH ;
DR   O87692, CBIC_PRIMG ;  Q05601, CBIC_SALTY ;  P74304, CBIC_SYNY3 ;
DR   O29534, CBIHC_ARCFU;
//
ID   5.4.99.61
DE   precorrin-8X methylmutase.
AN   HBA synthase.
AN   hydrogenobyrinic acid-binding protein.
AN   precorrin isomerase.
CA   precorrin-8X + 3 H(+) = hydrogenobyrinate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which participates in the aerobic (late cobalt insertion)
CC       adenosylcobalamin biosynthesis pathway, catalyzes the conversion of
CC       precorrin-8X to hydrogenobyrinate by methyl rearrangement.
CC   -!- The equivalent enzyme in the anaerobic pathway is EC 5.4.99.60.
