ID   5.4.99.63
DE   ethylmalonyl-CoA mutase.
CA   (2R)-ethylmalonyl-CoA = (2S)-methylsuccinyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Rhodobacter sphaeroides,
CC       is involved in the ethylmalonyl-CoA pathway for acetyl-CoA
CC       assimilation.
DR   Q3IZ90, ECM_CERS4  ;  Q49115, ECM_METEA  ;
//
ID   5.4.99.64
DE   2-hydroxyisobutanoyl-CoA mutase.
CA   2-hydroxyisobutanoyl-CoA = (3S)-3-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Aquincola
CC       tertiaricarbonis, uses radical chemistry to rearrange the positions
CC       of both a methyl group and a hydroxyl group.
CC   -!- It consists of two subunits, the smaller one containing a cobalamin
CC       cofactor.
CC   -!- It plays a central role in the degradation of assorted substrates
CC       containing a tert-butyl moiety.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 5.3.3.20.
DR   I3VE77, HCMA_AQUTE ;  I3VE74, HCMB_AQUTE ;
//
ID   5.4.99.65
DE   pre-alpha-onocerin synthase.
CA   (3S,22S)-2,3:22,23-diepoxysqualene = pre-alpha-onocerin.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Lycopodium clavatum.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not act on (3S)-2,3-epoxy-2,3-dihydrosqualene and
CC       does not form any alpha-onocerin.
DR   A0A125SXN1, LCC_LYCCL  ;
//
ID   5.4.99.66
DE   alpha-onocerin synthase.
CA   pre-alpha-onocerin = alpha-onocerin.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Lycopodium clavatum.
DR   A0A125SXN2, LCD_LYCCL  ;
//
ID   5.4.99.67
DE   4-amino-4-deoxychorismate mutase.
CA   4-amino-4-deoxychorismate = 4-amino-4-deoxyprephenate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Streptomyces venezuelae
CC       and Streptomyces pristinaespiralis, participates in the biosynthesis
CC       of the antibiotics chloramphenicol and pristinamycin IA,
CC       respectively. cf. EC 5.4.99.5.
DR   F2RB77, CMLD_STRVP ;  P72541, PAPB_STRPR ;
