ID   5.6.1.7
DE   chaperonin ATPase.
AN   chaperonin.
CA   ATP + H2O + an unfolded polypeptide = ADP + phosphate + a folded
CA   polypeptide.
CC   -!- Multisubunit proteins with 2x7 (Type I, in most cells) or 2x8 (Type
CC       II, in Archaea) ATP-binding sites involved in maintaining an unfolded
CC       polypeptide structure before folding or entry into mitochondria and
CC       chloroplasts.
CC   -!- Molecular masses of subunits ranges from 10-90 kDa.
CC   -!- They are a subclass of molecular chaperones that are related to
CC       EC 5.6.1.5.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.4.9.
