DE   E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme.
AN   ubiquitin-activating enzyme E1.
CA   ATP + ubiquitin + [E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme]-L-cysteine = AMP +
CA   diphosphate + S-ubiquitinyl-[E1 ubiquitin-activating enzyme]-L-cysteine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the ATP-dependent activation of ubiquitin through the
CC       formation of a thioester bond between the C-terminal glycine of
CC       ubiquitin and the sulfhydryl side group of a cysteine residue in the
CC       E1 protein.
CC   -!- The two-step reaction consists of the ATP-dependent formation of an
CC       E1-ubiquitin adenylate intermediate in which the C-terminal glycine
CC       of ubiquitin is bound to AMP via an acyl-phosphate linkage, then
CC       followed by the conversion to an E1-ubiquitin thioester bond via the
CC       cysteine residue on E1 in the second step.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.2.19 and EC 6.3.2.21.
