CA   diphosphate + [E1 NEDD8-activating enzyme]-S-[NEDD8 protein]-yl-L-
CA   cysteine.
CC   -!- Some RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase (EC 2.3.2.27) are not able to
CC       bind a substrate protein directly.
CC   -!- Instead, they form complexes with a cullin scaffold protein and a
CC       substrate recognition module, which are known as CRL (Cullin-RING-
CC       Ligase) complexes.
CC   -!- The cullin protein needs to be activated by the ubiquitin-like
CC       protein NEDD8 in a process known as neddylation.
CC   -!- Like ubiquitin, the NEDD8 protein ends with two glycine residues.
CC   -!- The E1 NEDD8-activating enzyme activates NEDD8 in an ATP-dependent
CC       reaction by forming a high-energy thioester intermediate between
CC       NEDD8 and one of its cysteine residues.
CC   -!- The activated NEDD8 is subsequently transferred to a cysteine residue
CC       of EC 2.3.2.34, and is eventually conjugated to a lysine residue of
CC       specific substrates in the presence of the appropriate E3 transferase
CC       (EC 2.3.2.32).
