ID   6.3.1.19
DE   prokaryotic ubiquitin-like protein ligase.
AN   proteasome accessory factor A.
AN   Pup-conjugating enzyme.
AN   Pup ligase.
AN   Pup--protein ligase.
CA   ATP + [prokaryotic ubiquitin-like protein]-L-glutamate + [protein]-L-
CA   lysine = ADP + phosphate + N(6)-([prokaryotic ubiquitin-like protein]-
CA   gamma-L-glutamyl)-[protein]-L-lysine.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from the bacteria Mycobacterium
CC       tuberculosis and Corynebacterium glutamicum.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the ligation of the prokaryotic ubiquitin-like protein
CC       (Pup) to a target protein by forming a bond between an epsilon-amino
CC       group of a lysine residue of the target protein and the gamma-
CC       carboxylate of the C-terminal glutamate of the ubiquitin-like protein
CC       (Pup).
CC   -!- The attachment of Pup, also known as Pupylation, marks proteins for
CC       proteasomal degradation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.2.n2.
