DE   lipoate--protein ligase.
AN   lipoate protein ligase.
AN   lipoate-protein ligase A.
AN   LPL.
CA   L-lysyl-[lipoyl-carrier protein] + (R)-lipoate + ATP = N(6)-[(R)-lipoyl]-
CA   L-lysyl-[lipoyl-carrier protein] + AMP + diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme participates in lipoate salvage, and is responsible for
CC       lipoylation in the presence of exogenous lipoic acid.
CC   -!- The enzyme attaches lipoic acid to the lipoyl domains of certain key
CC       enzymes involved in oxidative metabolism, including pyruvate
CC       dehydrogenase (E2 domain), 2-oxoglutarate dehydrogenase (E2 domain),
CC       the branched-chain 2-oxoacid dehydrogenases and the glycine cleavage
CC       system (H protein).
CC   -!- Lipoylation is essential for the function of these enzymes.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use octanoate instead of lipoate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.7.63.
