DE   phosphoribosylglycinamide formyltransferase 2.
AN   5'-phosphoribosylglycinamide transformylase 2.
AN   GART2.
AN   GAR transformylase 2.
AN   GAR transformylase T.
AN   glycinamide ribonucleotide transformylase 2.
CA   N(1)-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)glycinamide + formate + ATP = N(2)-formyl-
CA   N(1)-(5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)glycinamide + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- Two enzymes are known to catalyze the third step in de novo purine
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- This enzyme requires ATP and utilizes formate, which is provided by
CC       the hydrolysis of 10-formyltetrahydrofolate by EC 3.5.1.10.
CC   -!- The other enzyme, EC 2.1.2.2, utilizes 10-formyltetrahydrofolate
CC       directly.
CC   -!- Formyl phosphate is formed during catalysis as an intermediate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli can also catalyze the
CC       activity of EC 2.7.2.1.
