//
ID   6.3.4.6
DE   urea carboxylase.
AN   ATP--urea amidolyase.
AN   UALase.
AN   UCA.
AN   urea amidolyase.
AN   urea carboxylase (hydrolyzing).
AN   urease (ATP-hydrolyzing).
CA   urea + hydrogencarbonate + ATP = urea-1-carboxylate + ADP + phosphate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- A biotinyl-protein.
CC   -!- The yeast enzyme (but not that from green algae) is bifunctional
CC       (resulting from gene fusion) and also catalyzes the reaction of
CC       EC 3.5.1.54, thus bringing about the hydrolysis of urea to CO2 and
CC       NH3.
CC   -!- cf. EC 6.3.4.26.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.5.1.45.
DR   A5H0J2, DUR1_LACKL ;  P32528, DUR1_YEAST ;  P38095, LAMA_EMENI ;
//
ID   6.3.4.7
DE   ribose-5-phosphate--ammonia ligase.
AN   5-phosphoribosylamine synthetase.
AN   ribose 5-phosphate aminotransferase.
CA   D-ribose 5-phosphate + NH4(+) + ATP = 5-phospho-beta-D-ribosylamine +
CA   ADP + phosphate + H(+).
//
ID   6.3.4.8
DE   imidazoleacetate--phosphoribosyldiphosphate ligase.
AN   5-phosphoribosylimidazoleacetate synthetase.
CA   imidazole-4-acetate + 5-phospho-alpha-D-ribose 1-diphosphate + ATP +
CA   H2O = 1-(5-phosphoribosyl)imidazole-4-acetate + ADP + phosphate +
CA   diphosphate + H(+).
//
ID   6.3.4.9
DE   biotin--[methylmalonyl-CoA-carboxytransferase] ligase.
AN   biotin--[methylmalonyl-CoA-carboxyltransferase] ligase.
AN   biotin--[methylmalonyl-CoA-carboxyltransferase] synthetase.
AN   biotin--[methylmalonyl-CoA-carboxytransferase] synthetase.
