//
ID   6.3.4.21
DE   nicotinate phosphoribosyltransferase.
AN   niacin ribonucleotidase.
AN   nicotinic acid mononucleotide glycohydrolase.
AN   nicotinic acid mononucleotide pyrophosphorylase.
AN   nicotinic acid phosphoribosyltransferase.
CA   5-phospho-alpha-D-ribose 1-diphosphate + nicotinate + ATP + H2O =
CA   nicotinate beta-D-ribonucleotide + ADP + phosphate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is involved in pyridine nucleotide recycling,
CC       can form beta-nicotinate D-ribonucleotide and diphosphate from
CC       nicotinate and 5-phospho-alpha-D-ribose 1-diphosphate (PRPP) in the
CC       absence of ATP.
CC   -!- However, when ATP is available the enzyme is phosphorylated resulting
CC       in a much lower Km for nicotinate.
CC   -!- The phospho-enzyme is hydrolyzed during the transferase reaction,
CC       regenerating the low affinity form.
CC   -!- The presence of ATP shifts the products/substrates equilibrium from
CC       0.67 to 1100.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.4.2.11.
