//
ID   6.3.5.4
DE   asparagine synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
AN   AS-B.
AN   asparagine synthetase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
AN   asparagine synthetase B.
AN   glutamine-dependent asparagine synthetase.
CA   L-aspartate + L-glutamine + ATP + H2O = L-asparagine + L-glutamate +
CA   AMP + diphosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli has two active sites that are
CC       connected by an intramolecular ammonia tunnel.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes three distinct chemical reactions: glutamine
CC       hydrolysis to yield ammonia takes place in the N-terminal domain.
CC   -!- The C-terminal active site mediates both the synthesis of a beta-
CC       aspartyl-AMP intermediate and its subsequent reaction with ammonia.
CC   -!- The ammonia released is channeled to the other active site to yield
CC       asparagine.
