ID   6.3.5.8
DE   Transferred entry: 2.6.1.85.
//
ID   6.3.5.9
DE   hydrogenobyrinic acid a,c-diamide synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
CA   hydrogenobyrinate + 2 L-glutamine + 2 ATP + 2 H2O = hydrogenobyrinate
CA   a,c-diamide + 2 L-glutamate + 2 ADP + 2 phosphate + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, which participates in the aerobic (late cobalt
CC       insertion) cobalamin biosynthesis pathway, generates
CC       hydrogenobyrinate a,c-diamide, the substrate required by EC 6.6.1.2
CC       which adds cobalt to the macrocycle.
CC   -!- The equivalent reaction in the anaerobic cobalamin biosynthesis
CC       pathway is catalyzed by EC 6.3.5.11.
