ID   6.3.5.13
DE   lipid II isoglutaminyl synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
CA   beta-D-GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)-
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + L-glutamine + ATP + H2O =
CA   beta-D-GlcNAc-(1->4)-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)-
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + L-glutamate + ADP +
CA   phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme complex, found in Gram-positive bacteria, consists of two
CC       subunits.
CC   -!- A glutaminase subunit (cf. EC 3.5.1.2) produces an ammonia molecule
CC       that is channeled to a ligase subunit, which adds it to the activated
CC       D-glutamate residue of lipid II, converting it to an isoglutamine
CC       residue.
