ID   7.1.1.4
DE   caldariellaquinol oxidase (H(+)-transporting).
AN   aa3 quinol oxidase.
AN   aa3-type quinol oxidase.
AN   cytochrome aa3.
AN   cytochrome aa3-type oxidase.
AN   terminal quinol oxidase.
CA   2 caldariellaquinol + O2 + n H(+)(in) = 2 caldariellaquinone + 2 H2O +
CA   n H(+)(out).
CC   -!- The enzyme from thermophilic archaea is part of the terminal oxidase
CC       and catalyzes the reduction of O2 to water, accompanied by the
CC       extrusion of protons across the cytoplasmic membrane.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.10.3.13.
//
ID   7.1.1.5
DE   menaquinol oxidase (H(+)-transporting).
AN   cytochrome aa3-600 oxidase.
AN   cytochrome bd oxidase.
CA   2 a menaquinol + O2 + n H(+)(in) = 2 a menaquinone + 2 H2O(in) +
CA   n H(+)(out).
CC   -!- Cytochrome aa3-600, one of the principal respiratory oxidases from
CC       Bacillus subtilis, is a member of the heme-copper superfamily of
CC       oxygen reductases, and is a close homolog of the cytochrome bo3
CC       ubiquinol oxidase from Escherichia coli, but uses menaquinol instead
CC       of ubiquinol as a substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme also pumps protons across the membrane bilayer, generating
CC       a proton motive force.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.10.3.12.
//
ID   7.1.1.6
DE   plastoquinol--plastocyanin reductase.
AN   cytochrome b6f complex.
CA   2 oxidized [plastocyanin] + a plastoquinol + 2 H(+)(in) = 2 reduced
CA   [plastocyanin] + a plastoquinone + 4 H(+)(out).
CC   -!- Contains two b-type cytochromes, two c-type cytochromes (cn and f),
CC       and a [2Fe-2S] Rieske cluster.
CC   -!- The enzyme plays a key role in photosynthesis, transferring electrons
CC       from photosystem II (EC 1.10.3.9) to photosystem I (EC 1.97.1.12).
CC   -!- Cytochrome c-552 can act as acceptor instead of plastocyanin,
CC       but more slowly.
CC   -!- In chloroplasts, protons are translocated through the thylakoid
CC       membrane from the lumen to the stroma.
CC   -!- The mechanism occurs through the Q cycle as in EC 7.1.1.8 (complex
CC       III) and involves electron bifurcation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.10.9.1 and EC 1.10.99.1.
