ID   7.2.1.4
DE   tetrahydromethanopterin S-methyltransferase.
AN   N(5)-methyltetrahydromethanopterin--coenzyme M methyltransferase.
AN   tetrahydromethanopterin methyltransferase.
CA   5-methyl-5,6,7,8-tetrahydromethanopterin + coenzyme M + 2 Na(+)(in) =
CA   5,6,7,8-tetrahydromethanopterin + methyl-coenzyme M + 2 Na(+)(out).
CC   -!- Involved in the formation of methane from CO in methanogenic archaea.
CC   -!- The reaction involves the export of one or two sodium ions.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the archaeon Methanobacterium thermoautotrophicum is
CC       a membrane-associated multienzyme complex composed of eight different
CC       subunits, and contains a 5'-hydroxybenzimidazolyl-cobamide cofactor,
CC       to which the methyl group is attached during the transfer.
CC   -!- A soluble enzyme that is induced by the presence of CO has been
CC       reported as well.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.86.
