DE   ABC-type sulfate transporter.
AN   sulfate ABC transporter.
AN   sulfate-transporting ATPase.
CA   sulfate(out) + ATP + H2O = sulfate(in) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli can interact with either of two
CC       periplasmic binding proteins and mediates the high affinity uptake of
CC       sulfate and thiosulfate.
CC   -!- May also be involved in the uptake of selenite, selenate and possibly
CC       molybdate.
CC   -!- Does not undergo phosphorylation during the transport.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.25.
