DE   ABC-type tungstate transporter.
AN   tungstate-importing ATPase.
AN   tungstate-specific ABC transporter.
AN   tungstate transporter.
CA   tungstate(in) + ATP + H2O = tungstate(out) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Pyrococcus furiosus,
CC       the Gram-positive bacterium Eubacterium acidaminophilum and the Gram-
CC       negative bacterium Campylobacter jejuni, interacts with an
CC       extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and mediates the import of
CC       tungstate into the cell for incorporation into tungsten-dependent
CC       enzymes.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.55.
