ID   7.3.2.7
DE   arsenite-transporting ATPase.
AN   arsenical pump-driving ATPase.
AN   arsenical resistance ATPase.
AN   arsenite-translocating ATPase.
CA   arsenite(in) + ATP + H2O = arsenite(out) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- This bacterial transporter does not belong to the ABC superfamily,
CC       and instead is a member of its own family, referred to as the Ars
CC       family.
CC   -!- The enzyme usually contains two subunits where one (with 12 membrane-
CC       spanning segments) forms the 'channel' part and the other (occurring
CC       in pairs peripherally to the membrane) contains the ATP-binding site.
CC   -!- It forms an arsenite efflux pump that removes arsenite from the
CC       cytoplasm, and can also remove antimonite anions.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.16.
