ID   7.4.2.2
DE   ABC-type nonpolar-amino-acid transporter.
AN   nonpolar-amino-acid-transporting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + nonpolar amino acid-[nonpolar amino acid-binding protein]Side
CA   1 = ADP + phosphate + nonpolar amino acidSide 2 + [nonpolar amino acid-
CA   binding protein]Side 1.
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in bacteria, interacts with an extracytoplasmic
CC       substrate binding protein.
CC   -!- This entry comprises enzymes that import Leu, Ile and Val.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.22.
//
ID   7.4.2.3
DE   mitochondrial protein-transporting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + mitochondrial-proteinSide 1 = ADP + phosphate +
CA   mitochondrial-proteinSide 2.
CC   -!- A non-phosphorylated, non-ABC (ATP-binding cassette) ATPase involved
CC       in the transport of proteins or preproteins into mitochondria using
CC       the TIM protein complex.
CC   -!- TIM is the protein transport machinery of the mitochondrial inner
CC       membrane that contains three essential Tim proteins: Tim17 and Tim23
CC       are thought to build a preprotein translocation channel while Tim44
CC       interacts transiently with the matrix heat-shock protein Hsp70 to
CC       form an ATP-driven import motor.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.51.
//
ID   7.4.2.4
DE   chloroplast protein-transporting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + chloroplast-proteinSide 1 = ADP + phosphate + chloroplast-
CA   proteinSide 2.
CC   -!- A non-phosphorylated, non-ABC (ATP-binding cassette) ATPase that is
CC       involved in protein transport.
CC   -!- Involved in the transport of proteins or preproteins into chloroplast
CC       stroma (several ATPases may participate in this process).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.52.
