ID   7.4.2.5
DE   bacterial ABC-type protein transporter.
AN   peptide-transporting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + proteinSide 1 = ADP + phosphate + proteinSide 2.
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- This entry stands for a family of bacterial enzymes that are
CC       dedicated to the secretion of one or several closely related proteins
CC       belonging to the toxin, protease and lipase families.
CC   -!- Examples from Gram-negative bacteria include alpha-hemolysin,
CC       cyclolysin, colicin V and siderophores, while examples from Gram-
CC       positive bacteria include bacteriocin, subtilin, competence factor
CC       and pediocin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.43.
