ID   7.4.2.8
DE   protein-secreting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + cellular proteinSide 1 = ADP + phosphate + cellular
CA   proteinSide 2.
CC   -!- A non-phosphorylated, non-ABC (ATP-binding cassette) ATPase that is
CC       involved in protein transport.
CC   -!- There are several families of enzymes included here, e.g. ATP-
CC       hydrolyzing enzymes of the general secretory pathway (Sec or Type
CC       II), of the virulence-related secretory pathway (Type III) and of the
CC       conjugal DNA-protein transfer pathway (Type IV).
CC   -!- Type II enzymes occur in bacteria, archaea and eucarya, whereas type
CC       III and type IV enzymes occur in bacteria where they form components
CC       of a multi-subunit complex.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.50.
