ID   7.5.2.5
DE   ABC-type lipopolysaccharide transporter.
AN   lipopolysaccharide-transporting ATPase.
AN   lipopolysaccharide transport system.
CA   ATP + H2O + lipopolysaccharideSide 1 = ADP + phosphate +
CA   lipopolysaccharideSide 2.
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- Does not undergo phosphorylation during the transport process.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli,
CC       functions as part of the lipopolysaccharide (LPS) export system,
CC       a seven protein system that translocates LPS from the inner- to the
CC       outer membrane.
CC   -!- The ATPase activity in this system is implicated in releasing LPS
CC       from the inner membrane.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.39.
DR   Q0P9C4, PGLK_CAMJE ;
//
ID   7.5.2.6
DE   ABC-type lipid A-core oligosaccharide transporter.
AN   ATP-dependent lipid A-core flippase.
AN   lipid flippase.
CA   ATP + H2O + lipid A-core oligosaccharideSide 1 = ADP + phosphate + lipid
CA   A-core oligosaccharideSide 2.
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- The enzyme, best characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli,
CC       is located in the inner membrane and mediates the movement of lipid A
CC       attached to the core oligosaccharide from the cytoplasm to the
CC       periplasmic side of the inner membrane, an important step in the
CC       lipopolysaccharide biosynthetic pathway.
CC   -!- Not to be confused with EC 7.5.2.5, which is implicated in the
CC       translocation of LPS from the inner membrane to the outer membrane
CC       and acts later in the process.
