DE   ABC-type D-xylose/L-arabinose transporter.
CA   (1) D-xylose(out) + ATP + H2O = D-xylose(in) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CA   (2) L-arabinose(out) + ATP + H2O = L-arabinose(in) + ADP + phosphate +
CA   H(+).
CC   -!- ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter with a 10-transmembrane-
CC       spanning (TMD) subunit and a single nucleotide binding domain.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the archaeon Sulfolobus acidocaldarius interacts with
CC       an extracytoplasmic sugar-binding protein and mediates the uptake of
CC       of D-xylose and L-arabinose (cf. EC 7.5.2.10 and EC 7.5.2.12).
