ID   7.5.2.14
DE   ABC-type homopolymeric O-antigen exporter.
CA   ATP + a lipid-linked O antigencytosol + H2O = ADP + phosphate + a lipid-
CA   linked O antigenperiplasm.
CC   -!- Unlike heteropolymeric O antigens, which are polymerized in the
CC       periplasm by EC 2.4.99.27, homopolymeric O antigens are polymerized
CC       inside the cytoplasm by a progressive transfer of sugar monomers to a
CC       growing chain attached to a polyprenyl diphosphate membrane anchor.
CC   -!- When the chain reaches its full length it is transported across the
CC       cytoplasmic membrane by this ABC-type transporter, which consists of
CC       an ATP-binding subunit (Wzt) and an integral membrane protein (Wzm).
CC   -!- Wzm proteins are poorly conserved in their primary sequence.
CC   -!- Once in the periplasm, the O antigen is ligated to the lipid A-core
CC       complex by EC 2.4.99.26.
//
ID   7.6.2.1
DE   P-type phospholipid transporter.
AN   flippase.
AN   phospholipid-transporting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + phospholipidSide 1 = ADP + phosphate + phospholipidSide 2.
CC   -!- A P-type ATPase that undergoes covalent phosphorylation during the
CC       transport cycle.
CC   -!- Different forms of the enzyme move phospholipids such as
CC       phosphatidylcholine, lyso-phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylserine,
CC       phosphatidylethanolamine, phosphatidyglycerol, sphingomyelin and
CC       glucosylceramide from one membrane face to the other ('flippase').
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.1.
