ID   7.6.2.2
DE   ABC-type xenobiotic transporter.
AN   ATP phosphohydrolase (steroid-exporting).
AN   MDR protein.
AN   multidrug-resistance protein.
AN   PDR protein.
AN   P-glycoprotein.
AN   pleiotropic-drug-resistance protein.
AN   steroid-transporting ATPase.
AN   xenobiotic-transporting ATPase.
CA   ATP + H2O + xenobioticSide 1 = ADP + phosphate + xenobioticSide 2.
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- Does not undergo phosphorylation during the transport process.
CC   -!- The enzymes from Gram-positive bacteria and eukaryotic cells export a
CC       number of drugs with unusual specificity, covering various groups of
CC       unrelated substances while ignoring some that are closely related
CC       structurally.
CC   -!- Several distinct enzymes may be present in a single eukaryotic cell.
CC   -!- Many of them also transport glutathione--drug conjugates (see
CC       EC 7.6.2.3) while others also show some 'flippase' activity (cf.
CC       EC 7.6.2.1).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.44.
