DE   ABC-type guanine transporter.
AN   guanine-transporting ATPase.
CA   guanine(out) + ATP + H2O = guanine(in) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- An ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter found in insects that
CC       transports guanine and other purines into pigment granules in the
CC       eye, where they are converted to pteridine pigments.
CC   -!- The transporter is a hererodimer composed of two different peptides,
CC       each containing one membrane-spanning and one cytoplasmic ATP-binding
CC       domain.
