ID   7.6.2.15
DE   ABC-type thiamine transporter.
AN   thiamine ABC transporter.
AN   thiamine transporting ATPase.
CA   thiamine(out) + ATP + H2O = thiamine(in) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Salmonella typhimurium,
CC       is a heterodimeric complex that interacts with an extracytoplasmic
CC       substrate binding protein and functions to import thiamine, thiamine
CC       monophosphate and thiamine diphosphate.
